{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5","id":1524711,"title":"Review of W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-29T13:38:56-07:00","id":1524711,"title":"Review of W5","content":"Late last month, I finally got my copy of W5 at my LGS. It was twenty-five dollars off with my pre-order discount and store credit, otherwise I might not have bought it. I am sort of a completist. I was hoping it wasn't as horrible (or great, depending upon your choice of social media) as I've been seeing. Now that I feel that I have gone over it enough, I will be reviewing it. To be as fair as possible, I will be reviewing it in four phases. Phase one will be a basic review of the book, divorced completely from any outside influences. I feel this will be the fairest way to be as neutral as possible. The second phase will be comparing it with the other WOD5 books, basically just V5 as my LGS hasn't been able to get H5 yet (not to mention any of the other books released since last winter). Ever since Renegade broke with some major distributors, many store haven't been able to get some of the new books. Phase three will be a comparison with the previous editions of Werewolf. Much of this will be based on W20, as most of my older books were destroyed in a flood some twenty years ago, and I wasn't able to replace most of them. (I'm slowly working getting the PDFs now that I've finished getting the WOD20 books.). The final phase will be based on the various &quot;issues&quot; raised since W5 was announced a year ago. Even though I want to be neutral and fair, such controversies need to be taken into account, just on their own and not with the main reviews of the book. As an example, I would give V5 B+, B, C+, and C respectively. So, without further ado, here is part one of my Phase one review.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW: PART ONE</span><br /> <br /> General Art Design/Layout<br /> The first thing one notices about W5 is the color of the pages. They aren't the standard white; they are more of a sepia tone with traces of grey. The bottom of the pages are also grey, as if they were mountains or a torn edge. Almost as if it were handmade. While this is a unique choice, the artwork suffers for it. Much of the art appears muddled on this tone, giving it a muddy look. The few traces of bright colors are almost garish next to these darker mixes. <br /> <br /> For many of the illustrations, the anatomy appears just a little off, making both humans and wolves an unworldly nature. While this can work with some of the more horrific forms, the 'regular' people just appear slightly off for it. Some of the pictures feature stock posing, almost unnaturally so. It doesn't help that many of the proportions and perspectives are also off. While this helps convey the otherworldly nature of the setting, using for almost every picture is unsettling. A little variety would have been nice. Art is subjective, so maybe there are those who like this style.<br /> <br /> The layout is non-standard as well. Multiple fonts are used on each page, giving a busy look. Chapter title are in a font similar to multiple stencils and slightly off-center, leading to a do-it-yourself vibe. A similar broken font style is used for major section headings, in a dried-blood looking dark red. This same color is used for smaller sidebars, with white lettering. (A sickly looking yellow-ochre is used for larger sidebars.) Subheading are in totally different font in dark green. In dim-lighting, both colors look similar, making it hard to differentiate. Those with difficulties with discerning colors might have problems as well. <br /> <br /> In all, the choices in color make the book feel closer to a text book than anything else. The uses of multiple colors and fonts weaken the layout, even without making it harder to read. Not the best way to introduce people to a new game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T11:21:07-07:00","id":1524872,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW: PART TWO</span><br /> <br /> Introduction<br /> After a somewhat muddier repeat of the from cover, there is the credit listing, followed by the Table of Contents. Some pages have two or three listing for them. That seems like it is more than necessary. I prefer sweeps of page numbers rather than going down to such minutiae. Also, the first typo is on the second page. Just a missed capital, but still strange. After three full-page artworks and a brief in-character reference to the world, the actual introduction begins. Apparently, this Fifth Edition has absolutely no continuity to previous editions. Technically, that would make it a new &quot;First Edition,&quot; but I guess that someone wanted to maintain something of the past. The first few sections try to tell you what the game is about and what these &quot;Garou&quot; werewolves are. They are nothing similar to werewolves in folklore or most movies, but there is nothing to explain any differences. What these Garou do do is fight in the name of their spirituality-driven duty to defend the earth. Following this is a section of storytelling games. Not sure if there needs to be such a lengthy discussion up front, but it could help newer players. The final section of the Intro is on mature themes. It might have been set off somehow, considering how important this part is, but it wasn't. After all of this is a one-page lexicon. Most of the unfamiliar and important terms are found here. However, there are quite a bit of terms that aren't here. Most of these are defined in the main text near where they are first used, but not all of them are. While their definitions can usually be sussed out, there still could be some confusion.<br /> <br /> Chapter One: A World of Darkness<br /> This is the setting chapter for the book. Basically, the world is dying, if not all but dead, and it is up to the Garou to to whatever they can to ...do something? The text is kind of vague on what exactly they should do, beyond they need to do it. This includes the spirit world that reflects physical reality, bound by an imbalance of three primal forces of creation, order, and destruction, called Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm respectively. It is the Wyrm that appears to be the main problem, although it could just be a reflection of what is truly wrong. Whatever, the actual causal relationship might not be important.<br /> <br /> Next, there is a discussion of how the game world works and looks. It boils down to Gothic and Punk, or at least some of the elements of these two styles. This includes the fact that the characters are not the good guys, just the stars of the story. That is going to be hard for some players to take in.<br /> <br /> Following this is a large section on just how bad the world is. Very depressing and very disheartening. Even the parts that shine a little are just barely hopeful. Why the designers chose such a dark mood with so little light is unknown. It does make a very dark game.<br /> <br /> The chapter ends with a section on some of the enemies of the Garou, divided mostly along the spiritual lines Garou follow. This might be a lot for newer players to take in so early in the book, even before exploration of Garou proper can take place. Personally, I would have placed the 'heroes' of the story before the 'villains,' but I guess the designers know what they are doing. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T11:46:14-07:00","id":1524874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524872#post1524872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the setting chapter for the book. Basically, the world is dying, if not all but dead, and it is up to the Garou to to whatever they can to ...do something? The text is kind of vague on what exactly they should do, beyond they need to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the fundamental problem of the book and it gets more explicit later on: The book has a deeply pessimistic attitude about what Garou are and what they can do. Their history is marked by failures and mistakes, the present is apocalyptic and the writers express very little faith in Garou being able to turn things around.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T13:06:41-07:00","id":1524985,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW: PART THREE</span><br /> <br /> Chapter Two: Being Garou<br /> This is where one would think a big hunk of information would be found, but it isn't quite that way. Much of what is found here is contradicted just a later on. While such open-ended freedom can be appreciated, this chapter almost borders on laziness. I hope it is just the designers trying to be vague as the game world develops, and they can figure something solid out. As is, one can't be sure just what to expect. The chapter starts with a section on history, kind of. While the broad swaths are well known to the Garou, the details change from the telling. It is implied that this is due to the oral tradition of the Garou, except they do appear to have a writing system and their own language, so something had to be written over time, especially in the last few centuries. Apparently, the Garou have been around longer than humanity. Somehow. Anyway, during those many centuries/millennia, The Garou went from hunters of humans to hiding from them. Over time, the various Garou organized into tribes and created a set a rules that all Garou should live by. What is strange is that nothing is given even an inexact range of when things happened. This includes events that may have happened fairly recently according to later chapters, so a more exact timeframe should be known. It is almost as if large chunks of the past were deliberately forgotten.<br /> <br /> This section ends with an in-game letter comparing the Garou with indigenous tribes in North America. I'm not sure what the comparison is. Is it about how young Garou aren't being taught by their elders or how lost Garou aren't able to learn anything? Both versions are supported by the text, as well as others. This letter seems so out of place as to be confusing, even if was meant to be very important.<br /> <br /> The next section covers Auspice and Tribe, the two main ways of classifying Garou. Auspice is basically one's moon sign and determines one's duties as a Garou. Tribe is based upon which Parton spirit and their teachings one follows. (One of the tribes are out of alphabetical order in the listing here.) Information of each is in the next chapter.<br /> <br /> In the next section, the how's of becoming Garou are discussed. Although determined at birth, no one knows who will become a werewolf until it happens. Although it does run in some families, and many new Garou find out they had a distant ancestor. After who know how long, someone should have figured out something. After being accepted as Garou, one joins a Tribe and enters into a pack, frequently with other new Garou. While a pack of five, with one of each Auspice, was once considered the best type, no one is forcing anyone to follow that advice, and just come up with whatever one wants to play. Then why mention that this was once the best way?<br /> <br /> The next section is on culture. Garou law is based on The Litany, a code that is semi-flexible, but most newer Garou question its authority in modern times. The individual tenets are not dealt with clearly, and they are barely even featured in a small sidebar at the bottom of a page. Again, why bring something up without actually going deeper into why it's important or not. This is followed by an understanding of how Garou divide into larger groups and how they meet up. Basically, it can lead to more trouble than good, so players are subtly pushed to try and avoid such larger interactions.<br /> <br /> The chapter ends with a discussion of the emotional state of being Garou. Apparently, Garou are prone to bipolar swings of despair over the fate of the world and intense action of trying to do anything to change things. Both are to be avoided, with the action part being considered worse for some reason. Actual systems are to be found in a later chapter, but they were important enough to merit an early mention, outside of the main range of concepts in the rest of the chapter.<br /> <br /> Chapter Three: Auspices and Tribes<br /> This chapter should be the one where the nitty-gritty behind the main character types should be found, but it just barely scratches the surface of what each character class could be.<br /> <br /> The first part deals with the Auspices, moon-signs of the Garou upon which they first changed. Each of the five Auspices get three brief paragraphs that boil down to roleplaying hints. Aside from a list of exclusive Gifts, Garou powers, there's really no mechanical advantage of choosing one Auspice over another. A player could always break the mold and not take the roleplaying hints into consideration. A real missed opportunity here for something.<br /> <br /> Each of the eleven Tribes get two pages to explain themselves. However, half that space is given over examples of who would belong to each Tribe and illustrations of them. Some Tribes are given more history than others, while most just get an unclear explanation of their mindset. The main mechanics are the Tribe's Patron Spirit and the Favor and Ban it sets on their charges. Each Favor is basically the same, &quot;Get a bonus in performing X action,&quot; without any variation among the Tribes. Bans are pretty much the same. &quot;Suffer a penalty if Y action isn't performed on a regular basis.&quot; While such acts are different among the Tribes, a little more variation would have been liked. It does make it easier to remember them, since they are all mostly alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T13:24:09-07:00","id":1524986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524985#post1524985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next section is on culture. Garou law is based on The Litany, a code that is semi-flexible, but most newer Garou question its authority in modern times. The individual tenets are not dealt with clearly, and they are barely even featured in a small sidebar at the bottom of a page. Again, why bring something up without actually going deeper into why it's important or not. This is followed by an understanding of how Garou divide into larger groups and how they meet up. Basically, it can lead to more trouble than good, so players are subtly pushed to try and avoid such larger interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, THIS is why the Litany section pisses me off so much. In older editions, each tenet was discussed and then the reality of it being used was given.<br /> <br /> The lack of this bites the writers in the arse, as one of the tenets is against cannibalism yet is not singled out. So W5 garou can munch on long pig and roasted dog all they want XD<br /> <br /> But more than that, what use is there to include the Litany if it is then stated to be ignored/abused?<br /> <br /> THEN, there is the &quot;you shouldn't try anything&quot; message. Which in a game about environmental destruction is... poorly thought out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T13:46:40-07:00","id":1524988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524985#post1524985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The chapter ends with a discussion of the emotional state of being Garou. Apparently, Garou are prone to bipolar swings of despair over the fate of the world and intense action of trying to do anything to change things. Both are to be avoided, with the action part being considered worse for some reason. Actual systems are to be found in a later chapter, but they were important enough to merit an early mention, outside of the main range of concepts in the rest of the chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because the &quot;do something&quot; is associated with the Cult of Fenris, and some of the paint that they used to cover up the prior development cycle work shows through in a later place - the statement about hauglosk being a way to introduce ecofascism as an issue.<br /> <br /> What it's covering up is that the creative director was hellbent on making the Get of Fenris of the prior/legacy material into dyed in the wool nazis, each and every one. The problem? The Get had explicitly killed off the members of their tribe that indulged in fascist idiocy, or driven them so far underground that they couldn't think about their racist agenda without several other Fenrir giving them the side eye (the aforementioned camp had never been the majority in the tribe). But the director insisted, over and over again, until people under him ended up getting canned and replaced and the legacy connection was downplayed into this &quot;reimagining&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the reason why &quot;do something&quot; is bad is because the creative direction wanted to make the Garou inevitably turn into nazis. And that is now the official rule of the game, in addition to the defining trait of the Cult of Fenris... among other, ill-thought out details, but that's for the discussion of a published adventure.<br /> <br /> (It's also worth noting that one of the tribes of W5, the Galestalkers, was a vast majority Indigenous American and Canadian tribe in legacy material, and the director had planned on killing them off because there was another tribe that was also majority Native, and he didn't think that they needed two. This would have followed on other legacy material that had already killed off a Native-majority Garou tribe in the history of the game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T13:53:49-07:00","id":1524989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524986#post1524986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, THIS is why the Litany section pisses me off so much. In older editions, each tenet was discussed and then the reality of it being used was given.<br /> <br /> The lack of this bites the writers in the arse, as one of the tenets is against cannibalism yet is not singled out. So W5 garou can munch on long pig and roasted dog all they want XD<br /> <br /> But more than that, what use is there to include the Litany if it is then stated to be ignored/abused?<br /> <br /> THEN, there is the &quot;you shouldn't try anything&quot; message. Which in a game about environmental destruction is... poorly thought out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intention was to be an easter egg or something, and also to create this atmosphere that the Garou lost their culture for... reasons and somehow this creates a parallel with people who have lost contact with their culture and TRY to make a social critique with this. As for the ignoring and abusing part, I think that's the thing he put in at the beginning, the Garou are not the heroes of the story, which makes me wonder who it would be, maybe no one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T14:20:20-07:00","id":1524991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524989#post1524989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the intention was to be an easter egg or something, and also to create this atmosphere that the Garou lost their culture for... reasons and somehow this creates a parallel with people who have lost contact with their culture and TRY to make a social critique with this. As for the ignoring and abusing part, I think that's the thing he put in at the beginning, the Garou are not the heroes of the story, which makes me wonder who it would be, maybe no one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that they then paint the lost culture as &quot;well oral histories suck&quot; is amazing tone deaf ESPECIALLY in Werewolf. Oral histories aren't a game of telephone, they are carefully watched BECAUSE they are histories.<br /> <br /> The 'no heroes in the story' works if the game focuses on faction wars. But once you have polluting vs non-polluting, it is hard to call the polluting side good guys.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T15:04:55-07:00","id":1524995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524985#post1524985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This chapter should be the one where the nitty-gritty behind the main character types should be found, but it just barely scratches the surface of what each character class could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> What's interesting about this is that when you look at what came before, it's noticeable how beside the short summaries in one section no Auspices and Tribes are mentioned by name. This contributes to the very surface-level descriptions of the setting. It's like you had a setting-description for VtM but Camarilla, Anarchs and Sabbat aren't mentioned and no Clan is mentioned by name either.<br /> <br /> There's the very obvious question with this setting of &quot;What has changed in the Age of Apocalypse?&quot; and the fact that the W5 corebook already does a bad job explaining what has led up to the present state of things only gets worse as basic concepts (like Auspice and Tribe) aren't framed satisfactorily in how they slot into the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524985#post1524985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Favor is basically the same, &quot;Get a bonus in performing X action,&quot; without any variation among the Tribes. Bans are pretty much the same. &quot;Suffer a penalty if Y action isn't performed on a regular basis.&quot; While such acts are different among the Tribes, a little more variation would have been liked. It does make it easier to remember them, since they are all mostly alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I slightly disagree with this description. There actually are differences in how the Tribe-Favors and Bans are portrayed. The principle is as you say &quot;Favor: When you do x, you get a bonus die. Ban: Don't do this or only recover only 1 WP next session.&quot;. Where this stops working is that despite such a simple formula barely any attention has been paid to staying consistent in how this is phrased.<br /> <br /> There are four distinctions of Favors in the W5 corebook:<ul><li>Whenever you try to do something that falls into this category...: Example Black Furies &quot;add a die to a pool used to oppose or circumvent someone or something in a position of power (relative to themselves or someone in their care).\u200b&quot;</li> <li>Whenever you use this skill under these circumstances...: Example Glass Walkers &quot;add one die to Technology or Science dice pools related to building or repairing things\u200b.&quot;</li> <li>Whenever you use this skill...: Example Hart Wardens &quot;add a die to any dice pool involving Survival, Animal Ken or nature-related Craft\u200b.&quot;</li> <li>Sometimes it's three Skills, sometimes two: Example Silver Fangs &quot;add one die to Persuasion or Leadership dice pools related to making others follow their advice, suggestions, or outright orders.\u200b&quot; vs Ghost Council &quot;add one die to Investigation, Occult, or Subterfuge dice pools related to revealing a kept secret.\u200b&quot;</li> </ul>With the Bans you run into the issue that one, it is never made clear whether actions under the effect of Rage also count and two, similarly to the Favors they are inconsistent. Example:<ul><li>Black Furies: If they let persist an injustice that they could\u2019ve prevented or addressed, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b</li> <li>Children of Gaia: If a Child of Gaia must lie or misdirect, or hides truths specifically for personal gain, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating. (If you have to argue whether it\u2019s \u201cfor personal gain,\u201d that\u2019s maybe an indicator of the intent\u2026)\u200b</li> <li>Hart Wardens: If harm comes to someone while under a Hart Warden\u2019s hospitality, the Hart Wardens may regain only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b</li> </ul>Some of these are just easier to avoid than others while in some cases you have some very serious debilitating Bans (like the one for CoG that forbids you from lying).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T18:06:16-07:00","id":1525005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524991#post1524991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that they then paint the lost culture as &quot;well oral histories suck&quot; is amazing tone deaf ESPECIALLY in Werewolf. Oral histories aren't a game of telephone, they are carefully watched BECAUSE they are histories.<br /> <br /> The 'no heroes in the story' works if the game focuses on faction wars. But once you have polluting vs non-polluting, it is hard to call the polluting side good guys.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Look... if I understand correctly, W5 is so vague that I can't even say if this is still the theme, it just seems like a thrown element that's there, but if you want you don't even need to care about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T11:24:42-08:00","id":1525084,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW, PART FOUR</span><br /> <br /> Chapter Four: Characters<br /> This is where the actual character creation happens. At the start is a small sidebar summarizing the process. I would have wanted something larger with all of the option together, as one has to go back to the previous chapter for some of the necessary information. Apparently, one can create a wolf-born character as well as the standard human one, but there are no particular rules to do so. The example suggests that wolves would be good at working with animals. I'm sure no one thought that a predator would know how to calm a prey animal such as a horse just because they once were a wolf. There should have been a more directed process for wolf characters.<br /> <br /> The first phase involves Attributes, the major traits used in most actions. These traits also help determine starting Health and Willpower. Theoretically, one could start out as a very weak and/or weak-willed character, which could be very detrimental. Next comes Skills, secondary traits used to focus on particular actions. Not everyone has every skills this is a way to individualize. Some skills can have specialities, but they should only occur in certain situations. I'm not sure if specialties should be so limiting, or work exactly that way.<br /> <br /> Next come Advantages. These traits are highly individualized. They are divided into Merits and Backgrounds, with Flaws that can cause problems for players . It is not clear if Flaws net players extra points to be used on other traits or not. Otherwise, why take a trait that is so debilitating. Also, it feels like that there aren't enough of any to these traits, like there might be something missing to add more variation.<br /> <br /> The next section covers Renown. It feels like Renown should factor into a sort of power level hierarchy, but that is not the case. It just helps determine the level of Gifts one can purchase and the number of dice used to roll for them. Really, this trait feels underused and underwhelming. There's a brief section about Gifts and Rites following this, but they are covered in a later chapter. Following this is a section on Touchstones, the people that a werewolf uses to stay in touch with their human, or wolf, side. <br /> <br /> The rest of the chapter is about finishing touches to round out a character, an explanation on awarding and using experience points to evolve a character, and notes on using a 'relationship map' to see how various player characters interact. This last part feels weak, as such things could change by the end of the first session, if not sooner. Maybe it is important to some groups, but this might not be as important to more experienced player.<br /> <br /> Chapter Five: Rules<br /> This is where the actual action of playing takes place. Hidden in the second paragraph of the chapter is a notice of free downloadable material for extended rules. However, unlike other web addresses found later on, this one is not set appear, and it could easily be overlooked. Anything that could benefit a player should be more readily apparent. The first section details how to time is handled in the game and how to use dice to determine results. Illustrations of a fight between two Garou are interspersed among the text, with the possibility that one is out of order. Special rules are presented for dealing with damage and a few basic maneuvers that could be found in combat. Straightforward material.<br /> <br /> Next is a section on rules specific to Garou. First is Rage, the animalistic 'fuel' a Garou uses for their supernatural powers. The more Rage one has, the more they can do with it, but the harder it will be to interact with humans. With less Rage, working with humans is easier, but you can't do as much on the supernatural side. There are even special 'Rage dice' a player uses to help show these negative effects. The dice used for the game are ten-siders without actual numbers on them, based on the description, but regular ten-sided dice in two separate colors could be used. [The dice especially meant to be used for this game are in an orange-pink for regular use and lime-green for Rage, although the actual photographs might not show the colors accurately.] Rage is used for regenerating damage, transforming into one of a Garou's five forms (human, near-human, wolf-man, big wolf, and wolf), using Gifts, and a few other things. The text suggests that wolves could sometimes be mistaken for big dogs in some places, but that is unlikely.<br /> <br /> The chapter ends with a discussion on some mental states. Frenzy happens when a Garou gives in to their Rage and can't control themselves. Harrano and Hauglosk are the depressive and active states mentioned previously. Renown is shown as a way to influence social interaction, while its opposite of Chagrin is a state of being outcast. Finally, Delirium is a state that most humans get when facing Garou in an obvious supernatural situation. Overall, none of these mental conditions are overly difficult, but just lacking in some minor quality to make them feel important.<br /> <br /> Chapter Six: Gifts, Rites, and Gear<br /> Finally, we get to the 'cool powers' chapter. <br /> First come Gifts, the main powers of the Garou. Gifts are divided into three classes: Native (which would be better called natal or ingrained), Auspice, and Tribe. Each type of Gift is further divided into three levels, unlike every other trait which is on a one to five/ten scale. Each variety of Gift uses a different scale to measure each level, based on one's total Renown. Each level goes up by three Renown, starting from a different base number (Native at one, four, and seven; Auspice at two, five, and eight; and Tribe at three, six, and nine). Theoretically, two more levels of Gifts might be available, as total Renown could go up to fifteen. Why they aren't mentioned is unknown.<br /> <br /> Native Gifts are available to every Garou, but Auspice and Tribe Gifts are usually only available to those of the particular group. Multiple mistakes in what Renown levels are used can be found, but one should follow the system mentioned above and just ignore any difference. The Gifts feature a wide range of abilities, but they do have limits. Supposedly, Gifts can only be used in supernatural forms, but there are so many exceptions that this rule really isn't so important. Some Gifts say that similar Gifts can't be used at the same time, but not all such Gifts seem to be classified as such, even it they could be.<br /> <br /> Rites are what they say, special rituals used for a special effect. Rites don't have ranks, so this mean a starting character could theoretically know something ridiculously overpowered. Rites are supposed to work better in groups, with just one character having to know the Rite. This feels off, as some Rites are rather singular or personal in nature. <br /> <br /> Next come Talismans, objects either permanently or temporarily possessed by a spirit that causes a supernatural effect. Only eight are mentioned (nine if you included a legendary one seen in a sidebar), but it feels like there could have been many more. There just doesn't seem to be a wide variety. Technically, Talismans are unranked, but some have an optional rating if used for the Talisman Background. Again, a good reason to have more variety.<br /> <br /> Caerns, the spiritual areas of the world that the Garou cherish and protect, are next, but they probably should have been listed after Rites, since Rites frequently work better at such locations. Various systems and traits of Caerns are included, but they are basically unranked beyond basic qualities.<br /> <br /> Lastly, various types of regular weapons and armor are listed. Types really aren't used, as simple generic descriptions are enough in most cases. In fact, this section almost feels like an afterthought, as it reduces weapons to a bare minimum of information. Somewhat disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T12:14:46-08:00","id":1525085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525084#post1525084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, one can create a wolf-born character as well as the standard human one, but there are no particular rules to do so. The example suggests that wolves would be good at working with animals. I'm sure no one thought that a predator would know how to calm a prey animal such as a horse just because they once were a wolf. There should have been a more directed process for wolf characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I really don't like how wolf-born are treated in this book. Honestly, it would've been better to not mention them at all or just erase them. It's clear the writers had no interest in wolf-born PCs when they wrote the book. I would call out the sidebar on pg 109 &quot;Wolf-Born and Wolf Touchstones&quot; for its patronizing and dismissive tone. Either it's a player-option or not. Making it a player-option and then whining about it being one doesn't help anybody.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525084#post1525084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following this is a section on Touchstones, the people that a werewolf uses to stay in touch with their human, or wolf, side.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I always have to call it out because it bugs me: Both H5 and W5 explain Touchstones like this: &quot;The more Touchstones the character has, the better they\u2019re able to mitigate their monstrous impulses, but the more vulnerabilities they have.\u200b&quot; And with W5 this is now the <i>second (!) </i>time this formula doesn't apply to how Touchstones actually work. Incredibly as well, H5 and W5 fail in two <i>different </i>ways in how Touchstones work compared to this stated goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525084#post1525084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, unlike other web addresses found later on, this one is not set appear, and it could easily be overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Ha! They recently overhauled the WOD-website (it's now a sub-section of the Paradox-website), so the web-address is wrong actually.<br /> <br /> For anybody reading this who's still interested: It's under the Community-header and then &quot;Free Downloadable Content&quot; on the new website. But I have my doubts that everybody will find that quickly...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525084#post1525084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites are supposed to work better in groups, with just one character having to know the Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The system is set up to do the exact opposite of that. It's even mentioned on pg 180: &quot;the more werewolves involved in performing a Rite thus make its performance more fraught but potentially increase the margin for success.\u200b&quot; What is meant by that is that the system has participants add Rage-dice (a Rage-die and a normal die if they know the Rite) and most Rites have extra rules for Brutal Outcomes (pairs of 1s/2s on Rage-dice) doing bad stuff to the participants. This gets especially ugly for those Rites like &quot;Rite Of Caern Building&quot; with high difficulties. You need a lot of participants but also the chance of bad stuff happening increases. This also means that with Rites of lower difficulties having a lot of participants would be counterproductive. The likelihood of bad stuff happening would be increased for no reason.<br /> <br /> If anything this is a system supporting the idea that huge crowds of Garou participating in a Rite should be avoided. The same way the book believes the idea of the Garou-Nation to be a failed idea, it has no faith in Garou acting collectively and this gets reinforced with this system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525084#post1525084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, none of these mental conditions are overly difficult, but just lacking in some minor quality to make them feel important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harano and Hauglosk are <i>very </i>important in W5. In addition to dying, these are two additional failstates for a PC. The moment you hit Harano 5 or Hauglosk 5 your character becomes an NPC. And Touchstones only allow you switch a dot from one to the other once per story (which makes little sense narratively). Other than a rare Talisman there's no way to reduce your Harano or Hauglosk track. This is essentially a death-spiral-mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T12:38:36-08:00","id":1525086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525085#post1525085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> I really don't like how wolf-born are treated in this book. Honestly, it would've been better to not mention them at all or just erase them. It's clear the writers had no interest in wolf-born PCs when they wrote the book. I would call out the sidebar on pg 109 &quot;Wolf-Born and Wolf Touchstones&quot; for its patronizing and dismissive tone. Either it's a player-option or not. Making it a player-option and then whining about it being one doesn't help anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the time-honored, Gary Gygax-pioneered &quot;Okay, I&quot;ll Let You Play It, But I'm Not Going To Like It And Neither Are You&quot; method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T16:30:17-08:00","id":1525093,"title":"","content":"How do Caerns work? I mean, I don't think they can be used to recharge rage (at least I don't think that makes sense) and with so much lost Garou history and lack of contact with the Umbra, among others, I think the traditional Caerns have kind of lost their fuction. By the way, the packs would only need places like bases/hideouts or are the Caerns just places of Gaia or something?<br /> <br /> Another thing that struck me, how does W5 approach the relationship between tribes? As they are no longer unified within a nation, it is to be expected that they have become somewhat fearful of each other, although they already were a little. Now that I think about it, that would be an interesting concept, tribes that used to cooperate now fight over resources or territory. Kind of like an AU.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I understand why there isn't a hierarchy like there was before.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T16:31:11-08:00","id":1525094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525086#post1525086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the time-honored, Gary Gygax-pioneered &quot;Okay, I&quot;ll Let You Play It, But I'm Not Going To Like It And Neither Are You&quot; method.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are this from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T17:09:32-08:00","id":1525098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525093#post1525093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Caerns work? I mean, I don't think they can be used to recharge rage (at least I don't think that makes sense) and with so much lost Garou history and lack of contact with the Umbra, among others, I think the traditional Caerns have kind of lost their fuction. By the way, the packs would only need places like bases/hideouts or are the Caerns just places of Gaia or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still supposed to be the same but previously they were these reserves of spiritual energy... which they still are. But before you had Gnosis as a concept to quantify and define that. And Gnosis isn't a thing in W5 anymore, though. Also, since WtA has an animistic perspective there was a spirit at the heart of the caern. That isn't the case either anymore. You can buy &quot;Spirit Guardians&quot; via the caern-management-system but caerns aren't naturally represented with a spirit. They are just big batteries of spiritual energy now. And mechanically really the only thing that makes a caern distinctive beyond the bonuses you buy via this management-system is that the Gauntlet is thin there. But of course, if none of the PCs has bought the Rite to enter the Umbra or chosen it during character-creation, that group can't enter the Umbra anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, Moonbridges have been written out of the game because... street-level-only.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure they gave an artist the wrong prompt or didn't give enough of an explanation of what they wanted... Because on pg 185 you get an art-piece of piles of stones since whoever the artist was probably got the prompt to draw a caern. And he ended up drawing cairns (man-made piles of stones) instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525093#post1525093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that struck me, how does W5 approach the relationship between tribes? As they are no longer unified within a nation, it is to be expected that they have become somewhat fearful of each other, although they already were a little. Now that I think about it, that would be an interesting concept, tribes that used to cooperate now fight over resources or territory. Kind of like an AU.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I understand why there isn't a hierarchy like there was before.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're talking about here is actually embracing stuff like &quot;Age of the Apocalypse&quot;. But you won't get anything definitive from the W5 corebook. Take the Litany: According to the book, the elders abuse it, the young ones ignore it/rebel against it - and <i>somehow </i>it's still a norm in some fashion. You'd think the Litany can't still be relevant while also being seen as completely dysfunctional... but that's how the W5 corebook portrays it.<br /> <br /> As for the actual book... So what is the difference between the Garou-Tribes before the fall of the Garou-Nation and after...? Who knows. How have the Tribes changed in the Age of Apocalypse? Who knows. And so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T18:24:24-08:00","id":1525101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525094#post1525094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are this from?</div> </div> </div> </div>GG and his group were notorious for being at odds about what inspirations they favored for D&amp;D. Gygax favored sword and sorcery sources with typically human protagonists like Conan, while his fellows frequently preferred Tolkien and wanted to bring in elves, dwarfs, hobbits and what have you. So, he &quot;compromised&quot;, and by that I mean he allowed them but put in things like negative stat modifiers, level limits, and onerous roleplaying restrictions to discourage people from playing the Tolkien-inspired material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T12:30:23-08:00","id":1525216,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW PART FIVE</span><br /> <br /> Chapter Seven: Storytelling<br /> I really don't have much to say about this chapter. While I might not have chosen some of the ways the designers chose to convey this information, it still is fairly decent. This chapter usually is one of the least interesting ones in rulebooks. Necessary, but mostly important to newer players. There might be something here for those more familiar, so it still needs at least some looking over.<br /> <br /> Chapter Eight: The Umbra and Spirts<br /> This is the secondary setting for the game, the spiritual side of the world where almost anything could happen and is almost nothing can be easily defined. This includes something called 'Gaia's Howl,&quot; a feeling Garou get when entering the Umbra. I wish I could explain it better, but the citation for more information just refers back to the previously read paragraph on the same page. This is a very bad case of pasting/editing.<br /> <br /> Basically, it is very hard to enter the Umbra, but easy to leave. The environment is inherently hostile, and it could kill you the longer you stay there. The relative locations and spirits could change at any time. Things may have been different in the past, but this is how it is now. Why include such an interesting possibility for play, and then make it so difficult to actually use it?Anything more than a quick foray will be tough. The sidebars calls this &quot;mysterious,&quot; but it feels more like the designers don't want players to spend much time here, if any.<br /> <br /> The chapter ends (it's barely fourteen pages long) with rundown on how Garou categorize spirits in relative power terms. The spirits themselves 'know' their places in the hierarchy, but don't really use the same terms. The most powerful spirits rarely if ever come into contact with lesser beings such as Garou, but the weaker ones frequently do. A few ideas for dealing with spirits are mentioned, but not many firm examples are given.<br /> <br /> Chapter Nine: Allies and Antagonists<br /> This chapters covers many of the secondary characters players can face. The chapter's title is slightly wrong, though, as the vast majority presented here are likely enemies and not friends. In fact, hardly any of the examples given would flat out be friendly to most characters. I would have called this chapter &quot;Antagonists and Possible Allies,&quot; but I guess it doesn't have the same ring to it. As the book says, Garou have lots of enemies.<br /> <br /> The first section covers spirits. Apparently, spirits love to possess people and things in the physical world for various reasons, most of them leading to conflict with werewolves. Why they can't just form their own bodies is unknown. Most are considered hostile to indifferent to Garou, making them enemies. The spirits are classified by primary patron: Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld, or Gaia. With the first one being most likely to be foes, and the last as indifferent to friendly. <br /> <br /> Next comes Fomori, people who have been possessed by Banes, corrupt Wyrm spirits for lengthy periods of time. Being possessed for so long gives them abilities far beyond 'average' spirits. They feel like they are to be seen as a primary type of enemy. They are given a wide range of powers, of various levels of commonality. They are often found working with/for a multi-national holding corporation known as Pentex. This enemy feels like the typical evil corporation clich\u00e9. While the overwhelming majority of its 'evilness' isn't supernatural, even its mundane practices can be seen as bad. I'm not sure I like how they are presented as the &quot;man-behind-the-curtain&quot; who really is the big-bad that takes multiple chapters to locate, yet that is how the storytelling chapter prefers to set such game sessions up. <br /> <br /> Following this is a section on Garou and other shapeshifters as enemies. Three 'fallen' tribes are presented, with just a bit more sense of history than the eleven playable ones. In fact, two of them could almost be playable if the rules and designers really wanted them to be. Then there are werewolves who are not Garou who got their abilities through other means. Very little information is given to them, but they seem to be more like the werewolves from folklore than the Garou. There are also 'spirit' Garou who got trapped in the Umbra and became a type of &quot;ghost&quot; starving for a way out. Finally, there are shapeshifters based on two other animals, ravens and spiders. There are hints that there are others possible as well. Not enough information is given in the two examples to figure out anything about what they are looking for.<br /> <br /> Next comes other supernatural beings. Vampires are the primary focus, as they appear in the first book in the game line. Magic-users, ghosts, and fairies round out this section, hinting at what games are in the pipeline. This is followed by a small section on werewolf hunters, who feel unimportant in the big scheme. The last part feature mundane humans who might come into conflict with Garou and a smattering of common animals. Both feel like afterthoughts, just there to round out all of the basic types of threats. Although, why horses are mentioned as a source of blood suggests that this listing may have, in part, been lifted from a book for vampires","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T13:48:32-08:00","id":1525218,"title":"","content":"I would say that the mention of horses as a source of blood is like a smoking gun with clear fingerprints that they just copy-pasted from Vampire. Much like how a sample character from some early promotional material makes mention of being turned rather than changing, very few heads were in the Werewolf space proper when writing W5 Probably because they give off the air of hating it and wanting to get it over with to get back to writing florid prose about Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T16:21:33-08:00","id":1525224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525216#post1525216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter Seven: Storytelling<br /> I really don't have much to say about this chapter. While I might not have chosen some of the ways the designers chose to convey this information, it still is fairly decent. This chapter usually is one of the least interesting ones in rulebooks. Necessary, but mostly important to newer players. There might be something here for those more familiar, so it still needs at least some looking over.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I have something to say about this chapter: What this chapter shows is a text that has an axe to grind, and really wants to emphasize that Garou are terrible and because of that PCs can't do anything. And it isn't because this is a horror-game, it's because this chapter just expresses an intense dislike for the idea of Garou.<br /> <br /> Take the section &quot;The Real Problem with the Garou&quot; on pg 202. It starts depressingly with &quot;The Garou are built to act, but they\u2019re probably too late. Worse, the resources they have aren\u2019t what they need.\u200b&quot; But at the end, you get a glimpse of hope by establishing that at least the PCs are different and yet... that wasn't enough. This section still needed to get in another gut-punch to the whole idea of a game revolving around Garou because the section ends like this: &quot;In a world that is dead and dying, they are the ones with the best chance to right <i>some part</i> of a worldwide wrong \u2026 they just need to understand the limitations of the tools at their disposal.\u200b&quot; (Emphasis from the source-text)<br /> <br /> So why was &quot;some part&quot; emphasized there, you might wonder? Well, for that we go to a later section called &quot;The Antagonist Axis: Scope and Aggresiveness&quot; and here only scope matters. There it distincts between systemic and individual but here's how the W5 corebook wants its readers to look at this distinction: &quot;The other axis is that of systemic / individual. Systemic antagonists are large, overarching entities or ideals. Systemic antagonists are massive and often decentralized and, in general, cannot be directly defeated. They can certainly face setbacks at the hands of the characters, but total defeat is almost never an option. Most systemic antagonists have local proxies that can be defeated, thereby hurting the global antagonist\u2019s plans and relieving tension \u2014 the \u201clittle victories\u201d that mean so much in Werewolf, because they address the player characters\u2019 immediate goals.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some parts&quot;, &quot;little victories&quot;... This is a game supposedly in the &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; which the PCs are supposed to fight against - and at the same time this chapter establishes a deeply pessimistic tone in regards to such efforts. I could understand if the idea were &quot;The Garou have lost, the world is dying and now it's all about survival.&quot; but it isn't. Instead it feels like somebody was forced to write about a game where you play a faction that said writers absolutely hate and so the consistent undertone is that the sort of characters you're asked to play actually suck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525216#post1525216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the secondary setting for the game, the spiritual side of the world where almost anything could happen and is almost nothing can be easily defined. This includes something called 'Gaia's Howl,&quot; a feeling Garou get when entering the Umbra. I wish I could explain it better, but the citation for more information just refers back to the previously read paragraph on the same page. This is a very bad case of pasting/editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> This is an especially bad mistake because we learn from the Lexicon in the Introduction what Gaia's Howl is supposed to be: &quot;Gaia\u2019s Howl: An audible indicator (capable of sometimes affecting other senses) of the age of Apocalypse, perceptible only by Garou and perhaps some spirits\u200b&quot;. This is one of THE distinct aspects of the W5 setting compared to previous editions and the section explaining it is just missing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525216#post1525216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three 'fallen' tribes are presented, with just a bit more sense of history than the eleven playable ones. In fact, two of them could almost be playable if the rules and designers really wanted them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Making the Stargazers non-playable doesn't make sense. And it isn't like their section makes any sense either. The whole bit of Chimera not being their Patron-Spirit anymore is just such bad writing. The Garou know Chimera isn't their Patron-Spirit anymore but have no idea who the new one is or whether there is a new one. And at no point does the text indicate that the Stargazers themselves are secretive and refuse to talk about it. It's just described as the Garou not knowing. But the Stargazers aren't enemies. Why wouldn't some Garou ask them about it at some point? The whole thing is portrayed as mysterious for no reason. Also, the example of how Stargazers operate makes Garou look bad. There's nothing deep, mystical or strange about the example provided in this section. Personally, I would expect Garou in general to be potentially capable of what's described in the section. There's nothing special about the described approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525216#post1525216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, there are shapeshifters based on two other animals, ravens and spiders. There are hints that there are others possible as well. Not enough information is given in the two examples to figure out anything about what they are looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> It has to be called out that this section hints at the idea that the War of Rage is still part of the W5-setting and that all the shapeshifter-Breeds remember that - except for the Garou. <i>Somehow </i>the Garou have absolutely no clue why these other shapeshifters might dislike the Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T13:28:36-08:00","id":1525323,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE ONE REVIEW PART SIX</span><br /> <br /> Appendix<br /> At the end of the book, there are three appendices, an index, a two-page character sheet, and a set of templates, specifically designed to be a well-rounded start for character creation. I'll take the designers word about how well they work. The character sheet is fairly average, with nothing that stands out. The appendices and index do have things that stand out.<br /> <br /> Appendix One: Loresheets<br /> These are the Backgrounds mentioned in the character creation process, specifically designed to allow players a deeper connection to the lore/backstory of the game. However, since there has been so little world-building, these Loresheets are quite bare. There are only five of them, none of which have any limitations to them. They also don't add much extra to the game at such an early point in the product cycle.<br /> <br /> Appendix Two: No Matter How Small<br /> This is the introductory scenario for new players. Such products are frequently separate, so having one with the main book can be a godsend for newer players. It is fairly brief and follows many of the guidelines set up in previous chapters. Maybe a little too straightforward, but I might not be the best judge of such things.<br /> <br /> Appendix Three: Advise for Considerate Play<br /> This is an unusual section, as such advice is frequently presented at part of the introduction or storytelling chapters. Someone must have thought it was important enough to warrant its own section, but not enough to present until the very end of the book. Much of this section deals with advice various Nordic roleplaying groups, with web addresses provided for those who want more information or a deeper understanding. Some of the ideas are unfamiliar to me, but they might be helpful to others. Of particular note are the trigger warnings. While the ones for sex and violence are fairly common, there is also a warning about fascism. This is unusual, as I'm not sure this would be a trigger warning for many people, although I could be wrong. Someone must be have had strong feelings about this to include a warning. Maybe this a generational or personal, I can't be sure.<br /> <br /> Index<br /> Normally, an index doesn't merit the need for review. However, some of the ways this index is set up need to be addressed. First, some of the entries have their page number directly beside them. This makes them slightly harder to read/find. Second, almost all of the entries direct to just one instance. This can lead to problems if you are looking for some details. For example, while looking over the section on damage, I remembered a sidebar mentioning that silver can cause problems for Garou, but I couldn't find any systems for that yet. I looked in the index and was directed to the original sidebar only, missing the entry for silver damage directly above it. I would have combined some entries as opposed to this book's system, but that is a personal preference.<br /> <br /> The most unusual thing about this index is the capitalization. While important words in main entries are capitalized, this isn't so in sub-entries, where only the first letter is capitalized, with one exception. This includes names that are usually capitalized, like the ones for Gifts and Tribes. For example, &quot;Children of gaia.&quot; Now, most spell-checkers would automatically correct that to a capital &quot;G,&quot; like the one on my computer. For it to be overridden is unusual. Especially since the one exception is found under &quot;Caern Traits,&quot; &quot;Balm of Gaia.&quot; I have no idea how something could be capitalized in one instance and not the other. It should be impossible for this to happen, but it did. It, it just is so beyond what should be possible.<br /> <br /> OVERALL GRADE: C<br /> After reviewing this game, I have three conclusions. First, this book was rushed through to finish it upon some deadline. While all books would have some mistakes in them, the number and types of mistakes I have found leave a lack of confidence in this publisher for future work. It feels like things were being changed right until the very end. This is not the way to edit a book. <br /> <br /> Second, this book feels like it was made for a target demographic--inexperienced player in their late teens/early twenties. Maybe one/two years playing TTRPGs, little to no heavy violence, no mature themes. The simple rules set, the introduction scenario, the 'fair-play' advice, all point to this type of player. While older, more experienced players, like myself, might be able to get something out of this game, I have doubts that it can retain players unless later books can add a larger experience.<br /> <br /> Third, it feels that this game had a direct mindset guiding it. Whether a singular individual or a groupthink venture, it feels that certain things had to be placed in the book, possibly to cater to the second point above. This mindset may have changed at some point during development, leading to confusing issues and the mistakes in the first point. Some designers may have tried to direct the game away from this vision as a means of adding some other ways to play, but got overruled at one point or another. This just added to the confusion.<br /> <br /> While there feels like there is a strong foundation to this game, I just find it is to focused on providing a certain level of gameplay. Anything that distracts from this style was removed whenever possible. Players can try to add some of this back on their own with house rules, I do think that players would leave if more material to allow different aspects of play are not considered. If this happens, maybe I could raise the grade to a C+ or B-. Until then, I just have to give this a C for just an average game. Nothing too horrible, but nothing great to stand out either.<br /> <br /> Phase two will compare W5 to V5, where many points I only hinted about will be further fleshed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T14:36:42-08:00","id":1525328,"title":"","content":"The weird thing that you note about Appendix 3 is, once again, because the creative director seemingly cannot conceive of the Get of Fenris as anything but the worst people that showed up to LARP. Even when completely retconning everything, that is the one thing he insists on leaving in place.<br /> <br /> Capitalization woes in editing also bring up an interesting question - are there any times in the text that the words Native or Indigenous show up, and if so, are they capitalized? Because, again, not capitalizing them in reference to actual groups of people was representative of another of the creative director's shortcomings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T18:39:19-08:00","id":1525337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525328#post1525328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing that you note about Appendix 3 is, once again, because the creative director seemingly cannot conceive of the Get of Fenris as anything but the worst people that showed up to LARP. Even when completely retconning everything, that is the one thing he insists on leaving in place.<br /> <br /> Capitalization woes in editing also bring up an interesting question - are there any times in the text that the words Native or Indigenous show up, and if so, are they capitalized? Because, again, not capitalizing them in reference to actual groups of people was representative of another of the creative director's shortcomings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one instance of &quot;Native American&quot;. In the weird &quot;Historical Trauma&quot; text it uses &quot;native people&quot;. Other are not references to Native people.<br /> The only other place Native is prominently capitalised is when it references the general gifts of the Garou which are called &quot;Native&quot; now.<br /> <br /> Indigenous is capitalised in the &quot;Historical Trauma&quot; text (twice).<br /> There are three references to Indigenous peoples in the book. None of them are capitalised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T03:16:54-08:00","id":1525342,"title":"","content":"W5, to me, seems to work the best as an introduction for Vampire-only players. I have heard multiple people say it was easier to get into W5 than from Legacy.<br /> <br /> But as someone who legit got the book as a 14-year-old with ZERO idea of vampire, I feel for true newbies WtA is not too difficult.<br /> <br /> At the core of everything, W5 refuses to commit to a cohesive setting that could be used. W5 brings up a lot of things, but then doesn't elaborate on them much. Even important things like the Litany, the two outsider tribes and other shifters are left vague in a way that doesn't actually allow the ST to use them. W5 also wants its PCs to hold human jobs, but then makes them nearly impossible with its Rage Dice which then make losing the wolf far too easy.<br /> <br /> W5 still has BSDs, yet places most sins on the feet of a tribe that still fights against the Wyrm with the PCs.<br /> <br /> W5 allows you to play both human-born and wolf-born, but spends most of the book absolutely hating the very idea of a wolf-born PC.<br /> <br /> If W5 had been a post-apocalyptic setting where the young garou truly are on their own and have to figure out everything themselves, it would have worked. But that is not the W5 we got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T10:43:02-08:00","id":1525350,"title":"","content":"Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17984\" data-vbnamecard=\"17984\">Toby Weingarten</a> thank you for doing the review and the comparisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T10:44:40-08:00","id":1525351,"title":"","content":"I think one of the principal mistakes this game makes is that it takes its pessimistic outlook on Garou and does nothing with it. Garou suck. That's it. One of the themes is supposed to be &quot;Theme: Old Dogs, New Tricks, Young Blood\u200b&quot; where you get the description that the old ways have failed but older Garou will still cling to them and so there's a struggle between young Garou trying to find new ways and those veterans.<br /> <br /> But what are the new ways?<br /> <br /> The outlook in W5 may be pessmistic but strangely, it's a game entirely stuck in retrospective. It's all about how a past ridden with mistakes and failures led to an apocalyptic present - and nothing beyond that. The book is very clear about that much at least. The war against the Wyrm? Lost. The Apocalypse? It's happening. You fight against the Apocalypse - and you can't stop it. Garou have powers - that aren't the solution to the world's problems.<br /> <br /> So, what do you do then? Good question. Pity the W5 corebook never gets to that part.<br /> <br /> Instead what you get is this: You still fight the Wyrm and its minions. You still fight against the Apocalypse. You still use Rage and Gifts to fight your enemies. You still accrue Renown and practice Rites in the same way your Garou-ancestors have done. So where are the new, supposedly better ways? They're nowhere to be found. Because what this game does instead is set up PCs for failure and hopes players will feel bad about it. To borrow Monster-Hearts-terminology, following the mechanics of the game is to embrace your &quot;Darkest Self&quot;, in this case the Garou's &quot;Darkest Self&quot;.<br /> <br /> Harano and Hauglosk are these two fail-states with the former being &quot;depression&quot; (don't like the book's explicit link to genuine mental health issues here but that's how the book portrays it) and the latter being some fascistic zealotry (also don't like the book's explicit links between Hauglosk and fascism). These tracks are linked to Chronicle Tenets and Touchstones but there are two systems that express those same ideas elsewhere in the game. With Harano you have the concept of &quot;losing the wolf&quot; which for whatever reason allows a character to just abandon Rage and their supernatural Forms for an indefinite amount of time. There's nothing more Harano-like than a genuine option to just give up and walk away from being a Garou. For Hauglosk, you have the whole Rage-Dice-system with Brutal Outcomes. With Rage being fuel for Gifts, Regeneration and shifting you need high Rage. Brutal Outcomes even become beneficial when you're doing something brutal and/or violent. Meanwhile, Brutal Outcomes turn your rolls into automatic failures when you don't do that. So what if you were to just... not do the latter? In fact, the system will reward players for sticking to high Rage and focusing on direct, brutal solutions to problems. You get rewarded for acting like a rampaging monster while low Rage limits your use of Gifts, Regeneration and shifting while also potentially triggering &quot;losing the wolf&quot; for your character.<br /> <br /> And where's the way out of this...? There isn't one, strangely. So in a way, the vague suggestions of young Garou trying to do better and overcoming the problems with the old ways is the part that really doesn't fit into this game. The old Garou were failures and the young Garou you're asked to play in W5 are set up for failure as well. The vision of doing better and being better never once materializes in this book.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there's another glaring issue with the book: worldbuilding. The W5 corebook finds plenty of words to castigate the past of the W5-setting, like with the Litany-section and blaming Garou for the apocalyptic state of the world. Other than that, you get a lot of &quot;Who knows&quot; that's less about setting up mysteries and more akin to a student in an oral exam trying to cover their ass for not knowing an answer. Not knowing something isn't a mystery, it's ignorance. You can't build a setting with ignorance. The current WOD5E's direction of disliking lore/worldbuilding, in general, is more a handicap to corebooks like this than anything else.<br /> <br /> Even game-play-wise the street-level-only scope is a handicap and nothing else. Your PC-Pack defeats an enemy, gets a caern... and then what? The horizon ends there. And same as with H5's direction of &quot;You <i>have to</i> play a local hunter-cell! Hunter-orgs are evil!&quot;, this game is running into the same wall. What's particularly bothersome is that it's one thing to focus on a particular scope, it's another to be invested in actively sabotaging any effort to expand the scope. So in a way, W5's pessimistic take on Garou and the stringent regulation of games being street-level-only really ended up being a match made in heaven for this game. Both are efforts to restrict and restrain what you do with this game and rather than enhance gameplay it's more invested in blocking people from playing in a way that disagrees with the developers' vision.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's better than H5, so there's that at least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T10:38:13-08:00","id":1525376,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all for following this thread.<br /> Time for Phase Two. This part of the review is mostly a comparison of W5 with V5. When the Fifth Edition books first came out, hopes were high that each of the game lines would be more able to interact with other. Many of the original WOD games introduced mechanics that were only useful for themselves, making crossover games difficult to manage, if not impossible on some levels. COD managed to to that fairly well; it was a major benefit to the games and one thing many players would like to see in 5th. I hinted about some of these possibilities in Phase One, but will follow through here. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE TWO PART ONE</span><br /> Comparison of W5 and V5<br /> <br /> Overall Views.<br /> As I look over my copy of V5 for this review for the first time in awhile, I'm surprised at how much I missed when I first got it. The first thing is that V5 is smaller than W5, by about an eighth of an inch shorter in width and height. [Note, my copy of V5 is an early Modiphius printing. I believe that the current Renegade edition might have different dimensions.] For some people, this slight difference could be a trigger. It might also be a subtle hint for people to buy newer printing just that their collections look/feel even.<br /> <br /> W5 is also just slightly thicker than V5, which is odd since V5 has 400 pages 330, or 332 is you count the endpaper. Part of this is due to the fact that the covers to W5 are also slightly thicker than those on V5. Also, V5 used a thinner grade of paper which worked better with the photographic artwork, while W5 used a thicker grade that gives it a do-it-yourself vibe. This makes the two books look like they have the same amount of material in them, but that obviously is not the case. <br /> <br /> As I just mentioned, the majority of the artwork inV5 is photographs. Some of the artwork is the prominent part of the page, while on others it is worked into the background instead. Some portions are set with two columns, others have three. Sections are set off with a mixture of fonts and sizes. Sidebars are usually set off with just a set of thick bars at the top of bottom of the section. Overall, the effect reflects the style of a high-end fashion magazine or a coffee table book. A sense of exquisiteness pervades the book, setting it off from previous editions.<br /> <br /> In contrast, V5 has illustrations only, much of them using a subdued palette, all but muddy in places. The pages themselves are yellowed, almost sepia-toned. Multiple fonts are used per page, dependent on the type of heading required. Multiple colors are also used. Sidebars are in a dark yellow or rusty red, with the former using bold and the latter using white lettering . Every page is in two columns, with some shifted due to artwork. Sections are set off in standard style without any variance. Overall, the effect reminds me of a grade-school textbook, one that has been in use for many years. While that could fit the do-it-yourself themes of W5, it also makes the book feel childish, as if it is more for kids than adults, which is it most assuredly not","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T13:57:42-08:00","id":1525387,"title":"","content":"Of course, as you outlined <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17984\" data-vbnamecard=\"17984\">Toby Weingarten</a>, in the fourth Phase about the controversies and problems, there's definitely gonna be a discussion about tracing. But ignoring that, I especially like the pieces at the beginning from WolfSkullJack and I think their style was the best fit for a fifth edition of WtA. That style was a nice bridge between the comics of previous editions and a new revised aesthetic. For the most part, the abstract stuff for the Umbra is... okay. It looks good but I don't think it helps a lot in depicting the Umbra. I would've liked to see more examples of spirits or what the influence of the Wyrm or the Weaver looks like in the Umbra. There's also that sequence of artworks from pg 117 to pg 134 which depicts a fight between two werewolves and... it's kinda just sits there on those pages. It's probably a victim of this book's convoluted development-history that this was drawn and now it's just a series of context-free images in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a fan of the gangly Crinos-Form shown in this book. It's on pg 119 and the page after, for example. Also, the first thing I was thinking off while looking at the artwork on pg 59 was &quot;Manbat&quot; from Batman rather than werewolf. The face especially just seemed way more reminiscent of a big bat to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T10:51:28-08:00","id":1525566,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE TWO PART TWO</span><br /> <br /> Introductions<br /> V5 starts with thirty page in-universe collection of documents that hint at what the game will be about. Some of the points brought up have yet to be explored in any supplements so far. Further documents are found throughout the book. This gives a feeling of history, that things have happened and are still happening. These documents are backed by quotes and passages by in-universe characters, deepening this connection. There is a four-page lexicon that gives both current slang and archaic terms that suggests the struggles of ancient vampires and the more modern ones that are a strong part of the plot lines of the game. Much deeper into the book, just after the chapter on character creation, there is a list comparing how the vampires of the game differ with those found in folklore and fiction. The rest of the early sections of the book give not just a brief summation of the basic history of the Kindred of the game up to the current nights, but also a piece on how to run a game for those unfamiliar with the concepts.<br /> <br /> W5 offers no introduction beyond a few paragraphs summing up the broad strokes of the game-style. While there are quotes and even some passages by in-game characters, they feel more like opinions rather than anything deeply integral to the game. There are also a few in-universe documents, but they almost feel out of place. The one-page lexicon doesn't even cover all the terms used in the book, some of which aren't even given a solid definition within the text. There is no one section comparing the Garou to more traditional representations of werewolves found elsewhere. The first two chapters of W5, which I must admit are easier to read than the broad sections of V5, give hints about the game world and the history of the Garou, yet something feels missing. For instance, V5 gave two pages to discussions the Traditions of the Kindred, basic laws that all vampires usually abide by, and how they are followed differently by different vampires of different ages and sects. W5 give two columns across two pages about the Garou's comparable set of laws, the Litany. However, most of the tenets aren't explained beyond the fact that many of the youngest generation don't think much of them. <br /> <br /> Even with what information is given, W5 is open-ended to the point where players are all but given total leeway to do what they want concerning the history of the Garou and even current events.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T04:37:07-08:00","id":1525587,"title":"","content":"W5 has way too many areas in its worldbuilding where you're presented with a blank slate or something pretty close to it. And the issue is that this isn't set up as a mystery or is blank stuff built on any foundation. For example, the question of &quot;What happens at a Moot and how does it proceed?&quot; is left blank. It's not that people at the table can bring their own spin to it, it's a thing in the setting and that's all you get. Or &quot;How is a Sept organized?&quot;. Games that have that many blank spaces usually at least have genre-conventions or leading questions to guide people in filling out those blank spaces. But W5 still has Garou which are unconventional compared to what you'd normally expect of werewolves and connecting that to the animistic worldview as well as peculiarities like the Wyrm, there's plenty of things here that you can't just throw to the people at the table and say &quot;You go figure it out.&quot;. I get the idea of easing up on lore/worldbuilding for the sake of accessibility but W5 goes way too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:39:54-08:00","id":1525651,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE TWO PART THREE</span><br /> <br /> Clans vs. Tribes<br /> In V5, an entire section is given over to introducing the Clans, as well as non-Clan options. Six of the seven Clans have six pages dedicated to them, while the seventh only has four pages. (of the non-Clan options, one has six pages and the other four.) Two full pages are given over to artwork for each Clan. The start of each section has a large symbol for the Clan at the top of the page with a unique logo for each. Alternate designations for the Clan are on the opposite page with the artwork. The next part is a brief discussion about generalities about the Clan. This is followed by five character archetypes, each a few sentences long. The next part are paragraphs explaining how each of the Clan's three favored Disciplines are viewed within the Clan. Finally, there is part on the Clan Bane, a weakness that affects every member to a different degree. Each Bane offers different roleplaying opportunities even when some use the same mechanics to deal with them. Clan Compulsions could have been added to this section, and latter supplements would include this information when introducing the other Clans. (The two non-Clan options no not have a symbol nor a unique logo. The Discipline and Bane sections are replaced with a brief discussion on the special rules for these options instead.)<br /> <br /> In W5, Tribes are treated a little differently. Each of the eleven Tribes mentioned (three other NPC options are found in the Antagonists and Allies Chapter, but they offer slightly less information than for the main Tribes in some regards) have only two pages. On the top of the first page there are illustrations of the four character archetypes mentioned on the second page. Each archetype has a longish paragraph detailing them. This takes up about half of the second page. Below the illustrations is the name of the Tribe, given in the same font for each. The same font is the one used for section headings throughout the book. Beside the name is a small glyph that represents the Tribe. Under this is a discussion on the Tribe. The vague hints that plagued the history chapter continue here. After this is a section on the Tribe's patron spirit, the one that unifies the Tribe and gives the Tribe its special powers. Of note, this section also mentions the Tribes' primary Renown, the only place where it is found. This is actually a very important part of character creation, and it should have also been repeated elsewhere. The patron spirit also gives its Tribe a special Favor and Ban. The Favor is basically a bonus on certain dice roles involving particular actions. The Ban is a failure to regain full Willpower at the end of a session if a certain action was/was not performed. While there is a variety of actions that cause this penalty among the Tribes, having different results beyond not regaining Willpower would have shown the differences between the Tribes better. Finally, there are the archetypes mentioned previously. There are no non-Tribe options currently available.<br /> <br /> The Auspices are also found in this chapter. Each Auspice gets a column for them spread over three pages. They are presented in the chronological placement of moon phase, instead of alphabetically or other way, but there isn't a clear reason why this is done. The top part of the column features an illustration of a character of the Auspice combined with the Auspice's glyph. Below this is a quote from someone of that Auspice. Next, there is a discussion on how that Auspice is perceived in Garou culture and what roles that Auspice performs. Aside from a unique set of Gifts, there are no mechanics currently involved in playing one Auspice over another.<br /> <br /> Basically, while the Tribes and Auspices have about the same amount of information given over to them as do the Clans, V5 tried to make each Clan separate from each other, while W5 emphasizes what each Tribe and Auspice have in common with each other. Less variety and more unity, even when the previous chapter suggests otherwise.<br /> <br /> Character Creation<br /> Each book has basically the same considerations for character creation, but the two books have many differences.<br /> <br /> V5 starts with multiple pages on considering what a new character should be, including discussions with the other players in the group. There is also a brief summary of the process at the start of the chapter. W5 goes directly into character creation without this step, with just a small sidebar mentioning the steps and a note on how to create wolf-born characters (basically, not much of a difference).<br /> <br /> Next, V5 goes into how to set up the 'human life' portion of traits, those that would continue on after the Embrace. Namely, Attributes and Skills. V5 even offers some tips on choosing tips for certain professions, as well as alternatives on how to divide skill points. The actual explanation of these traits are to be found after the full discussion of creation. W5 goes straight to these traits, practically combining them with just a little break in describing how to calculate the Health and Willpower scores. As a side note, both books use the same example involving Muay Thai martial arts as not being an option for a Skill specialty for the Brawl Skill, as it too broad.<br /> <br /> V5 goes over the values of Convictions, Touchstones, and Ambitions before moving onto the vampire specific traits. The explanations for these Traits are given after the part on Skills. The only one of these W5 uses is Touchstones, but they don't cover it until the end of the creation process. Initially, V5 said that only living humans could be Touchstones, but this got expanded to other things in later supplements. W5 only allows humans, and/or wolves, as Touchstones at this time.<br /> <br /> The first part of the vampire traits to consider are Disciplines. While the rules for choosing them are here, the actual descriptions are in a later chapter. The W5 counterpart, Gifts, aren't mentioned until later in their process, but are also fully treated in a separate chapter. Next for V5 is Predator type, the primary means a vampire hunts for blood, but it is not the only means they use. By choosing a Predator type, a vampire gains extra traits, such as a Skill specialties Disciplines, Advantages, and/or Flaws. Types are mentioned int eh next section following the previous one. W5 offers no such means as a counterpart, although it could have been possible. For example, one could have tied Auspice to certain roles to achieve a similar effect, probably without Gifts as a benefit as they are granted on a slightly different system. Still, it would have given a greater use for Auspice beyond roleplaying or a Gift list.<br /> <br /> Next for both books are Advantages, which are divided into Merits and Backgrounds. The former are usually tied directly to the character and usually can't be altered during play. The latter can change from story to story and can be taken multiple times. Of note, V5 allows coteries to share Backgrounds but W5 does not allow packs to do so, even though packs are supposedly tied much closer together than coteries. This should be changed later on as it seems very natural to occur. Also, not all of the Backgrounds are the same. For example, vampires have multiple physical helper Backgrounds, while werewolves only have a spirit guide. V5 gives vampires the Haven Background, while W5 has the equivalents Caern and Safe House as Merits instead. Strangely enough, W5 has no equivalent to the V5 Background Status, which is unusual since it is later mentioned in the mechanics chapter as being a possible trait for some social rolls. For all the talk about how the current generation of Garou distrusts their Elders, not having any mechanic to determine this is odd.<br /> <br /> The rest of the V5 traits are more thoroughly covered in the following chapter on mechanics. However, W5 has one last special mechanic for character creation, Renown. While Renown is used to determine what Gifts a Garou can purchase and as dice rolls for those Gifts, it feels like it should have something else tied to it equal to the Status state mentioned above. This mechanic just feels incomplete on some level.<br /> <br /> Both books end with discussions on experience, both in awarding of points to increase traits and creating veteran characters at the start. While both books have the same basic concepts covered, W5 just seems to give the basic tools needed to create a character, while V5 helps players more along the way in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":17984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","user":"Toby Weingarten","date":".  Further information on the Status Background 11-23-2023, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T12:32:45-08:00","id":1525694,"title":"","content":"No real surprise that everything but V5 was stripped bare and thrown off a cliff. Also, Renown rolls used to be a thing in legacy editions; they helped as bona fides and generally helped foster trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T03:43:21-08:00","id":1525717,"title":"","content":"Renown is a great example of how badly the transition from V5 to both H5 and W5 was handled. And also the awkwardness that's created by staying within some strict boundaries. There are so many times in H5 and W5 where things that couldn't be easily translated from V5 to the other splats are instead just thrown out. Status from V5 doesn't quite fit W5...? Well, then let's throw it out and... that's about it. Instead what WtA had was Rank but I guess if you included the whole five-dot-spectrum that would imply a PC at some point could become an Elder themselves - but as the game alleges all Elders are evil/incompetent. And also: Street-level only. God forbid, you wanna play a Garou who isn't the young, new Garou rebelling against the &quot;bad Elders&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mechanically what this ends up doing with Renown is that it's more of a hurdle than anything else. In some cases you can use Renown to add dice to social rolls (when appropriate). And other than that, the only reason to buy Renown with XP is to bolster dice-pools for Gifts and clear the Total Renown requirements for Gift-options. You more or less buy Renown to buy another thing (Gifts). Also, in the way Gifts are structured, the most efficient way to deal with Renown is to focus on the Renown of your Tribe (since all Tribe-Gifts use the same Renown whereas Auspice and Native Gifts are mixed).<br /> <br /> I also don't like how the W5 corebook recommends buying new Renown only after a worthy deed - but it never links acquiring Renown to a social occasion of storytelling and boasting. Even WtF which doesn't have the big social megastructure of something like a Garou-Nation at least mentioned that acquiring Renown could also include storytelling with only spirits as the audience. W5 is the same with Chagrin just happening in the moment when your PC does something the ST considers shameful. The social aspect is missing in those explanations.<br /> <br /> That's one way to look at it. Another is that it could be that the proofreader was asleep at the wheel again because to quote the W5 corebook from pg 141:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In certain cases, various Renown types may add dice to Social pools, as they represent not only the individual Garou\u2019s growing legend but also their reputation among spirits and other werewolves. The Storyteller determines whether a Garou may rely upon their Renown to affect an interaction with a spirit or another werewolf. In most cases, this use of Renown shouldn\u2019t be the case \u2014 <b>specific Skills and the Status\u200b Background</b> represent such an episode more fully. But in certain situations, calling upon one\u2019s Renown as a cultural gesture makes sense.\u200b </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> So you see, the W5 corebook actually mentions the Status Background in the book. It's just that it doesn't appear in the Background section... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:14:34-08:00","id":1525852,"title":"","content":"I keep finding mistakes and issues the further in I go. Anyway, time for the next part of the Review.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE TWO: PART FOUR</span><br /> <br /> Mechanics<br /> While the two types of supernatural being are different on the basic level, one being alive and the other not, one would expect similar mechanic when applicable. This is not always the case. The main mechanic is the &quot;bonus/penalty&quot; dice system. In V5, these are Hunger dice and represent the craving for Blood, as well as the influence/interference of the Beast on the vampire's mind. The less blood/greater need a vampire has, the more dice they have to substitute for rolls, causing the higher chances for something to go not they way they were planning. This happens until the hunger is taken care. This can also lead to Compulsions, subtle influence from the Beast upon a vampire's actions, whenever things go wrong a roll. If a vampire is fully sated, they have no Hunger dice and act however they want.<br /> <br /> The W5 version is Rage dice. While having more dice substituted for some in a pool leads to similar problems, they are not quite the same. For one, there are no long term conditions such as Compulsions is one's Rage is too high. For another, having more Rage is considered a positive for Garou, as it can lead to better outcomes in some situations. On the downside, not having any Rage at all mean that the character is just a regular human, for all intents and purposes, until they can regain Rage. No supernatural abilities at all, the opposite for V5. Also, the range is different for the two systems. In W5, a '2' on a Rage die equals a Brutal Failure. In V5, a '2' on a Hunger die is just a failure. [The dice really should have numbers. I don't have the new sets, but I don't think the number are printed on them, making them useless for other purposes.]<br /> <br /> A main factor for vampires is Humanity, a measure of how one can remain close to their original state. Various benefits and penalties exist along the scale. W5's closest equivalent is Harano and Hauglosk (that is a very unwieldy word0. The former is measure of futility with the latter a measure of straightforwardness. For some reason, a Garou can suffer from both at the same time, which shouldn't really be possible. One should cancel the other out, but they don't. A Garou gains Harano whenever they suffer a major setback and Hauglosk whenever they violate a Chronicle tenet. There aren't any repercussions until either one reaches the maximum of five, although there are hints that suggest that such mechanics might exist, but were not included in the rules.<br /> <br /> A major mechanic for V5 is Blood Resonance and Dyscrasias. Emotions can 'flavor' blood and provide bonuses in experience or additional dice to Discipline rolls. At certain times, blood can provide even greater advantages. W5 has no equivalent, but it could. Various spots could provide 'spiritual resonance' to act similarly. Certain spirits flock to locations in the spirit world that are attractive to their type. Garou could also use such sites for certain bonuses, such as regaining Willpower or Rage, healing damage faster, not having to spend points on effects, or other uses. There could even be 'tainted' areas that could provide such bonuses, but pose a threat to the character, leading to their potential end. For instance, a Wyld tainted area could allow a Garou to shapeshifter without needing a Rage check, but could also lead to the Garou to start shifting uncontrollably over time.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are the main supernatural powers for vampires in V5. They are scaled from one to five, with multiple options per level, and a limit on one power per slot on the scale. In W5, the powers are called Gifts. They are divided into three types (Native, Auspice, and Tribe) and are roughly gauged into three tiers. One must possess a minimum amount of Renown to purchase a Gift. Also, each type of Gift has different minimums of Renown for each level of Gift. While Renown is on a 1-5 scale, Gifts are not, and there really isn't a good reason why, since it is theoretically possible to achieve five levels of Gifts. There is no limit to the number of Gifts at any level a Garou can learn. Maybe this system is more complicated because Gifts have no other limits on learning them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T13:43:07-08:00","id":1525864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525852#post1525852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W5 version is Rage dice. While having more dice substituted for some in a pool leads to similar problems, they are not quite the same. For one, there are no long term conditions such as Compulsions is one's Rage is too high. For another, having more Rage is considered a positive for Garou, as it can lead to better outcomes in some situations. On the downside, not having any Rage at all mean that the character is just a regular human, for all intents and purposes, until they can regain Rage. No supernatural abilities at all, the opposite for V5. Also, the range is different for the two systems. In W5, a '2' on a Rage die equals a Brutal Failure. In V5, a '2' on a Hunger die is just a failure. [The dice really should have numbers. I don't have the new sets, but I don't think the number are printed on them, making them useless for other purposes.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<ul><li>Josh Heath talked about the playtest and the versions of Rage-Dice he tested were <i>more </i>punishing than this final version.</li> <li>It's weird that they didn't just copy the V5 versions of Messy Criticals and Bestial failures. Instead, W5 has a system that actually rewards staying in high Rage and being violent/brutal and situationally punishes players for trying to be not violent/brutal.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525852#post1525852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, a Garou can suffer from both at the same time, which shouldn't really be possible. One should cancel the other out, but they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Same here. This systemic conception never sat right with me. It also creates the weird formula where the best place to be is to have a couple boxes filled on both the Harano and Hauglosk trackers.<br /> <br /> First of all, why exactly does this game need two additional fail-states to begin with...? Are Harano and Hauglosk truly served best by being countdowns to failstates for PCs...? All I see here is yet another mechanism purely fuelled by a dislike for WtA. Some developer was insistent on the idea that Garou suck and wanted to show that off with the mechanics. But a VtM-PCs struggle with Humanity is supposed to be a struggle. That's the point. Meanwhile, for whatever reason the people working on W5 thought that mechanically enforcing a doom-spiral is the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525852#post1525852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 has no equivalent, but it could. Various spots could provide 'spiritual resonance' to act similarly. Certain spirits flock to locations in the spirit world that are attractive to their type. Garou could also use such sites for certain bonuses, such as regaining Willpower or Rage, healing damage faster, not having to spend points on effects, or other uses. There could even be 'tainted' areas that could provide such bonuses, but pose a threat to the character, leading to their potential end. For instance, a Wyld tainted area could allow a Garou to shapeshifter without needing a Rage check, but could also lead to the Garou to start shifting uncontrollably over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> Well, anything Umbra-related would theoretically make up for that... but in W5 the Umbra is a sideshow. In W5 PCs are disincentivized from getting too invested in the Umbra (despite what the Introduction says about what werewolves do...) and with Wyrm-taint and things like that gone, the idea is that W5-PCs don't really know how to engage with spirits. In the previews, Justin Achilli mentioned the example that a werewolf-pack might deal with a disease-spirit and not be sure if it's aligned with the Wyrm or the Wyld. And only through further investigation would they figure that out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525852#post1525852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, each type of Gift has different minimums of Renown for each level of Gift. While Renown is on a 1-5 scale, Gifts are not, and there really isn't a good reason why, since it is theoretically possible to achieve five levels of Gifts. There is no limit to the number of Gifts at any level a Garou can learn. Maybe this system is more complicated because Gifts have no other limits on learning them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Ha! Oh, there certainly is a limit! The XP-cost for Gifts is &quot;New Gift-Amount x 2&quot;. Say you have three Gifts - the next one costs 8 XP. You wanna buy another one...? 10 XP. And yeah, this system doesn't give a shit about Renown-requirements. So you better spend your XP first on buying Renown so that you then can buy better Gifts. What are you gonna do with the Renown...? Most of the time: absolutely nothing. Ranks aren't a thing in W5 anymore after all. The conflict is just &quot;youngsters vs elders&quot;. That's the big conflict supposedly... not that the W5 corebook is really gonna help a ST in portraying that but that's what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T10:41:51-08:00","id":1525967,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE TWO PART FIVE</span><br /> <br /> Storytelling, Setting, and Antagonists<br /> <br /> Mostly, there isn't too much difference in these chapters, aside from game line specific needs. In fact, W5 basically adapted (lifted) some material from V5 to use as their own. There is something I'll be mentioning at the end, with the final grade, though, that needs its own spot.<br /> <br /> Appendices<br /> <br /> V5 doesn't really have any appendices, as it just has sections that blend into one another. However, it does have a section on Loresheets after the main body of the book. V5 has fifteen of them, with two Clan specific and others that easily could be tied to a certain Clan. W5 only has five Loresheets, none of the with any exclusions. None of the five really provide much for the Background or go too deeply into game lore, retaining the vagueness that pervades W5.<br /> <br /> W5 also provides an introductory scenario and information for conduction fair/safe play. V5 had a separate introductory scenario, which I didn't have, so I won't compare them. Also, V5 did include the fair play information, but it was added later only to the PDF version. I lost my PDF when my old computer died recently, and I didn't feel like buying the PDF just for that one section, so I am not reviewing it either.<br /> <br /> If there is one thing that W5 does better than V5 is the index. V5 just lists everything without explanation, so you might not have an idea what something is just by looking at its entry. On the other hand, W5 uses subheadings to divide various categories. Therefore, one knows what some of the more obtuse entries are when just looking, or they have an idea of where they should be looking. Even with the odd capitalization, this is plus for looking things up.<br /> <br /> Finally, both books have a two-page character sheet and some quick templates. V5's templates are on the inside front and back covers. They are for random victims. Why waste the space on something so basic is unusual, but it might be better than just graphics. W5 has six templates as either bases for character creation or random encounters. The developers' choices might not be the ones I would have chosen, but they might be workable.<br /> <br /> Final grade: C-/D+<br /> <br /> One would expect two game lines set in the same universe should be comparable and compatible, but V5 and W5 aren't quite there. While it is obvious that the two books share many systems and rules, they don't feel or look like they have much in common. V5 has a more sophisticated air about it. It features a deep sense of lore that can be used when needed. The systems are fairly easy and scalable to a group's needs.<br /> <br /> W5 feels like it is targeted to a different, younger demographic. Much of the world-building is left to the group, with only the barest of hints of greater lore. The rules are mostly simplified, or even removed, to allow a more basic style of play. The one complicated system, that of Renown/Gifts, is way more complex than it needed to be, to the point where it is almost better not trying to improve those categories than actually using them. So much just feels missing and/or incomplete.<br /> <br /> If this was all that was going on, my final grade would be C- on how W5 is connected to V5. However, there is one last thing to bring up that lowers my grade. In the chapter on the Umbra, the special spirit world setting in W5, there is an interesting sidebar. It describes that while other supernatural beings have their own ways of entering the spirit worlds, they are almost never entering the same Umbra as the Garou. In fact, the Umbra is pretty much for Garou only. This little fact not only encourages future game lines from dong their own thing, but it discourages any attempt at allowing crossovers from ever happening. Each game line would be its own thing, with their own rules totally unlike other game lines. This is not the way a shared universe should work. If this remains so throughout any future releases, then the disparity and disunity featured within just these two game lines will grow. Some interaction must exist, even if such crossovers are frowned upon. Otherwise, the game lines could collapse on themselves without a shared unified structure to build upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T10:39:13-08:00","id":1526013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525967#post1525967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 only has five Loresheets, none of the with any exclusions. None of the five really provide much for the Background or go too deeply into game lore, retaining the vagueness that pervades W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all just brings to mind how the V5 Players Guide describes Loresheets: &quot;Loresheets exist to highlight a certain aspect of the world for the interested player and Storyteller,\u200b without forcing every player to master the entire minutiae of the Vampire setting. A Loresheet foregrounds some group, historical event, or elder<i> as it relates specifically to the player</i>, encouraging them to take ownership of that aspect and reminding the Storyteller that vampiric arcana exists to serve the story at the table tonight, not as mandatory history lessons.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> The team working on this book really (who were also involved in the development of the V5 Players Guide) was of the opinion that lore is a bad thing. And this book as a whole is a culmination of that attitude. Fewer Loresheets but also less lore/worldbuilding in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525967#post1525967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is one thing that W5 does better than V5 is the index. V5 just lists everything without explanation, so you might not have an idea what something is just by looking at its entry. On the other hand, W5 uses subheadings to divide various categories. Therefore, one knows what some of the more obtuse entries are when just looking, or they have an idea of where they should be looking. Even with the odd capitalization, this is plus for looking things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> On a sidenote, the Index refers the reader for Gaia's Howl to the same page where it says to go to another page for more information - except the mentioned page is the very page this is mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1525967#post1525967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this was all that was going on, my final grade would be C- on how W5 is connected to V5. However, there is one last thing to bring up that lowers my grade. In the chapter on the Umbra, the special spirit world setting in W5, there is an interesting sidebar. It describes that while other supernatural beings have their own ways of entering the spirit worlds, they are almost never entering the same Umbra as the Garou. In fact, the Umbra is pretty much for Garou only. This little fact not only encourages future game lines from dong their own thing, but it discourages any attempt at allowing crossovers from ever happening. Each game line would be its own thing, with their own rules totally unlike other game lines. This is not the way a shared universe should work. If this remains so throughout any future releases, then the disparity and disunity featured within just these two game lines will grow. Some interaction must exist, even if such crossovers are frowned upon. Otherwise, the game lines could collapse on themselves without a shared unified structure to build upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Neither H5 nor W5 do a good job of connecting to V5 with an eye on crossovers. If anything, it reverts back to that attitude where the specificity and detail of other splats are toned down. The vampires in W5 aren't Kindred or in the Camarilla. The Mages aren't part of the Technocracy or the Traditions (who even knows what M5 will end up looking like considering how W5 was handled...). And there's no crossover with H5 here either. You might have Project Twilight as some sort of Second Inquisition representation but H5 has the firm stance that all hunter-orgs are bad and you're not allowed to play them. So you can't even build a bridge there by having Project Twilight PCs. For leaving so many blank spots in terms of lore/worldbuilding it's weird how restrictive WOD5E can be sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T15:49:05-08:00","id":1526021,"title":"","content":"Add to that that most of the Umbral Traveller loresheet is composed of things that every baseline Garou should be able to do intrinsically and the large chunks of the Project Twilight one makes zero sense. I have a bunch of issues with the BSD and CoF ones as well the CoF one in particular clashes hard with pretty much all the CoF depictions post Corebook.....and if we're being honest within the corebook as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T00:01:13-08:00","id":1526165,"title":"","content":"No Lore as a philosophy works fine if you don't have to do much explaining from what a person would know from popular culture. Vampire doesn't need you to explain what a vampire is or how one functions. Even if you have only consumed Twilight, you'd still know the basics. An undead blood-drinking creature that avoids the sun.<br /> <br /> But that is not true with WtA. Even if we go solely by the <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/177987070427/werewolves\" target=\"_blank\">folkloric werewolf facts</a>, we still are left with MASSIVE gaps we need to explain to the players. The Wyrm has no role in werewolf folklore or media, there is no entropic force of destruction a werewolf has to fight. Same with the other members of the triat, they have no role in werewolf myths nor is there even anything close to a similar concept in them. In werewolf myths/media/folklore, the focus is not on protecting nature over humanity. Most focus on what being a werewolf is like and the closest to a united mission are the <a href=\"https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Thiess_of_Kaltenbrun\" target=\"_blank\">Benandanti</a> who go to hell every night to fight devils for the Christian God.<br /> <br /> This is why you often see people not in the WoD community call WtA Furry Captain Planet. Because they wanted a werewolf game and instead they got a game about environmental destruction.<br /> <br /> This is why I find the &quot;lore light&quot; approach so dishonest, it is taking something that works for one game and then forcing another to use it without thinking of the game itself. If they wanted a lore light werewolf game, they could have always just followed the actual popular culture/folklore rather than gutted WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T02:07:36-08:00","id":1526170,"title":"","content":"There are two angles where W5 is at odds with itself:<ul><li>W5 wants to get away from old WtA-lore - but old WtA is still very much the foundation for the game: This leads to various concepts still remaining but in a poorly-explained fashion (for example, as presented the book doesn't really make a good case for why Stargazers are even part of the game - except that they used to be a Tribe in previous editions).</li> <li>W5 wants to emphasize the Apocalypse by setting the game in the Age of Apocalypse - but this isn't supposed to be a game about dealing with that. The Storytelling-chapter talks about &quot;small victories&quot; instead and says you will never defeat &quot;systemic antagonists&quot;. But the game never wrangles with how those &quot;small victories&quot; change then in meaning with that context in mind. Fighting the Wyrm, &quot;taking back what has been lost&quot; and &quot;building your own legend&quot; have a very different ring to them if you recontextualize those things with the explicit premise of the game that you can't defeat the Wyrm, can't save Gaia and and won't prevent the Apocalypse.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T11:42:15-08:00","id":1526280,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART ONE</span><br /> <br /> This is going to be the hardest part. This phase focuses one the differences between W5 and previous editions (I refuse to use the term &quot;legacy,&quot; as I feel that it doesn't really do justice to older versions.) Of particular note, I'll mostly be working from memory here on the earlier editions. About twenty years ago, most of my WOD collection got destroyed. While I was able to replace some of the books, I wasn't able to restore all of them, as the original game lines were being replaced with what would become the COD. As to the WOD20 line, while I do have most of the W:tA material, they were on my old computer when it died recently. I haven't had the time to re-download them, as I've had a lot to do lately. As such, I will probably make a few mistakes about the older material, which I hope will be pointed out to me.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, much has already been said and posted about the differences among the editions, basically W5 and the older ones collectively. This phase will try to focus on points that I either feel have not been mentioned as frequently as they should have or on those points that have been mostly ignored. I will probably be going over much that is already old, but it is to set up a pattern (along with the previous two phases and the final upcoming one) for the ultimate comprehensive review. Please bear etapwith me as I continue this undertaking.<br /> <br /> Metaplot and Back Story<br /> <br /> The overall story for the original <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> games is that the world is in grave danger, on the verge of being destroyed, predominately by the influence of the Wyrm. While there are secondary problems involving the Weaver and other forces, the main antagonists are those in league with this spirit of destruction and corruption. In W5, the Apocalypse has already happened. No one knows when, why, or how, but it is currently happening. One would think that there would be at least some concrete answer, or at least an inkling, but there isn't one mentioned. The Garou were supposed to help forestall this from happening, but they failed. This is a major shift in how the game is played. There could be a fair amount of gameplay involved in surviving such an outcome, but it is suggested that it will be for naught. While small victories can be made, there is no suggestion that the Apocalypse can be reversed or even halted. This is a very nihilistic view, one that sets out the characters as 'losers' from the start. The previous generations failed, so we can't do anything but try and survive.<br /> <br /> Another change is that the Wyrm, as well as the other two members of the Triat the Weaver and Wyld, are no longer individual spirits, but just the names for the cosmological powers of creation, order, and destruction. While each has a number of spirits that follow them, they are no longer 'real' spirits themselves. Yet, according to W5s own rules, they could be. In fact, in some places, they are almost considered spirits. While previous editions hinged upon the Triat being powerful spirits that could be met with, at least on some level, the Triat is now just the combination of forces that define the cosmos. Basically, the Triat is now just the Garou terms for Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy from Mage.<br /> <br /> This change is important, as the original editions tied theTriat's problems from when the Weaver grew a level of sentience great enough to capture the Wyrm, leading to the Worm's corruption. Without spiritual being, the Wyrm's corruption in W5 has no explanation. How can a force of nature become 'corrupted' enough to break the cycle of creation to renewal? For example, how can gravity be corrupted when it is just a force of nature? By removing this spiritual component, the entire underpinning of the game breaks down. One is just left with widespread destruction without reason, barely removed from real life woes. In fact, W5 even suggests to peg every little problem upon humans, leaving the spiritual side as the effect more than the cause. It is subtle distinction from previous editions, where some of the direct attacks on a cosmological scale are definitely outside of humanity's blame.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T12:23:26-08:00","id":1526286,"title":"","content":"W5: &quot;I know that the cosmologies of Werewolf and Mage are mutually exclusive, but what if we tried anyway?&quot;<br /> <br /> And no one lived that night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T13:34:15-08:00","id":1526291,"title":"","content":"Yeah, W5 has a real problem with following through on the idea that this is a setting with an animistic worldview. It doesn't feel like it certainly. And of course like usual for W5 the big excuse in the book is &quot;Who knows. From the section &quot;Animistic Worldview&quot; on pg 20: &quot;Much like knowledge of exactly what\u2019s in the sea eludes most humans, definitive knowledge of the true depths of the Umbra eludes the Garou. Werewolves\u2019 legends (and even some of the tales of elder werewolves\u2019 travails) tell of a time when the Umbra wasn\u2019t as broadly hostile to the Garou. Those times are gone, however, and werewolves now find the Umbra can be a fearsome place if they are unprepared for a visit there. It\u2019s another of the tragedies that punctuates Garou existence, that they find themselves monstrous outsiders in both of the worlds they call their own.\u200b&quot; Humans don't know much, Garou know a little bit more but only a little bit. Things used to be better in the past but another who knows for when that was and these days Garou aren't welcome in the Umbra anyway. And this is supposed to be one of the main-things players are supposed to interact with.<br /> <br /> This is especially egregious because this is one of the areas where WtA's animism could link to Native cultures' beliefs and practices. Through that, it could solidify what Garou believe as well as build bridges between human culture and Garou culture. It's also one of the things that distinguishes WtA. You're not just playing Joe Schmoe who happens to find out one day that he can shapeshift into a wolf. There's supposed to be more to it than that.<br /> <br /> And instead, the first two chapters want to put humanity into the driver's seat. First of all, having an &quot;animistic worldview&quot; means having a particular lens through which you look at things. Capitalism, climate-change, greed, corruption, all sorts of other human foibles, big and small... It's all still there. A regular human would look at some coal-plant blasting dirty shit into the air and call it &quot;environmental pollution&quot; but a Garou would look at it and talk about the corruption of the Wyrm. And the W5 corebook immediately ignores that distinction by starting with this whole bit about the &quot;Capitalocene era&quot;. That's also ironic because later you get that sidebar on pg 26 called &quot;Drawing Distinctions&quot; where it talks about &quot;environmental apocalypse&quot; as an &quot;emotional issue&quot;. And that you shouldn't think companies are bad by default. But that &quot;Capitolecene era&quot;-comment is first presented under the section-title &quot;Age Of Apocalypse&quot;. As presented, the first section in Chapter One is quite clear in saying that capitalism is synonymous with the Age Of Apocalypse in W5. They really haven't thought this through, it seems.<br /> <br /> By putting humanity in the driver's seat, you also get to another uncomfortable bit and that's the Impergium. Here's how the end of the Impergium is described on pg 36 under &quot;A Concord And Secrecy&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some werewolves realized what terrible violence the Garou had done to humankind, and they felt that people were, <b>if not justified</b>, at least understandable in their anger. Thus, they believed that perhaps it was time to approach humanity with more compassion, and teach them, in turn, to respect Gaia. Other werewolves wanted humanity\u2019s <b>just punishment</b> to continue. Still other Garou believed that humans had overstepped their boundaries and <b>needed to be slaughtered</b> wholesale for their crimes. And some felt that the Garou must turn inward,\u200b leave humanity to its own devices, and focus instead on the damage werewolves caused.\u200b </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> It's very telling how that section starts by saying that humans weren't &quot;justified&quot; in being angry about the Impergium but Garou could &quot;understand&quot; their anger. And then it continues to describe the idea of the Impergium as &quot;just punishment&quot; being the moderate position between the &quot;wholesale slaughter&quot;-faction and the &quot;let's leave humanity alone&quot;-faction. How did the Concord even come to pass if that were the actual political situation? And by starting like that, you could read into this part that W5 thinks the biggest mistake of the Impergium was that it stopped.<br /> <br /> Together with the Hauglosk/fascism-stuff, this refocusing on humanity as the &quot;real villain&quot; is... weird.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't help that while the Fenrir are these supposedly overzealous fanatics, the Red Talons are still a playable Tribe despite being huge fans of a &quot;Second Impergium&quot;. And human-born Garou being able to join the Tribe is a really bad vibe. You will play a psychopath if you play a human-born Red Talon with the mostly unchanged Red Talon mindset from older editions. But somehow the Fenrir are uniquely bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:23:01-08:00","id":1526293,"title":"","content":"There were moments before W5 was released that made me go &quot;Who wants to play this?&quot; and it still seems to be the case. I get the feeling most running W5 are ignoring the 'can't do shit' rule.<br /> <br /> In a larger way, I don't think W5 truly grasps what animism is. The way the umbra is closed off and hostile, the way garou only have tribal totems to choose from and the way the game refuses to let you make spirits touchstones all hint of a world that is utterly without spirituality. Because animism is not just about the spirits of nature, the spirits are everywhere and everything has a spiritual reflection. The umbra is not some magical land of Immersion Breaking Fantasy, it is the mirror to the physical. In w5, there is no resonance, there is no need to offer chimanage to the local spirits.<br /> <br /> Ironically, W5 brings a much more monotheistic and strict view of supernatural.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:28:03-08:00","id":1526294,"title":"","content":"Who is the antagonist of this game anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:37:37-08:00","id":1526295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526294#post1526294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is the antagonist of this game anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elder garou, from what I've heard from people who've played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:46:19-08:00","id":1526296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526293#post1526293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were moments before W5 was released that made me go &quot;Who wants to play this?&quot; and it still seems to be the case. I get the feeling most running W5 are ignoring the 'can't do shit' rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although, I would firmly blame the W5 corebook for that. There's a part in the introduction that's almost comical in how contradictory it is. On pg 10 you have one paragraph that ends with the depressing line &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; and the very next paragraph goes like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s no cause for fatalism, however. The Apocalypse may be upon them, but that means every victory now becomes that much more important. Garou before them have failed Gaia, but this generation of Garou still has purpose. Take back lost places of power, repair the blights in the spirit world, and rip the goddamn throats out of the death merchants who profiteer their way through a world their actions make miserable, even \u2014 especially \u2014 the pack\u2019s home territory. Otherwise, there will be no tomorrow.\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's like one person wrote the section ending with the depressing &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; and then somebody added a paragraph having read nothing of what came before it. &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; and &quot;Otherwise there will be no tomorrow.&quot; are mutually exclusive. Only one of these things can be true.<br /> <br /> But it goes through the whole book where sometimes it talks about &quot;fighting the Apocalypse&quot; and then it talks about the PCs being in the Apocalypse/Age of Apocalypse. And that indecision (or contradiction) is what also keeps it from completely committing to an apocalyptic setting in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526293#post1526293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a larger way, I don't think W5 truly grasps what animism is. The way the umbra is closed off and hostile, the way garou only have tribal totems to choose from and the way the game refuses to let you make spirits touchstones all hint of a world that is utterly without spirituality. Because animism is not just about the spirits of nature, the spirits are everywhere and everything has a spiritual reflection. The umbra is not some magical land of Immersion Breaking Fantasy, it is the mirror to the physical. In w5, there is no resonance, there is no need to offer chimanage to the local spirits.<br /> Ironically, W5 brings a much more monotheistic and strict view of supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also see that in how caerns are described in W5. They're just &quot;batteries of spiritual energy&quot;. There's nothing alive about them that you could communicate with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526294#post1526294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is the antagonist of this game anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way W5 wants this to go is that you have your Pack of PC-Garou who occupy a caern and they're the <i>only </i>Garou occupying that caern. And the rest is just local stuff. Getting into some scuffles with bad guys of the local variety. A Fomor here and there, some local small business that's getting a bit too close to Pentex, a roving Cult of Fenris Pack, some Pack of Black Spiral Dancers, interacting with some Sept with Elders who are arrogant assholes and all failures...<br /> <br /> Also, the world is ending around you - but that's not what the game is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T13:19:07-08:00","id":1526469,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART TWO</span><br /> <br /> Garou History and Social Structure<br /> <br /> In the previous edition of W:tA, much of Garou history was recorded in the Silver Record, a repository of knowledge preserved in the special language of the spirits and guarded by a Keeper. Apparently, the Record doesn't exist in W5, as much of Garou history is only oral and prone to change over time in its retelling. This feels off, as there does appear to be some form of written language in the few glyphs seen in the book (as well as some more online, if one could call some of those glyphs). Too bad there isn't a Tribe dedicated to using technology as a means of serving Gaia. Oh wait, there is. It is hard to believe that there isn't more of a written record of events, of at least some of the more current ones after the invention of the printing press. Many of the new glyphs don't even convey the same sense of language as the older one did. As such, history in W5 is mostly just vague senses of what may have happened. This could be that the designers are planning some big reveals later on or that they want players to make their own history. Or it could be laziness. Most likely, The designers and management couldn't agree on what should be brought forward, so only the most important events necessary are included in W5.<br /> <br /> The one critical event mentioned was the Impergium, the culling of the human herd. There's no agreement about when it happened, why, how long it lasted, or what caused it to actually end. Basically, it feels that the was only even included as to give a reason for the Delirium mechanic. This also let to the founding of the Concord and the Garou Nation. There is no mention of the Wars of Rage from previous editions, although there is a mirror to the Croatan sacrifice and an obtuse mention of Garou in the Philippines. The possibility of other Tribes disappearing beyond the known sixteen is intriguing though, as it offers a broader look on the Garou experience. What is strange is that event fairly recent events don't have specifics known. Two Tribes have 'recently' left the Concord, but no timeline is given. It is suggested that both left relatively recently, but whether that is less than ten years or greater than thirty is unclear.<br /> <br /> A big deal has been made on how W5 has gotten rid of Kinfolk, and that shows in how one becomes Garou. Basically, no one knows anything. The oddest part, though, is that many modern Garou discover that they have a Garou ancestor. In fact, some lineages seem to have a good chance of having at least one Garou per generation or so. After until centuries or more, at least some research would've been done, at least some elite families seem to know something. Just another attempt at keeping some of the older material while trying to be new as well. Auspice is now determined when one undergoes their First Change. Tribe is usually found out through the help of a guardian who found the new Garou, and the new Garou frequently choses their guardian's Tribe. [I will be going over Auspice and Tribe more fully in the next part.]<br /> <br /> The main component of Garou society is still the pack. Some suggestions for packs are given, mostly very proactive types. However, the original 'balanced' pack of one of each Auspice is downplayed. Based on how the relationship map examples I've seen only feature four characters, I guess developers don't think troupes of more than three or four with a ST are common anymore. <br /> <br /> The main code of Garou society is still the Litany, sort of. Instead of the grand listing of the many tenets and a discussion over each individual tenet, W5 places the Litany in a sidebar in the lower right corner of a left hand page, with only a general paragraph on how the current generation of Garou don't believe in the Litany so much as it is to focused on how older, more powerful Garou retain their power.<br /> <br /> Finally, the structure of Garou society is explained. Packs are either formed by elders for current needs, or just when a Buch of werewolves just happen to be together at the same time. Packs from septs around caerns. Unfortunately, there aren't enough caerns to go around, so this leads to competition for them. Sept positions don't seem to exist any more, as there aren't enough caerns to support such a structure that could tame the competition. This combative nature is also why moots are rarer as well. No rules are given for them either.<br /> <br /> Basically, everything about the past of the Garou is left vague, and much about the current state of the Garou Nation is left in doubt. Even previous edition core books gave more information than this at the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T15:41:08-08:00","id":1526480,"title":"","content":"One of the main pillars of WtA was Sept politics and they've just ripped it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T00:48:22-08:00","id":1526508,"title":"","content":"There are many parts in W5 that show both its troubled production AND how it was in the end rushed.<br /> <br /> For one, there are three auspices that focus on lorekeeping and SOMEHOW no one has any clue of garou history, how garou pop up and when stuff happened. It isn't even that things are vague, they are straight up missing. I am reminded of how in math, -5+5 equals zero. The removal of old lore and the vague addition of new doesn't create new lore, it creates a vacuum.<br /> <br /> Then there are the cases of wanting their cake and to eat it too. Like how no one knows HOW garou are created BUT there are bloodlines. Or that septs arrange pack like in older editions, but also that there aren't many septs around. So there is a constant want to use the old lore conflicting heavily with not the new lore but the LACK of new lore.<br /> <br /> Compared to V5, it is amazingly messy. V5 has a clear idea what it is and what its world is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526469#post1526469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main code of Garou society is still the Litany, sort of. Instead of the grand listing of the many tenets and a discussion over each individual tenet, W5 places the Litany in a sidebar in the lower right corner of a left hand page, with only a general paragraph on how the current generation of Garou don't believe in the Litany so much as it is to focused on how older, more powerful Garou retain their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part of W5 that makes me laugh. Because the text says that young garou don't like it because elders abuse it. But if you look at the tenets, there are maybe three focused on that AND one has an opposite.<br /> <br /> What makes it hilarious, though, is that they only removed two tenets and reworded one a bit. So these young garou are, by the book, opposed to the following; fighting the Wyrm, not killing someone during a challenge, respecting others' territory, NOT EATING HUMANS, respecting all creations of Gaia, protecting caerns, KEEPING THE VEIL and challenging unfit elders.<br /> <br /> So either the Litany WAS supposed to be changed to be more restrictive or no one checked the actual litany. Thus, long pig is on the table!\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T11:13:31-08:00","id":1526521,"title":"","content":"Actually, let's focus on one tenet they removed;<br /> <br /> <b>Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</b><br /> <br /> While this tenet might read as the eugenics tenet, I'd say it is more the &quot;if you get too old/injured, it is best you retire&quot; in practise. I don't know if it was removed due to the former, but I'd say its removal creates this interesting situation.<br /> <br /> If the elders aren't beholden to keeping themselves fit and if there is no tenet to punish going off the rails mentally, then W5's situation makes sense.<br /> <br /> But, it is another removal of a way to do something. Taking out a corrupt elder due to the Litany tenet could be affecting change, something W5 is opposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T12:08:43-08:00","id":1526523,"title":"","content":"The history of Garou in W5 isn't just a testament to the WOD-team's stringent aversion to lore/worldbuilding but also illustrates a poor understanding of history in general. Who knows who did what when it came to the creation of these first two chapters in the W5 Corebook but what they show is a piss-poor attempt at outlining a group's history. The very first of Chapter Two's section &quot;The Shadow Of The Past&quot; says it all: &quot;A history of the Garou is both impossible and reductive.&quot; First of all, imagine saying this about any group's history that still has living members in this world. And what a choice of words! The infinite absoluteness of calling something &quot;impossible&quot; and at the same time invoking the limited confinement of it all being &quot;reductive&quot;. If anything, we got the developers' mission-statement here: Garou-history of previous editions gets cut down a size with reduction being the primary tool and making sure it's impossible to understand Garou-history the primary goal.<br /> <br /> Additionally, oral storytelling as a mode of transferring information through the ages matters little here as real-world-history has shown multiple times. It's pretty ahistoric how the second chapter treats this concept in regards to what Garou could know about their past. The text goes for a more superficial understanding of oral history as it reduces it to a game of telephone that has gotten things to a point where nobody knows anymore what was originally said. And it's portrayed with the implication that this means said history has just been lost. Oral history doesn't work like that, though. It's even more insulting that investing in Native American representation on the writing-staff more strongly probably could've led to a more informed perspective on this. But you wouldn't have even needed that. With a Western perspective, you still could point to things like Arthuriana, Robin Hood or the Illiad where oral storytelling shifts and changes depending on when and by whom the story gets told but at the core of these stories are still fundamental story-beats and truths that matter to the story and get carried throughout the ages. Or take some of these Viking-sagas from the middle-ages like the Heimskringla. It's a written work but without oral history that author wouldn't have been able to write it. Or a more modern example like Grimm\u2019s Fairy Tales. Without oral storytelling/history you wouldn\u2019t even have that.<br /> <br /> The most basic form of describing a history is to just rattle off people, places and events. Just a chain of &quot;who did what and when&quot;. Cause and effect. And it all sounds pretty straightforward and obvious because it's a retrospective. Hindsight is 20/20, as they say. A leads to B, B leads to C, and so on. And the actual study of history is in explaining how and why A led to B and B led to C and so on. W5 sucks at doing precisely that. And the justification is this: &quot;The finer details, locations, and players in these grand dramas may shift with the times, and with the storytellers spinning the tale for those listening to them. But the Garou consider a few common events to be undeniable truths in their collective story.&quot; Following that, it really does only focus on a few \u201cundeniable truths\u201d while even expressing uncertainty about that. And the writers couldn\u2019t even muster the imagination for the CliffsNotes-version, instead we got the CliffsNotes of the CliffsNotes. Talk about being reductive...<br /> <br /> Take for example what the first paragraph on the Cult of Fenris casually drops on the reader: \u201cAt a great meeting of the tribes, the Cult of Fenris called for one final, glorious charge into the Wyrm\u2019s maw to avert the Apocalypse, but the assembled Garou of other tribes called out their rally as suicide, whereupon most of the Cult of Fenris camp decided that all Garou had fallen, and only the Cult\u2019s pure vision could serve Gaia.\u201d Representatives from all the Tribes gathering to discuss what Garou should do would have been quite the event in previous editions. You\u2019d think the Garou-Nation gathering to discuss the onset of the Age of Apocalypse would be an important event (not least because that\u2019s when the Fenrir left). But that\u2019s another issue with W5 in general. The text gets all fussy about Fenrir abandoning caerns and being too fanatical in fighting the Wyrm. Sure\u2026 so what do the other Garou do? This supposed gathering of all the Tribes is a good example. The Fenrir want to go all-out and attack the Wyrm directly. Okay, insane idea but\u2026 what are the other Garou proposing? What is the alternative to that vision? And the adventure \u201cDeepest of Wounds\u201d has the same issue. The Fenrir go off to fight the Wyrm after their caern just dries up \u2013 and that makes them the bad guys. Meanwhile, the Garou who stayed behind are inherently good just because they\u2019re protecting a caern. Of course, Garou lost the war against the Wyrm when \u201cgood\u201d Garou only care about it if it\u2019s within walkable distance from a caern.<br /> <br /> The other thing is to have history communicated through storytelling. Legends, myths and epics that may or may not be fictional but illuminate lived experiences of the past and societal norms and traditions. On that front W5 fails as well. First, it's hard to tell a story with lines like &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia?&quot;. This is just expressing a lack of knowledge. There's no story and no history here. This is the book just giving up and saying &quot;Who knows.&quot;. It's insane just how much word-count gets wasted in the second Chapter on being extremely non-specific at the best times and being completely non-descriptive at other times.<br /> <br /> Instead, I suspect that the lack of thought put into the history is that it was written backwards. The Age of Apocalypse, the fall of the Garou-Nation, Gaia dying: Those were the only ideas. And the game wants you to have the same reductive perspective. Don't wonder about the how, don't wonder about the why and don't wonder about the when\u2026<br /> <br /> It's now and it's bad.<br /> <br /> That's all you're supposed to think about. &quot;Capitalocene era&quot;... &quot;That's edgy, right?&quot; was probably the thought when that was put into the book - but what has that got to do with Garou? That's one of the worst aspects here: It's the lack of imagination. In the same way the Garou of the game supposedly look at the world via their animistic worldview, the Garou you're expected to play are supposed to be a new lens to view our world through. \u201cCapitalocene\u201d is a human term for a human perspective. The fictional Garou are a way to use fiction/fantasy to explore different horizons and perspectives. So you have to be imaginative in how you portray an idea like \u201ccapitalocene\u201d. Instead W5\u2019s approach to history sees &quot;reduction&quot; as its main-tool and renders the understanding of the past &quot;impossible&quot; as its main-goal. This isn't just an aversion to lore/worldbuilding, this is an outright bad approach to a fictional setting.<br /> <br /> And this all then leads back again to the overly pessimistic perspective of W5. If you go to the section \u201cThe Real Problem With The Garou\u201d, you get that heavy dose of pessimism about how Garou suck and just aren\u2019t the right tool to save the world. And Garou-history is just another part of that pessimistic vision. A past full of \u201cWho knows\u201d, a worldbuilding focused on \u201cIt is now and it is bad.\u201d and the pessimistic attitude towards what you\u2019re supposed to play as in \u201cGarou suck.\u201d. This is how you toss the premise of WtA in the trash. And really any premise for a setting would end up in the trash when its treatment is so careless and incurious.<br /> <br /> I will write tomorrow more about my thoughts about the depiction of Garou-society in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T07:01:13-08:00","id":1526553,"title":"","content":"Karims weird grudge against oral history is deeply stupid when I'm coming from a country where oral histories have been successfully preserved and past on for tens of thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T07:11:50-08:00","id":1526555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526553#post1526553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Karims weird grudge against oral history is deeply stupid when I'm coming from a country where oral histories have been successfully preserved and past on for tens of thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is as much a Karim issue as it is; &quot;We need to show the old garou ways are bad so let's make it so their oral histories are inaccurate to MODERN methods.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ignoring, naturally, that many Indigenous people around the world have functioning oral histories. Something that Legacy understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T10:30:35-08:00","id":1526559,"title":"","content":"I also wonder how the writing of the first two chapters was impacted by Justin Achilli leaving in January. Not just him leaving so suddenly but since he immediately landed in a different job after that, this couldn't have been a process that only just started in late 2022. And who knows how that influenced the writing-process for the book. This is certainly not how these things normally go.<br /> <br /> But it does feel like they worked backward from the Age of Apocalypse, the Garou-Nation has fallen and Gaia's dead/dying. And I guess, since the present of the W5-setting is so full of destruction, I guess, you could look at Garou-history and think it isn't that important to the game. I don't agree with that but considering the WOD-team's negative attitude towards lore/worldbuilding this might be a conclusion they could've reached, I would say. Karim's obsessive insistence on GoF=Nazis didn't help much either. And there's the view on Garou as fascists in the W5 corebook without much curiosity for the how and why. It's all just pessimism about how much Garou suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:19:36-08:00","id":1526616,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART THREE</span><br /> <br /> Auspices and Tribes<br /> <br /> Much has already been mentioned about the changes to these two traits, but I still want to highlight some important bits about both.<br /> <br /> First, Auspices. W5 has kept all five Auspices and kept their roles in Garou society about the same. However, the mechanics of them has changed. In previous editions, Auspice determine a character's starting Rage. In W5, Rage has the same potential in all Garou, meaning that the main mechanic tied to Auspice was removed. Instead of having some werewolves better suited to interact with regular humans at the cost of being more combat-oriented, and vice-versa with others, there was some real considerations for choosing an Auspice. In W5, not only is that consideration gone, there was nothing to replace it with. The only real mechanical side that has stayed the same is the Gift list. At the very least, howling at the moon during the phase of your Auspice should offer some extra benefit, but no. Sure, Auspices can provide social uses, but without a mechanical benefit, there is no real difference in playing one over another.<br /> <br /> The Tribes have had many changes made, with the primary one being that Tribes are no longer tied to any one human culture/genetic line. In some instances, this makes a great deal of sense, even though much of the genetic side had been already phased out by Revised. However, without at least some human cultural attributes, Tribes kind of blur into one another. One could say that the caern where a Tribe came into being shaped much of the traditions of it, even after spreading far from the source, to explain why so much human culture is found within a Tribe, without tying them to a specific human group. The two just developed together, in sort of an expanded form of how local human culture shapes individual septs.<br /> <br /> Some of the Tribes had their names changed, which one could say had to be done. I'm perfectly fine by this, as I never thought that the names were their &quot;official&quot; one's in the Speech anyway, just close approximations in human languages. The ones that were changed were more phonetic, and the true meaning behind their names were never given. I admit, I would have chosen different names for the Uktena and Wendigo besides Ghost Council and Galestalkers (my first guesses being Trackers of the Unseen and Wind Racers, mostly to keep the alphabetical order the same), but they are just similar enough to the originals' scope as to be acceptable.<br /> <br /> The Fianna are a different matter. Their new name is Hart Wardens. For anyone who doesn't know, hart is another name for the European red deer. So, cultural ties are bad, but geographical ones aren't? Also, the Tribe associated with Stag has a name with a type of deer in it. Warden also used to be a title for a sept position, which no longer seems to be a thing either. I would have gone for the near-pun with Heart or Hearth Wardens instead, focussing on emotional well-being or family relationships respectively. Finally, the Tribe's main function involving the acquisition of territory is awfully close to that of British Imperialism and Colonialism, which is a little on-the-nose for the Tribe originally based in the British Isles.<br /> <br /> Two other Tribes had major changes. The Red Talons now accept Homids and the Black Furies accept all males. Admittedly, the Talons still have the highest percentage of Lupus of the Tribes, but the change to the Furies is odd. Not the acceptance, but in keeping the name, as fur color isn't inherited, so 'black' is not really adequate. [As an aside, I don't remember seeing anything about how fur color relates to hair color. Most of the art shows the regular grey to light brown seen in normal wolves, but I don't know if there is any other possibilities beyond those for Gaian Garou.] 'Furies' has feminine connotations, so it isn't that adequate either. At least 'red' can refer to bloody talons, so that still counts, but what does 'black' now refer to?<br /> <br /> The Furies are also one of the Tribes to have its Patron, formally Totem, changed. Instead of Pegasus, which has strong ties to Greek myth, they now have Gorgon, which has just as strong ties to Greek myth and is less familiar, aside as the term for Wyld-possessed beings. If the designers didn't want to use Pegasus, they could have just used Winged-Horse. They kept Gryphon for the Talons after all. (For those who don't remember their Greek myths, the immortal Gorgon sisters of Medusa did have wings as well as the serpentine features.) That's what they did changing Uktena with Horned Serpent. The final change was with the Glass Walkers in swapping Cockroach with Spider. That might be too close to Weaver-aligned spirits, but I can give it a pass.<br /> <br /> Gone are the starting WP and Background restrictions that defined previous editions. Instead, Patrons now offer a Boon and a Ban, similar to what Pack Totems did. However, such uses are at about the same level of power as those, even though a Tribe Patron should offer a greater degree of power, just by dint of being a more powerful entity. Boons are just the addition of a die to performing certain specific type of roll. Useful, but limited. Bans are about as bad. Instead of the varied nature of the optional Tribe Weaknesses from the previous editions, the Bans are about the same. If a Garou fails to perform a certain action when needed, or does perform a forbidden act, then they don't recover full WP at the start of the next session. While the actions are varied, having the same outcome is kind of lazy. Yes, WP is very hard to recover in W5 and other WOD5 games, but having the same outcome for each Tribe doesn't allow the differences among them to come through. There is just less there to make their differences stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T12:17:10-08:00","id":1526620,"title":"","content":"In terms of fur colour, WtA garou have always been pretty varied. If you look at the tribe arts for W20, there is a lot of variation among the garou. The Red Talons being, yes, red-furred.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Talons, since cannibalism is now allowed, there is a concept that is just a cannibal. That and if we go over what the Talons are in W5, one has to ask why they are playable at all. They do worse things than the CoF and they aren't even affected by hauslosk.<br /> <br /> I mentioned the lack of animism in W5 and the way the tribal patrons are written and used showcases another aspect of this. These powerful patrons are boiled down to small benefits and unbalanced bans. Not only that but by the book, these are the ONLY patrons the pack can have. There is even an implication that packs just don't have patrons anymore. There is no longer this close relationship with spirits, some concepts like the Ghost Council's monk even imply you don't need other garou to join a tribe anymore. Everything is boiled down to stats if that.<br /> <br /> Auspices,though, have completely lost their purpose. Outside gift lists, the gift of Luna no longer exists in stats.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder if this was due to writers not understanding that auspice=rage and instead thinking Rage in terms of Hunger which is universal for all vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T14:57:46-08:00","id":1526633,"title":"","content":"I think a good illustration of how much thought was put into the Tribes is the Ghost Council. This will become a bigger topic in the controversy-phase of the review but it's just such an illustrative symbol that something just went wrong here.<br /> <br /> Old WtA had its issues and so any new edition would've to tackle those. One way was to remove any mention of ethical or cultural ties between the Tribes and humanity. And already on that count, there's plenty of evidence that this process hasn't been very thorough. But the focus of this effort were the Native American Tribes and so the Older Brother Tribe and the Younger Brother Tribe were renamed to Ghost Council and Galestalkers. We've learned that from James Sambrano speaking out and this will become a topic later but what matters here is how we ended up with the version of Ghost Council that is found in the released version of W5.<br /> <br /> There was a previous aborted attempt at a W5 Corebook by Hunters Entertainment which James Sambrano worked on and that's where the idea of the new name of Ghost Council was introduced. Fast forward to the next version where James Sambrano wasn't around anymore but Ghost Council was still the new name. But while James' writing was used in the released book it's clear nobody talked to him because of this section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To the Ghost Council \u2014 or \u201cGhosts,\u201d individually \u2014 the destination or the path might be the objective; what matters most is that the seeker understands why they have undertaken a particular journey and can therefore learn about the Garou\u2019s world. The journey itself is of great import to Ghost Council werewolves, as it represents an opportunity for discovery along the way\u2026 as well as a chance to tease out the secrets of the journey\u2019s environment.\u200b </div> </div> </div>You look at those two pages and the reader gets no explanation for why the name is Ghost Council. And you can see that in the cited section because - why would these Tribe-members call each other &quot;Ghosts&quot;...? Also, that should've been the clue that more is going on here. What is one of the the main-supernatural types of things Garou interact with? Spirits. And this Tribe calls itself the <i>Ghost</i>-Council. Instead what the writer took away from the name is this: &quot;Whether tricking an unsuspecting spirit into letting them pass unmolested or <b>learning where in his mistress\u2019 apartment the executive hid incriminating documents</b>, werewolves of the Ghost Council look for the boundaries others draw around themselves, the flaws they build into their own armor.\u200b&quot; (Emphasis mine) What the new version focuses on instead is to understand &quot;Ghost&quot; as some euphemism for this Tribe being some sort of rogue-ish knowledge-seekers that skulk around and are fans of trickery.<br /> <br /> More so this new version adopted this weird idea of &quot;using taboos against your enemy&quot;. The short blurb on pg 40 summarizes this idea: &quot;Garou of the Ghost Council favor unconventional approaches and challenge taboos to use rivals\u2019 weaknesses against them in service to Gaia.&quot; This is just such a convoluted idea! So you do something that's taboo for you but doing that also exposes a rival's weakness, in other words, this weakness wouldn't exist without breaking the taboo. But what does that even mean? And for that, we go back to the Tribe-section which has this illuminating bit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This philosophy has earned the Ghost Council a reputation as subversives among more traditional Garou \u2014 and Ghosts don\u2019t seem to care. \u201cThe ends justify the means\u201d usually comes across as a dangerous political doctrine, but for the Ghost Council, finding an answer or opportunity excuses how it\u2019s accomplished. If something comes of maintaining a relationship with a confidant\u200b from a fallen tribe or forging pacts with forbidden spirits, the Ghost is satisfied \u2014 and validated, in their minds.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Besides making this Tribe another Tribe that should be far closer to being a candidate for going rogue than the Fenrir, giving a playable Tribe an &quot;ends justify the means&quot;-attitude is a strange choice, to say the least. By that logic, a Ghost Council PC allying with BSD and Wyrm spirits shouldn't be considered out-of-place if it serves them. And that makes this version simply villains. The moment you make this convoluted idea of &quot;breaking taboos to expose new enemy-weaknesses&quot; more legible, it immediately becomes clear what it's outlining could be summarized with another idiom as well: &quot;The road to hell is paved with good intentions.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Setting that aside, read the section again and wonder: Where did the Tribe come from? What does the Tribe think about the Age of Apocalypse? The fall of the Garou-Nation? Or Gaia's Howl...? Honestly, how would you even play a Ghost Council Garou using the W5 Corebook...? Besides coming up with a PC-concept what is the actual Tribe like? In all those questions the STs and players are just left alone. And they're left alone because there isn't even a hint of support for guiding the process of making this Tribe work. The main-thing that was done here was to strip away lore/worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> And Auspices have been mostly written out of the game. Litany doesn't matter (so Ragabash and Philodox can't serve their purpose), entering the Umbra is hard and Spirits generally don't like Garou (so Theurges can't serve their purpose), nobody knows anything about Garou-history (so Galliards can't serve their purpose) and looking to bring the fight to Gaia's enemies sounds like something Fenrir would do and Fenrir are bad of course (so Ahroun can't serve their purpose). I guess in the way this version of W5 is conceptualized there really isn't a place for the Auspices of previous editions in this version of W5...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T16:28:50-08:00","id":1526639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526521#post1526521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, let's focus on one tenet they removed;<br /> <br /> <b>Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</b><br /> <br /> While this tenet might read as the eugenics tenet, I'd say it is more the &quot;if you get too old/injured, it is best you retire&quot; in practise. I don't know if it was removed due to the former, but I'd say its removal creates this interesting situation.<br /> <br /> If the elders aren't beholden to keeping themselves fit and if there is no tenet to punish going off the rails mentally, then W5's situation makes sense.<br /> <br /> But, it is another removal of a way to do something. Taking out a corrupt elder due to the Litany tenet could be affecting change, something W5 is opposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the old books there was always the section to discuss what this means for different Tribes and different contexts. It could be such a thing as finding a duty that's appropriate to your limitations. It wasn't necessarily toss your wounded/elders out into the cold. This is something that I really feel is missing in W5. A discussion of what the Tenets actually mean and how different people treat them. We had a basic discussion in all the old editions, but here, they're just an afterthought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T00:46:52-08:00","id":1526656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526639#post1526639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the old books there was always the section to discuss what this means for different Tribes and different contexts. It could be such a thing as finding a duty that's appropriate to your limitations. It wasn't necessarily toss your wounded/elders out into the cold. This is something that I really feel is missing in W5. A discussion of what the Tenets actually mean and how different people treat them. We had a basic discussion in all the old editions, but here, they're just an afterthought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. But the tenet's removal and the way the litany is treated in general shows the idea of it being discussed and debated is just ignored. Looking at V5, the traditions were discussed and explained there, so there isn't even a precedent for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T01:57:20-08:00","id":1526664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526656#post1526656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I know. But the tenet's removal and the way the litany is treated in general shows the idea of it being discussed and debated is just ignored. Looking at V5, the traditions were discussed and explained there, so there isn't even a precedent for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fascinating to go back to the Discord Q&amp;A with Justin Achilli and hear him talk about it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>How does the Litany look as of right now?</b><br /> Eleven tenets, cutting the ones about who you're allowed to fuck and the attitude you're supposed to have about &quot;disability.&quot; Much emphasis on the Litany being abused by outsized personalities, and the inherent hypocrisies and gray areas in it. Big takeaway is &quot;If this Litany is so great, why are we living in the Apocalypse?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Of course, with &quot;much emphasis&quot; he actually meant &quot;that's all that will be talked about&quot;. And the game never really did find an answer to the question of &quot;If Garou are so great, why are we living in the Apocalypse?&quot; beyond just stating over and over again that Garou suck.<br /> <br /> Also, it was always a weird move to first remove bits from the Litany because they were considered &quot;bad&quot; and then still make the &quot;big takeaway&quot; that the Litany is bad. If you're just gonna say that the Litany is bad anyway, why remove anything...? And of course, a very surface-level-reading there of those removed bits of the Litany while the eventual overall negative &quot;big takeaway&quot; completely ignores the bits of the Litany that are good.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T02:26:23-08:00","id":1526666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526664#post1526664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it was always a weird move to first remove bits from the Litany because they were considered &quot;bad&quot; and then still make the &quot;big takeaway&quot; that the Litany is bad. If you're just gonna say that the Litany is bad anyway, why remove anything...? And of course, a very surface-level-reading there of those removed bits of the Litany while the eventual overall negative &quot;big takeaway&quot; completely ignores the bits of the Litany that are good.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling there was very little actual reading of the Litany. Because who the heck looks at a set of laws that say 'do not eat humans' and still writes how it is either abused or ignored?<br /> <br /> I get that cannibalism is a trope in werewolf media, but if a law says not to do it, why is that not pointed out at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T02:37:48-08:00","id":1526667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526666#post1526666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling there was very little actual reading of the Litany. Because who the heck looks at a set of laws that say 'do not eat humans' and still writes how it is either abused or ignored?<br /> <br /> I get that cannibalism is a trope in werewolf media, but if a law says not to do it, why is that not pointed out at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the thing it reminds me of the most is someone looking at the whole thing primarily through the lens of VtM: Arrogant, manipulative Elders (any Prince of a city or other older vampire), oppressive hypocritical hierarchical structure (Camarilla) and young newcomers who are trying to figure out their own path (Anarchs). That's what is attempted to be replicated here, I think. But WtA (even in its reduced W5 form) isn't VtM and that's why it doesn't really work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T03:50:38-08:00","id":1526670,"title":"","content":"VtM is a game about being fundamentally selfish. Anything and everything exists only in the service of perpetuating your existence and nothing really has value beyond yourself. WtA is a game about protecting others and sacrificing yourself for a chance something better may come.<br /> <br /> It's a tonal dissonance that's very hard to explain to many people coming in from VtM, but it is the core of why W5 strikes so hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T04:23:22-08:00","id":1526671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526670#post1526670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a tonal dissonance that's very hard to explain to many people coming in from VtM, but it is the core of why W5 strikes so hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>At times, I feel people WANT that selfish setting where nothing with the myths is truly true. I've had conversations with people who'd like Gaia be like Caine, maybe existing maybe not.<br /> <br /> And W5 seems to be made with that in mind. At least in part.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T06:49:13-08:00","id":1526675,"title":"","content":"That goes back to what degree the book was actually successful in its &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-approach. The Litany is a good example of how in the end the book did neither. It just presented the old Litany with some removed and a conceptual presentation that left a lot to be desired. Instead, the issue isn't even how it compares to previous editions, it's that the presentation of the Litany in this book just doesn't work. Without the context of previous editions, it would be even worse! At least that way you can get some understanding through these older sources of what the deal is with the Litany and how to portray it. If you were to use just what's on offer in the W5 corebook, most of the time it will simply not play a role in the game, I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T09:38:12-08:00","id":1526681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526666#post1526666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling there was very little actual reading of the Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the sheer amount of basic WtA setting and lore that freelancers had to explain multiple times to the Developer.........there was indeed fuck all reading done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T14:05:45-08:00","id":1526687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526681#post1526681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the sheer amount of basic WtA setting and lore that freelancers had to explain multiple times to the Developer.........there was indeed fuck all reading done.</div> </div> </div> </div>One gets the impression that the most recent W:tA book read by any of the people giving the marching orders was the player's guide. From first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T03:04:41-08:00","id":1526697,"title":"","content":"One trend that I've seen in online-discourse of W5 is that a lot of people digest the WtA-concepts in the W5 corebook and then say &quot;I wanna know more about this.&quot;. And the response they get is to refer them back to the previous editions. That's a mark of how the &quot;not continuation&quot;-part hasn't worked out. The W5 corebook doesn't stand on its own. There are parts of it that only get legible once you read stuff from previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T05:44:37-08:00","id":1526701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526697#post1526697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One trend that I've seen in online-discourse of W5 is that a lot of people digest the WtA-concepts in the W5 corebook and then say &quot;I wanna know more about this.&quot;. And the response they get is to refer them back to the previous editions. That's a mark of how the &quot;not continuation&quot;-part hasn't worked out. The W5 corebook doesn't stand on its own. There are parts of it that only get legible once you read stuff from previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really showcases the way W5 has been in flux far longer than V5 was and instead of pruning the game to create a cohesive whole, we have basically a series of diverticolite aspects to the street level main channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T06:01:24-08:00","id":1526702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526701#post1526701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really showcases the way W5 has been in flux far longer than V5 was and instead of pruning the game to create a cohesive whole, we have basically a series of diverticolite aspects to the street level main channel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at no point did it all come together to form a cohesive whole. You have the people at Paradox with their wishes for street-level-only and how the Umbra should be deemphasized, then you have Karim with all his &quot;hot takes&quot; about what WtA is really about (particularly the role of the Fenrir in the game) and then you add Justin Achilli to that who had his own &quot;hot takes&quot; of what WOD5E should be about (he had that whole Twitter-thread about his grand theory of what WOD5E is about) and all his other ideas (like his insistence on making the &quot;verbs&quot; a thing, for example). Then the general disdain for lore/worldbuilding which extended to stuff like lowering the number of Loresheets in books.<br /> <br /> And now Renegade is gonna come in via the supplements and offer their own &quot;hot takes&quot; about W5, like we've already seen with the depiction of the Fenrir in that one adventure and how the first Loresheet for a Pack that can be an ally immediately came with a custom Pack-Patron-Spirit (which isn't something PCs can have in the W5 corebook).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T13:04:44-08:00","id":1526872,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART FOUR</span><br /> <br /> Character Generation Part One<br /> <br /> By default, all characters are now Homid. Since Gnosis has been removed as a mechanic, there is no different, or need, for three different Breeds. However, one can still create a Lupus character. There is. just no formal rules for doing so. It is recommended that certain Skills (i.e. Abilities) be restricted, but it doesn't have to be. So, if you want a starting Lupus character who is a stunt-driving, computer hacker, there is nothing in the rules preventing you from doing so. Technically.<br /> <br /> This also means that the Metis breed is no more. Unlike other terms, I guess there was too much baggage to just change the name. On the other hand, there is nothing anywhere in the rules suggesting what the offspring of two Garou are. It has been suggested that they are just regular humans/wolves with the same odds of undergoing a First Change. Or not, as the vagueness on Garou continues. <br /> <br /> [As an aside, my take would be the Hybrid Breed. This Breed is characterized by the features of animals other than wolves in the three supernatural forms, particularly Crinos. These features are almost always beneficial. There are many theories, such as spirit interference or a shapeshifter ancestor, but the only thing known is that a Hybris has at least one parent or grandparent who is the offspring of two Garou. While they are rarely in the forefront of battles, their real usefulness is in the fact that they have fairly high chance of having Garou children. The elite lineages try to keep this secret, as it could weaken the families.]<br /> <br /> Attributes and Skills are the same as those in V5. This isn't too different from the older editions. One note though, Primal-Urge and Rituals are missing, as the mechanics that were based on these two abilities have been altered. More on that later.<br /> <br /> The biggest changes have been to the Advantages. Many favorite Merits and Flaws are absent. It is unsure if any of the missing ones will ever return, since many of them would unbalance W5's mechanics. Backgrounds are very different. As Garou are no longer genetic, basically, there is no need for a Kinfolk BG. If one wants to represent a relative, it would be through Allies or the new Touchstone mechanic, and neither really reflect what Kinfolk were. Not having an ally such as this could end up hurting the game. Likewise, Pure Breed is now unnecessary. While there appears to be some sort of elite qualities, there is no mechanic to reflect this. Strangely enough, Ancestors, formerly Past Life, is also removed. With the strong hatred for knowing anything about the past, this seemed a fairly safe bet to be removed. As of yet, there is no information if such spirits exist. While mentioned in another section, a Status BG appears to have been left out. Maybe the designers were limited in the number of Backgrounds they could put in, and the Mask, formerly the Alternate Identity Merit, was more important. With the constant hatred towards elders, such a Background would be useful, especially since Rank has been removed.<br /> <br /> The biggest removal would be Rites. While the actual powers are still here, there is no secondary mechanic to go with it. This basically means that there is no power rating on Rites, as all are equal. This also means that there really isn't a rarity to Rites either. Beginning characters could start with Rites well beyond what they should be capable of. Even if PCs are exceptional, this might be takin things too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T00:28:44-08:00","id":1526906,"title":"","content":"Oddly, the whole Kinfolk thing is even more ridiculous because you could easily just say, &quot;Everyone has a little Garou DNA in it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T00:44:35-08:00","id":1526907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526697#post1526697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One trend that I've seen in online-discourse of W5 is that a lot of people digest the WtA-concepts in the W5 corebook and then say &quot;I wanna know more about this.&quot;. And the response they get is to refer them back to the previous editions. That's a mark of how the &quot;not continuation&quot;-part hasn't worked out. The W5 corebook doesn't stand on its own. There are parts of it that only get legible once you read stuff from previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. W5's designers said, &quot;We think what new players want is an experience that doesn't bog down their creativity with established lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then actual new players said, &quot;This is kind of cool, but we want a lot more lore. Where do we get that?&quot;<br /> <br /> The designers had their ideas about the best way to proceed, and the intended audience of new players immediately rejected it and wanted something more substantive.<br /> <br /> Clown shoes edition.<br /> <br /> Inevitably, people who ARE interested in Werewolf for the first time are just going to do deep dives into the old material anyway. Whether that's by buying all the old books on PDF, or having existing fans explain it to them. Trying to silo off all the &quot;legacy&quot; material is fruitless. Especially if the new books deliberately avoid saying anything concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T13:22:53-08:00","id":1526939,"title":"","content":"It was already pretty easy to imagine from the history of V5\u2019s development that a significant contingent of the legacy fan base was going to take umbrage with what W5 put out if it was designed along similar principles.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think I would have preferred, if one was going to put out a W5 product with similar design principles as V5 or H5, I would have liked to see the designers fully commit to a redesign of the setting to fit their principles.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying that I would have preferred that product over legacy or that there wouldn\u2019t still be controversy and debate, but at least in that case there would be a way to contrast the old and new materials against one another and see what one prefers. There are plenty of problems with the old material, problems that a lot of people acknowledge. Even just seeing ways that one might go about resolving the old material\u2019s issues would have been interesting and in some cases might have seen certain ideas back-ported into legacy. For instance I know that if this hypothetical W5 had fully committed to a redesign of the setting and had included elements such as the Sambrano rework of Older Brother, Middle Brother, &amp; Younger Brother; I probably would have back ported those things into my legacy settings, even if nothing else, and I don\u2019t think I would have been the only one either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T16:54:11-08:00","id":1526950,"title":"","content":"I'm probably the absolute worst person in the world to do a review of W5 because everyone knows that my W:TA experience is heavily V:TM inspired. It leaks over between my fandom and my takes aren't what most people think of when they talk about the game. I emphasize the personal horror element much more that was still a thing when I bought my first Werewolf supplement that emphasized creepy houses and werewolves investigating evil toys. It also strongly played up the Garou Nation being divided and probably unable to successfully complete their mission due to the sins of the past and old grudges.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/image/jpeg;base64,\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/image/jpeg;base64,&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> When I heard about the premise of W5, I should share that I DIDNT HATE IT. I actually think ending the Apocalypse was a possibly bold and interesting direction to take the line. So much of the game is basically, &quot;The End of the World is Nigh! Get those Banes!&quot; that the idea of what Garou would have to do when the war was over was an intriguing possibility. I admit the Forsaken influence was expected but I was hoping they'd go with the idea of existentialism.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Apocalypse is over and now we have to figure out what to do with our lives.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead, the game just feels CONFUSED about what it's trying to achieve. I understand the changing terminology (Metis, Wendigo, and so on), I understand the getting rid of Lupus, and I understand trying to get rid of the racial superiority angle. W:TA has always had a problem with Nazi fans and this was told to me by Ethan Skemp way back when. It's why they purged the Swords and got rid of Pure Breed as a concept. Even though the joke was that the most Pure Bred werewolves were the most inbred and insane.<br /> <br /> But it all feels like half-measures and the thing still goes, &quot;It's no longer the way it used to be....except we're going to allude to being EXACTLY the same way it was.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T17:32:42-08:00","id":1526952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526939#post1526939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was already pretty easy to imagine from the history of V5\u2019s development that a significant contingent of the legacy fan base was going to take umbrage with what W5 put out if it was designed along similar principles.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think I would have preferred, if one was going to put out a W5 product with similar design principles as V5 or H5, I would have liked to see the designers fully commit to a redesign of the setting to fit their principles.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying that I would have preferred that product over legacy or that there wouldn\u2019t still be controversy and debate, but at least in that case there would be a way to contrast the old and new materials against one another and see what one prefers. There are plenty of problems with the old material, problems that a lot of people acknowledge. Even just seeing ways that one might go about resolving the old material\u2019s issues would have been interesting and in some cases might have seen certain ideas back-ported into legacy. For instance I know that if this hypothetical W5 had fully committed to a redesign of the setting and had included elements such as the Sambrano rework of Older Brother, Middle Brother, &amp; Younger Brother; I probably would have back ported those things into my legacy settings, even if nothing else, and I don\u2019t think I would have been the only one either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably fair to say that the vast majority of WtA players and storytellers had already fixed most if not all of the issues in their own games, almost every ST I know online and in RL has, for example, been using Warborn or Crinosborn for literally decades and Younger Brothers Patron has been swapped out for Angklut or Glooskap or, more often, <b>Amaroq. </b><br /> <br /> I think its also often forgotten that a whole bunch of other relatively minor issues were fixed in Revised but then those fixes were rolled back in 20th or others introduced in an effort to make it Metaplot agnostic, I think this was a major mistake as it punted a lot of lore back to early 2nd Ed which was pretty rough even at the time.....glares at Thrall of the Wyrm and resurrecting the SoH.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T18:28:03-08:00","id":1526956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526952#post1526952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its also often forgotten that a whole bunch of other relatively minor issues were fixed in Revised but then those fixes were rolled back in 20th or others introduced in an effort to make it Metaplot agnostic, I think this was a major mistake as it punted a lot of lore back to early 2nd Ed which was pretty rough even at the time.....glares at Thrall of the Wyrm and resurrecting the SoH.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't mind the Sword of Heimdall existing. Just, you know, as the cut-and-dry <i>antagonists</i> they should be. It's an obvious way to square the circle of having a problematic aspect of a player character faction.<br /> <br /> Revised wanted to just get rid of them. W20 wanted to bring them back as-is. And W5 made the entire Get of Fenris into Swords of Heimdall.<br /> <br /> Which, of the three, was clearly the worst option. We don't need ALL the werewolf vikings in the game to be fascists. This isn't Warhammer 40K, and the Get of Fenris aren't the Space Wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T18:55:11-08:00","id":1526958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526956#post1526956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I don't mind the Sword of Heimdall existing. Just, you know, as the cut-and-dry <i>antagonists</i> they should be. It's an obvious way to square the circle of having a problematic aspect of a player character faction.<br /> <br /> Revised wanted to just get rid of them. W20 wanted to bring them back as-is. And W5 made the entire Get of Fenris into Swords of Heimdall.<br /> <br /> Which, of the three, was clearly the worst option. We don't need ALL the werewolf vikings in the game to be fascists. This isn't Warhammer 40K, and the Get of Fenris aren't the Space Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't even &quot;werewolf vikings&quot; to begin with, since they were a counter-mythological point to the figures that the people grouped into &quot;vikings&quot; revered. To the vikings, they were the devil, but in W:tA, that kind of thing is good (see also: Black Furies being opposed to a lot of Greek mythological figures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T22:15:07-08:00","id":1526966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526956#post1526956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I don't mind the Sword of Heimdall existing. Just, you know, as the cut-and-dry <i>antagonists</i> they should be. It's an obvious way to square the circle of having a problematic aspect of a player character faction.<br /> <br /> Revised wanted to just get rid of them. W20 wanted to bring them back as-is. And W5 made the entire Get of Fenris into Swords of Heimdall.<br /> <br /> Which, of the three, was clearly the worst option. We don't need ALL the werewolf vikings in the game to be fascists. This isn't Warhammer 40K, and the Get of Fenris aren't the Space Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand that was the INTENT with the Sword of Heimdall when they were introduced in the first place. However, what happened was that a bunch of racist players ended up showing up to LARPs as part of them and doing the racism as part of their characters.<br /> <br /> So that's why they killed them off in Revised.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the same thing that happened with the Kuei Jin. Racist players used them as an excuse to be racist against Asian gamers and try to force them to play them instead of, say, Tremere.<br /> <br /> A Hong Kong friend of mine who plays V:TM basically said, &quot;No one plays Kindred of the East here. They sign up to play Tremere and Ventrue in Hong Kong.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T01:03:25-08:00","id":1526969,"title":"","content":"The difference between SoH+Kuei-Jin and Cult of Fenris in W5 is that both SoH and Kuei-Jin were intended to add to the setting. Especially Kuei-Jin, since they were a depiction of non-european vampires.<br /> <br /> Cult of Fenris are not made to enrich the setting, they are clearly intended to take away from it. CoF exists to guilt trip the garou from dedicating their life to the war. As well as serving as a villain faction that is clearly meant to replace the BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T02:05:39-08:00","id":1526970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526969#post1526969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between SoH+Kuei-Jin and Cult of Fenris in W5 is that both SoH and Kuei-Jin were intended to add to the setting. Especially Kuei-Jin, since they were a depiction of non-european vampires.<br /> <br /> Cult of Fenris are not made to enrich the setting, they are clearly intended to take away from it. CoF exists to guilt trip the garou from dedicating their life to the war. As well as serving as a villain faction that is clearly meant to replace the BSDs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it wrong that I think it's meant to just provide the Pure equivalent for the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> The weird thing is how LOCALIZED it is for me. If they'd gone full FORSAKEN then it would make a certain amount of sense. Albretch's reforms don't take (maybe he's assassinated, maybe he's just failed) and an extremist group of Garou are created of the worst Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Get, and Red Talons that exist. The guys who are the worst stereotypes of the bigoted, racist, pure blood obsessed, War of Rage and Impergium were great ideas assholes of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Say, 30% of those tribes.<br /> <br /> There, you have a villain faction and it fits the lore just fine. It also isn't just, &quot;Norse Tribe = Bad.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T02:58:31-08:00","id":1526973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526970#post1526970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it wrong that I think it's meant to just provide the Pure equivalent for the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> The weird thing is how LOCALIZED it is for me. If they'd gone full FORSAKEN then it would make a certain amount of sense. Albretch's reforms don't take (maybe he's assassinated, maybe he's just failed) and an extremist group of Garou are created of the worst Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Get, and Red Talons that exist. The guys who are the worst stereotypes of the bigoted, racist, pure blood obsessed, War of Rage and Impergium were great ideas assholes of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Say, 30% of those tribes.<br /> <br /> There, you have a villain faction and it fits the lore just fine. It also isn't just, &quot;Norse Tribe = Bad.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> It's a very compelling image, really. A certain percentage - maybe even not that big - of multiple Tribes who cannot face the reality of Garou failures, past and present. Cannot accept the complexity of the modern world and in the modern Tribes. Cannot accept the Garou are losing because they screwed the pooch in multiple ways (destroying other Fera, the Impergium, leaving the White Howlers to go it alone, etc). In short, they cannot accept that the Garou need to change.<br /> <br /> Instead, they cling to a simplistic, false version of reality. Where the Garou cannot work together because of &quot;degenerate&quot; ideas and behaviors &quot;infecting&quot; the Tribes. That the strangling of the world isn't a result of systemic issues, but that humans are just innately horrible and poisonous to the environment. That Garou are losing because they've been &quot;stabbed in the back&quot; by...whomever the reactionaries see fit to blame for their problems. That everything would be better if both humans and Garou at large would simply bow to &quot;their betters&quot; (read: the fascist Garou). That they don't need to change or learn anything, because they already feel in their hearts what &quot;the truth&quot; is. And that anyone who insists otherwise - anyone who disagrees or wants to stop and think - is a traitor.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Black Spiral Dancers, who have embraced the Wyrm out of despair, this alliance of Garou Fascists embrace lies, told by and to themselves, out of fear, pride, and self-interest. And they'll react violently and cravenly to defend their flattened model of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> (It also neatly allows the Red Talons to start accepting Homid members. The most vehemently anti-Homid members of the Tribe have joined the Fascist Garou. And everyone left behind, by definition, are moderates or progressives.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T04:24:49-08:00","id":1526977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526966#post1526966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand that was the INTENT with the Sword of Heimdall when they were introduced in the first place. However, what happened was that a bunch of racist players ended up showing up to LARPs as part of them and doing the racism as part of their characters.<br /> <br /> So that's why they killed them off in Revised.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the same thing that happened with the Kuei Jin. Racist players used them as an excuse to be racist against Asian gamers and try to force them to play them instead of, say, Tremere.<br /> <br /> A Hong Kong friend of mine who plays V:TM basically said, &quot;No one plays Kindred of the East here. They sign up to play Tremere and Ventrue in Hong Kong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What's Larps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T05:54:48-08:00","id":1526979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526966#post1526966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand that was the INTENT with the Sword of Heimdall when they were introduced in the first place. However, what happened was that a bunch of racist players ended up showing up to LARPs as part of them and doing the racism as part of their characters.<br /> <br /> So that's why they killed them off in Revised.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the same thing that happened with the Kuei Jin. Racist players used them as an excuse to be racist against Asian gamers and try to force them to play them instead of, say, Tremere.<br /> <br /> A Hong Kong friend of mine who plays V:TM basically said, &quot;No one plays Kindred of the East here. They sign up to play Tremere and Ventrue in Hong Kong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What always confuses me about this anecdote is the idea of players just &quot; showing up&quot; to LARPs without having themselves and their characters fully vetted beforehand......your just asking for creepers, arseholes and assaults if you don't do basic screening.<br /> <br /> Hell, I had to bounce enough folks from LARPs back in the 90s that did practice thorough vetting......running one without would be horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T07:36:45-08:00","id":1526981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526970#post1526970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it wrong that I think it's meant to just provide the Pure equivalent for the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> The weird thing is how LOCALIZED it is for me. If they'd gone full FORSAKEN then it would make a certain amount of sense. Albretch's reforms don't take (maybe he's assassinated, maybe he's just failed) and an extremist group of Garou are created of the worst Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Get, and Red Talons that exist. The guys who are the worst stereotypes of the bigoted, racist, pure blood obsessed, War of Rage and Impergium were great ideas assholes of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Say, 30% of those tribes.<br /> <br /> There, you have a villain faction and it fits the lore just fine. It also isn't just, &quot;Norse Tribe = Bad.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSCGoefBO7Q\" data-code=\"DSCGoefBO7Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DSCGoefBO7Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I think that they were grinding an axe about the Get AND trying to copy the Pure, because they copied so much else from Forsaken that they might as well do that, too. Also, because it can't really be over-emphasized, all Garou end up turning into &quot;the Pure&quot; in this case if they get to Hauglosk 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T09:39:05-08:00","id":1526982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526979#post1526979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What always confuses me about this anecdote is the idea of players just &quot; showing up&quot; to LARPs without having themselves and their characters fully vetted beforehand......your just asking for creepers, arseholes and assaults if you don't do basic screening.<br /> <br /> Hell, I had to bounce enough folks from LARPs back in the 90s that did practice thorough vetting......running one without would be horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's incredibly well-run efficient LARPS and &quot;put up a notice to invite guys and gals over.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T10:59:29-08:00","id":1526988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526982#post1526982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's incredibly well-run efficient LARPS and &quot;put up a notice to invite guys and gals over.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I shudder to think how often the cops need to roll up on the second type......Vampire LARPs without <u>very</u> strict boundaries on behaviour would be very, very uncomfortable for anyone who had normal levels of bodily autonomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T11:08:25-08:00","id":1526989,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART FIVE</span><br /> <br /> Character Generation Part Two<br /> <br /> One Background that has returned is Totem, now renamed Spirit Pact. So far, there is not much that goes into this BG. Since there are no rules for communal traits, all such Pacts are with one Garou, not an entire pack, thus limiting the strength of this BG. Basically, this allows a Garou to have spirit around to help out. It doesn't provide any Boons, like those of the Tribe Patrons, but they don't have Bans either, unless one purchases a Flaw to do so. The Fetish BG has also returned, now renamed Talisman, which was already a Mage term for something slightly different that isn't harboring a spirit. No example was provided of how to rank Talismans, although a later section offers suggestions on how to do so. Seriously, there should have been more text given to this. How one ranks a BG if there aren't any examples nearby?<br /> <br /> Finally, Renown is still around, but in an altered form. Instead of being tied to Auspice and Rank, each type of Renown is tied to a Tribe. Rank &quot;technically&quot; no longer exists, even though the game is built around the disparity between elders and the current generations. How does one define these things if Rank is no longer a thing? While there are no longer lengthy charts detailing how almost every type of act can affect Renown, there is no replacement to determine it. It is just guess-work, and circular logic could lead one down multiple routes in determine what new Renown will be. Now, Renown is directly tied to Gifts, without the interference of Rank in the way. I'll explain this in more detail when I get to Gifts, but the process is a lot more complicated than what it used to be. (The Rules chapter also adds that Renown can be used to determine social rankings, but doesn't provide full context on how and why.)<br /> <br /> The remaining points of Character Generation in W5 are unique to the new edition, and they will not be covered here. Check earlier Phases of this Review for information.<br /> <br /> Rules and Systems<br /> <br /> Most of the rules for rolls are close enough to the old rules , save for the lack of numbers on dice. I need to mention that there is a homage to the classic Jonas vs. Mari fight from the older editions sprawled across the first part of the chapter on rules. Nothing is provided about the original influence, which is the fair thing to do when an artist is doing an homage. It also doesn't help that one of the pieces of art appears to be out of order, as well as some images may have been 'flipped' from their original orientation. <br /> <br /> Some portions have been cut out, with many others included in a supplement that I mentioned previously that had an incorrect web address. There are no longer specific rules for dealing with certain types of damage, such as poisons, drugs, or more exotic sources such as radiation. As biological beings, such sources have repercussions, and they needed to be mentioned. <br /> <br /> The main type of roll is the Rage roll. All other types of rolls from previous editions have pretty much been condensed into this type, save those dealing with WP. Depending upon how much Rage a Garou has, that many dice replace regular dice in a roll. This can lead to what is known as 'Brutal' results upon failure. Garou also use Rage to regenerate, shapeshift, or to use Gifts. While using just one power source for multiple things makes the game easier, the economy does not. Even if not spent, Rage can be lost so fast, that the game is almost rigged to suggest that playing as a normal human might be the best option.<br /> <br /> The five forms of a Garou are still here, but with major changes. Homid and Lupus can handle silver without damage, but they cannot regenerate. Only the three 'supernatural' forms can do that. The Glabro is still just slightly bigger, but most people are still afraid of it. Crinos is still big, but one can only maintain this form for a short length of time, unless they try to kill something. Upon leaving this form, Rage drops to 1, or 0 if it ends in a frenzy. Hispo is misdescribed as a really, really, big dog, instead of what the form used to be, but then Lupus is presumed to dog-sized, neither of which is entirely accurate.<br /> <br /> The final rules are mostly about the new Harano and Hauglosk mechanics. While they are extremes, one can suffer from both at the same time. To be honest, I really can't see how to incorporate both into the same setting in a single character. Maybe one or the other, but not both. In fact, Hauglosk almost seems to be beneficial in certain regards. Delirium is also brought up, but without the fine delegation of effects that is used to have, even though Willpower is a more direct track of comparison than it used to be. What is't included are other systems for things such as Aging or Battle Scars (which doesn't seem to be a problem with regenerating any more). Since this is a new game, I guess they didn't think anyone needed such time-progressive systems. Or maybe the developers didn't think anyone would stay with the game long enough for this to become important.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T12:13:16-08:00","id":1526990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526989#post1526989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hispo is misdescribed as a really, really, big dog, instead of what the form used to be, but then Lupus is presumed to dog-sized, neither of which is entirely accurate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason I can think of why this is a thing is to avoid Veil Breaches while running in hispo or lupus in a city. Since the Veil no longer has to be kept, I assume the doggy forms are to ensure werewolves stay a secret.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, in Legacy, I could buy some high purebreed garou being mistaken for dogs. But W5 has no goofy coat colours to justify it.<br /> <br /> This might be a small nitpick in a sea of bedbugs, but making lupus and hispo dog-like bothers me in terms of themes. The game is called wereWOLF the apocalypse and wolves are still a divisive species. That is why Red Talons as a tribe exist, humanity has hunted wolves to near extinction and the Talons want to get even. If garou can be born to wolfdogs or even pariah dogs, it erases so much of the horror a wolf-born PC faces.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that even your basic grey wolf is so big that people would call animal control, or that a large loose dog draws attention in most places. A large loose wolf-like dog with no collar or leash would get people chasing after it for no other reason than to get it to safety.<br /> <br /> The above is all just the lupus form, imagine what a pony-sized canine with gnashing jaws would cause?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T12:37:15-08:00","id":1526991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526988#post1526988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I shudder to think how often the cops need to roll up on the second type......Vampire LARPs without <u>very</u> strict boundaries on behaviour would be very, very uncomfortable for anyone who had normal levels of bodily autonomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, that was a thing for a long time.<br /> <br /> AKA V:TM Larps being sometimes known as &quot;Sexual Harrassment: The RPG.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T13:49:49-08:00","id":1526998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526989#post1526989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Background that has returned is Totem, now renamed Spirit Pact. So far, there is not much that goes into this BG. Since there are no rules for communal traits, all such Pacts are with one Garou, not an entire pack, thus limiting the strength of this BG. Basically, this allows a Garou to have spirit around to help out. It doesn't provide any Boons, like those of the Tribe Patrons, but they don't have Bans either, unless one purchases a Flaw to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is still a Rite for getting a spirit to become a Pack-Patron-Spirit but the Rite reduces the choice to it having to be one of the Tribe-Patron-Spirit. And I think the main-reason for that they didn't bother to figure out any underlying framework to answer the question of how to represent Spirit-Allies or Pack-Patron-Spirits in terms of dots or in general. As anatgonists or allies they can just present these stat-blocks which are these lists of abilities with dice-pools but transforming that into dots of a Background or a Pack-Patron-Spirit takes a bit more work - which wasn't done in the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526989#post1526989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, Renown is still around, but in an altered form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, I would mention that now both Chagrin (the name for reducing Renown for doing something unworthy) and recognizing a Renown-worthy deed for the sake of whether Renown can be advanced with XP is all now firmly in the hands of the ST. The social component of things like Moots or a Galliard having to turn it into a tale isn't central to this anymore. How it's presented in the W5 corebook it's all just the ST making judgment-calls. So rather than social Garou-events being the pivot-points, W5 is now fine with Renown (advancing or being recognized to have done something shameful) just happening on the ST-player-level. I don't think it's intentional but more or less just a victim of avoiding lore/worldbuilding and once again just presenting a system that is entirely reliant on the ST's ability to make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526989#post1526989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While using just one power source for multiple things makes the game easier, the economy does not. Even if not spent, Rage can be lost so fast, that the game is almost rigged to suggest that playing as a normal human might be the best option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the system will help you the most if you stick to high Rage and consistently go for a brutal/violent approach. Also starting arguments with NPCs whenever you can also helps.<br /> <br /> But the system can get quite swingy if a player is unlucky. And there are some ways around it. You can take a Harano-dot to immediately go to Rage 5. You can enter Crinos and voluntarily enter Frenzy... You look at those Rage-pools of your players... Abstractly it's pretty easy: High Rage for combat, low Rage for social scenes.<br /> <br /> The first issue is the imbalance of what threats a Garou-PC can handle. There's a vast gulf between what you can throw at a PC with 1 or 2 Rage and one with 3, 4 or 5 Rage. You only need to look at the NPCs at the end of scenarios like Deepest Of Wounds and No Matter How Small. Huge dice-pools get thrown around. And since the Crinos-Form is in the mix... why not? But in W5 there are times when PCs <i>can't</i> use their Crinos-Form. And if the PC &quot;lost their wolf&quot; and lost access to their supernatural forms entirely, they can't use a lot of Gifts either.<br /> <br /> Another issue is what narratively happens. It's modeled after Hunger but the dynamic is easy to grasp in that case. The higher it gets, the worse for the vampire and since it's all related to bloodthirst and the Beast there are easy ways to understand what's going on when Hunger is rising in terms of dots. But the way Rage is structured both high <i>and </i>low Rage are bad. And the low-Rage-dynamic is essentially &quot;the Hulk who isn't angry enough to transform&quot;. The point of Rage is that it's supposed to be that you can't control your anger. It isn't about how you sometimes run out of anger at inopportune times. It's also why the Hulk feels like a curse to Bruce Banner (well, depending on the version and who writes him, of course...). What is a scene about that says &quot;I would like to do something but looking at my Rage-pool, my character doesn't have enough Rage to do something.&quot;? In a way that's a moment where the player feels more rage than the player-character.<br /> <br /> I think one problem in the conception of Rage in W5 is that it missed an important detail: Hunger is about thirst. Hunger is entirely about acquiring a resource external to yourself. Anyone can understand being thirsty is about and how to relieve it. But Rage? It's something inherent to Garou, it's something that comes from within and yet... it's treated like a resource that requires action to acquire. Rage should be at 0 because your character exhausted themselves, did all they could, can do no more - and not because the player was unlucky with some dice-rolls. What one worries about gaining too much Rage too quickly and losing control. Why would you make it a bit to worry about not having enough Rage? Losing the wolf is a stumbling-block, nothing more. I mean, what does W5 want you to do with a PC who has &quot;lost the wolf&quot; except just grounding their ass until they can howl at the moon...? What is supposed to happen in this time-frame where this PC has &quot;lost the wolf&quot;...? What is the point of making a PC go through that? That aspect feels like a waste of time.<br /> <br /> Also, making PCs &quot;gather Rage&quot; gets old pretty fast.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The final rules are mostly about the new Harano and Hauglosk mechanics. While they are extremes, one can suffer from both at the same time. To be honest, I really can't see how to incorporate both into the same setting in a single character. Maybe one or the other, but not both. In fact, Hauglosk almost seems to be beneficial in certain regards. </div> </div> </div>I think Hauglosk in the W5 corebook is the way it is because it's the remnants of Karim Muammar's vision of &quot;Fenrir=Nazis&quot; and linked concepts like Hauglosk. They were able to reach a compromise unlike in the Hunters Entertainmant version - but you can see just how nearly immovable Karim's position on the idea has been in the way Hauglosk doesn't make sense. But we've heard from what James F. Sambrano shared with the public that for Karim Muammar the conflict with the Fenrir is <i>the essence </i>of W5. And it doesn't seem like he treated this like a point that was up for discussion on the writing-team during the Hunters-Entertainment-version at least. Can't imagine that attitude changed much when they switched over to the in-house-team. What we got in the eventual book is the compromise with an extremist position. The Fenrir aren't outright Nazis but that was the starting-point and then they just toned down a couple of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T15:10:35-08:00","id":1527003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1526998#post1526998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Hauglosk in the W5 corebook is the way it is because it's the remnants of Karim Muammar's vision of &quot;Fenrir=Nazis&quot; and linked concepts like Hauglosk. They were able to reach a compromise unlike in the Hunters Entertainmant version - but you can see just how nearly immovable Karim's position on the idea has been in the way Hauglosk doesn't make sense. But we've heard from what James F. Sambrano shared with the public that for Karim Muammar the conflict with the Fenrir is <i>the essence </i>of W5. And it doesn't seem like he treated this like a point that was up for discussion on the writing-team during the Hunters-Entertainment-version at least. Can't imagine that attitude changed much when they switched over to the in-house-team. What we got in the eventual book is the compromise with an extremist position. The Fenrir aren't outright Nazis but that was the starting-point and then they just toned down a couple of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing?<br /> <br /> I actually understand where Muammar is coming from. I mean, I think he handled it in the worst possible way imaginable but I also can follow his train of thought unlike most executives.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Divorcing the Garou from Human Culture</b><br /> <br /> There's a good financial reason for wanting to have a universalist system out there and it's the same reason that they got rid of the Kuei Jin. Suddenly, you have a literal entirely new species to represent Asian people. This way, there's 12 Tribes to draw from no matter where you are in the world.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Nazis are good punching bags</b><br /> <br /> We live in a time of Right Wing ascendency and W:TA has always been a vehicle for expressing anger at a world gone horribly wrong by late stage capitalism, fascism, and authoritarianism. Having political relevancy is hardly a bad thing.<br /> <br /> One of my book series is all about the fun to be had in slaughtering the Hydra equivalent that superheroes massacre left and right in the Supervillainy Saga.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The treatment of Native Peoples in Werewolf has always been cringe</b><br /> <br /> The [Blank] guys were never handled particularly well. In addition to the use of the taboo name and as another type of werewolf, there's the fact that they were always treated as essentially dismissively in their anger over Indiginous oppression. But it goes beyond that, there's also the fact that the gameline really did throw them all together in a blender that basically was always going to be greatly disrespectful.<br /> <br /> The Bunyip for example is a particularly notable one given their place in the Garou Nation as a tribe wholly wiped out and forgotten with their culture as well as spiritual connection to the land severed to their great shame.<br /> ...<br /> Except there's a million aborigines in the world right now and they make up 4% of Australia's total population. Twice more than those in America and that's stretching numbers. They're not GONE and neither is their culture (despite many attempts).<br /> <br /> The problem seems to be that Muammar seems to have two major issues:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Get are really fucking popular among people who hate Nazis</b><br /> <br /> A huge chunk of gamers in Europe and America who absolutely fucking hate Nazis love the Get because they're awesome Klingons and werewolf Vikings that are great concepts regardless of white supremacy.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The issue was over and done with</b><br /> <br /> It was settled twenty fucking years ago and decisively so in a way that most people were fine with. This is like raising the issue of slaughtering orc babies in Dungeons and Dragons and setting it as the PRIMARY focus of 6th edition.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Native Erasure is kind of a shit solution to the problem of cringe</b><br /> <br /> As someone said about removing the Native woman off the Butter jars but leaving the landscape, &quot;they took the land but got rid of the native.&quot; The general take I've heard from W:TA has always been, &quot;The representation isn't great but bad representation is usually better than no representation.&quot;<br /> It's also NOT A HARD THING TO DO to keep it.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: &quot;Gale Stalkers and Ghost Council have very strong camps related to Native Americans in the United States and numerous other indigineous people. They are heavily involved with their mortal relations and the issue of Native rights.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> There, done. Make them a camp if you're going universalist for the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T15:52:09-08:00","id":1527009,"title":"","content":"<b>4. If you want faction X to be bad, you can't have faction Y be worse and still good.</b><br /> This, if nothing else, hints at how there was very little consideration of the whole in W5. CoF are the fascist bad guys and definitions of extremism and are clearly meant to be the main bad guys, yet BSDs are not at all changed and are stated to be foes as well. Yet THEY are allowed to be redeemed where CoF are not.<br /> <br /> But more important, Red Talons are now much worse than they were in Legacy and munch humans even if they no longer are historically only wolf-born. Yet, you can still play a Red Talon cannibal with zero Hauglosk point, while a CoF member who would never do that is considered irredeemable.<br /> <br /> It doesn't do a good job of creating a cohesive world, if allowed player characters are clearly worse than the stated bad guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T15:53:24-08:00","id":1527010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527003#post1527003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing?<br /> <br /> I actually understand where Muammar is coming from. I mean, I think he handled it in the worst possible way imaginable but I also can follow his train of thought unlike most executives.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Divorcing the Garou from Human Culture</b><br /> <br /> There's a good financial reason for wanting to have a universalist system out there and it's the same reason that they got rid of the Kuei Jin. Suddenly, you have a literal entirely new species to represent Asian people. This way, there's 12 Tribes to draw from no matter where you are in the world.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Nazis are good punching bags</b><br /> <br /> We live in a time of Right Wing ascendency and W:TA has always been a vehicle for expressing anger at a world gone horribly wrong by late stage capitalism, fascism, and authoritarianism. Having political relevancy is hardly a bad thing.<br /> <br /> One of my book series is all about the fun to be had in slaughtering the Hydra equivalent that superheroes massacre left and right in the Supervillainy Saga.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The treatment of Native Peoples in Werewolf has always been cringe</b><br /> <br /> The [Blank] guys were never handled particularly well. In addition to the use of the taboo name and as another type of werewolf, there's the fact that they were always treated as essentially dismissively in their anger over Indiginous oppression. But it goes beyond that, there's also the fact that the gameline really did throw them all together in a blender that basically was always going to be greatly disrespectful.<br /> <br /> The Bunyip for example is a particularly notable one given their place in the Garou Nation as a tribe wholly wiped out and forgotten with their culture as well as spiritual connection to the land severed to their great shame.<br /> ...<br /> Except there's a million aborigines in the world right now and they make up 4% of Australia's total population. Twice more than those in America and that's stretching numbers. They're not GONE and neither is their culture (despite many attempts).<br /> <br /> The problem seems to be that Muammar seems to have two major issues:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Get are really fucking popular among people who hate Nazis</b><br /> <br /> A huge chunk of gamers in Europe and America who absolutely fucking hate Nazis love the Get because they're awesome Klingons and werewolf Vikings that are great concepts regardless of white supremacy.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The issue was over and done with</b><br /> <br /> It was settled twenty fucking years ago and decisively so in a way that most people were fine with. This is like raising the issue of slaughtering orc babies in Dungeons and Dragons and setting it as the PRIMARY focus of 6th edition.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Native Erasure is kind of a shit solution to the problem of cringe</b><br /> <br /> As someone said about removing the Native woman off the Butter jars but leaving the landscape, &quot;they took the land but got rid of the native.&quot; The general take I've heard from W:TA has always been, &quot;The representation isn't great but bad representation is usually better than no representation.&quot;<br /> It's also NOT A HARD THING TO DO to keep it.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: &quot;Gale Stalkers and Ghost Council have very strong camps related to Native Americans in the United States and numerous other indigineous people. They are heavily involved with their mortal relations and the issue of Native rights.&quot;<br /> <br /> There, done. Make them a camp if you're going universalist for the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you've already put more thought into this than Karim Muammar did. For comparison, we also know that for him, for example, the Black Furies were &quot;the Feminist Tribe&quot;. And that's how the whole &quot;Black Furies need to change&quot;-thing started. The women-only-&quot;feminist-Tribe&quot; had to change because now everybody should be able to join any Tribe. They did the same thing for the Red Talons - except they could keep their anit-human, pro-wolf ideology... somehow.<br /> <br /> It's all twisted into knots when it comes to W5's design. And it's me just speculating but I think one big reason for these knots is that you had two very uncompromising visions for what W5 should be like with Karim Muammar and Justin Achilli. And the W5 corebook is the heap of a mess that was left behind after the dust cleared... or before the dust cleared in the case of Justin Achilli, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T16:30:28-08:00","id":1527011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527003#post1527003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing?<br /> <br /> I actually understand where Muammar is coming from. I mean, I think he handled it in the worst possible way imaginable but I also can follow his train of thought unlike most executives.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Divorcing the Garou from Human Culture</b><br /> <br /> There's a good financial reason for wanting to have a universalist system out there and it's the same reason that they got rid of the Kuei Jin. Suddenly, you have a literal entirely new species to represent Asian people. This way, there's 12 Tribes to draw from no matter where you are in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were already ways that this was being addressed in Revised and a usable model to have a much wider historical range as well. The former was in most tribebooks acknowledging that most tribes don't and never did just stick to one ethnic group*. The latter was in how the Shadow Lords were set up - there was a European and likely North African branch (the one that most people think of), a Central Asian branch, and an East Asian branch (what became the Hakken). Various legends of moon and sun-eating monsters could have done the same for the Get's historical range (though in both cases and for the larger body of the Garou, that is, again, historical - everyone, by the time of the Apocalypse, had spread out pretty far).<br /> <br /> (I say likely North Africa with Europe with the Lords because they did have some involvement in Rome and Spain, so hopping over probably wouldn't have been quite so much trouble for them. That's sort of reading into canon, though, so I can't necessarily cite it.)<br /> <br /> *The description of the Pure Breed background in Black Furies and Get of Fenris was anomalous; they're the only two tribes that actually associate European heritage with PB ratings. Not even the Silver Fangs or Winter's Teeth (you know who I mean) did this, and the latter are explicitly descended at least in part from Native people of Turtle Island. Yet, their PB involves violet eyes, silver-tinged white fur that self-cleans, and an aurora-like battle aura. Yes, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T16:56:08-08:00","id":1527013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527009#post1527009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>4. If you want faction X to be bad, you can't have faction Y be worse and still good.</b><br /> This, if nothing else, hints at how there was very little consideration of the whole in W5. CoF are the fascist bad guys and definitions of extremism and are clearly meant to be the main bad guys, yet BSDs are not at all changed and are stated to be foes as well. Yet THEY are allowed to be redeemed where CoF are not.<br /> <br /> But more important, Red Talons are now much worse than they were in Legacy and munch humans even if they no longer are historically only wolf-born. Yet, you can still play a Red Talon cannibal with zero Hauglosk point, while a CoF member who would never do that is considered irredeemable.<br /> <br /> It doesn't do a good job of creating a cohesive world, if allowed player characters are clearly worse than the stated bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, the Pure were fine.<br /> <br /> It was a funny joke in Forsaken. &quot;All of the stereotypes about the Old Garou are the villains.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension also did it fine. The Technocracy vs. The Traditions vs. The Nephandi.<br /> <br /> (I'm of the mind Technocracy apologia has aged like cheese)<br /> <br /> So there's nothing wrong with the Good (Garou), the Bad (Fenris), and the Evil (BSD)<br /> <br /> But the problem is that they went way too far by making the Get into full-blown white supremacists. They could have gone with any number of fake supernatural prejudices and it worked much better like, &quot;We won't tolerate people who aren't of our ridiculous pure breed fundamentalist Gaian terrorist doctrine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T18:40:01-08:00","id":1527024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527013#post1527013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, the Pure were fine.<br /> <br /> It was a funny joke in Forsaken. &quot;All of the stereotypes about the Old Garou are the villains.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension also did it fine. The Technocracy vs. The Traditions vs. The Nephandi.<br /> <br /> (I'm of the mind Technocracy apologia has aged like cheese)<br /> <br /> So there's nothing wrong with the Good (Garou), the Bad (Fenris), and the Evil (BSD)<br /> <br /> <b>But the problem is that they went way too far by making the Get into full-blown white supremacists.</b> They could have gone with any number of fake supernatural prejudices and it worked much better like, &quot;We won't tolerate people who aren't of our ridiculous pure breed fundamentalist Gaian terrorist doctrine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we've heard, that was Karim's plan from the start, so &quot;too far&quot; was the starting line, and we just kept running from there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T19:21:42-08:00","id":1527027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527024#post1527024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what we've heard, that was Karim's plan from the start, so &quot;too far&quot; was the starting line, and we just kept running from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get it, Nazi killing is fun.<br /> <br /> Fighting Right Wing/white supremacy is just as important as fighting ecological devastation for many people and the two are entwined.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying sometimes even the bad guys can be misappropriated as platforming vile ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T20:40:17-08:00","id":1527030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527013#post1527013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the problem is that they went way too far by making the Get into full-blown white supremacists. They could have gone with any number of fake supernatural prejudices and it worked much better like, &quot;We won't tolerate people who aren't of our ridiculous pure breed fundamentalist Gaian terrorist doctrine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What what little has been leaked from writers, it sounds like that was the goal. The lead developer did not like the Get of Fenris and from the outset, wanted to turn them into the new villain faction, one as bad (or even worse) than the Black Spiral Dancers. There were a lot of other options that could have been done, but it sounds like the developer liked this idea the most because it would best place the Get of Fenris in the position where he wanted them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T21:52:37-08:00","id":1527034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527027#post1527027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I get it, Nazi killing is fun.<br /> <br /> Fighting Right Wing/white supremacy is just as important as fighting ecological devastation for many people and the two are entwined.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying sometimes even the bad guys can be misappropriated as platforming vile ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean that he has some kind of thing about the Get where he feels that they need to be punished for being written badly, in spite of being fictional characters that are only what they are written as. So, just think of Lashet's posts about hating the Garou, and apply it as what the head creative editor of the present WoD thinks about the Garou in general but the GoF in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T22:11:21-08:00","id":1527035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527013#post1527013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's nothing wrong with the Good (Garou), the Bad (Fenris), and the Evil (BSD)</div> </div> </div> </div>But that isn't how it is actually set up, which in addition to the fascism, creates even worse problems.<br /> <br /> For one, Red Talons do worse things than the CoF. They openly eat people, want humanity dead and in a move that is baffling indeed; Support the prison system. Yet, you can play a Red Talon, but you cannot a CoF member. They aren't even suffering from Hauglosk OR Harano, the Talons do what they do with clear heads. Yet these guys are seen as fine PC material.<br /> <br /> Second, becoming a fascist in W5 is a mechanic, one that has no way back from and that can happen to anyone.<br /> <br /> Third, despite the written actions of the CoF in the core being far less drastic than what the Talons do and what BSDs do, the CoF are the ones that are irredeemable.<br /> <br /> So it isn't like with the Pure, where the worst parts of WtA were made into bad guys and the Pure very much ARE worse than the Forsaken. The writing of W5 says CoF are the worst, but not only does it make the 'worse' into a mental illness, but there are more accepted groups that do worse.<br /> <br /> Which to me hints that making the CoF the worst was done separately from the writing of other tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T22:31:11-08:00","id":1527036,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. You've convinced me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T00:52:54-08:00","id":1527041,"title":"","content":"Something which does worry me is the absence of a valid counter narrative to fascist cof. Irl pretty much all ideologies have an articulated defence (even ones I hate)against fascism and proposals going forward . The garou in w5 less so and the cult ultimately win the ideological arguement by being the ones to present an arguement while everyone else just stays at home and guards the caern.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the fact the cult are almost certainly way more proactive in waging war on pentex, banes and the spirals.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T05:18:39-08:00","id":1527046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527041#post1527041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which does worry me is the absence of a valid counter narrative to fascist cof. Irl pretty much all ideologies have an articulated defence (even ones I hate)against fascism and proposals going forward . The garou in w5 less so and the cult ultimately win the ideological arguement by being the ones to present an arguement while everyone else just stays at home and guards the caern.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the fact the cult are almost certainly way more proactive in waging war on pentex, banes and the spirals.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone ever feel like W5 is like a Russian nesting doll of bad choices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T06:06:19-08:00","id":1527047,"title":"","content":"While Haglusk is really weird since it's a form of insanity that makes you a demented fascist. It's supposed to be the consequence of extremism and taking amoral actions that turn you into a monster.<br /> <br /> However, there is absolutely no reason to gain Haglusk in game where the Tenets are set up in such a way to reinforce the themes of the Tribes. You could pretty much play even worse characters with the Tenets that support Red Talon Tribal themes and NEVER EVER gain Haglusk or be in risk for losing your character from it. Yet the CoF will still be the unsalvagable horrors.<br /> <br /> The whole way it's set up is just incredibly disjointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T06:15:20-08:00","id":1527049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527047#post1527047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, there is absolutely no reason to gain Haglusk in game where the Tenets are set up in such a way to reinforce the themes of the Tribes. You could pretty much play even worse characters with the Tenets that support Red Talon Tribal themes and NEVER EVER gain Haglusk or be in risk for losing your character from it. Yet the CoF will still be the unsalvagable horrors.<br /> <br /> The whole way it's set up is just incredibly disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I think there was very little communication or cross-referencing between Hauglosk+CoF and the other tribes. If the point is that being an extremist is bad, why keep the Red Talons?<br /> <br /> The goal was to villify the Fenrir, other tribes of brutality be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T07:28:00-08:00","id":1527051,"title":"","content":"One thing I thought about now is that there could be variations of the Hauglosk, like each tribe responds differently to the Hauglosk becoming the extreme that their tribe represents, like the Red Talons would go into total war mode against the Weaver, Glass Walkers would become the worst version of the Cyberdogs, BG would become very paranoid survivors, I don't know if it would be viable, but it could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T08:15:39-08:00","id":1527053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527051#post1527051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I thought about now is that there could be variations of the Hauglosk, like each tribe responds differently to the Hauglosk becoming the extreme that their tribe represents, like the Red Talons would go into total war mode against the Weaver, Glass Walkers would become the worst version of the Cyberdogs, BG would become very paranoid survivors, I don't know if it would be viable, but it could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was essentially how the early version of what became Hauglosk was written up by the Hunters Entertainment writers group. James has released a little of what he wrote for the Harano/ Ghrrna Tribal information. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T10:32:56-08:00","id":1527057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527053#post1527053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was essentially how the early version of what became Hauglosk was written up by the Hunters Entertainment writers group. James has released a little of what he wrote for the Harano/ Ghrrna Tribal information.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did he mention why it didn't make it into the final material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T10:40:11-08:00","id":1527058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527057#post1527057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did he mention why it didn't make it into the final material?</div> </div> </div> </div>The team got dumped and Paradox decided to make a new version of Werewolf in house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T15:50:02-08:00","id":1527069,"title":"","content":"For me the constricting part of Harano/Hauglosk is that you have to figure out what having dots in both means. I mentioned in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526394#post1526394\">other thread my personal solution</a> which is to redefine Hauglosk to be more about giving up fighting for a cause. In that paradigm, both Harano and Hauglosk are paths to giving up on being a Garou. But this also includes redefining how Chronicle Tenets work because as others have mentioned, that implicit link between Hauglosk and Chronicle Tenets gets no explanation whatsoever in the W5 corebook. The ST-section's bit on Chronicle Tenets is wholly unconnected to Hauglosk - even though they are mechanically closely tied to each other.<br /> <br /> If you were to just dump the whole framework of W5 there are a lot more options to figure out what a Humanity-equivalent from V5 could look like in W5. I think the only good thing to say about that is that it could've been worse: At least, W5 isn't as bad as H5.<br /> <br /> Now there's a system that's just bad: H5's Danger-Track, for example, is just an utter mess. A fine idea but the H5 corebook forgot the game-part and didn't give it any mechanics. I'm not joking about this. H5 has no mechanics for the Danger-Track - it's just vibes. The Danger-Track is whatever your ST tells you it is.<br /> <br /> That's the thing with H5 and W5: There isn't just this disdain for the lore/worldbuilding of previous editions but also this aversion to work with the system (as introduced by V5). Like, if you think the interaction between Hauglosk and Chronicle Tenets is awkwardly handled in W5... guess how H5 handled Chronicle Tenets...? Of course, it didn't. Chronicle Tenets are a waste of space in the H5 corebook with no relevance. Basic Session Zero stuff already covers the Chronicle Tenets stuff. The point of Chronicle Tenets was to mechanically integrate aspects of Session Zero into the game. The moment you remove that, the concept of Chronicle Tenets is pointless. But that's why I talk about disdain for the system... Both with H5 and W5 the creative move was often to just remove bits and pieces and replace them with nothing. Not change it or replace it but just remove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T12:45:36-08:00","id":1527089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527046#post1527046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone ever feel like W5 is like a Russian nesting doll of bad choices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah, the obvious question is why arnt the garou blowing up pipelines over first nation territory or launching campaigns of extermination against the spirals when the cult almost certainly are.<br /> <br /> it has some worrying implications irl where i find it increasingly difficult not to justing not engaging in at least industrial sabotage to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-19-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T16:44:38-08:00","id":1527094,"title":"","content":"Accelerationism is a good point of reference for that. The term comes up two times in the book (and it's interesting when it does):<ul><li>The Black Furies Tribe section (pg 61): &quot;At their most extreme, Black Furies can even become accelerationists, consumed by infinite campaigns of bloody vengeance. Why wait for the crypto farm to waste a small nation\u2019s GDP in energy costs when you can wreck the mining operation before a bunch of techbro choads can buy new Teslas? Fuck Tesla anyway, since most of the power for their \u201cgreen\u201d electrical cars comes from fossil fuels. And fuck you for doubting.&quot;</li> <li>The Black Spiral Dancers section (pg 277): &quot;What Do They Want: From the Black Spiral Dancer perspective, the Apocalypse is over, Gaia is dead, the Garou lost, and they are now simply nursing the corpse of their spirit-mother. The Wyrm has done its duty, and all that\u2019s left is for the remains to decay. In this respect, Black Spiral Dancers are perverse accelerationists trying to hasten the End of It All, so that the cosmological cycle can renew. Those Garou still loyal to Gaia are obstacles preventing the wheel from turning \u2014 and thus must those Garou be destroyed.\u200b&quot;</li> </ul>The basic idea of accelerationism is that things getting worse is a necessary stepstone to things getting better. Stuff like &quot;the night is darkest before the dawn&quot;. There are many variants of accelerationism because what does &quot;getting worse&quot; mean exactly (&quot;getting worse&quot; for who and how, to be more specific) and what is this &quot;better world&quot; that is envisioned here... For example, the <a href=\"https://gnet-research.org/2021/09/02/understanding-accelerationist-narratives-there-is-no-political-solution/\" target=\"_blank\">Christchurch-mass-shooter considered himself an &quot;accelerationist</a>.<br /> <br /> The irony is that by not delving too deep and trying to stay neutral somewhat, they made things more complicated actually. There is a broad spectrum of things like &quot;accelerationism&quot;. What W5 does is ignore the substance of the issue. They were so concerned about people thinking that capitalism is bad (despite invoking &quot;capitalocene era&quot; at the very beginning) that they had a whole sidebar trying to make clear that capitalist companies aren't inherently bad. But apparently, there was no concern for carelessly throwing around a term like &quot;accelerationism&quot;.<br /> <br /> And let's not forget that section at the end that invites the player to play around with Hauglosk by playing &quot;eco<i>fasicst</i> characters&quot;.<br /> <br /> What's also relevant here is how W5 is deemphasizing the Umbra. Where before you could take a lot of issues related to WtA into the realm of fantasy and allegory, now the game is pushing werewolf-PCs to be warriors for Gaia mainly in the real world. Also, the removal of Wyrm-Sense invites the idea of wrongful killings - in addition to the general lack of knowledge of PCs when it comes to the setting.<br /> <br /> W5 would've been better off choosing a particular political take on the WtA-setting... I don't think anybody on the political spectrum likes to see such political ideas being invoked while feigning such a surface-level political understanding. At the end of the day, politics is about communication and what this W5 corebook is doing is an example of bad communication. Terms are thrown around in a way that neither adds anything interesting nor reflects an interesting perspective from the writers on the subject.<br /> <br /> If anything, the W5 corebook is sure about one thing: What it isn't about. The book has made very clear what the writers disliked about the Garou - but the positive pitch for why you would want to play them is missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T17:44:42-08:00","id":1527100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527089#post1527089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much yeah, the obvious question is why arnt the garou blowing up pipelines over first nation territory or launching campaigns of extermination against the spirals when the cult almost certainly are.<br /> <br /> it has some worrying implications irl where i find it increasingly difficult not to justing not engaging in at least industrial sabotage to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that in W5 wants the PCs in a very specific narrative and wants to position them as &quot;punks&quot; who are trying to fix or oppose &quot;the Establishment.&quot; So there was an intentional design choice to make the Tribes and their leaderships fuckups so that the PCs can oppose them. Note that setting up Garou society and its leaders up as &quot;the Establishment&quot; (or at least part of it) that PCs are fighting against is a huge change from the earlier editions where &quot;the Establishment&quot; the PCs were opposing was the concept of modern industrial society in general (with more specific groups like Pentex serving as something the PCs could oppose directly).<br /> <br /> In W5, the Tribes got together, held a big moot, and decided not to go off crusading and fighting the Wyrm. The only group that did, the Fenrir, are presented as clear cut bad guys, even moreso than the Black Spirals. At the same time however, the game also reinforces this idea that the leadership of the Tribes is out of touch and wrong for allowing the Apocalypse to happen as well as for not fighting hard enough. So the PCs are in this weird narrative situation where, unlike the Tribes, you're supposed to fight the Wyrm, but also only on a part-time basis, rather than dedicating yourself to the fight like the Cult of Fenris.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's problematic that the Garou Tribes aren't doing the things you mention, but that was an intentional design choice. The Tribes and their leadership is supposed to come off as out-of-touch screwups, so that the punk-PCs get to rage at them for screwing everything up so badly while the Cult of Fenris serves as a warning for what happens if you take the fight too far in the other direction.<br /> <br /> I think it's a bizarre design choice, but it is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T18:41:56-08:00","id":1527101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527100#post1527100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's a bizarre design choice, but it is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not really bizarre at all, given that everyone at the top of the rpg department that PDX corporate probably doesn't care about hates W:tA. Sad, terrible, a waste, and numerous other things, yes, but within the context of a bunch of too edge Vampire mains who only cared about LARP being in charge of the entirety of the WoD, it makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T05:22:21-08:00","id":1527112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527100#post1527100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is that in W5 wants the PCs in a very specific narrative and wants to position them as &quot;punks&quot; who are trying to fix or oppose &quot;the Establishment.&quot; So there was an intentional design choice to make the Tribes and their leaderships fuckups so that the PCs can oppose them. Note that setting up Garou society and its leaders up as &quot;the Establishment&quot; (or at least part of it) that PCs are fighting against is a huge change from the earlier editions where &quot;the Establishment&quot; the PCs were opposing was the concept of modern industrial society in general (with more specific groups like Pentex serving as something the PCs could oppose directly).<br /> <br /> In W5, the Tribes got together, held a big moot, and decided not to go off crusading and fighting the Wyrm. The only group that did, the Fenrir, are presented as clear cut bad guys, even moreso than the Black Spirals. At the same time however, the game also reinforces this idea that the leadership of the Tribes is out of touch and wrong for allowing the Apocalypse to happen as well as for not fighting hard enough. So the PCs are in this weird narrative situation where, unlike the Tribes, you're supposed to fight the Wyrm, but also only on a part-time basis, rather than dedicating yourself to the fight like the Cult of Fenris.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's problematic that the Garou Tribes aren't doing the things you mention, but that was an intentional design choice. The Tribes and their leadership is supposed to come off as out-of-touch screwups, so that the punk-PCs get to rage at them for screwing everything up so badly while the Cult of Fenris serves as a warning for what happens if you take the fight too far in the other direction.<br /> <br /> I think it's a bizarre design choice, but it is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of that &quot;grant theory&quot; Justin Achilli had about WOD5E. For example, to him, V5 is about playing young Anarch Neonates who oppose the corrupt Camarilla and the evil Sabbat while they're mostly just busy surviving each night. For him it was about that - and <i>only </i>that. Gothic punk, street-level-only... he had a very specific way of playing WOD5E in mind and then he applied that same &quot;You play a young Anarch&quot;-idea to all the splats. If they follow his directions on M5, for example, it will be all about playing rebellious young Tradition-mages who oppose the older mages (who are losers) and battling the super-evil Technocracy.<br /> <br /> But how do the Fenrir fit into this...? They don't actually. If you compare it to the general formula I mentioned before: Are the Fenrir against the status quo? Check. Do they think the Garou-Nation has failed? Check. Do they think Garou-Elders can't be trusted? Check. Are they opposed to the evil forces in the setting (in this case, the Wyrm)? Check. Without the heavy-handed descriptions of the Fenrirs' particular evil they would fit very neatly into the pattern of the &quot;young Anarch&quot;-model for the PCs of WOD5E. But the whole Fenrir-thing is only there because the other main-developer for the book, Karim Muammar, seems to have been obsessed with the idea of &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot; and making that a central element of W5. In the end, it was toned down from the way he talked about when they were working on the Hunters Entertainment version but you can still see the traces of that idea in the book (and in the way Hauglosk is described).<br /> <br /> And now it's up to the Renegade-writing-team to make sense of this. If the Deepest of Wounds adventure with its torture/brainwashing-stuff is anything to go by, this is gonna be a wild ride...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T08:33:33-08:00","id":1527120,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to the big crossover reveal that links the Cult of Fenris to Junko Enoshima from Danganronpa!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T23:25:57-08:00","id":1527143,"title":"","content":"I distanced myself for a while from WtA. After few months I clearly revised my opinion about the game and the publisher. <br /> <br /> 1. I wanted continuity of the plot, something that could move the game foreward and i didn't get it.<br /> <br /> 2. It is a sandbox game with unclear past and unnecessary changes. While I understand rebuilding game mechanic and gifts, I'm against changing the core - tribe names, tribe past, elminiating some tribes, masking Fenris antagonist, concentrating on Pentex including Fly totem, changes in umbra, changes in caerns, lack of gnosis. <br /> <br /> 3. I'm totaly dissapointed in company choices with Muammar and Achilli. Their game concept and their view how WtA should works and about what is the game are in opposition to my personal ideas. After what I get in W20 edition with very good Book of Wyrm 20 I hoped that the continuity of their work will be natural choice for new Werewolf edition. The team felt the game as I expected and I am still impressed with their work. Sadly company had own ideas.<br /> <br /> 4. Future. Again I hoped for something like Rage aginst the New York but we will get a place and mini campaign to play there, it remindes me Denver for WtF. Somehow ,,Rage against&quot; books looks different for me than new kind of books discribing places to play there. So maby some tribebooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T06:40:58-08:00","id":1527152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527143#post1527143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distanced myself for a while from WtA. After few months I clearly revised my opinion about the game and the publisher.<br /> <br /> 1. I wanted continuity of the plot, something that could move the game foreward and i didn't get it.<br /> <br /> <b>2. It is a sandbox game with unclear past and unnecessary changes. While I understand rebuilding game mechanic and gifts, I'm against changing the core - tribe names, tribe past, elminiating some tribes, masking Fenris antagonist, concentrating on Pentex including Fly totem, changes in umbra, changes in caerns, lack of gnosis.</b><br /> <br /> 3. I'm totaly dissapointed in company choices with Muammar and Achilli. Their game concept and their view how WtA should works and about what is the game are in opposition to my personal ideas. After what I get in W20 edition with very good Book of Wyrm 20 I hoped that the continuity of their work will be natural choice for new Werewolf edition. The team felt the game as I expected and I am still impressed with their work. Sadly company had own ideas.<br /> <br /> 4. Future. Again I hoped for something like Rage aginst the New York but we will get a place and mini campaign to play there, it remindes me Denver for WtF. Somehow ,,Rage against&quot; books looks different for me than new kind of books discribing places to play there. So maby some tribebooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I feel like there's actually some points here.<br /> <br /> Quite a few of the names are slurs or blasphemies to Native peoples.<br /> <br /> There's some nuance here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T08:26:31-08:00","id":1527163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527152#post1527152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I feel like there's actually some points here.<br /> <br /> Quite a few of the names are slurs or blasphemies to Native peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Four. Three of which have already been removed and are now the Ghost Council, Winter's Teeth*, and Stolen Moons. The last one had a too little, too late kind of differentiation in A World of Rage (the actual people that get associated with the name are mentioned and always have their name spelled with an accent that the Crinos-born word doesn't have), but could be easily renamed if W20 hadn't been conceived of originally as a greatest hits edition, or if the people who were doing the new WoD had any inkling at all to solve the game's problems instead of trying to make it into a clone of Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T08:27:19-08:00","id":1527164,"title":"","content":"For the above post, because editing is tricky:<br /> <br /> * No way in hell I'm using Galestalkers when a better name was proposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:34:51-08:00","id":1527167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527164#post1527164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the above post, because editing is tricky:<br /> <br /> * No way in hell I'm using Galestalkers when a better name was proposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Winter's Teeth is &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:50:02-08:00","id":1527169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527164#post1527164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the above post, because editing is tricky:<br /> <br /> * No way in hell I'm using Galestalkers when a better name was proposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I still can't believe back that in October 2022 when they announced the name-changes for the Tribes there wasn't even the hint of acknowledging how these name-changes came to be. Back then, I simply assumed that that after the switch from the Hunters Entertainment version to the in-house team they had scrapped everything and restarted back at 0. But no, they actually carried over stuff from the Hunters Entertainment version - like the name Ghost Council. And this was never acknowledged - until James F. Sambrano spoke out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T10:25:15-08:00","id":1527173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527163#post1527163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Four. Three of which have already been removed and are now the Ghost Council, Winter's Teeth*, and Stolen Moons. The last one had a too little, too late kind of differentiation in A World of Rage (the actual people that get associated with the name are mentioned and always have their name spelled with an accent that the Crinos-born word doesn't have), but could be easily renamed if W20 hadn't been conceived of originally as a greatest hits edition, or if the people who were doing the new WoD had any inkling at all to solve the game's problems instead of trying to make it into a clone of Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, being upset the 20th Anniversary Editions are &quot;greatest hits compilations&quot; seems to complaining about what the entire design philosophy of the 20th Anniversary Lines was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T11:06:15-08:00","id":1527175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527173#post1527173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, being upset the 20th Anniversary Editions are &quot;greatest hits compilations&quot; seems to complaining about what the entire design philosophy of the 20th Anniversary Lines was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeh. The 20th Anniversary Edition grew way past the whole &quot;greatest hits compilation&quot;. While Werewolf and Vampire were the least changed in the cores, Wraith, Changeling and Mage were huge revamps. And then cam the supplements and those went waaaay beyond &quot;greatest hits&quot; and into a ton of new material for a new age. So the idea that the 20th anniversary line was just about greatest hits is rather faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T11:11:08-08:00","id":1527176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527175#post1527175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eeeeh. The 20th Anniversary Edition grew way past the whole &quot;greatest hits compilation&quot;. While Werewolf and Vampire were the least changed in the cores, Wraith, Changeling and Mage were huge revamps. And then cam the supplements and those went waaaay beyond &quot;greatest hits&quot; and into a ton of new material for a new age. So the idea that the 20th anniversary line was just about greatest hits is rather faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> You are correct that I also remember how I was nonplussed as a Mage fan that OPP was doubling down on the attempt to redeem the Technocracy when it seemed like the absolute worst time to try to say the guys embodying capitalism and authoritarianism were secretly okay dudes.<br /> <br /> But that argument is 20 years old and always down to how you saw them (appropriate enough for mage).<br /> <br /> I admit, not being a W20 player, I probably missed out on a lot of updates by my favorite RPG company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T11:42:29-08:00","id":1527177,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to still feeling annoyed that Paradox actively tried to make WtA edgier and, worse, actively prevented W20 writers from fixing those things that they fixed in W5................and then it turns out that W5 was a reboot anyway so there was literally no reason for that behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:29:13-08:00","id":1527182,"title":"","content":"It seems worth noting that W20's authors wanted to fix a bunch of things in supplements once the 20th books became more than omnibus things, and Paradox explicitly stopped them (and even made them insert more offensive material into W20), and then &quot;fixed&quot; it in W5. W5 shouldn't get credit for problems left in the game on the companies instructions when there was an attempt to start to fix it earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T13:08:30-08:00","id":1527190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527176#post1527176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably missed out on a lot of updates by my favorite RPG company.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your favourite RPG Company?<ul><li>The original White Wolf with its myriad Line Devs and freelancers?</li> <li>Onyx Path?</li> <li>Paradox White Wolf?</li> <li>Onyx Path under Paradox?</li> <li>Modiphius under Paradox?</li> <li>By Night Studios under Paradox?</li> <li>Paradox WoD team under Justin Achilli?</li> <li>Paradox Wod team under Karim Muamar?</li> <li>The new Renegade team under Juhanna Petterson?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T13:18:59-08:00","id":1527191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527190#post1527190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is your favourite RPG Company?<ul><li>The original White Wolf with its myriad Line Devs and freelancers?</li> <li>Onyx Path?</li> <li>Paradox White Wolf?</li> <li>Onyx Path under Paradox?</li> <li>Modiphius under Paradox?</li> <li>By Night Studios under Paradox?</li> <li>Paradox WoD team under Justin Achilli?</li> <li>Paradox Wod team under Karim Muamar?</li> <li>The new Renegade team under Juhanna Petterson?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> To summarize my opinion, &quot;It turns out I wasn't a fan of V5, I was a fan of Onyx Path Publishing's V5.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is doubly funny because I wasn't a big fan of V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T13:40:37-08:00","id":1527194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527191#post1527191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> To summarize my opinion, &quot;It turns out I wasn't a fan of V5, I was a fan of Onyx Path Publishing's V5.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is doubly funny because I wasn't a big fan of V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, what are your thoughts on the deeper cuts and changes OP made to V20? Like Black Hand and BJD?<br /> <br /> For instance the Werewolf community has quite a few choice words for some of the new developments that came along with Shattered Dreams and Changing Ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T04:02:57-08:00","id":1527228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527194#post1527194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense, what are your thoughts on the deeper cuts and changes OP made to V20? Like Black Hand and BJD?<br /> <br /> For instance the Werewolf community has quite a few choice words for some of the new developments that came along with Shattered Dreams and Changing Ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny because my impression of V20 was that it was very interested in the elements of Vampire that I wasn't a big fan of like the Children of the Inquisition, Black Hand, and behind the scenes theology of the setting. Which isn't that they were badly done, quite the opposite, but aren't really my thing. The handling of the True Hand was about as good as you could do it and very good. But as a guy who was interested in the metaplot, street level, and Signature Characters -- it wasn't my bag.<br /> <br /> However, it was ANARCHS UNBOUND and BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY that caused me to do a 180 on them. Anarchs Unbound was the first time I felt anyone had really done the Anarchs justice. BJD is my all time favorite supplement period. I was actually hoping that the Apocalyptic Record was this.<br /> <br /> What was the problems with SD and Changing Ways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T06:00:48-08:00","id":1527231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527228#post1527228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny because my impression of V20 was that it was very interested in the elements of Vampire that I wasn't a big fan of like the Children of the Inquisition, Black Hand, and behind the scenes theology of the setting. Which isn't that they were badly done, quite the opposite, but aren't really my thing. The handling of the True Hand was about as good as you could do it and very good. But as a guy who was interested in the metaplot, street level, and Signature Characters -- it wasn't my bag.<br /> <br /> However, it was ANARCHS UNBOUND and BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY that caused me to do a 180 on them. Anarchs Unbound was the first time I felt anyone had really done the Anarchs justice. BJD is my all time favorite supplement period. I was actually hoping that the Apocalyptic Record was this.<br /> <br /> What was the problems with SD and Changing Ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh I'm not surprised in you geeking out over Anarch's unbound. I've been doing a deep dive WIP on Apocalyptic Record and sadly it's not a BJD. It's too disconnected and too shallow to work out like that did. There are brilliant sections but it's not really clicking as a whole compared to the BJD.<br /> <br /> Shattered Dreams was a book that was supposed to explore the history through the lens of the shifters. The Dragon Kings, Wars of Rage and Shame, The Impergium and similar things. It was really well put together and really good at setting the tone and opening up multiple ways how things could play out and what led us where we are. However, the whole book was pronounced as not canon by Karim personnally with giant sidebars and a very ugly text box on the back cover. WoD has always been weird and messy, but this is the only book ever published that came out with multiple disclaimers by people in charge disawoving anything in it.<br /> <br /> Changing Ways on the other hand was supposed to be something of a Garou culture/Player Handbook book dealing with how Garou deal with modern life. There are come rather uncomfortable bits in the book regarding transphobia, bioexistentialism, reductive thoughts on Society that were written in. This caused quite a bit of a stir when people found out about the Trans garou that were being murdered or were mutilating themselves with silver. Then two authors spoke up about those sections and said that this was not in the original draft and was added by Paradox in the final edit passes.<br /> <br /> Let's just say that these two incidents may have made the Werewolf fanbase overly cautious about anything coming from Paradoxes kitchen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T06:12:28-08:00","id":1527233,"title":"","content":"Yikes.<br /> <br /> That's about all I can say there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T07:45:39-08:00","id":1527237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527233#post1527233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yikes.<br /> <br /> That's about all I can say there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it gets better. Since this was before the Chechenya fiasco, it was still the original team handling it. So there was an effort to include elements from BNS version, such as male non garou born Black Furies, hostile umbra and such. Changing Ways also has some clear sections that weren't edited well, such as an NPC appearing out of thin air. And where all W20 books had previously done their best to be considerate how its content was written, Changing Ways has the biggest shock jockey moment I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> So, years before W5, we were given a good reason to be careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T09:01:04-08:00","id":1527243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527233#post1527233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yikes.<br /> <br /> That's about all I can say there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also they wanted to change naming and treatment of the Garou born children, breeding, problematic tribal names and patrons put into context and given alternatives in the Apocalyptic Record. They were told no &quot;as it needs to be classic&quot;. And then these were some of the first things they rolled out as features of W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:19:31-08:00","id":1527255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527243#post1527243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also they wanted to change naming and treatment of the Garou born children, breeding, problematic tribal names and patrons put into context and given alternatives in the Apocalyptic Record. They were told no &quot;as it needs to be classic&quot;. And then these were some of the first things they rolled out as features of W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that strikes me as a &quot;we want the credit for that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T13:19:50-08:00","id":1527264,"title":"","content":"Sorry this is taking so much time, but work and real life keep getting in the way. Hopefully, I can catch up with a few things over the holidays. Strangely enough, that part of my life is relatively easy right now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART SIX</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Kewl Powerz&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of the Garou innate abilities have already been mentioned, such as shapeshifting and regeneration. Their other major abilities, such as taking extra actions and stepping sideways (What?! More on this later.), have been removed. Furthermore, nothing new was added, such as what happened with the Kindred in V5. Still, some things have returned.<br /> <br /> Gifts are still the primary supernatural powers of the Garou, and they are still taught by spirits. However, much of the ways about Gifts have changed. While there are still three main types of Gifts, the removal of different Breed means that the Breed category has been renamed 'Native,' combining the three previous Breed types into one. Not the best choice of terms, I would've went with 'Natal,' but it at least keeps three categories. Auspice and Tribe Gifts are still here.<br /> <br /> What isn't here is the ratings of Gifts. Instead of the 1-5/10 used for literally every other trait across the entire WOD line, Gifts are instead divided into three 'tiers,' roughly corresponding to groupings of the old ratings. They are based entirely on Renown, instead of having the pesky Rank getting in the way. What's weirder is that each category of Gift has different minimum levels for each type. Native Renown minimums are at 1, 4, and 7; Auspice at 2, 5, and 8; and Tribe at 3, 6, and 9. Yet, Renown is based on a 1-5 scale for each of the three types. Therefore, the minimums could be expanded so that each category of Gifts could have five levels. Maybe the developers didn't think any players would get enough Renown to reach such levels?<br /> <br /> Gifts have some restrictions placed on them, but feel similar to older rules. A main difference is that a player combines a type of Renown in the dice roll of many of them. The cost is either a Rage roll or WP, as Gnosis is no longer a thing. A further limitation is that most Gifts can only be used in the three supernatural forms (Glabro, Crinos, and Hispo) although there seems to be many exceptions to these rules. Considering that the Homid form usually needs the most help, these limitations feel off somehow.<br /> <br /> Rites are also still here, but they have a few changes as well. Like Gifts, Rites no longer have a range, which kind of makes sense as the Ability/Background that went with Rites got removed. However, this also means that some fairly powerful Rites are now quite common and available to starting characters. This includes the Rite of Shadow Passage, the substitute for stepping sideways. I'll mention more on this later when discussing the Umbra, but I have to bring up the Gauntlet rating which makes up the Difficulty. Apparently, even a powerful Caern has a Gauntlet of 2, while a sterile lab can go as high as 6. Why make it slightly harder to enter the Umbra from the spiritual heart of Garou society, but slightly easier from the most Weaver aspected places a Garou would go?<br /> <br /> Talismans are still the go-to tools for Garou. (I'm terrified at what will happen to Mage 5 which already used this term for something completely different.) Talismans are no longer always inhabited by a spirit, although why they still have special abilities without this isn't explained. One-use versions, still called talens, are still around as well. Unfortunately, only eight examples are given. This sadly includes the klaive, which has gone from being the main weapon of the Garou to being a ceremonial dagger whose main benefit is doing Aggravated Damage to Garou due to being silver. There is a sidebar on the Silver Crown, possibly setting up a storyline involving the Albrecht family of Fangs, but there doesn't seem to be any other reason for its inclusion.<br /> <br /> Caerns are mentioned, mostly in how they are constructed using shared pools, and how to grant them special abilities. For instance, some parts of Caern can add die to rolls to cross the Gauntlet, but not to lower it. Odd<br /> <br /> Finally, gone are the lengthy lists of various types of weaponry and other forms of equipment. Weapons are reduced to a basic, short chart on damage value. All of the former traits are irrelevant now. Sure, they added a sense of complexity to the game, but the developers strongly don't want that to be the focus any more. A few specialized types of weapons are mentioned, but were mostly included for their additional effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T14:15:44-08:00","id":1527268,"title":"","content":"Some gifts are the definition of jank, such as Heightened Senses. Now a higher level gift is bestows the garou with... the senses of a wolf.<br /> <br /> Wat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T00:35:37-08:00","id":1527291,"title":"","content":"Tying the Gifts to the supernatural Forms was a bad decision, I think. First, there's a long list of Gifts that ignore it but then sometimes it feels like the Gift effect is so subtle that it shouldn't require a supernatural Form. The second thing is how this ties into burdening Rage and Willpower as resources. A Gift that comes with a Rage check and can be only used with a supernatural Form actually asks for two or three Rage checks in reality. If a player isn't careful enough, you Land at Rage 0...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T11:15:49-08:00","id":1527388,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART SEVEN</span><br /> <br /> The Umbra<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, the Umbra and the various structures of the Otherworlds has always been my most favorite part of the WOD, ever since I got Mage, about a month before Werewolf. I was constantly amazed by the opportunities the Umbra provided, in all of its forms. I have frequently posted my thoughts on the WOD forums about both it and possible reconfigurations. While I wouldn't call myself an expert, as I never read every possible book nor do I still own those I did read, I feel that I am at least fairly knowledgeable on the subject. When I first read V5 and noted that vampires no longer had the only common power that allowed any contact with the Otherworlds, the Auspex power of Astral Projection, I was worried. While Astral Projection and similar powers were somewhat problematic into working into the greater Umbra at large, I had come up with some ideas to make everything work, so I was hoping that the designers were just doing the same by delaying including this power and not just diminishing the Umbra altogether.<br /> <br /> My fears were realized in W5.<br /> <br /> The old Umbra is no more. Gone are the familiar representations of the Penumbra, the discoveries of the Near Realms, and the mysteries of the Deep Umbra. Instead, everything gets jumbled together in a nebulous blob. The main structure still appears to closely resemble the Penumbra, with weirder things 'further' out, but it is dangerous/deadly to even to try and find out. Literally, as Garou suffer one point of Aggravated Damage for every scene after the first, unless 1 WP is spent per additional scene. Considering how hard it is to regain lost WP, this mechanic feels designed to prevent any meanwhile exploration of the Umbra. There is not even a Gift or Talisman that would allow longer stays, just a spot on a Loresheet. <br /> <br /> Spirits are almost the same, but with the same vagueness one sees throughout W5. The Triat is still the fundamental 'top dogs,' although the text can't seem to agree if they are entirely forces or spirits themselves. Each of the three still have their own broods, although the Wyrm's brood isn't entirely corrupted. The same basic hierarchy is intact, although it is implied that even human deities might be included among them. One thing that spirits don't have is Charms. Instead, spirits just have 'powers' that they use to do things. The most common power is possession, because that appears to be easier than creating a form out of nothing like with Materialize. It also allows the fighting to take place outside of the Umbra with actual consequences. Possession also means that Fomori are still a thing, although the text suggests treating them as long-term possessions of longer than a few days instead of the total integration of spirit and flesh. At least Gaian spirits rarely do that sort of thing, and usually only do so with what they represent. Considering that some of the most types of spirits have been reclassified as just elementals, such as the various emotion-based categories, this would make possession very hard. One thing that doesn't seem to occur is that awakening an object's spirit is no longer possible. Not sure if that is helpful or not yet.<br /> <br /> The biggest change to the Umbra, I feel, is that is only for Garou. Again, literally. While other splats might have their own spiritual habitats and ways to enter them, most cannot enter the Umbra. Those few who do will not experience the Umbra as the Garou do. This feels like a big step backwards. It has always been a cornerstone of the WOD that pretty much anyone could enter the Spirit Wilds of the Middle Umbra. While the exact mechanics were never completely revealed, especially for Wraiths, any splat could go there and experience pretty much the same thing. No longer. This step strongly discourages any sort of crossover. One wonders if such limitations will be found for each niche Otherworlds territory. This is especially worrisome for Mages, who already had much of their Umbra travel diminished in Revised. <br /> <br /> It is from this last point alone that makes me want to lower my final grade by a complete letter, but I will try to keep this review as impartial as I can. There will be about two more parts before the final grade will be given for this phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T11:49:07-08:00","id":1527389,"title":"","content":"The way W5 treats spirits makes them sound less like aspects of the world and more like creatures from another unrelated realm. Which completely misses the point of animism and therefore the core what the garou are.<br /> <br /> In a VERY ironic turn, I feel like they essentially converted the animistic spirit world into a more modern christian one. Where the spiritual is far away and hard to access and the creatures that DO access the mundane world are the evil ones.<br /> <br /> This sounds like a harsher version of the Fade in Dragon Age, if I am being honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T02:42:31-08:00","id":1527412,"title":"","content":"That time-limit via WP and aggravated damage is such a feel-bad mechanic. That plus restricting access to those who know the Rite... It's clear that W5 doesn't want you to spend too much time in the Umbra. That Garou don't have to eat or drink feels like an insult at that point. It's not like you gonna spend long enough in the Umbra to worry about that anyway.<br /> <br /> Also using scenes as an indicator of time is so weird. Since the definition hasn't been changed since V5 it's still way too small. But here with the Umbra and with the Edges in H5, relying on scenes really turns the dial to feel-bad, to disempower players. I think a real time measurement like hours or days would have been more useful (with advice that STs should ultimately use their own judgment for how big the intervals are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T08:17:36-08:00","id":1527425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527388#post1527388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART SEVEN</span><br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> The biggest change to the Umbra, I feel, is that is only for Garou. Again, literally. While other splats might have their own spiritual habitats and ways to enter them, most cannot enter the Umbra. Those few who do will not experience the Umbra as the Garou do. This feels like a big step backwards. It has always been a cornerstone of the WOD that pretty much anyone could enter the Spirit Wilds of the Middle Umbra. While the exact mechanics were never completely revealed, especially for Wraiths, any splacould go there and experience pretty much the same thing. No longer. This step strongly discourages any sort of crossover. One wonders if such limitations will be found for each niche Otherworlds territory. This is especially worrisome for Mages, who already had much of their Umbra travel diminished in Revised.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know the stupidest part of that? The whole original idea behind 5th edition was this &quot;one world of darkness&quot; where different splats would clearly be part of the same world rather than existing in their own bubble.<br /> <br /> There's some epic level of incompetence here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T23:50:08-08:00","id":1527454,"title":"","content":"The one constant they now do have is mortal hunters as antagonists. Second Inquisition, hunter-orgs and Project Twilight... All three corebooks featured mortal hunters as a prominent enemy-faction. The irony is that even in the game where you play mortal hunters, the hunter-orgs are enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T02:37:38-08:00","id":1527455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527425#post1527425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know the stupidest part of that? The whole original idea behind 5th edition was this &quot;one world of darkness&quot; where different splats would clearly be part of the same world rather than existing in their own bubble.<br /> <br /> There's some epic level of incompetence here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's still the goal. It's why the Umbra has largely become extraneous to the Werewolf play experience. 95%+ of a W5 game will be taking place in the same world that Vampire and Hunter do (the normal, mundane world). The Umbra is not somewhere that you spend a large amount of time in. I imagine they'll do the same thing with Mage, argely remove the Umbral, otherworldly elements and ensuring that players stick to the real world. Not sure how you could still run Changeling or Wraith under that paradigm, but then those were not terribly popular games so it wouldn't surprise me if they don't get a full 5th edition update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T02:59:32-08:00","id":1527457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527455#post1527455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's still the goal. It's why the Umbra has largely become extraneous to the Werewolf play experience. 95%+ of a W5 game will be taking place in the same world that Vampire and Hunter do (the normal, mundane world). The Umbra is not somewhere that you spend a large amount of time in. I imagine they'll do the same thing with Mage, argely remove the Umbral, otherworldly elements and ensuring that players stick to the real world. Not sure how you could still run Changeling or Wraith under that paradigm, but then those were not terribly popular games so it wouldn't surprise me if they don't get a full 5th edition update.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet they still listed &quot;exploring the Umbra &quot; in the Introduction as a thing werewolves do... I wonder how often players even entered the Umbra during playtests.<br /> <br /> As for Changeling and Wraith in 5th edition, they can always do the same thing they did with H5: Keep the name - but the game has nothing to do with the previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T06:47:32-08:00","id":1527459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527457#post1527457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet they still listed &quot;exploring the Umbra &quot; in the Introduction as a thing werewolves do... I wonder how often players even entered the Umbra during playtests.<br /> <br /> As for Changeling and Wraith in 5th edition, they can always do the same thing they did with H5: Keep the name - but the game has nothing to do with the previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just guessing, but maybe they thought the Umbra would give Garou too much of an advantage over human hunters, which I find strange is why they didn't just remove the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T06:55:33-08:00","id":1527460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527457#post1527457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet they still listed &quot;exploring the Umbra &quot; in the Introduction as a thing werewolves do... I wonder how often players even entered the Umbra during playtests.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Exploring the Umbra&quot; seems like it just means jumping across, spending no more than a couple of scenes scouting and looking around, and then jumping back to the normal world. They got rid of the Deep Umbra and all of those other locations because they don't intend for people to go there. They want One World of Darkness and that &quot;One World&quot; is the normal world. It feels like they don't even want to give you the tools or the ability to run Chronicles or even longer sessions that don't take place in the normal world. I would expect that Mage and other games will be the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T11:09:52-08:00","id":1527464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527459#post1527459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just guessing, but maybe they thought the Umbra would give Garou too much of an advantage over human hunters, which I find strange is why they didn't just remove the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not human hunters, vampires. Apparently, one reason the umbra was limited was because the original devs didn't want garou to umbra snipe Princes.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, though, I think exploring the umbra might have once been a viable option. But since W5 is a bit disjointed, that aspect wasn't then actually used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T19:09:07-08:00","id":1527475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527464#post1527464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not human hunters, vampires. Apparently, one reason the umbra was limited was because the original devs didn't want garou to umbra snipe Princes.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, though, I think exploring the umbra might have once been a viable option. But since W5 is a bit disjointed, that aspect wasn't then actually used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this over in the Vampire: The Masquerade forum that the Umbra sniping was always stupid because any Vampire Prince was going to be almost untouchable in their haven because that place is going to be incredibly high Gauntlet rating and full of Banes from their longtime inhabitation as well as how many demons they have. I know some people say, &quot;Oh, just wear a Baneskin&quot; or whatever but at that point they're just pointing out the same kind of logic as, &quot;Why not blow up their haven with semtext.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T19:35:47-08:00","id":1527478,"title":"","content":"Even if &quot;Umbral ambushing the Prince&quot; was ever a functional tactic (by the rules, it really wasn't even without the Gauntlet and Bane issues until you have a high enough Rank and XP character that the Umbra part is the least of the impediment), you don't need to change the Umbra the way W5 does to address that.<br /> <br /> Here's a simple fix:<br /> <br /> No matter how well a Garou rolls, side-stepping takes a full turn during which they can do nothing else. Stealth during that turn is impossible, and reflexive supernatural sensory powers with automatically sense something suspicious happening even if the Garou is using Gifts or items to help hide their activities.<br /> <br /> That's addressing the problem (how real it might be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T02:14:47-08:00","id":1527486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527475#post1527475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mentioned this over in the Vampire: The Masquerade forum that the Umbra sniping was always stupid because any Vampire Prince was going to be almost untouchable in their haven because that place is going to be incredibly high Gauntlet rating and full of Banes from their longtime inhabitation as well as how many demons they have. I know some people say, &quot;Oh, just wear a Baneskin&quot; or whatever but at that point they're just pointing out the same kind of logic as, &quot;Why not blow up their haven with semtext.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 'umbra snipe' happened once in a LARP and from there, the original devs became paranoid about it. Aided by this mentality that the umbra was too 'silly' for a horror game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T03:10:39-08:00","id":1527487,"title":"","content":"The Umbra is another one of these poorly handled concepts. Sure, they don't like the Umbra - so what should be the Umbra like then? Instead, they set it up in a way where it's there but mechanics push against players going there and wanting to be there. They didn't create a new version of the Umbra, they just recontextualized it by building barriers between it and the players enjoyment.<br /> <br /> Imagine starting every scene transition with &quot;Mark one WP or take one aggravated damage.&quot;. And then add a fight on top of that! I'm sure the players will be overjoyed by the Crinos-bit of &quot;Each round spend 1WP, kill something or immediately Frenzy.&quot; in that new context... And role-playing Frenzy will be especially &quot;fun&quot; once both Umbra and Crinos Form have drained the WP track...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T07:08:27-08:00","id":1527493,"title":"","content":"I mean they're seeing it as weirdo fantasy land, I'm seeing it as &quot;oh and Werewolves can slip into Silent Hill on occasion.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T07:20:13-08:00","id":1527494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527493#post1527493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean they're seeing it as weirdo fantasy land, I'm seeing it as &quot;oh and Werewolves can slip into Silent Hill on occasion.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Silent Hill is more the Hisil. The Umbra is more of a continuum from Splatter House to various safer-feeling Save Points across gaming, except that at some point they come under siege from the Splatter House stuff and aren't so safe. So, on the whole, kind of like Darkest Dungeon, in terms of thematics, but flip the positions of the Weald and Hamlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T07:33:00-08:00","id":1527495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527493#post1527493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean they're seeing it as weirdo fantasy land, I'm seeing it as &quot;oh and Werewolves can slip into Silent Hill on occasion.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean parts are like Silent Hill, but I think the mentality of making the umbra into something always dangerous is taking away the point of it.<br /> <br /> It is a literal version of the concept of reciprocity in animism. What you put in, you get out and the umbra shows that in practice. The polluted river spirit is gunky and no longer looks like itself. The garden in the middle of the city tended by the community looks bright and joyful, etc.<br /> <br /> I know you meant Silent Hill in the sense of &quot;scary otherworld&quot; rather than &quot;purgatory&quot;, but I feel it also showcases how spirits are treated as the Other in W5. The creatures in Silent Hill are demons who test you, in both the Christian sense and the Buddhist sense. They are hell creatures that make your journey hard, but they don't want to harm others. They are to make you get over your issues, nothing more.<br /> <br /> But that is not what the spirits in WtA are. They are reflections of what is and are as part of the world as the creatures on the flesh side are.<br /> <br /> This is not directed at you, Phipps, but I often find it amusing how reluctant people are to consider spirituality that isn't the distant modern Christian one. Anything that requires you to believe that the surrounding world is alive spiritually is seen as childish and naive. Something out of a cartoon. To many in the West, the mentality of any supernatural is silly and not worth considering. W5 takes the modern Christian stance, with distant Patron <s>Saint</s>s and spiritual world that is hostile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T11:27:57-08:00","id":1527506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527495#post1527495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean parts are like Silent Hill, but I think the mentality of making the umbra into something always dangerous is taking away the point of it.<br /> <br /> It is a literal version of the concept of reciprocity in animism. What you put in, you get out and the umbra shows that in practice. The polluted river spirit is gunky and no longer looks like itself. The garden in the middle of the city tended by the community looks bright and joyful, etc.<br /> <br /> I know you meant Silent Hill in the sense of &quot;scary otherworld&quot; rather than &quot;purgatory&quot;, but I feel it also showcases how spirits are treated as the Other in W5. The creatures in Silent Hill are demons who test you, in both the Christian sense and the Buddhist sense. They are hell creatures that make your journey hard, but they don't want to harm others. They are to make you get over your issues, nothing more.<br /> <br /> But that is not what the spirits in WtA are. They are reflections of what is and are as part of the world as the creatures on the flesh side are.<br /> <br /> This is not directed at you, Phipps, but I often find it amusing how reluctant people are to consider spirituality that isn't the distant modern Christian one. Anything that requires you to believe that the surrounding world is alive spiritually is seen as childish and naive. Something out of a cartoon. To many in the West, the mentality of any supernatural is silly and not worth considering. W5 takes the modern Christian stance, with distant Patron <s>Saint</s>s and spiritual world that is hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh.<br /> <br /> Silent Hill is a reflection of the Hellish awful nature of the town that was affected by Alessa Giulesspie's nightmares and torture at the hands of the Cult. It's effectively what I envision a Wyrm tainted town would look like. However, I'm going to point out that the Umbra is not really &quot;safe&quot; for Garou save for a very rare bunch of places to begin with. Much of the Earth is covered in Wyrm taint and pattern spiders and even if you're in the pristine wilderness, it's a lot of dangerous and powerful spirits that aren't going to be your friends.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest managed to capture that feeling well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T11:48:07-08:00","id":1527509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527506#post1527506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhh.<br /> <br /> Silent Hill is a reflection of the Hellish awful nature of the town that was affected by Alessa Giulesspie's nightmares and torture at the hands of the Cult. It's effectively what I envision a Wyrm tainted town would look like. However, I'm going to point out that the Umbra is not really &quot;safe&quot; for Garou save for a very rare bunch of places to begin with. Much of the Earth is covered in Wyrm taint and pattern spiders and even if you're in the pristine wilderness, it's a lot of dangerous and powerful spirits that aren't going to be your friends.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest managed to capture that feeling well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silent Hill might have started as a reflection of Alessa's own psyche, but by Silent Hill 2 the town is serving as a purgatory that either kills you or makes you face your worst sins and come out a changed person. When left to its own devices, Silent Hill functions like that. The events of 1 and 3 are situations where the cult's meddling changes how the town functions.<br /> <br /> Which is why it really isn't a good example of a wyrm tainted town in the umbra. While things in the umbra hold symbolism, they aren't custom-made for you or entirely made out of someone else's issues.<br /> <br /> For me, your basic city umbra would be a mix of They Live and Condemned.<br /> <br /> Also, I never said the umbra is safe for the garou, just not always dangerous. It isn't hostile, just its own world with its own issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T13:52:53-08:00","id":1527515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527509#post1527509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Silent Hill might have started as a reflection of Alessa's own psyche, but by Silent Hill 2 the town is serving as a purgatory that either kills you or makes you face your worst sins and come out a changed person. When left to its own devices, Silent Hill functions like that. The events of 1 and 3 are situations where the cult's meddling changes how the town functions.<br /> <br /> Which is why it really isn't a good example of a wyrm tainted town in the umbra. While things in the umbra hold symbolism, they aren't custom-made for you or entirely made out of someone else's issues.<br /> <br /> For me, your basic city umbra would be a mix of They Live and Condemned.<br /> <br /> Also, I never said the umbra is safe for the garou, just not always dangerous. It isn't hostile, just its own world with its own issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you could do Silent Hill 2 pretty easily by just having the town riddled with Banes who can manifest.<br /> <br /> If they're Banes of Guilt, they'll take the forms of James and the other characters' traumas rather than Alessa's.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't remain static but often cater to the viewer but this is more a Mage thing than a Werewolf one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T14:15:38-08:00","id":1527517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527515#post1527515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, you could do Silent Hill 2 pretty easily by just having the town riddled with Banes who can manifest.<br /> <br /> If they're Banes of Guilt, they'll take the forms of James and the other characters' traumas rather than Alessa's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everything unpleasant has to be corrupted, though. WtA has plenty of non-Wyrmy realms which are challenging but aren't tainted. Silent Hill is basically like Erebus, it tests you painfully but it is there to help. Same with Silent Hill in its natural state.<br /> <br /> But I think your point does kind of show why W5's take on spirits feels so Christian. You saw the creatures of Silent Hill not as forces to test you but forces that by their inherent nature are corrupted and 'evil.' Like W5 says mostly banes possess humans, therefore most interactions with spirits outside the accepted Patrons are bound to be with creatures that are bad. It isn't hard to see that as someone blessed by a saint fighting demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T15:22:25-08:00","id":1527518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527515#post1527515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, you could do Silent Hill 2 pretty easily by just having the town riddled with Banes who can manifest.<br /> <br /> If they're Banes of Guilt, they'll take the forms of James and the other characters' traumas rather than Alessa's.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't remain static but often cater to the viewer but this is more a Mage thing than a Werewolf one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers for SH2!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">James killed Mary, so it might not just be guilt that he's struggling with in a W:tA Umbral context. If you kill someone and spirits notice, you might find Psychomachiae trying to get you to do it again. The &quot;clean&quot; alternative is merely just spirits that relate to pain and suffering, because they were noticing Mary and that she suddenly stopped being there.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, given that, no one is up for Splatter House or Darkest Dungeon as references, then?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T00:14:03-08:00","id":1527536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527518#post1527518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given that, no one is up for Splatter House or Darkest Dungeon as references, then?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given so much of the established spirit infrastructure has been lost, I could definitely see mosquito spirits taking over a bunch of trustfund yuppies to redo the Crimson Court.<br /> <br /> Two games I'd use for inspiration as well are Little Nightmares (1 and 2) and Library of Ruina/Limbus Company. Especially Limbus Company really delves into the sheer despair of the City. I have rarely seen games depict this sense of deep hopelessness towards change as the Project Moon games do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T01:18:47-08:00","id":1527539,"title":"","content":"I'll readily admit that I tend to use local Dreaming stories for the most part with a dash of urban legends and folklore to flavour my local Umbra so the idea of even referencing something like a video game for it is a bit jarring and kinda out of my wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T04:56:46-08:00","id":1527545,"title":"","content":"I think the Umbra needs to exist in the context of an animistic worldview. It's about the shamanistic and ritualized dealings with various categories of spirits, both good and bad. For Garou these practices are just even more real because they personally can enter the spirit realm. And the Theurge Auspice specializes in dealing with these ritualized communications with spirits or practicing the right Rites to sanctify a hunt or honor an Ancestor spirit before summoning it.<br /> <br /> Just making it a horror realm where entering it means going through hell misses the mark, I think. At that point, the Theurge Auspice becomes superfluous - in the same way Galliards become irrelevant when W5 degrades the effectiveness of oral history in the name of getting away from deeper lore/worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T07:46:16-08:00","id":1527550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527545#post1527545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just making it a horror realm where entering it means going through hell misses the mark, I think. At that point, the Theurge Auspice becomes superfluous - in the same way Galliards become irrelevant when W5 degrades the effectiveness of oral history in the name of getting away from deeper lore/worldbuilding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if the umbra is only dreadful a lot of the reason to fight for Gaia goes away. There ARE things of beauty still and WtA is about preserving those.<br /> <br /> Plus, making umbra into a horror realm takes away from the Hisil being one in WtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T08:46:06-08:00","id":1527554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527536#post1527536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given so much of the established spirit infrastructure has been lost, I could definitely see mosquito spirits taking over a bunch of trustfund yuppies to redo the Crimson Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a wide-range of bloodsuckers, including mosquitoes. You'd also need the worst person to instigate and escalate the situation (a situation which Garou are regrettably familiar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T13:21:45-08:00","id":1527573,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART EIGHT</span><br /> <br /> Storytelling<br /> <br /> The main considerations for storytelling remain mostly the same, although there does seem to be slight change of focus on the emotional well-being of the players, as opposed to the long-range development of the characters. This might be due to the 'Nordic' style of playing that is favored by the developers. While subtle, this change leads to shorter, one-and-done stories, instead of longer campaigns. The rules favor this, such as the new experience tracks for Gifts that are complicated yet still unstructured to a degree. <br /> <br /> Strangely, the trigger warnings are incredibly detailed and include outside links to other sources. It might be a generational thing, but I've never had so many potential problems called out. Not really a bad thing, just somewhat unusual<br /> <br /> Antagonists and Others<br /> <br /> I've already mentioned spirit antagonists in the section on the Umbra, so this part will focus on the more corporeal enemies, as there really isn't anything that could particularly be called an ally since Kinfolk have been removed.<br /> <br /> Pentex is still around, although they are now an international holding company rather than an actual corporate entity, although this is a fine distinction. Instead of a servant of the Wyrm, Pentex is now beholden to Fly as its Patron, who even offers the executives Gifts. Sure, there are still Banes and Fomori about, but the interaction between Pentex and the Wyrm is different. [As an aside, it was the Fianna who initially named the Ban-possessed Fomori after the enemies of the Fae allies of the Tribe. Since that connection is now gone, as well as the cultures that spawned them, how did the name come about?]<br /> <br /> A common ally of Pentex is the Black Spiral Dancer Tribe. Somehow, their origin remains about the same. The White Howlers went into a cavernous area to confront the Wyrm, only to wind up corrupted instead. Now, the exact time this happened is unknown, but it was in the fairly distant past. How did every Howler across the world wind up in the same place at that right time, even if it was in the Umbra? How does the Tribe manage to continue, if there is now genetic component to being Garou? Is there 'recruitment' drives to convert other Garou? Does the BSD's new patron Bat manage to trigger the transformation and hope the new cub chooses a path of corruption? Doesn't really make sense. Also, the new BSDs see themselves as ushering Gaia into the next phase of the cycle so that something new will be born, as opposed to just making things worse. Odd philosophy. At least it seems to be easier to cure them, even without Erebus.<br /> <br /> There are also two other Tribes that have left the Garou Nation. The Stargazers left to try new means of saving Gaia, under a new unknown Patron. For some reason, no Garou has sought to ask who their new Parton is after Chimera left under mutual terms. Stargazers are likely to help in many situations, just not in the expected ways. (The other Tribe, a reimagining of an old one, will not be mentioned here. Look for this Tribe to be highlighted in Phase Four.)<br /> <br /> There are new types of lycanthropes beyond the Garou, and the old Skinwalkers. No one really knows how many of these shifters came about, and that is actually a good idea. A variety of wolf-changers outside of the Garou adds a layer of intrigue that was missing from previous editions, but was added to the CoD Werewolf game. This is the best new treatment I have seen in W5. While previous editions had only one known way of becoming a werewolf outside of being born one, and that had the prerequisite of being Kinfolk, having multiple ways suggests that there are mysteries beyond even Gaia and that Garou really don't have everything figured out.<br /> <br /> The Fera still exist, or at least some do. Apparently, they still know their cultural history, but they aren't telling the Garou anything about why they really don't like each other. Only a raven-shifter and a spider-shifter are mentioned, so there is no way of knowing what else is out there. Not much is told about them. For instance, we aren't told if they have a form similar to Crinos, only that they can shift into an animal form, swarm for spiders. More vagueness. Here, this isn't as helpful as it was for the other werewolves.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural splats get write-ups, longer ones as their details are being 'fleshed' out, as it were. While the vampires feel similar, the other three don't. This is especially true for the fae character who is not acting like a Changeling at all. I fear this will bode even more changes to the other lines, perhaps greater than what happened to the Garou.<br /> <br /> A few mortal hunters and animals are mentioned. No major changes from previous encounters, although I would say the hunters feel even more narrowly defined and more generic than in previous editions. Much of the part on animals has been pasted from V5 with a few changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T15:51:42-08:00","id":1527578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527573#post1527573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE THREE PART EIGHT</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Pentex is still around, although they are now an international holding company rather than an actual corporate entity, although this is a fine distinction. Instead of a servant of the Wyrm, Pentex is now beholden to Fly as its Patron, who even offers the executives Gifts. Sure, there are still Banes and Fomori about, but the interaction between Pentex and the Wyrm is different. [As an aside, it was the Fianna who initially named the Ban-possessed Fomori after the enemies of the Fae allies of the Tribe. Since that connection is now gone, as well as the cultures that spawned them, how did the name come about?]<br /> <br /> There are new types of lycanthropes beyond the Garou, and the old Skinwalkers. No one really knows how many of these shifters came about, and that is actually a good idea. A variety of wolf-changers outside of the Garou adds a layer of intrigue that was missing from previous editions, but was added to the CoD Werewolf game. This is the best new treatment I have seen in W5. While previous editions had only one known way of becoming a werewolf outside of being born one, and that had the prerequisite of being Kinfolk, having multiple ways suggests that there are mysteries beyond even Gaia and that Garou really don't have everything figured out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, these two points at least I found curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T17:18:26-08:00","id":1527582,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Stolen Moons are probably one of the few positives I've found in W5......and once again the groundwork for those is Sambranos ( also once again uncredited).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T17:43:04-08:00","id":1527584,"title":"","content":"Stolen Moons aren't the Skindancers with another name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T20:54:18-08:00","id":1527589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527584#post1527584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stolen Moons aren't the Skindancers with another name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially, they were reworked to remove 'Skindancer' for fairly obvious reasons ( <i>yee naaldlooshii</i> ) and include numerous different ways of becoming a 'werewolf' from Fomori-like possession to Hedge Magic to Demon/Spirit Pacts and others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 12-28-2023, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T22:21:39-08:00","id":1527591,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think that opening up those options, while a positive in other situations, in this case is just another uninspired flattening to make the game more like Vampire: the Agglutination of a Bunch of Random Vampire Types From Other Sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T01:01:05-08:00","id":1527593,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a reason to be that cynical about it. First, legacy editions already had lots of things in the WoD that could shapeshift without being Garou; so that's nothing new. Second, they had Sambrano's good work on it already in their hands so they didn't really have to do anything but shove it into the W5 box. Lastly, the removal of the kinfolk as a meaningful part of Garou life would make a single path towards being a Stolen Moon nonsensical; there isn't a single demographic group already educated into the Garou way of thinking that could foster a desire to become one of Gaia's chosen instead of being breeding stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-29-2023, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T02:37:11-08:00","id":1527594,"title":"","content":"The only problem with the Stolen Moons is that you can't play them. Because some people want to play bitten werewolves, not born ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T02:51:07-08:00","id":1527595,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the Stolen Moons only work in contrast to the Garou. And since W5 is invested in toning down the specificity of Garou, the concept doesn't really pop. If the PCs aren't too strongly invested in Garou concepts, it will be hard to distinguish between the Garou PCs and Stolen Moons.<br /> <br /> And I think you have to add a bit more than what you get from the W5 corebook. Weaker werewolves of different origin isn't that interesting by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T03:06:44-08:00","id":1527596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527595#post1527595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think the Stolen Moons only work in contrast to the Garou. And since W5 is invested in toning down the specificity of Garou, the concept doesn't really pop. If the PCs aren't too strongly invested in Garou concepts, it will be hard to distinguish between the Garou PCs and Stolen Moons.<br /> <br /> And I think you have to add a bit more than what you get from the W5 corebook. Weaker werewolves of different origin isn't that interesting by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it is the narrative that matters. If you want to play a game where your pc gets cursed and has to fight against their wolf nature, even W5 isn't exactly fulfilling that fantasy. Stolen Moons can give that, if you finagle their creation so it can be unwilling as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T04:19:00-08:00","id":1527598,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of it will come down to supplements. If there's a W5 supplement that elevates Stolen Moons up to something like V5 thinbloods as just a different play experience from the standard Kindred? Not my speed, but completely functional. If they stay as they are now and never get more than a few antagonist stat blocks in books/modules that use them? Wasted potential.<br /> <br /> The sheer amount of W5 that feels like it could be improved significantly with a few supplements is a bit staggering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T15:12:48-08:00","id":1527611,"title":"","content":"We did get that one antagonist from Renegade Games already. There the Stolen Moon was this conservative &quot;men's rights&quot; activist radio host with a big following who came across a bad spirit. And then he became this vessel for this Rite where he has to kill Garou in order to increases his own werewolf powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T17:41:55-08:00","id":1527614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527611#post1527611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did get that one antagonist from Renegade Games already. There the Stolen Moon was this conservative &quot;men's rights&quot; activist radio host with a big following who came across a bad spirit. And then he became this vessel for this Rite where he has to kill Garou in order to increases his own werewolf powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean you probably could have stopped at MRA if you wanted 95% of the PCs in my chronicles to murderise him......having him make a pact with a Bane and murder Garou is just overegging the pudding. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T19:02:42-08:00","id":1527618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527614#post1527614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=