.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T19:20:57-08:00","id":1527619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527618#post1527618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haight Tribe is my favorite clan. I am so offended he's a member.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before becoming a Stolen Moon, Haight was a globetrotting adventurer and big game hunter, aka the biggest group of toxically masculine douchebags that there ever were. Never forget that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T01:19:27-08:00","id":1527622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527614#post1527614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean you probably could have stopped at MRA if you wanted 95% of the PCs in my chronicles to murderise him......having him make a pact with a Bane and murder Garou is just overegging the pudding. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>He's more of a social threat by using his platform and his fanbase to go after the PCs and their Touchstones, I would say. With the Rite he would have to kill quite the number of Garou to be able to compete with three or four Garou in Crinos Form as far as I remember. Other than that the PCs will make mincemeat out of him quicker than he can say &quot;Family court&quot; in a direct confrontation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T05:55:15-08:00","id":1527626,"title":"","content":"Oops. Looks like I offended a couple of Tatertots based on the dislikes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 12-30-2023, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T04:37:21-08:00","id":1527651,"title":"","content":"Another thing where it's unclear what exactly W5 is trying to do are the Stargazers. What exactly is an ST supposed to do with this version of the Stargazers? Chimera isn't their Patron Spirit anymore and nobody knows who it's instead. Nobody cares but also... who cares? The text doesn't even make a case for why it could be of interest to anyone whothenew PatronSpirit is. And then it tries to explain how different the Stargazers' MO is supposed to be but there's nothing special or weird about the example that's mentioned.<br /> <br /> And why is it a non-playable Tribe that left the Garou Nation in the first place? The only explanation is that this was conceptualized with an eye on continuation, rather than reimagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T10:46:27-08:00","id":1527659,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">OVERALL GRADE: C-/D+ (lowered to D- if personal feelings on the Umbra are added in)</span><br /> <br /> Whenever a new edition of a game comes out, especially one that is tagged with numerical subtitle (such as 'Fifth Edition'), one feels the need to compare it to the previous editions. Although W5 clearly states that it is more of a recon rather than a 'real' new edition, that subtitle suggests otherwise. While many terms and core concepts are brought forth, many other things, such as mechanics and metaplot, were not carried over. In all fairness, this game should be titled <i>Generic Paradox/Renegade Werewolf Game</i>, or, less facetiously perhaps, <i>Werewolf: the Extinction</i>, although I'd prefer to hold that subtitle out for a new, different game in the WOD that I have had thoughts about.<br /> <br /> Many problematic terms and ideas were either changed or excised for W5. Some sort of change for these things were necessary, even if they could have been executed a little better. However, other things that most players didn't have many, if any, problems with were also changed. Not all of these changes were integrated well into the existing systems. In fact, many feel like they were just shoved in without thinking about what it would do to greater gameplay. <br /> <br /> A main issue is the vagueness about the history of the Garou. The designers leave hints about what may have still occurred in the current game, but it comes out almost like laziness without having even a trace of why this has happened. Maybe entire generations of Garou were wiped out in the final battles, leaving not enough to carry on history and traditions. Maybe the spiritual portion of Garou history was sacrificed in order to win, but leaving a hole in Garou society. Anything would have been better than the feeling that management held certain ideas that the designers wanted to work around however possible, even if that meant leaving empty portions within W5 that could be filled in later.<br /> <br /> There are a few new kernels of inspiration within the game, but nothing feels fleshed out. While there is the possibility that secrets were being held out for future supplements, this weakens the structure of the core book. Even a slightly deeper dive into these concepts would have been appreciated, but not enough background was given to help players build upon these ideas. Maybe, but more would have helped.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is just a generational things, but W5 feels like it is more an entirely different demographic than mine. While that isn't a 'bad' thing, alienating the older, core group of fans with so many changes is. Near total recons, like that of W5, can appeal to old and new fans alike, if done well. This book just misses the mark on that one point. Too much was changed just enough to hurt many long-time fans without justification. A primary example is that of the Umbra, in what used to be a location where players could spend entire campaigns for up to three months at a time has been reduced to an afterthought that becomes unusable after a few turns/minutes. The only reason I can see for a change this major feels like managerial fiat, as these rules function only to justify a strict style of gameplay, as opposed to previous editions that allowed multiple outlets for stories.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure with house rules, players could adapt the better parts of W5 for their own 'legacy' versions of the game. However, players shouldn't have to cobble together a mixed version of the old and new if the W5 just followed through with their own presumption of being an update for the game. As it is, W5 is more of a new game based on the old one than it is the latest iteration. As such, it is not the &quot;Fifth Edition&quot; of Werewolf, but it is its own thing. As I previously mentioned, it is an average game with some problems that should be resolved in future printings. It is not, however, an average update of Werewolf. Too much was not carried over, and too much was changed/added, to truly consider this to be 'Fifth Edition.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T10:53:38-08:00","id":1527660,"title":"","content":"The fourth and final phase of this review will start tomorrow, and it will focus on some of the issues and controversies raised since the news broke in the fall of 2022 that W5 had a release date. While using information outside of a game itself is not always standard for a review, in the special case of W5, I feel that it is necessary to do so. The amount of behind the scenes information that has come out since then reflects on how W5 was made, as well as the gaming industry as a whole. As such, a review of W5 based on said information would be useful in determining just why W5 has proven to be so decisive. So far, I have found it to be a just-below average game, with many mistakes and iffy ties to previous editions and other WOD games. This final phase should help clear up why such things have happened so far, and if there is any way to improve on any issues that have yet to be reconciled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T00:15:51-08:00","id":1527684,"title":"","content":"I feel in a lot of ways we're right back in that transition phase when oWOD turned into nWOD, all that 1E awkwardness of a game like Requiem. There's the attempt to do something new but the design is with one foot still stuck in the past. Here with fifth edition it gets even more awkward because the titles have to be kept while design-wise both H5 and W5 are closer to doing something CofD-like than staying true to the legacy editions.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would also work better if we publicly had a better understanding of what the bigger plan is like what are the three first supplements that are in the pipeline for W5, for example. But at this point you gotta wonder what the release schedule of Renegade even looks like when they're supposed to release supplements for V5, H5 and W5 in a year. The supplements that are coming out now in Q1 are partially there due to delays in distribution, so maybe there will be more supplements later in the year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T12:00:28-08:00","id":1527702,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART ONE</span><br /> <br /> This is going to be complicated. My presence in social media is not as great as I would like, so much of the information I'm basing this section on could be considered second-hand, at the very least. However, I still feel that I have enough of an understanding of what has been publicly going on to form an opinion and relate everything back to the creation of W5, as well as where the game is possibly headed. I know that this phase will have some mistakes, so bear with me. I'll be skipping some of the early stages of the creation of W5, as they are not really pertinent until later on in the release cycle.<br /> <br /> The Gutting of the Get<br /> <br /> When the announcement of the release date of W5 came out in the fall of 2022, it came with fanfare and many questions. The announcement started with a table listing the eleven Tribes, their Patrons/Totems, and lists of 'verbs' describing how the Tribes worked. Two Tribes were missing from that list. The first, Stargazers, had technically not been a part of the Garou Nation since Revised. The other Tribe, Get of Fenris, were more noticeable in their disappearance. In interviews soon after the announcement, the developers said that the Get would not be playable. Further announcements summed up the decision as &quot;The Get were fascist. Nobody likes fascists. So, the Tribe is not playable.&quot; <br /> <br /> Now, there were many possible ways to interpret this. First, the Get could simply be erased from the game. No mention at all. This could leave holes, but it would be a simple solution. Second, the Get could be eliminated 'off-camera' by some means. There could be a few left, mostly the ones not as bad, although there could be worse ones active too, but the Tribe would only exist as individuals, Third, a surprise, new twelfth Tribe could be formed, based on the positive attributes of the Tribe and minus the negative ones. Other Tribes had such a restructuring, so having the Get reformed wouldn't be a big deal. This would be a big secret to be revealed closer to the release or kept hidden until the actual game came out.<br /> <br /> However, the designers chose a fourth option.<br /> <br /> The Get, now renamed the Cult of Fenris, were now an antagonist, albeit one with similar aims at times. For some reason, the Tribe managed to keep a human cultural name when all others were changed. Apparently, the Cult were initially a camp of an unnamed Tribe that eventually took over their parent Tribe entirely. This even though 'camps' were never defined in W5 (normally as a division of a Tribe based on philosophical, cultural, or familial bases). How a Tribe like could keep up and expand like this, when genetic ties were removed is hard to grasp. Sure, the Tribe's Patron could chose, but the Cult is defined by their complete degeneration to Hauglosk which a new Garou cannot have. An adventure has since come out suggested how the Tribe 'recruits' new members, but there are suggestions that it was originally written for the BSD instead of the Cult. Regardless, this was a big slap in the face of a large segment of older fans.<br /> <br /> Now, many were unsure of why the developers chose this route. Many players came out saying that they never played the Get as fascist, possibly the majority of players. There were elements that could be considered fascist by some in other Tribes, but the developers possibly felt like these could be ignored without problem. And, despite a trigger-warning notice very late in the book, on the next-to-last page of the rules, there is nothing in the rules preventing players from using fascist-like tactics to further their goals. Concentrating power as a way of rebuilding the Garou Nation would be a sound decision, even if it could end up badly. <br /> <br /> Also, many people seem to be confusing other forms of vileness with fascism, even when they barely share many qualities. It is as if just calling something 'fascist' is an argument ender instead of having true debate. When people began decrying this decision online, their detailed explanations were drowned out by just such statements. Logic seemed to evaporate when the topic was brought up. This might be a generational thing on my part, but I can't seem to connect with why and how fascism became such a big deal and contentious topic. Sure, it was bad, but it was mostly historical to me, not something showing up in my current life. Even in recent news stories, I don't see why so many see such a big threat. Sometimes, I think some are just misusing the term just to make the worst possible comparisons possible, instead of looking deeply into an issue and discovering exactly what to call something.<br /> <br /> Back when the announcement on the Get not being playable came out, I mentioned something on a W20 Facebook group about how the game would deal with the Get. My idea, before the total recon would be known, was that Fenris would eat Antihelios, maybe unwillingly, and sacrifice himself to destroy the Perfect Metis, who was an avatar of the Defiler Wyrm. Its death howls would wrack the Tribe. Some would survive and join other Tribes. Others would go it alone, trying to reform the Get as something else. Others would fall, becoming a new threat. Now, a lot of this wouldn't be possible in W5, but the part about joining new Tribes is actually part of a Loresheet. There is no way of knowing exactly when in the development cycle the Loresheets were, although they reuse art from earlier in the book suggesting a rather late timeframe, especially considering how much was still being edited near the end. Maybe it was made early, as an attempt to appease older fans. Maybe it was created after the brouhaha started about losing the Get flamed online. There is no easy way to know. However, posts like mine could have influenced later decisions. <br /> <br /> While there may have been greater reasons for changing the Get, and speculations have been made on this matter, nothing greater has officially come out on this decision. The changes made to the playable Tribes were also a cause for detailed online discussions, none were as derisive as those for the Get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T12:33:46-08:00","id":1527704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527702#post1527702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This might be a generational thing on my part, but I can't seem to connect with why and how fascism became such a big deal and contentious topic. Sure, it was bad, but it was mostly historical to me, not something showing up in my current life. Even in recent news stories, I don't see why so many see such a big threat. Sometimes, I think some are just misusing the term just to make the worst possible comparisons possible, instead of looking deeply into an issue and discovering exactly what to call something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a location one rather than a generational one. From what we have seen from Muammar, the issue seems to be Nordicness itself. I have stated this many times before, but where Paradox is located (Sweden), there is very much an issue with racism towards POC and a fascist group called Sons of Odin do in fact cause trouble.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, there have been flare-ups of far-right people here in Europe recently.<br /> <br /> That and, personal anecdote, I have seen plenty of far-right-to-fascism related stickers around where I live. One even having a picture of Hitler with the text &quot;Don't you miss me now?&quot; written in Finnish.<br /> <br /> But this does not justify how the Fenrir were handled in W5. Not only is keeping the Nordicness and NPCs being mostly Nordic bad, but thanks to other tribes being at times WORSE than CoF, it implies that it is being Nordic that is the reason they are bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T13:04:05-08:00","id":1527705,"title":"","content":"In the end, thanks to the convoluted route of W5's development the Cult of Fenris we ended up with makes <i>no sense</i>.<br /> <br /> One developer's fanciful egomania plus a circuitous attempt to make sense of it in a new paradigm that ultimately failed... It's another wrong-headed idea where a WOD5E game shot itself in the foot like when the H5 corebook was so insistent on demonizing hunter-orgs.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't help that the traces of the original extreme idea of &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot; remain in the book.<br /> <br /> There were so many ways to deal with this but the version we got in the W5 corebook was clumsy, watered-down and unfocused while still being tied to this extreme idea. And it doesn't even fit into the paradigm of W5! The description of the Cult mentions Valhalla, their symbols in the sample-adventure are called runes, they're called the Cult of <i>Fenris</i>, for god's sake...! The same way JF Sambrano's idea for the Ghost Council got copy-pasted with some lazy re-writes, the Cult of Fenris is a lazy re-write of the Hunters-Entertainment-version. And it's lazy because it's clear that no effort was put into making this work. The worldbuilding surrounding the Cult of Fenris is pretty much non-existent and makes little sense. The text just mentions events that happen god-knows-when and those events... just happen because the writing is pretty lazy. The text has the vibe of &quot;Who even cares about why any of this matters or happens...?!&quot;...<br /> <br /> Of course, we can speculate why the Cult of Fenris ended up being this lazy piece of writing that makes no sense within the paradigm of the W5 corebook but in terms of reviewing the book, it can only mean one thing, I think: It's bad. The Cult of Fenris makes W5 worse. Forget all the meta-stuff, here's the W5 reason why the Cult of Fenris make W5 worse: They're a waste of space because - who cares?! The Cult of Fenris are supposed to show off the extremities of Garou-society... except it's the Age of Apocalypse and there is no Garou-society anymore. The W5 corebook makes a big stink about how little the Litany matters anymore and how much of a failure the Garou Nation has been. So why would somehing like &quot;extreme Garou behavior&quot; even be something interesting to address? It can't be too extreme, though, because you also still have BSD in the setting. Making Fenrir more extreme than BSD makes no sense (because that would mean sometimes the Wyrm followers are the better allies), making them as extreme as BSD makes no sense (because then why would you need the BSD as a faction in the first place) and if they're less extreme... then they aren't antagonists unless the idea is to kill every Garou who doesn't operate the same way the PCs do (which would make them the villains). Other than that, it would just be Garou having different opinions in a Sept. You don't need that Cult of Fenris faction for that stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:55:24-08:00","id":1527714,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, WoD5 suffers from a lot of choices that make no sense and are mostly based on the writer/dev wanting to highlight some real-life issue.<br /> <br /> The infamous ephebophile right-winger character from V5's public playtest possibly was there to critique the rise of far-right in Europe at the time. The reason the mention of Chechnya got the original team in hot water was <b>because</b> the book was published very soon after news broke about the LTGBAQ purges there.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition not being playable seems to stem from them being a religious zealot faction and the Hunter 5th ed anti-org is about rejecting the establishment.<br /> <br /> That is why, when Sambrano broke their news about the production of the book, I was mad because there clearly were no lessons learned from past mistakes. Cult of Fenris exists to decry the far-right in Nordic countries and that is pretty much it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T17:19:33-08:00","id":1527724,"title":"","content":"Honestly, when read as a whole, the situation with the Cult of Fenris is so lazy and ham-fisted that it makes for some really unfortunate implications when put into Werewolf: the Apocalypse specifically. As much as the beginning of the game bangs on about &quot;The Captialocene&quot; and how you have to &quot;rage&quot; against the destruction of the Earth or whatever, most of the non-Fenris Garou aren't doing a damn thing in this book. The vast majority of the example characters are just faffing around or even doing things contradictory to saving the planet. The gameplay, such as it is, mostly just seems to consist of sitting in one spot and protecting your city block while you wait for the world to end or you go crazy from depression or fascism. Who are the only ones actually doing anything? The only ones that actually seem to care? The Cult of Fenris, And then you have that passage near the end that suggests the players &quot;explore eco-fascism&quot;, and, well...<br /> <br /> W5 is a game that, in being so determined to shoehorn in a message that Fascism Bad regardless of trying to make it make sense within the universe that it's built (or, more accurately, haphazardly duct taped together at the last second) that it's mage a game that either says that caring = fascist, or that playing a fascist is probably the most fun you will have with this game. <i>Oops</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T17:33:15-08:00","id":1527725,"title":"","content":"Fantastic review, Toby.<br /> <br /> I give you five stars!<br /> <br /> Absolutely wonderful write up and I want to thank you for taking the time do your four part review.<br /> <br /> I do have one rebuttal, though, which I shall share in another post, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T17:39:53-08:00","id":1527726,"title":"","content":"<b>My Rebuttal: The Cult of Fenris is fine and logical in-universe</b><br /> <br /> I know, popular opinion.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, this is going to have an even more unpopular caveat. Specifically, the politics and out of universe reasons for the Get of Fenris being turned into the Cult of Fenris <i>don't matter</i>. If your opinion of the change is influenced by them, you should probably drop it because it won't help and isn't really relevant. What matters is the in-universe handling of the subject.<br /> <br /> Part of this is because is the telephone game and leaks have created the out of universe perception that the Get of Fenris have become Nazis or white supremacists. Which is objectively lying about what happened. It didn't make it to the cutting room floor and is just an idea someone had. The Swords of Heimdall? Not anywhere in the book. Racism? Not anywhere in the book.<br /> <br /> Fascism?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Comparison to Nazis?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> All of it justified in lore? Absolutely.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris have always struggled with their rage. The Get of Fenris has been battling the Beast of War for their entire career. In the end, the Beast of War won. Other clans have tetered on the edge as well with the Glass Walkers, Red Talons, and other tribes all potentially getting corrupted by the Wyrm. The original editions emphasized just how flawed and struggle orientated the Garou Nation was. These included abuse of kinfolk, honor killings, mass terrorism, and rule by strength/dueling.<br /> <br /> Because it's a horror game.<br /> <br /> REVISED had the Garou Nation start making some genuine inroads to saving its soul. They were far from perfect but getting better. It just might have been too late.<br /> <br /> The Get falling happened because they got to be the one tribe who failed to make with the times and decided to go suicidal in Ragnarok while everyone else hung back.<br /> <br /> Now they're the baddies and at war with the rest of the Garou Nation. It's a metaplot change but these things have happened before, see the Stargazers. They're bigoted evil fascists and you know what, ALL OF THEIR BIGOTRY IS FICTIONAL.<br /> <br /> And that's fine.<br /> <br /> Because that sort of thing happens in the game and there's rule for playing Get in the back of the book who have not lost their damned minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T18:23:36-08:00","id":1527727,"title":"","content":"You're still going to say that even after we've had that look backstage about what was going on? It's a purely meta move based on shit meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T18:26:33-08:00","id":1527729,"title":"","content":"&quot;Telephone game&quot;? We have direct notes from inside development that making them Actual Nazis was the intention, and they just awkwardly sanded off the white supremacist aspect off at the last second because writers like Sambrano basically had to beg for it, and even then there's hints back towards it everywhere through way of dogwhistling (why are they all Nordic and have constant references to Norse culture when all the other tribes had their cultural aspects removed? Hmmm.). You can't just pretend that the out-of-universe factors that went into this decision just don't matter when they muddy the game's tone and make the overall product worse. If anything, they give the ways that this game doesn't work a whole lot of context, and hell, make the decision-making behind other failed products context as well (looking at you, H5.)<br /> <br /> Nor can you just ignore all the game's faults and dismiss the criticisms people are giving with &quot;but it's horror tho&quot;. It being a horror game, and there being a precedent for the Garou dealing with the baggage of their own flaws doesn't mean the writers get a pass to not put things together in a way that makes sense (for example, if external factors don't matter, why have the Get fall and not the much more unstable Red Talons who are now openly cannibals? How is that not &quot;too far&quot; but the Cult is?). It doesn't really matter if the game doesn't explicitly say &quot;THE CULT ARE NAZIS AND THEY ARE THE BIG BADS OF THIS GAME FOR REAL.&quot; if the entire point of being a Garou is dismissed and more attention is given to fighting this fallen tribe than, you know. The Wyrm and the destruction of the planet, or the Umbra, or Gaia, or doing anything at all. If this wants to be a game primarily about werewolf vs. werewolf to the exclusion of actually saving the planet, it needs to not be called Werewolf: the Apocalypse anymore and drop all the metaplot baggage from its namesake. They need to just flat-out make a new game at this point. As it is now, it just pleases no one. Doesn't make sense to new players because there's way too much metaplot baggage from the old game, doesn't please old players because they spend most of their wordcount insulting their game of choice.<br /> <br /> The external factors matter because game's director really, really, really wanted this to be a game about sticking it to neo-nazis and nothing else, and has active disdain for the legacy the game shares a name with, and it shows. And it can't even do that former thing right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T19:40:49-08:00","id":1527734,"title":"","content":"If anything, that's a good argument for why the lore for the Cult makes no sense in W5: This edition's guiding principle is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. This sort of logic only shows how the lore obviously does not work in this case. This context for the Fenrir and other Tribes established in previous editions <i>does not exist in W5</i>. The Beast of War isn't a thing in W5. The Ghost Council and Galestalker Tribe don't work like that as well. You can't just point to the Native American Tribes and conveniently say &quot;Well, that lore is all gone now. Hope you weren't a fan of those Tribes.&quot; and then point to the Fenrir and be like &quot;Considering what the Fenrir used to be like in previous editions...&quot; (with an additional &quot;And if you were a fan of those guys in the past... Sucks to be you...&quot;). The only reason the Fenrir are bad guys in W5 is because of the idea of &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot;. Otherwise, it would have made more sense to bring them in line with the other Tribes by renaming them to remove any ties to human culture or ethnicity. There's no lore-reason for why the Fenrir above any other Tribe turn into the one Tribe falling to Hauglosk. Also, it completely goes against W5's idea of Tribes being these global, diverse entities with no ties to any particular human identity. How can any Tribe really &quot;fall&quot; in that conception...? Tribes have even less of an united identity in W5.<br /> <br /> But also: Why does W5 even need any Tribe to fall to Hauglosk in the first place? Take the Fenrir out of the equation and put it more generally: What exactly does the game even gain from having <i>another </i>fallen Tribe...? Because that's the thing: The extremities of Garou-behavior turned on itself, turning Garou against Garou... you already have all that with the BSD! And with no Garou-Nation, it's even less relevant who's doing what when it comes to the Tribes. I mean, consider this: If the Fenrir are supposedly these extremist, bad Garou... how did them leaving contribute to the fall of the Garou Nation? If they were truly bad, wouldn't the Garou-Nation want to get rid of them and be more united by them being gone? There was never anything like &quot;The White Howlers fell and turned into the BSD and then the Garou-Nation fell.&quot; or &quot;The Croatans sacrifices themselves, disappeared - and then the Garou-Nation fell.&quot; With the fall of the Garou Nation you just get another vaguely defined event that nobody knows about apparently. The lore just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, none of this matters because we're not talking about what makes sense in the past lore or the changes W5 has made... Instead what this is really about is one of the main-developer's personal investment in turning one particular Tribe from the previous editions into an antagonist-faction. Then of course it would make sense why erasure (like with the Native American Tribes) or reimagining (like with the Black Furies) weren't considered. Instead, this one particular Tribe got transplanted into W5 no matter how little sense it made lore-wise only so that it could be turned into an antagonist-faction.<br /> <br /> And the adventure Deepest Of Wounds shows how much the Cult of Fenris doesn't fit into W5. The notion of being worse than other Garou but not as bad as the BSD is an awkward place for the faction and the adventure ends up failing to do that balancing-act by starting with the Cult of Fenris as allies (!) of the Garou and then introduces them doing BSD-like stuff during the course of the adventure. Also, the CoF leaving the Garou Nation has been rendered meaningless by the W5 corebook because its status quo already has a fallen Garou-Nation: At the starting-point of W5, practically nobody is in the Garou Nation because there is no more Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Any argument based on &quot;But the Fenrir used to be like this and that&quot; just misses what W5 is trying to do. Pointing at past lore to make an argument for why something is the way it is in W5 is just an indication of how the lore in the W5 corebook doesn't work. Same with the Stargazers, the lore on that front doesn't make sense either.<br /> <br /> And the text in the W5 corebook <i>directly </i>links the Fenrir to Nazis as well, after all. Not seeing that link just means you ignore the W5 corebook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T20:06:12-08:00","id":1527738,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> could I possibly talk you into reading Get of Fenris Revised? It might help us discuss this topic on a better footing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T20:11:12-08:00","id":1527739,"title":"","content":"I'm confused, how much of the old lore I should take into consideration, or should I take into consideration, I don't even know anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T21:07:29-08:00","id":1527742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527726#post1527726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, the politics and out of universe reasons for the Get of Fenris being turned into the Cult of Fenris <i>don't matter</i>. If your opinion of the change is influenced by them, you should probably drop it because it won't help and isn't really relevant. What matters is the in-universe handling of the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get to demand everyone else only analyze things according to the Death of the Author or other deconstructionist methods.<br /> <br /> If you want to apply Death of the Author, that's on you. If you want the rest of us to, you need to convince us why it's important to do so. Demanding it just means your arguments don't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It didn't make it to the cutting room floor and is just an idea someone had. </div> </div> </div>This is lying by abusing the &quot;game of telephone.&quot; The head person in charge of the game wanted to make the Cult of Fenris explicitly Nazis based on the Swords of Heimdall from previous edition. He had to be talked out of it, over an extended period of time. Trying to paint it as just &quot;someone&quot; is some hardcore revisionism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Racism? Not anywhere in the book. </div> </div> </div>Please name one fascist movement that wasn't also racist. Please explain how comparing something to Nazism isn't further implying a fundamental racist character to the Cult of Fenris?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of it justified in lore? </div> </div> </div>No, it's not, because you're using lore from the old games. W5 says the old game lore doesn't count anymore. There was no Get of Fenris in W5 that was like the Get of Fenris from previous editions. The only lore that counts in W5 lore if you want to say the Cult of Fenris is justified being the way it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Get falling happened because they got to be the one tribe who failed to make with the times and decided to go suicidal in Ragnarok while everyone else hung back. </div> </div> </div>And yet, the Red Talons are still fine player characters.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Dude, we get it You need time to come around to WoD5e's fuck ups. You're going to find something you think is good, and use it to defend way more than you should, for years, until you finally can't any more. It's a pattern we're all very familiar with. But that's also draining on everyone else's patience. CT's &quot;V5 is not just the greatest VtM edition, but greatest game ever&quot; take 100, but the Cult of Fenris this time, is not endearing, enlightening, or insightful.<br /> <br /> It's just painful to watch you act out the same loop over and over instead of just realizing it's time to skip the ending that you get to every time anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-02-2024, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T21:26:16-08:00","id":1527743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527738#post1527738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> could I possibly talk you into reading Get of Fenris Revised? It might help us discuss this topic on a better footing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it presumes I haven't.<br /> <br /> Mind you, my entire premise is based on the Get NOT being racist in any RL way and getting better by Revised but I understand if that was missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T21:36:57-08:00","id":1527745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527727#post1527727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still going to say that even after we've had that look backstage about what was going on? It's a purely meta move based on shit meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean to say it's utterly irrelevant. The background doesn't matter for the world building save for the people involved in the production. For the world building, only what's on the text is important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527742#post1527742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't get to demand everyone else only analyze things according to the Death of the Author or other deconstructionist methods.<br /> <br /> If you want to apply Death of the Author, that's on you. If you want the rest of us to, you need to convince us why it's important to do so. Demanding it just means your arguments don't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying, &quot;I don't care what you think if you don't agree with my demanding that out of universe material be incorporating in analyzing in-universe portrayals&quot; is not the winning argument you think it is. You're welcome to say you don't want to discuss the issue with me but I am stating my position that I think discourse benefits from examining the material presented versus what's going on behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is lying by abusing the &quot;game of telephone.&quot; The head person in charge of the game wanted to make the Cult of Fenris explicitly Nazis based on the Swords of Heimdall from previous edition. He had to be talked out of it, over an extended period of time. Trying to paint it as just &quot;someone&quot; is some hardcore revisionism. </div> </div> </div>And there you have it there. He was talked out of it. Which is what exactly is the point I'm bringing up. There are no Swords of Heimdall, there is no Nazis, there is no death of Little Brother. The Get of Fenris as presented are villains based around their own fanaticism and devotion to the cult of Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please name one fascist movement that wasn't also racist. Please explain how comparing something to Nazism isn't further implying a fundamental racist character to the Cult of Fenris? </div> </div> </div>The Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Because they're fictional werewolves. They're black, white, and every other shade of the rainbow looking down on other Garou as well as human beings as a whole. They're every bit as racist as the Friends of Humanity against the X-men or the Galactic Empire against aliens.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;Against people who are not real because they are not real.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the way that Alt-Righters try to co-opt fiction, this is a smart move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it's not, because you're using lore from the old games. W5 says the old game lore doesn't count anymore. There was no Get of Fenris in W5 that was like the Get of Fenris from previous editions. The only lore that counts in W5 lore if you want to say the Cult of Fenris is justified being the way it is. </div> </div> </div>The old lore is absolutely not canon, except for all the stuff that is from the previous games that is alluded to. They could say none of it matters and it's a reboot but they haven't and they make frequent references to it. However, the old lore absolutely was building up to one of the Tribes falling.<br /> <br /> You know why I know that? Because it's literally one of the Apocalypse scenarios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude, we get it You need time to come around to WoD5e's fuck ups. You're going to find something you think is good, and use it to defend way more than you should, for years, until you finally can't any more. It's a pattern we're all very familiar with. But that's also draining on everyone else's patience. CT's &quot;V5 is not just the greatest VtM edition, but greatest game ever&quot; take 100, but the Cult of Fenris this time, is not endearing, enlightening, or insightful.<br /> <br /> It's just painful to watch you act out the same loop over and over instead of just realizing it's time to skip the ending that you get to every time anyway. </div> </div> </div>Actually, you can just say, &quot;CTP really loved Chicago by Night 5E and its books. He hated The Sabbat and Second Inquisition which he DID give too much slack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who claims that CBN and Cult of the Blood Gods aren't among the greatest books ever made for V:TM as a whole is wrong, though. They also are probably doing so because they want to pretend everything V5 is terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" tar