eep the get as a gaian tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-02-2024, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T18:22:45-08:00","id":1527793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527792#post1527792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part which occurred to me is their isn't any actual reason for the werewolf Sabbat to be the Get. Since its a reboot you could just as easily generate a new tribe (or even several), have that fill that niche then just keep the get as a gaian tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that the Garou don't need an equivalent of the Sabbat, not being the same type of game as Vampire. One could also argue that, even if there were a good alternate reason to have a Werewolf version of the Sabbat, it would take an entirely different person to bring it about that way, since it seems pretty well established that &quot;someone&quot; is fixated on the Get as solely being &quot;Nordic/Viking Garou&quot; and also racists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T18:38:21-08:00","id":1527795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527792#post1527792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part which occurred to me is their isn't any actual reason for the werewolf Sabbat to be the Get. Since its a reboot you could just as easily generate a new tribe (or even several), have that fill that niche then just keep the get as a gaian tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make my lengthy original response, TLDR, one of the Garou tribes falling to the Wyrm was a scenario in The Time of Judgement. &quot;A Tribe Falls&quot; is thus not unprecedented but something the WW people had for a long time on their minds.<br /> <br /> The Get falling versus the Red Talons or Little Brother is a CHOICE but it's not a choice without reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:15:57-08:00","id":1527802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527795#post1527795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To make my lengthy original response, TLDR, one of the Garou tribes falling to the Wyrm was a scenario in The Time of Judgement. &quot;A Tribe Falls&quot; is thus not unprecedented but something the WW people had for a long time on their minds.<br /> <br /> The Get falling versus the Red Talons or Little Brother is a CHOICE but it's not a choice without reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's possible. FOR THE APOCALYPSE! [/Triumph the Insult Comic Garou]<br /> <br /> A Tribe Falls was in Apocalypse for a reason. Any more of them falling meant that it was a kickoff to the end of things, and that there would be no going back to the way things were. The Red Talons unleashed methane clathrate deposits with the help of coastal spirits that caused widespread destruction; the Silver Fangs killed the BSDs and took their stuff and make Rorg launch a gigaton impact asteroid onto the Earth; the Get of Fenris get caught in a BSD-engineered White Howler repeat event and become cautious, outwardly genial infiltrators that seek to kill all the Crinos-born and cause widespread civic unrest and chaos with their presence (though Fenris can be recovered from being imprisoned in Malfeas, as he was never corrupted, only captured from the tribal homeland... which cost the Wyrm two Maeljin Incarnae in turn). It is a detonator like the other scenarios. You do not do this and intend to have a long term, playable and expandable setting afterward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:47:12-08:00","id":1527804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527792#post1527792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part which occurred to me is their isn't any actual reason for the werewolf Sabbat to be the Get. Since its a reboot you could just as easily generate a new tribe (or even several), have that fill that niche then just keep the get as a gaian tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but W5 can only rip off Forsaken a little. Recreating The Pure as a three Tribe alliance of enemy werewolves (and Forsaken still has the Bale Hounds as more direct equivalents of the BSDs), would just worsen the complaints on that end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:53:36-08:00","id":1527808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527795#post1527795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To make my lengthy original response, TLDR, one of the Garou tribes falling to the Wyrm was a scenario in The Time of Judgement. &quot;A Tribe Falls&quot; is thus not unprecedented but something the WW people had for a long time on their minds.<br /> <br /> The Get falling versus the Red Talons or Little Brother is a CHOICE but it's not a choice without reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I don't really mind having a Tribe &quot;fall&quot; or anything like that, but the way that W5 was written is, it just feels incredibly bizarre. It's the literal Apocalypse. The Wyrm has ascended. The world's days are numbered. It's only a matter of time before the Wyrm finishes killing Gaia (if she isn't already dead) and she's going to takes all of reality with her when she dies. So all of the Tribes get together and then decide that they <i>aren't</i> going to fight the Wyrm anymore. They're basically going to give up and let the world die. The only exception were the Get of Fenris who decided to keep fighting the Wyrm to try and save Gaia. And then the game's position is that this makes them bad guys (worse than the Black Spiral Dancers) and presents this idea that fighting against the Wyrm to try and save Gaia is a bad thing and players aren't supposed to do that.<br /> <br /> By having the Cult of Fenris, fascist/neo-Nazi's, as the only group actively trying to fight the Wyrm, it also creates a question in readers minds - &quot;Is working with the Cult the lesser of the two evils? If the alternative is the literal end of the world, maybe it would be better to team up with the fascist/neo-Nazis to try and save it.&quot; Which is honestly a really, really bizarre question for a work to leave readers asking themselves, but that's what I found myself wondering when I realized that, as written, nobody else seems interested in trying to save the world.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know what to make of W5 or what it expects players and Storytellers to do.<br /> <br /> There were a lot of options for having a Tribe fall. The Get were chosen specifically because of the project lead hates the Norse mythology that inspires them and wanted to turn them them into the baddest, most evil of bad guys in the game. Okay, sure, whatever. The problem is that the way this was done creates massive tonal issues that I, as a reader, just can't get past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-03-2024, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:55:01-08:00","id":1527809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527792#post1527792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part which occurred to me is their isn't any actual reason for the werewolf Sabbat to be the Get. Since its a reboot you could just as easily generate a new tribe (or even several), have that fill that niche then just keep the get as a gaian tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Werewolf already had a &quot;Sabbat-like&quot; group, the Black Spirals. Both are evil, monstrous, non-playable characters. Now Werewolf has two Sabbat groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T20:10:58-08:00","id":1527810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527809#post1527809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, Werewolf already had a &quot;Sabbat-like&quot; group, the Black Spirals. Both are evil, monstrous, non-playable characters. Now Werewolf has two Sabbat groups.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://xkcd.com/927/\" target=\"_blank\">And if people keep trying to bend games toward Vampire in every way...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T21:30:02-08:00","id":1527812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527808#post1527808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I don't really mind having a Tribe &quot;fall&quot; or anything like that, but the way that W5 was written is, it just feels incredibly bizarre. It's the literal Apocalypse. The Wyrm has ascended. The world's days are numbered. It's only a matter of time before the Wyrm finishes killing Gaia (if she isn't already dead) and she's going to takes all of reality with her when she dies. So all of the Tribes get together and then decide that they <i>aren't</i> going to fight the Wyrm anymore. They're basically going to give up and let the world die. The only exception were the Get of Fenris who decided to keep fighting the Wyrm to try and save Gaia. And then the game's position is that this makes them bad guys (worse than the Black Spiral Dancers) and presents this idea that fighting against the Wyrm to try and save Gaia is a bad thing and players aren't supposed to do that.<br /> <br /> <b>By having the Cult of Fenris, fascist/neo-Nazi's, as the only group actively trying to fight the Wyrm, it also creates a question in readers minds - &quot;Is working with the Cult the lesser of the two evils? If the alternative is the literal end of the world, maybe it would be better to team up with the fascist/neo-Nazis to try and save it.&quot; </b>Which is honestly a really, really bizarre question for a work to leave readers asking themselves, but that's what I found myself wondering when I realized that, as written, nobody else seems interested in trying to save the world.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know what to make of W5 or what it expects players and Storytellers to do.<br /> <br /> There were a lot of options for having a Tribe fall. The Get were chosen specifically because of the project lead hates the Norse mythology that inspires them and wanted to turn them them into the baddest, most evil of bad guys in the game. Okay, sure, whatever. The problem is that the way this was done creates massive tonal issues that I, as a reader, just can't get past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have read it the wrong way but I thought the way it was portrayed in the book was saying, &quot;The thing to understand is the Garou way wasn't working and when faced with the abolute undeniable indisputable fact, the Get of Fenris have decided to triple down on the Garou way and then kill any Garou who half asses it from now on.&quot; Which I admit is possibly giving it too much credit and could have phrased better but all the shitting on the Garou from the book is part of what the whole Cult of Fenris thing is about.<br /> <br /> This is definition of insanity to quote Vaas from Far Cry 3.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris is definitely MOTIVATED but every action they're doing will make things worse and are in part directly responsible for the failure to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T21:31:53-08:00","id":1527813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527810#post1527810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/927/\" target=\"_blank\">And if people keep trying to bend games toward Vampire in every way...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this is more the Technocracy than Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The BSD are the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> This is more, &quot;We have these people who ostensibly have a point but are actually the reason reality is busted.&quot; They may also develop the Misaimed FandomTM that the Union did by players agreeing with the general sentiment they have.<br /> <br /> Technocracy = Technology good<br /> <br /> Cult of Fenris = Get off your asses<br /> <br /> Except that misses again, neither is making the world BETTER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T23:09:37-08:00","id":1527816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527812#post1527812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have read it the wrong way but I thought the way it was portrayed in the book was saying, &quot;The thing to understand is the Garou way wasn't working and when faced with the abolute undeniable indisputable fact, the Get of Fenris have decided to triple down on the Garou way and then kill any Garou who half asses it from now on.&quot; Which I admit is possibly giving it too much credit and could have phrased better but all the shitting on the Garou from the book is part of what the whole Cult of Fenris thing is about.<br /> <br /> This is definition of insanity to quote Vaas from Far Cry 3.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris is definitely MOTIVATED but every action they're doing will make things worse and are in part directly responsible for the failure to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to tl;dr a bit of my own flagged post:<br /> <br /> The big problem with this is that W5 only tells us this out-of-character via authorial intent sidebars. There's no &quot;show&quot; to that &quot;tell&quot; in the lore of the world-building.<br /> <br /> So we, as the audience, know the Cult of Fenris are only going to make things worse because the authors told us that's true. The characters living in that world don't know this. All the characters know is that the Cult is trying to do something to meet the moment, and nobody else seems to be even making an attempt. Anyone that tries to do something different from tripling down on old school Garou methods still builds up Hauglosk and becomes a Cult of Fenris-lite unlayable character anyway.<br /> <br /> If we're going to compare things to Mage? It's the Technocracy if the Traditions never formed to oppose them and the PCs are just small groups of Orphans making do, and if they try to do something they either turn into the Technocracy, the Nephandi, or the Mauraders, or they turn into something different, but ultimately just as bad. The world building lacks the counterpoint to make the Cult of Fenris wrong from an in-character perspective. We only have the authors telling us they're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T00:02:06-08:00","id":1527817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527812#post1527812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have read it the wrong way but I thought the way it was portrayed in the book was saying, &quot;The thing to understand is the Garou way wasn't working and when faced with the abolute undeniable indisputable fact, the Get of Fenris have decided to triple down on the Garou way and then kill any Garou who half asses it from now on.&quot; Which I admit is possibly giving it too much credit and could have phrased better but all the shitting on the Garou from the book is part of what the whole Cult of Fenris thing is about.<br /> <br /> This is definition of insanity to quote Vaas from Far Cry 3.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris is definitely MOTIVATED but every action they're doing will make things worse and are in part directly responsible for the failure to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, the game gives no viable alternative. It's created a dichotomy of either futility fighting until the end like the Cult or just giving up. If fighting the Wyrm won't stop the world from dying, then the game desperately needs a group that's trying or implementing some sort of alternative. <br /> <br /> As is, if the destruction of Gaia and the death is inevitable, then it positions the Cult of Fenris in this weirdly heroic light. If death is inevitable then the most &quot;punk&quot; thing would be to die raging on your feet rather than rolling over and giving up.<br /> <br /> From an out-of-character perspective, we know the Cult is doomed. But we're also led to believe that the world is doomed anyway. Nobody is fighting to save it other than the Cult. And from an in-character perspective, well, maybe the Cult could save the world. It's not likely but it's more likely than what anyone else is trying (which is essentially nothing).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T00:27:01-08:00","id":1527819,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the way Apocalypse is handled in W5 feels like a remnant from the first iteration. There, since it was a continuation, the umbra going nuts and the Caerns dying made it all seem apocalyptic. But we don't have that context in W5.<br /> <br /> Also, with the focus on the CoF, I have to ponder what role do the BSDs serve in W5? Since the CoF is strongly implied to be the main threat, BSDs are left picking up the scraps. Which, given CoF are still fighting for Gaia and BSDs are not, results in the BSDs having little to do despite being the actual opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T00:59:11-08:00","id":1527821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527819#post1527819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the way Apocalypse is handled in W5 feels like a remnant from the first iteration. There, since it was a continuation, the umbra going nuts and the Caerns dying made it all seem apocalyptic. But we don't have that context in W5.<br /> <br /> Also, with the focus on the CoF, I have to ponder what role do the BSDs serve in W5? Since the CoF is strongly implied to be the main threat, BSDs are left picking up the scraps. Which, given CoF are still fighting for Gaia and BSDs are not, results in the BSDs having little to do despite being the actual opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The BSD's are in an odd spot. From the BsD narrative perspective, they've already won. Gaia is dead, or dying, and there's nothing that can be done to save her. The match has been called, the Wyrm is victorious and all that's left to do is celebrate.<br /> <br /> As such, they're not really in an active antagonistic role in the setting. They're not going to be too interested in dying, trying to fight other werewolves. For them, there's only 3 future possibilities for the remaining Garou Nation. 1) Futility dying trying to turn back the clock. 2) Giving up and committing suicide in the throes of Harano. 3) Recognizing the Wyrm's ascendancy and walking the Spiral. The BSD's will believe those are the only three options left.<br /> <br /> Most likely, at this point the Black Spirals are going to start setting themselves up as kings, coming out of the shadows to enjoy their success. Maybe they'll come into conflict with the PCs because they want to take over their caern or whatever, but they probably aren't interested in fighting Garou anymore, generally speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T01:08:58-08:00","id":1527823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527821#post1527821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely, at this point the Black Spirals are going to start setting themselves up as kings, coming out of the shadows to enjoy their success. Maybe they'll come into conflict with the PCs because they want to take over their caern or whatever, but they probably aren't interested in fighting Garou anymore, generally speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where the biggest rub comes in, setting themselves up as kings would mean they no longer hide since there is no reason. Which would mean the biggest face of the werewolf kind would be the BSDs since they seem to be doing fine.<br /> <br /> But that is not how W5 presents itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T01:23:30-08:00","id":1527824,"title":"","content":"I mean in one of the first released adventure scenarios a Sept literally sits on their arses and watches a Caern get bodied by a Cultist and does nothing, a single Cultist simply walks in and demands literally every resource the Sept has and barring a couple of grumbles the entire Sept just rolls over.......<br /> <br /> Sure the Cultists are going about things the wrong way but we know from the adventures background that while they were away they were shutting down factories, killing Fomori and raiding animal testing labs while the rest of the Sept sat around with their thumbs up their arses.<br /> <br /> The adventure does go out of its way to make one of the Cultists explicitly a neo-nazi just so we don't lose that thread but they are dead anyway and play no active part in the story so exist solely to remind us that the Cult are Fascists.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure what the lesson is supposed to be.....other than that those who take action are bad because their taking action will inevitably make them worse people or that sitting down and letting the world end is the far lesser of two evils or.............fucked if I know. <br /> <br /> Every single member of the Fenrir before they fell to Hauglosk and became the Cult are described as caustic, aggresive and terrible people to be around and spirits dislike them for using spirits as disposable tools.<br /> <br /> Then we come to the ' someone really liked that scene from Clockwork Orange but didn't actually understand it' that is The Maggot Symphony and its accompanying torture porn........cos apparently the Facist groups around my way that are recruiting young lads to their cause through Youtube personalities, giving hopeless young men targets to blame for their lives and absolving them of any actual responsibility and self reflection are going about it wrong......they should instead be driving metal spikes through their backs and streaming constant sound and images while shouting three words at them.......<br /> <br /> I'm putting this somewhere around the Gooshy Gooze level of stupid and I think thats being generous.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T01:25:43-08:00","id":1527825,"title":"","content":"In one place the W5 corebook does talk about a way that the book's negative outlook on Garou in general can be addressed (from the sidebar &quot;Changing Ways&quot; pg 47):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tonight, Gaia needs more than murderous maniacs\u2026 which is one of the tragedies of the Garou, in that they are so prone to Rage. Rage cannot solve every problem, however, so each Garou needs to find how they can best fulfill their spiritual charge \u2014 <b>or whether they must abandon it.</b> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> So, step one to dealing with the Age of Apocalypse: Don't be a Garou. You're instantly &quot;winning&quot; the game by just turning to your ST and say &quot;My character loses the wolf, never shapeshifts again and gives up on being a Garou.&quot;. And that's it! Problem solved! No lengthy gaming-sessions and handwringing over what to do as a Garou with the slow realization that being a Garou means being a failure and any effort to change things for the better is futile.<br /> <br /> What's entirely missing from W5 is its Anarch-equivalent. The Camarilla-equivalent, the Garou-Nation, has been blown up and with the BSD and the Cult of Fenris you have two Sabbat-like factions which are considered to be bad - but W5 has no dedicated &quot;Let's do something new.&quot;-faction. So practically all the paths a Garou can pursue have already been deemed pointless or been thrown into the &quot;That's evil and wrong.&quot;-box.<br /> <br /> And without that, the book's overly pessimistic outlook makes it hard to understand why anyone would even wanna play as a Garou in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T06:29:40-08:00","id":1527836,"title":"","content":"My best guess with the &quot;Let's do something&quot; faction missing is that if ronin were present, no one would want to join a tribe.<br /> <br /> I do ponder how are the W5 games going on solving this issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T08:35:38-08:00","id":1527841,"title":"","content":"With apologies for everyone I couldn't respond to because of my mishaps with posting, my short version of assuming this goes like this.<br /> <br /> &quot;The key to understanding this is that this is about going past the Apocalypse in Werewolf: The Apocalyspe.&quot;<br /> <br /> I write for a fanzine called GRIMDARK MAGAZINE and it's basically about incredibly bleak and antihero filled fantasy or sci-fi. It takes its name from Warhammer 40K and it reminds me a bit of a discussion I had about how to do the best Tabletop RPG Warhammer 40K game you could do. Most people assume that it would be about Space Marines, secret cults, and the extreme measures to save the world.<br /> <br /> My answer would be, &quot;Failure.&quot;<br /> <br /> The ideal Warhammer 40K game I'd love to play, preferably with Inquisitors is coping with the concept of failure on a massive scale. That the problem is impossible to deal with individually and the rot is intense and humantiy's Imperium WILL be destroyed by its various enemies. Maybe not today, maybe not a thousand years from now but inevitably and probably deserves to be. Knowing that this is absolutely impossible to prevent--what do you do?<br /> <br /> * Try to fix things anyway?<br /> * Go down in the blaze of glory?<br /> * Try to find individual joy?<br /> * Preserve some small fragment instead of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> I feel less off-put by W5 because I get that they're attempting to essentially put the Garou in a position of having freedom to do a lot more of what they want to with their powers. The war is over and you lost. Maybe there will be something else or maybe you just have to make time with what you have left. I write a lot of Noir and Punk books and that attitude applies to Cthulhu Armageddon (which is set after the Great Old Ones rise and humanity is going extinct--and there's nothing that can stop it), Moon Cops on the Moon (which is about being on a corrupt cyberpunk dystopia as the one honest cop), and Lucifer's Star (which is about a pilot whose side lost the Galactic Civil War--but they kind of had it coming).<br /> <br /> Or to use another example, FIREFLY.<br /> <br /> Mal and company aren't going to overthrow the Alliance. They have irretrivebaly lost. However, they can survive themselves for a time.<br /> <br /> It's very DARK SOULS original recipe I suppose.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can do a big &quot;What if we did X, Y, and Z and resurrected Gaia!&quot; but you can also do, &quot;I can't save the world but maybe I can save these campers!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:04:22-08:00","id":1527843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527841#post1527841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you can do a big &quot;What if we did X, Y, and Z and resurrected Gaia!&quot; but you can also do, &quot;I can't save the world but maybe I can save these campers!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where I think we are talking past each other and just have differing opinions.<br /> <br /> Because what differs WtA from Warhammer 40k or Dark Souls, is the focus and the themes. 40k, at its most hopeful, is about saving a planet or some people. But more often it is about the meat grinder that is the universe and how even the factions with the best intentions end up fighting because of intolerance. Dark Souls is about entering a pre-ruined world and figuring out why it happened, with a side of trying to fix things on the side.<br /> <br /> What neither of these games have that WtA does, is the role of the Apocalypse and the pollution of the environment in the game. In 40k, you got worlds upon worlds upon worlds. Destroying one is not the end of the game, you can find another Death World to hang out in. In Dark Souls, everything is already ruined and your job is to put together the pieces of how and why. But in WtA, the very title hints at the focus; the Apocalypse. Not the aftermath or how we got here, the very end of this one world.<br /> <br /> In addition, even in W5 a massive part of the game focuses on the way the planet is suffering and how people are hurting other people. The Wyrm, Fomori, the BSDs, the Weaver, etc. are all symbols of some way humanity and nature are being hurt. But the world is not destroyed yet, the end hasn't come yet. The tagline is When Will You Rage, meaning; When will you take action against all this wrongness?<br /> <br /> WtA is about CARING so much that it makes you RAGE. This does not apply for 40k because its a large scale game. This doesn't apply to Dark Souls because everything was already lost.<br /> <br /> So when that sort of game presents action as negative and sitting on your butt positive, you get why most of us have issues.<br /> <br /> Teal Deer; WtA is not the same genre as Dark Souls or 40k, and that is why the non-action annoys people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:32:15-08:00","id":1527847,"title":"","content":"There's also the issue that unlike Dark Souls and WH40k, WtA has to work with one huge limitation: Its wider context/setting is our world in the present. With Dark Souls and WH40k and its completely fictional settings you have a lot of room to express specific moods and themes in its worldbuilding. There's a strict limitation to how far you can go with the &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;-bit in W5. You could get a lot more out of the setting if the setting were actually a world in the middle of a global Apocalypse - but it isn't. It's our world. Right now. Bad stuff is happening but nothing world-ending-bad is happening at the moment. I'd wager the majority of people in Omaha, Nebraska don't believe they're living in an &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;. That's where W5 just got way too ambitious and didn't consider the implications of its worldbuilding. There are a couple of contradictions that the W5 corebook failed to resolve but in this particular case it's this: If the world is actually ending (experiencing the type of Apocalypse WtA is about), then you can't have our real world in the present as a backdrop. If you have our real world in the present as a backdrop, the setting won't come anywhere close to deserving the moniker of &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;. The previous editions got this right: &quot;It's looking bad out there and it seems like it can only get worse.&quot; That's where you want to be in terms of the titular Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> W5 would have to go way further in its worldbuilding to deserve a description like &quot;grimdark&quot;. In the way it's presented in the W5 corebook the game is currently not grimdark. And what is in its stead...? Who knows... That's part of the issue. Age of Apocalypse is a central part of W5 but the W5 corebook isn't very committed to that aspect - outside of shitting on Garou constantly, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:44:07-08:00","id":1527849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527847#post1527847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the issue that unlike Dark Souls and WH40k, WtA has to work with one huge limitation: Its wider context/setting is our world in the present. With Dark Souls and WH40k and its completely fictional settings you have a lot of room to express specific moods and themes in its worldbuilding. There's a strict limitation to how far you can go with the &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;-bit in W5. You could get a lot more out of the setting if the setting were actually a world in the middle of a global Apocalypse - but it isn't. It's our world. Right now. Bad stuff is happening but nothing world-ending-bad is happening at the moment. I'd wager the majority of people in Omaha, Nebraska don't believe they're living in an &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why the &quot;Eh, can't save the world&quot; mentality doesn't work. Because it is presenting real life issues and problems and then asking the player characters how they can solve them as chosen of Gaia.<br /> <br /> So when the faction meant to be bad is the only one taking action? It says action is not the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:52:28-08:00","id":1527863,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART TWO</span><br /> <br /> Put a Trace on That Artwork<br /> <br /> After the initial online 'discussions' about the way W5 was going, Renegade/Paradox decided to preview some of the Tribes with their write-ups, based on the results of a poll. Surprisingly, the Glass Walkers won. I honestly didn't think they were the most popular Tribe, but I never saw the tabulated results. Anyway, soon after the preview came up, someone noticed how one of the figures looked familiar. Now, tracing an image to create your own art is accepted, especially when things like tight deadlines are involved. However, the subject involved doesn't like his image used without his consent. A whole new round of speculation began, that only increased when more previews came out with artwork that looked like it had been traced from known individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, this could mean a few things. Let's give the benefit of the doubt and say that the art department hadn't gotten around to okaying the said artwork because of unexpected results in the polling. They were just getting around to it when, boom, they had to preview it and found out about the tracing. Renegade quickly announced that any depictions would be fixed in the final version. At the very least, this meant that the editing process was very rushed. I have already mentioned the many errors that crept in that weren't caught in time. When a fixed deadline is involved and problems come up, you need to change the deadline. Instead, only the suspect artwork got changed. A company that can't bear to adapt to sudden problems isn't one that garners much trust.<br /> <br /> A second possibility is that the art director and artists never communicated about certain possible issues. The art director should have told artists to make sure that got permission to use the images of any models they used, even if it was secondhand via tracing. Or make it less identifiable, at least. The artist should have informed the art director about their methods of creation, especially with techniques like tracing, so any issues with public figures could be avoided. Either way, this lack of communication does not bode well for a company and their freelancers. If basic communications about such basic standards aren't followed, what else are they not doing correctly.<br /> <br /> Third, maybe no one understood about the feelings about the subject in question. Just plain ignorance. Not a great excuse, but a relatable one. Considering the recent debacle about the Fenrir, one would expect such research would be made to prevent more online flaming, not to mention litigation. Again, if something like standard research isn't conducted by a company, what should a player expect about the quality of that company's products.<br /> <br /> Of course, maybe no one cared about doing any such things at all. Laziness. This isn't a promising outlook either. Considering how much of the rest of W5 was left empty, this cold be the case. No one cared to do anything else, until observant people spoke out and brought this problem to their attention. It did get W5 a bit more attention than his it would have had at the time.<br /> <br /> This brings up a final possibility. It is the least likely, but still within the realm of plausibility. What if the artwork was never the finished version, and it was never going to be published? There is a school of advertising that says &quot;any publicity is good publicity.&quot; While the known artwork did get changed for the final product, some of the other artwork that wasn't previewed may have been just as noticeably traced as well. It has been pointed out that at least one of the wolf illustrations looks like it was traced. Some of the other figures are in somewhat familiar poses, if not outright known. The artwork got altered and inserted rather quickly, relatively late in the process, especially when other errors were overlooked and not corrected.<br /> <br /> I am not sure which of these possibilities would put this situation in good light, especially that last one. Either we are dealing with a company that doesn't know what it is doing, doesn't care what it is doing, or doesn't mind possible litigation to trick potential buyers into looking into its new product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T12:14:22-08:00","id":1527864,"title":"","content":"The artist liberally uses tracing in their artwork, which as you said isn't a bad thing. But what made things worse was this; The same artist did multiple books for Renegade at the same time and so their quality dropped. When the artist is given time to refine their art, it looks great and not as obviously based on something.<br /> <br /> But this was not the case and at times it was clear the artist was just picking images from google images. Why that is an issue, is that at least one of the images was clearly not a stock photo but a combination of two pictures of a wolf with mange taken by Yellowstone scientists.<br /> <br /> The issue for me is that they were clearly rushed and they didn't use legal means to get their stock art or refine them enough to make them unique. On top of everything, the reason the Glass Walker image had to be changed was that it depicted facial tattoos that are not allowed to be copied. Aside from turning a Mongolian into a Sami.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T12:36:29-08:00","id":1527865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527849#post1527849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is why the &quot;Eh, can't save the world&quot; mentality doesn't work. Because it is presenting real life issues and problems and then asking the player characters how they can solve them as chosen of Gaia.<br /> <br /> So when the faction meant to be bad is the only one taking action? It says action is not the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it would be easy to fix, not just easy, it would be a necessary thing: Just explain what the counterpoint to the Cult of Fenris viewpoint is. And it's insane that W5 doesn't have one. In Deepest of Wounds, the Cult of Fenris NPCs are evil but they have been going around doing stuff. Meanwhile, the Sept at the center of the story is... just there. There's no sense of non-Fenrir-Garou doing anything important in particular. And the corebook doesn't help with that either. Aside from giving up and dying, there isn't much to W5. But with the Cult of Fenris you have the additional notion that wanting to die in glorious battle is bad (and the Fenrir are Nazis anyway, so now it's really clear that they're bad guys).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527863#post1527863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Put a Trace on That Artwork<br /> <br /> After the initial online 'discussions' about the way W5 was going, Renegade/Paradox decided to preview some of the Tribes with their write-ups, based on the results of a poll. Surprisingly, the Glass Walkers won. I honestly didn't think they were the most popular Tribe, but I never saw the tabulated results. Anyway, soon after the preview came up, someone noticed how one of the figures looked familiar. Now, tracing an image to create your own art is accepted, especially when things like tight deadlines are involved. However, the subject involved doesn't like his image used without his consent. A whole new round of speculation began, that only increased when more previews came out with artwork that looked like it had been traced from known individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having uncovered a couple of the source-images for these traced drawings myself, I think there are more issues with what has happened here than using particular people's looks without permission. As mentioned, there's nothing wrong with tracing when it's used as a reference. Some gesture, expression or the way the light falls on an object... all sorts of things one can trace in a drawing to support one's drawing-skills. Where it starts to get dicey is when it isn't just about tracing anymore but copying instead. Now there are also copyright-free databases you can use as reference-images, so in those cases copyright wasn't an issue. But even if you were to just turn a photo from such a database into a 1-to-1 drawing-copy, a good artist should still mention the database in the credits (especially when so much of the photo has been traced like in the drawings in W5). Photos from such databases have been used and traced by the artist. No database is mentioned in the credits, though. (For example, that refinery on the cover is a traced photo from such a database)<br /> <br /> And then there are the coyprighted images. At one point, a photo of a German cyberpunk fashion-line had been traced or another time it was a female Israeli soldier. It doesn't surprise me that a particular Maori activist's face would end up getting traced when this artist clearly didn't care what photos he used for his traced drawings. And he wouldn't just use the photos as a reference but would completely copy them instead. For example, one drawing was a mashup of a traced photo of the singer from the group Heilung and a traced photo of a DJ living in Seattle (with no rights to use either photo for something like this).<br /> <br /> The GW-preview also immediately showcased why having lax standards when it comes to art can become an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527863#post1527863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure which of these possibilities would put this situation in good light, especially that last one. Either we are dealing with a company that doesn't know what it is doing, doesn't care what it is doing, or doesn't mind possible litigation to trick potential buyers into looking into its new product.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, so far, we can be sure about two things: Both the art-director and the artist who could be considered to be the two people closest to the issue are still working for Paradox. The latest V5 book Blood Sigils still lists the same Art Director in the WOD-team and that same artist also contributed art to the Blood Sigils book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T12:41:29-08:00","id":1527866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527843#post1527843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is where I think we are talking past each other and just have differing opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Because the game absolutely isn't about giving up and giving up is viewed as a mental illness (neuraotypical here). Depression and defeatism is as bad as fanaticism.<br /> <br /> It's just acknowledging the Garou can't fix things with talons and can't do it alone.<br /> <br /> HUMANITY (us because this is the real world) might save the world but the Garou have to reorientate their thinking. They have to basically do what they can do and have faith in humanity that it will do its own part in all this.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:00:49-08:00","id":1527868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527866#post1527866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> Because the game absolutely isn't about giving up and giving up is viewed as a mental illness (neuraotypical here). Depression and defeatism is as bad as fanaticism.<br /> <br /> It's just acknowledging the Garou can't fix things with talons and can't do it alone.<br /> <br /> HUMANITY (us because this is the real world) might save the world but the Garou have to reorientate their thinking. They have to basically do what they can do and have faith in humanity that it will do its own part in all this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You say the game isn't about giving up, but the 'not giving up' state you present is basically saying you shouldn't play a garou. You should play a human who can actually make a difference.<br /> <br /> So the re-orienting you suggest is basically losing the wolf and doing what you can do as a human. Giving up your gift, your forms, your rites, the umbra, etc. Because no one of those can actually help Gaia.<br /> <br /> Because to stay a garou is to play defense and hope humanity fixes itself.<br /> <br /> How is that not giving up?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:06:07-08:00","id":1527869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527849#post1527849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is why the &quot;Eh, can't save the world&quot; mentality doesn't work. Because it is presenting real life issues and problems and then asking the player characters how they can solve them as chosen of Gaia.<br /> <br /> So when the faction meant to be bad is the only one taking action? It says action is not the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feeds into a larger theme I believe I've discussed before: W5 is plainly written from the perspective of a Neo-Liberal Centrist who has already given up.<br /> <br /> It's not that the world has actually ended yet. It's that the ecological (and societal) collapse is drawing ever closer. And the Neo-Liberal mindset cannot conceive of actually fixing or arresting this process. At least, not while maintaining the Status Quo.<br /> <br /> It's Capitalist Realism, baked into the fabric of an edition of Werewolf. It's easier to imagine the end of the world than the end of Capitalism. Which is why W5 takes space out of its book to defend Capitalism and absolve it of systemic responsibility for causing most of our problems. To a Neo-Liberal Centrist, forcing Capitalism to change or even die to save the world is unthinkable. And anyone who thinks it's a good idea is either a child who needs to be paternalistically dissuaded from &quot;rash action&quot;, or is a villain indistinguishable from the Fascists marching in the streets.<br /> <br /> Of course, Neo-Liberal Centrists often have a very impoverished understanding of what Fascism is, why people are radicalized into it, and how it differs from leftwing praxis. To a Centrist, &quot;both sides are the same&quot;. Hence, why Hauglosk is a blunt system for tracking one's &quot;corruption from wanting action&quot;, applied equally to the Cult of Fenris (who are all but stated to be literal Nazis) and any Garou who want to take the fight to the Wyrm &quot;too much&quot;.<br /> <br /> Earlier editions of WtA asked &quot;When Do You Rage?&quot;, because it took for granted that, in the face of systems trying to kill the world and everyone in it, Rage is not merely acceptable, but the only RATIONAL response. It was merely a question of how far you need to be pushed to act.<br /> <br /> W5 answers &quot;When Do You Rage?&quot; with a resounding &quot;Never, Because Rage Is Always Bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> An attitude that is not merely unhelpful in an age when the Status Quo freely uses all types of violence to protect itself (physical, economic, legal, etc), but deeply unsatisfying as the premise for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:13:26-08:00","id":1527871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527866#post1527866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> Because the game absolutely isn't about giving up and giving up is viewed as a mental illness (neuraotypical here). Depression and defeatism is as bad as fanaticism.<br /> <br /> It's just acknowledging the Garou can't fix things with talons and can't do it alone.<br /> <br /> HUMANITY (us because this is the real world) might save the world but the Garou have to reorientate their thinking. They have to basically do what they can do and have faith in humanity that it will do its own part in all this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, I get that but in terms of game-design this is terrible. W5 still asks players to play Garou. So if Garou have no impact on the larger setting because it's actually up to humanity to save the world then that means you're asking players to play characters with no agency. And if the PCs have no agency then you don't have a story. That's the issue: What story are you even supposed to tell with Garou-PCs in W5? A Pack of Garou-PCs kills a bunch of Fomori, saves the day but as ST following the guidelines of the W5 corebook, you step in and remind everybody that this hasn't changed a thing (&quot;Anyway, the world is still doomed, Gaia's still dying unless humanity can get its shit together and you Garou-PCs beating the crap out of some Fomori has nothing to do with that... Anybody excited for the next adventure?&quot;). That's not a game.<br /> <br /> And W5 is absolutely about giving up - by omission. The path to make a difference is <i>not </i>in the book. Even mechanically Harano and Hauglosk are <i>inevitable </i>for every Garou-PC. That's another way you could refocus W5: By just admitting that playing a Garou means playing a concept that's all about &quot;doomed to failure&quot; and similar to a PC in a Cthulhu-game there are only various types of bad endings waiting for the PC. The game isn't focused on that, though, but it's partially already there in how punishing Harano and Hauglosk are and in how pessimism dominates <i>every </i>description of Garou in the book.<br /> <br /> Also, refocusing on that type of horror in this case seems a bit silly to me. This is a game where you're playing werewolves. Your character can shapeshift into a super-powerful monster (aka Crinos) and use supernatural spirit-powers (Gifts). I don't think the horror should be focused on futility in that context (because then why make it a game about werewolves in the first place...?). And the tagline is &quot;When will you rage?&quot;, anyway. That isn't a tagline for a game where it's all about &quot;acknowledging that Garou can't fix things&quot;.<br /> <br /> If W5 strived to be radically different from previous editions, it failed... but it also failed in honoring what previous editions were going for. W5 is in that awkward place where it ended up doing neither and ended up being unfocused because of that. When it comes to W5's future, the game has to pick a lane: &quot;When will you rage?&quot; doesn't work for a game where Garou can't fix anything and the relentless horror of the Age of Apocalypse, Harano and Hauglosk doesn't work with a game of chasing Renown, beating the crap out of your enemies and honoring Tribal Patron-Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:37:27-08:00","id":1527873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527795#post1527795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To make my lengthy original response, TLDR, one of the Garou tribes falling to the Wyrm was a scenario in The Time of Judgement. &quot;A Tribe Falls&quot; is thus not unprecedented but something the WW people had for a long time on their minds.<br /> <br /> The Get falling versus the Red Talons or Little Brother is a CHOICE but it's not a choice without reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that really neccissary? It was a cool idea for the time of judgement book (although tellingly I've never used any of the books in a game except implying the existance of the unanmed) but this is a differant setting and this is the core book. We're looking to build a setting here, not conclude one. Introducing more bad guy tribes gives you stuff to build on and let's you keep the get and ideas to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:40:21-08:00","id":1527874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527868#post1527868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say the game isn't about giving up, but the 'not giving up' state you present is basically saying you shouldn't play a garou. You should play a human who can actually make a difference.<br /> <br /> So the re-orienting you suggest is basically losing the wolf and doing what you can do as a human. Giving up your gift, your forms, your rites, the umbra, etc. Because no one of those can actually help Gaia.<br /> <br /> Because to stay a garou is to play defense and hope humanity fixes itself.<br /> <br /> How is that not giving up?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is basically the exact opposite of my point. Because the point is that saving the world is not something that should be your PCs goals and it was the hubris and insane meglomania of the Garou that it was solely their job to do so in the first place.<br /> <br /> To switch genres again for an example.<br /> <br /> PC: I WANT TO SAVE THE WORLD!<br /> <br /> Villager: We need help! The kobolds are attacking our village!<br /> <br /> PC: No, I said SAVE THE WORLD.<br /> <br /> The game has reorientated its focus. Part of what I meant with Dark Souls is the fact that the ending of the game reveals....<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">you can't actually save the world. The light you restore would just be a little time longer before it goes back to the same problem as before. Another solution is to let the Light go out and start teaching people to live in the Dark. Which I think is the better one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris wants to save the world, but on their terms.<br /> <br /> They can't accept that the point should be they should be using their claws for good but incriminental progress or just for its own sake. The Garou may be doomed but they should be focused on what they can achieve here and now over some nebulous cause that warped humanity as well as themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:45:00-08:00","id":1527875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527804#post1527804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but W5 can only rip off Forsaken a little. Recreating The Pure as a three Tribe alliance of enemy werewolves (and Forsaken still has the Bale Hounds as more direct equivalents of the BSDs), would just worsen the complaints on that end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more Sabbat since w5 is heavily influenced. Have 2-4 wolf Sabbat tribes and then imply their are supplementary members of other tribes. If you're going to rip of forsaken and vtm you may as well do it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:46:30-08:00","id":1527876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527871#post1527871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thematically, I get that but in terms of game-design this is terrible. W5 still asks players to play Garou. So if Garou have no impact on the larger setting because it's actually up to humanity to save the world then that means you're asking players to play characters with no agency. And if the PCs have no agency then you don't have a story. That's the issue: What story are you even supposed to tell with Garou-PCs in W5? A Pack of Garou-PCs kills a bunch of Fomori, saves the day but as ST following the guidelines of the W5 corebook, you step in and remind everybody that this hasn't changed a thing (&quot;Anyway, the world is still doomed, Gaia's still dying unless humanity can get its shit together and you Garou-PCs beating the crap out of some Fomori has nothing to do with that... Anybody excited for the next adventure?&quot;). That's not a game.<br /> <br /> And W5 is absolutely about giving up - by omission. The path to make a difference is <i>not </i>in the book. Even mechanically Harano and Hauglosk are <i>inevitable </i>for every Garou-PC. That's another way you could refocus W5: By just admitting that playing a Garou means playing a concept that's all about &quot;doomed to failure&quot; and similar to a PC in a Cthulhu-game there are only various types of bad endings waiting for the PC. The game isn't focused on that, though, but it's partially already there in how punishing Harano and Hauglosk are and in how pessimism dominates <i>every </i>description of Garou in the book.<br /> <br /> Also, refocusing on that type of horror in this case seems a bit silly to me. This is a game where you're playing werewolves. Your character can shapeshift into a super-powerful monster (aka Crinos) and use supernatural spirit-powers (Gifts). I don't think the horror should be focused on futility in that context (because then why make it a game about werewolves in the first place...?). And the tagline is &quot;When will you rage?&quot;, anyway. That isn't a tagline for a game where it's all about &quot;acknowledging that Garou can't fix things&quot;.<br /> <br /> If W5 strived to be radically different from previous editions, it failed... but it also failed in honoring what previous editions were going for. W5 is in that awkward place where it ended up doing neither and ended up being unfocused because of that. When it comes to W5's future, the game has to pick a lane: &quot;When will you rage?&quot; doesn't work for a game where Garou can't fix anything and the relentless horror of the Age of Apocalypse, Harano and Hauglosk doesn't work with a game of chasing Renown, beating the crap out of your enemies and honoring Tribal Patron-Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, I'm a little surprised at that reaction because it's hardly a new one in games or even fiction in general.<br /> <br /> I bring up noir and detective fiction because that's basically the rules of the genre.<br /> <br /> &quot;The system is corrupt, the world sucks, and there is no possible systemic change that is going to happen. However, our protagonist can do THIS good thing now.&quot; To stick with the camper metaphor, saving the campers isn't going to meaningful affect the cosmic battle between good and evil that evil is winning.<br /> <br /> It does, however, save THESE campers and THIS day and has a meaningful impact on THOSE people.<br /> <br /> It's more or less a running theme in THE WITCHER where Geralt tries to be a hero of the typical fantasy mold but he's in a world where kings and aristocrats are all corrupt scheming bastards with petty wars fought for no good reason. So when Geralt saves a child, he's usually dealing with the fact there's a war going on that will destroy whole villages. I find that really evocative and interesting. Like playing in a cyberpunk setting where your PCs aren't going to overthrow Arasaka but maybe stop some slavers.<br /> <br /> This is also the 2nd time a WW game has reorientated itself this way.<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension went from being, &quot;Destroy the Technocracy! Blow up their base on Jupiter&quot; to &quot;save Becky from the Umbrood possessing her.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T14:20:16-08:00","id":1527878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527874#post1527874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is basically the exact opposite of my point. Because the point is that saving the world is not something that should be your PCs goals and it was the hubris and insane meglomania of the Garou that it was solely their job to do so in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you are taking the 'save the world' sentence and taking it too literally. Because it has always been taking out the Kobolts and helping the village that saves the world in WtA. In no game I have been in has there been this one big 'Save the World' quest or characters refusing to handle bane infestations.<br /> <br /> The incremental actions that you are talking about have been the norm in WtA. At most you create a Caern, go on an umbral quest or destroy a Hive. They do it to save Gaia, but saving Gaia is chipping away at a massive block slowly.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you don't have an overarching goal, why are you taking the incremental actions in the first place? Taking out a herd of banes makes the city block safer and if the city block is safer then more positive spirits can exist there, which means the area can heal.<br /> <br /> But more importantly; W5 is saying even the incremental actions are too much. In The Deepest Wounds, only the CoF took ANY action, while the PC sept just existed. The ideal is to sit in your caern and guard it, not helping the territory around you in small ways. Unless you are killing and eating scores of people, that is seen as okay for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T14:29:26-08:00","id":1527881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527876#post1527876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The system is corrupt, the world sucks, and there is no possible systemic change that is going to happen. However, our protagonist can do THIS good thing now.&quot; To stick with the camper metaphor, saving the campers isn't going to meaningful affect the cosmic battle between good and evil that evil is winning.<br /> <br /> It does, however, save THESE campers and THIS day and has a meaningful impact on THOSE people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know who told you otherwise, but the whole point of WtA is that saving those campers DOES affect the cosmic battle between good and evil. Because the alternative is that those campers will be, at best, eaten. At worst turned into fomori or BSD breeders. Which them increases suffering.<br /> <br /> Remember that the fight of the garou isn't of the mundane world only, but also the spiritual one. When you take out a puppymill, you aren't just saving those dogs. You are also ensuring that the hurt and corruption caused by that puppymill doesn't spread or dig in so deeply it becomes a Wyrmhole that then affects everything around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T16:03:09-08:00","id":1527883,"title":"","content":"There's also a big problem in that in WtA , you're not playing a random do-gooder or everyman that decides to be a hero. Saving the world is literally a Garou's Gaia-given purpose, and everything they do, whether they succeed or fail or give up, carries that baggage. If the message of the game with characters operating under this setup is &quot;roll over and let humans fix the world even though you're a supernatural creature with a literal divine mandate to Save The Planet&quot;, the game literally has no reason to exist. Just go do activism in real life at that rate instead of roleplaying it at a table.<br /> <br /> It's really, really hard to compare WtA to any of these other things, because expecting it to operate that way just breaks it. If you want a game like this, it needs to not be WtA anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T16:26:11-08:00","id":1527884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527881#post1527881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know who told you otherwise, but the whole point of WtA is that saving those campers DOES affect the cosmic battle between good and evil. Because the alternative is that those campers will be, at best, eaten. At worst turned into fomori or BSD breeders. Which them increases suffering.<br /> <br /> Remember that the fight of the garou isn't of the mundane world only, but also the spiritual one. When you take out a puppymill, you aren't just saving those dogs. You are also ensuring that the hurt and corruption caused by that puppymill doesn't spread or dig in so deeply it becomes a Wyrmhole that then affects everything around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's where the point is.<br /> <br /> You find out that doing the incremental stuff doesn't help but do you still doing or not?<br /> <br /> The point of W5 at its absolute TLDR-est is, &quot;Do the same thing you did but angst more.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T16:38:29-08:00","id":1527887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527876#post1527876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, I'm a little surprised at that reaction because it's hardly a new one in games or even fiction in general.<br /> <br /> I bring up noir and detective fiction because that's basically the rules of the genre.<br /> <br /> &quot;The system is corrupt, the world sucks, and there is no possible systemic change that is going to happen. However, our protagonist can do THIS good thing now.&quot; To stick with the camper metaphor, saving the campers isn't going to meaningful affect the cosmic battle between good and evil that evil is winning.<br /> <br /> It does, however, save THESE campers and THIS day and has a meaningful impact on THOSE people.<br /> <br /> It's more or less a running theme in THE WITCHER where Geralt tries to be a hero of the typical fantasy mold but he's in a world where kings and aristocrats are all corrupt scheming bastards with petty wars fought for no good reason. So when Geralt saves a child, he's usually dealing with the fact there's a war going on that will destroy whole villages. I find that really evocative and interesting. Like playing in a cyberpunk setting where your PCs aren't going to overthrow Arasaka but maybe stop some slavers.<br /> <br /> This is also the 2nd time a WW game has reorientated itself this way.<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension went from being, &quot;Destroy the Technocracy! Blow up their base on Jupiter&quot; to &quot;save Becky from the Umbrood possessing her.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Cyberpunk or the Witcher is that Werewolf the Apocalypse takes place with the backdrop being the literal end of the world. Sure you could save some campers, but if the world is on the verge of annihilation then how much of a sense of accomplishment do players get with the knowledge that the world is going to end and those campers will be dying pretty soon anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair you can have fun (and cathartic) roleplaying experiences with a nihilistic &quot;nothing your characters do ultimately matters because a bomb is going to go off and blow up the planet at the end of the campaign,&quot; setup for RPGs, but it's the kind of thing that the players and the ST need to walk into with eyes wide open and fully understanding what the theme and the mood of the game is about. It's also extremely different from previous Werewolf games, where your goal was to <i>prevent</i> the end of the world. Now though, the game starts with the premise that the world has already died, it's just that most people don't realize it yet.<br /> <br /> To make a comparison to a Noir movie, imagine a detective movie set with the premise that there's a huge asteroid getting ready to smash into the Earth. The movie follows the detective as he solves some crime, arrests someone and then in the closing seconds of the movie, the asteroid slams into the planet and everyone dies. That might seem like it would be a pretty absurd movie, and it is, but that's essentially what W5 is doing - the world is ready to end, neither the PCs nor anyone else can do anything to stop it, so run some games during the final gasps of Gaia's death throes.<br /> <br /> In W5, there is no meaningful &quot;cosmic battle between good and evil,&quot; the battle is already over and good has lost. Again, that's a huge thematic change from earlier editions and it's not something that everyone is going to be interested in or enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-03-2024, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T17:17:52-08:00","id":1527888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527884#post1527884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's where the point is.<br /> <br /> You find out that doing the incremental stuff doesn't help but do you still doing or not?<br /> <br /> The point of W5 at its absolute TLDR-est is, &quot;Do the same thing you did but angst more.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, just doing it helps, because even in W5 there are banes.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the game says you shouldn't do it, you shouldn't take incremental actions. You either guard your caern or you eat and infect people to make their species die faster.<br /> <br /> I get you like nihilism, but that's not how WtA is set up and even W5 still holds onto the old setups, it just doesn't want you to act towards them. WtA is about caring, not the futility of action.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Red Talons, once more, eating and infecting people is an okay method is a sign of how hilariously disjointed the lore is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T17:19:41-08:00","id":1527889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527878#post1527878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel you are taking the 'save the world' sentence and taking it too literally. Because it has always been taking out the Kobolts and helping the village that saves the world in WtA. In no game I have been in has there been this one big 'Save the World' quest or characters refusing to handle bane infestations.<br /> <br /> The incremental actions that you are talking about have been the norm in WtA. At most you create a Caern, go on an umbral quest or destroy a Hive. They do it to save Gaia, but saving Gaia is chipping away at a massive block slowly.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you don't have an overarching goal, why are you taking the incremental actions in the first place? Taking out a herd of banes makes the city block safer and if the city block is safer then more positive spirits can exist there, which means the area can heal.<br /> <br /> But more importantly; W5 is saying even the incremental actions are too much. In The Deepest Wounds, only the CoF took ANY action, while the PC sept just existed. The ideal is to sit in your caern and guard it, not helping the territory around you in small ways. Unless you are killing and eating scores of people, that is seen as okay for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Thats been my experience these past three decades.<br /> <br /> You go to protests and sit ins and community meetings because you still believe that you can make a small difference that will improve things for the better, thats why WtA has always spoken to me because you keep fighting the fight because of that glimmer of hope and because those who will come after you are relying on you.<br /> <br /> W5 by contrast states categorically that the fight is over and that hope is dead and that you are the problem if you keep fighting for change. Its language I've heard my entire life......but the last place I expected to hear it was WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T17:25:51-08:00","id":1527890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527881#post1527881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know who told you otherwise, but the whole point of WtA is that saving those campers DOES affect the cosmic battle between good and evil. Because the alternative is that those campers will be, at best, eaten. At worst turned into fomori or BSD breeders. Which them increases suffering.<br /> <br /> Remember that the fight of the garou isn't of the mundane world only, but also the spiritual one. When you take out a puppymill, you aren't just saving those dogs. You are also ensuring that the hurt and corruption caused by that puppymill doesn't spread or dig in so deeply it becomes a Wyrmhole that then affects everything around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% and as we've seen so far from Parawolf/Renegade the only ones doing anything about said puppymill or campers are the CoF.<br /> <br /> I mean the corebook says that the Garous main problem is that they are too quick to act with violence but then every single IC and OOC depiction of non-CoF Garou shows them doing absolutely nothing of the sort and instead just kinda camping at their Caerns while the world burns.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T17:36:06-08:00","id":1527891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527890#post1527890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100% and as we've seen so far from Parawolf/Renegade the only ones doing anything about said puppymill or campers are the CoF.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Further to that we have the CoF depicted as working together with humans in an alliance to achieve their goals....much like Legacy Garou and Kinfolk did whereas Gaian W5 Garou interactions with humans seem predicated mostly on killing them based on the Tribal Stereotypes and the mechanics of Crinos ( cos average humans are the only opponents in the book that your reliably killing in one round which is what you need to do to keep yourself under control.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T17:57:59-08:00","id":1527892,"title":"","content":"Just look at the example characters. Maybe like... Two? Of them out of all the tribes are actually even making an attempt at helping people.<br /> <br /> The rest? Well, honestly, they're reskinned Vampire archetypes. Dicking around, fighting over turf and messing with normie because They Can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T18:52:44-08:00","id":1527894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527889#post1527889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly.<br /> <br /> Thats been my experience these past three decades.<br /> <br /> You go to protests and sit ins and community meetings because you still believe that you can make a small difference that will improve things for the better, thats why WtA has always spoken to me because you keep fighting the fight because of that glimmer of hope and because those who will come after you are relying on you.<br /> <br /> W5 by contrast states categorically that the fight is over and that hope is dead and that you are the problem if you keep fighting for change. Its language I've heard my entire life......but the last place I expected to hear it was WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>One almost expects to see some really transparent pseudonym of Maine du Bois in the credits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T21:19:10-08:00","id":1527899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527890#post1527890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100% and as we've seen so far from Parawolf/Renegade the only ones doing anything about said puppymill or campers are the CoF.<br /> <br /> I mean the corebook says that the Garous main problem is that they are too quick to act with violence but then every single IC and OOC depiction of non-CoF Garou shows them doing absolutely nothing of the sort and instead just kinda camping at their Caerns while the world burns.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly that seems to track with the mechanics. Mechanically, for any Garou there's basically only 4 endings. 1) They die, 2), they give up the wolf, 3) they fall into Harano, 4) they fall into Haglusk. Points gained in Harano or Haglusk are permanent and can't be reduced, so over the course of years or decades, it's only a matter of time before a werewolf collects enough of those points (and it's only 5) to permanently fall into one of those two states.<br /> <br /> In the setting, this is reflected in the fact that most of the Garou Nation has fallen into Harano. They've given up, they've retreated and they're not interested in fighting anymore. The remainder has fallen into Haglusk and are out to fight against the Wyrm in any way possible. There's no third path or third option because that simply doesn't exist. <br /> <br /> PCs, of course, haven't fallen to one or the other, yet, but eventually they'll fall too (unless they die first or willingly give up the wolf). This is one of those cases where the setting actually reflects the rules as written (and that's honestly pretty rare in RPGs and I have to give Parawolf/Renegade recognition for that) but unfortunately in this case, the rules suck and and that's reflected onto the setting.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this makes W5 a profoundly pessimistic game because you can't win, you can't change things, you were born too late to save the world or make any major, lasting difference, and there's a legitimate argument that having your character die or give up on being a werewolf is better than the only other two long-term alternatives - falling into Harano or Haglusk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-04-2024, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T21:42:57-08:00","id":1527900,"title":"","content":"I think that the position of the Garou not doing naything is an exaggeration or misrepresentation of what is in the books. The Cult of Fenris aren't the only people doing anything. The Cult of Fenris are engaged in war against other Garou and eco-terrorism/fascism that only accelerates the destruction of the world while the regular Garou are doing their own thing that includes defending their places and each other plus, if they're good folks, the humans.<br /> <br /> The Litany still says to fight the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T22:01:14-08:00","id":1527903,"title":"","content":"Except the W5 corebook takes a firm anti-Litany-stance. The section on the Litany ends like this: &quot;For all of the self-glorifying tales that old Garou tell around the fires, younger werewolves note that the Garou Nation didn\u2019t collapse because the Litany was so goddamn perfect.&quot; So a tenet like &quot;Combat the Wyrm Wherever It Dwells and Whenever It Thrives\u200b&quot; is thrown under the bus by the W5 corebook along with the other tenets. Of course, it's precisely because of tenets like the Wyrm-one that the conversation about the Litany deserves more nuance than what was offered by the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> And the sidebar &quot;Changing Ways&quot; as mentioned before floats the idea that the Garou abandoning their mission is one valid way to solve the issues according to W5. Additionally, the section &quot;The Real Problem With The Garou&quot; ends like this: &quot;In a world that is dead and dying, they are the ones with the best chance to right <i>some part</i> of a worldwide wrong\u2026<br /> \u2026 they just need to understand the limitations of the tools at their disposal.\u200b&quot; The &quot;not doing anything&quot;-part isn't just about the Garou literally not doing anything but also about how Garou <i>can't</i> do anything to make things better. The book heavily questions whether there's <i>anything</i> Garou can meaningfully contribute to improving things in the Age of Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T22:09:43-08:00","id":1527904,"title":"","content":"See, I think this is where a lot of the frustration is coming from:<br /> <br /> To use another game that I play. imagine if Paizo started publishing a lot of level 1-10 Adventure Paths, but starting at level 3 your characters start running into more and more setbacks, taking on more and more inherent debuffs whenever they finish encounters that you can't get rid of, and at level 5 you are hit with an unkillable brick wall of a boss that makes it impossible to progress, and the DM is then ordered to lecture that you, the player, is the only one able to stop slavery or evil cults or whatever the big bad was doing in real life, and that by trying to do so in a game you're being just as evil as the villains.<br /> <br /> And then, when Pathfinder fans are understandably upset about this, I go onto Pathfinder subreddits and forums and start arguing that hey, I haven't played Pathfinder in years but I do play a lot of Call of Cthulhu and 40k so every single TTRPG ever is supposed to be an exercise in futility and nihilism, regardless of what the game's name implies about what a player can expect, so all the criticisms of this new direction are overblown and wrong.<br /> <br /> Why should WtA be held to a different standard? Why should a game called Werewolf: the Apocalypse, a game whose main theme for over 30 years been about raging to your last breath against the dying of the light, be any different? Why should its fans have to just accept that its newest iteration is about spinelessly hiding in a hole until you die or go crazy just because uhhh that's what other games that aren't even in the same gameline, or even the same medium do?<br /> <br /> If you like more fatalistic games and stories, that's absolutely fine, and I mean that. There's definitely a time and place for those. But it's not within WtA and it never has been. And trying to cram WtA into that framework just creates the ugly, confused tonal trainwreck that is W5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T23:27:33-08:00","id":1527906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527899#post1527899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly that seems to track with the mechanics. Mechanically, for any Garou there's basically only 4 endings. 1) They die, 2), they give up the wolf, 3) they fall into Harano, 4) they fall into Haglusk. Points gained in Harano or Haglusk are permanent and can't be reduced, so over the course of years or decades, it's only a matter of time before a werewolf collects enough of those points (and it's only 5) to permanently fall into one of those two states.<br /> <br /> In the setting, this is reflected in the fact that most of the Garou Nation has fallen into Harano. They've given up, they've retreated and they're not interested in fighting anymore. The remainder has fallen into Haglusk and are out to fight against the Wyrm in any way possible. There's no third path or third option because that simply doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> PCs, of course, haven't fallen to one or the other, yet, but eventually they'll fall too (unless they die first or willingly give up the wolf). This is one of those cases where the setting actually reflects the rules as written (and that's honestly pretty rare in RPGs and I have to give Parawolf/Renegade recognition for that) but unfortunately in this case, the rules suck and and that's reflected onto the setting.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this makes W5 a profoundly pessimistic game because you can't win, you can't change things, you were born too late to save the world or make any major, lasting difference, and there's a legitimate argument that having your character die or give up unw being a werewolf is better than the only other two long-term alternatives - falling into Harano or Haglusk.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that would make sense......except the Author of said scenario has stated that the Sept isn't suffering from Harano.<br /> <br /> *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T23:33:14-08:00","id":1527907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527900#post1527900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the position of the Garou not doing naything is an exaggeration or misrepresentation of what is in the books. The Cult of Fenris aren't the only people doing anything. The Cult of Fenris are engaged in war against other Garou and eco-terrorism/fascism that only accelerates the destruction of the world while the regular Garou are doing their own thing that includes defending their places and each other plus, if they're good folks, the humans.<br /> <br /> The Litany still says to fight the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty ballsy to say the folks bringing quotes and page references are the ones misrepresenting things.<br /> <br /> As others have said the entire corebook has nary a positive thing to say about the Litany and those who follow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T23:40:08-08:00","id":1527908,"title":"","content":"And on top of all of this, the game then has the gall to offer example characters that outright kill people, eat people, spread disease,do wetwork, etc. Without a shred of consideration how it looks when compared to the Hauglosk rules Or the CoF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T00:40:24-08:00","id":1527910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527907#post1527907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty ballsy to say the folks bringing quotes and page references are the ones misrepresenting things.<br /> <br /> As others have said the entire corebook has nary a positive thing to say about the Litany and those who follow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, in light of the rejection of the Litany, the example characters doing what they do ends up muddling the message even more.<br /> <br /> So, with the ideal that you should stay in your caern and not do stuff, but also the Litany is bunk and no sane garou follows it, in addition to the example characters you get this;<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no use fighting for Gaia, that just leads to Hauglosk. So let's set up a meth lab/merc company/prepper compound/cult and make cash!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T01:47:35-08:00","id":1527915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527907#post1527907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty ballsy to say the folks bringing quotes and page references are the ones misrepresenting things.<br /> <br /> As others have said the entire corebook has nary a positive thing to say about the Litany and those who follow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's pretty ballsy to discuss the premise of the game on a game board. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not taking it personally.<br /> <br /> This is just my impressions. Agree or disagree as you will.<br /> <br /> And yes, it extremely harshly criticizes the Litany. However, that's because the Garou nation needs reform. However, the book doesn't provide answers and leaves it to the PCs to come up with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-04-2024, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T03:44:34-08:00","id":1527917,"title":"","content":"The problem remains that it's impossible to distinguish between your impression, and wishful thinking about what W5 would have been like if it written to the same quality as books like CbN5.<br /> <br /> We're trying to point out objective facts about what the text actually says, and you're countering with &quot;well it's just subjective impressions, so I'm right too.&quot; You sound like someone that would have their entire psyche crushed if you acknowledged that yet another Paradox led WoD game didn't have some redeeming value to make it worth defending, not like someone that wants a real honest discussion about what's actually in the text. You repeatedly shut down anything that wasn't strictly the text as useless to the discussion, until people kept citing the text at you to show that what you were saying doesn't match with the text, and now you're shifting to making it about how you &quot;feel&quot; about the text instead (which we were all wrong to do before) because that doesn't allow your stances to have to stand up to scrutiny (even though opinions are not actually free from being debated or countered).<br /> <br /> You. Are. Not. Discussing. The. Premise. Of. The. Game. You're talking about what you want the game to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T04:28:16-08:00","id":1527918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527915#post1527915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, it extremely harshly criticizes the Litany. However, that's because the Garou nation needs reform. However, the book doesn't provide answers and leaves it to the PCs to come up with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't criticise the Litany, it says old garou abuse it and young garou don't care for it. If the Litany in W5 was just laws like &quot;Submission to the Higher Station&quot; and &quot;Leader Shall Not be Challenged During War Time&quot; which the book does address, then sure. But it isn't just those tenets that have stayed.<br /> <br /> For example, The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted. The law that keeps the garou a secret. The text doesn't address it at all. Nor does it address the cannibalism, caern destruction, being kind to others, respecting territory and such laws. There is no section saying &quot;Of course, some laws such as <b><i>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</i></b> and <b><i>You Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans</i></b> are still followed for the safety of all garou and potential Kin.&quot; It simply mentions the tenets that are easily abused and gives no examples of them being used correctly.<br /> <br /> This is akin to saying that there is no need to keep up the Masquerade in V5, because its just Camarilla Elder propaganda. Is doing so dumb? Yep! That is why it needs to be said in the text that even young garou follow THAT law.<br /> <br /> Instead, we are given the impression that younger garou follow the Litany at their own leisure. Which means, in the absence of text disproving it, that they might not keep the Veil and we KNOW some eat humans.<br /> <br /> (And, just to be certain, I checked, the book mentions the Veil once in the lexicon, once in the history section and finally in the Litany section. There is no mention if the Veil is still kept other than the assumption humans don't know about the garou.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T04:35:38-08:00","id":1527919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527918#post1527918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't criticise the Litany, it says old garou abuse it and young garou don't care for it. If the Litany in W5 was just laws like &quot;Submission to the Higher Station&quot; and &quot;Leader Shall Not be Challenged During War Time&quot; which the book does address, then sure. But it isn't just those tenets that have stayed.<br /> <br /> For example, The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted. The law that keeps the garou a secret. The text doesn't address it at all. Nor does it address the cannibalism, caern destruction, being kind to others, respecting territory and such laws. There is no section saying &quot;Of course, some laws such as <b><i>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</i></b> and <b><i>You Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans</i></b> are still followed for the safety of all garou and potential Kin.&quot; It simply mentions the tenets that are easily abused and gives no examples of them being used correctly.<br /> <br /> This is akin to saying that there is no need to keep up the Masquerade in V5, because its just Camarilla Elder propaganda. Is doing so dumb? Yep! That is why it needs to be said in the text that even young garou follow THAT law.<br /> <br /> Instead, we are given the impression that younger garou follow the Litany at their own leisure. Which means, in the absence of text disproving it, that they might not keep the Veil and we KNOW some eat humans.<br /> <br /> (And, just to be certain, I checked, the book mentions the Veil once in the lexicon, once in the history section and finally in the Litany section. There is no mention if the Veil is still kept other than the assumption humans don't know about the garou.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Second Inquisition didn't come around because the Six Traditions of the Camarilla were so goddamn perfect.&quot; lmao <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T06:51:41-08:00","id":1527922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527900#post1527900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the position of the Garou not doing naything is an exaggeration or misrepresentation of what is in the books. The Cult of Fenris aren't the only people doing anything. The Cult of Fenris are engaged in war against other Garou and eco-terrorism/fascism that only accelerates the destruction of the world while the regular Garou are doing their own thing that includes defending their places and each other plus, if they're good folks, the humans.<br /> <br /> The Litany still says to fight the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably something that happens, but we aren't told it happens or see it happening. Pretty much the only thing we've seen in the core book and the adventure is Garou sitting around their caerns not fighting. And we do see that the Litany is largely ignored by most werewolves, so this part is likely ignored too. I imagine if some Wyrm tainted monster shows up in a Garou's backyard they'd kill it, but it seems pretty clear that the W5 Garou Nation just isn't terribly interested in fighting the Wyrm at large and its members aren't going out of their way to fight it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, werewolves <i>probably</i> fight the Wyrm, if it's convenient, but from the published material it seems pretty clear that they're taking very much action past that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T07:33:08-08:00","id":1527923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527917#post1527917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem remains that it's impossible to distinguish between your impression, and wishful thinking about what W5 would have been like if it written to the same quality as books like CbN5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, Heavy Arms, that's a very dismissive attitude. It's also highly biased based on the idea that, a couple of times, I was overly forgiving to some vampire books.<br /> <br /> I have my issues with Werewolf Five and my review wasn't even that positive.<br /> <br /> My general statement was that the book doesn't utterly trash the idea of doing anything to fight against the Wyrm but suggests that it is going for the idea that any action might be pointless but that provides the player character context for doing their actions anyway. Which is an interesting mood to explore for a roleplayer, IMHO.<br /> <br /> It's not for everyone but it's not even something that wasn't present in other installments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-04-2024, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:00:58-08:00","id":1527931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527923#post1527923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, Heavy Arms, that's a very dismissive attitude. It's also highly biased based on the idea that, a couple of times, I was overly forgiving to some vampire books.<br /> <br /> I have my issues with Werewolf Five and my review wasn't even that positive.<br /> <br /> My general statement was that the book doesn't utterly trash the idea of doing anything to fight against the Wyrm but suggests that it is going for the idea that any action might be pointless but that provides the player character context for doing their actions anyway. Which is an interesting mood to explore for a roleplayer, IMHO.<br /> <br /> It's not for everyone but it's not even something that wasn't present in other installments.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are times for saying &quot;but maybe it's pointless...&quot; and the core of W:tA is not one of them. Again, you don't need the book feeling like it was inspired or directly written by the hand of the Urge Wyrm of Lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:39:51-08:00","id":1527938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527923#post1527923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general statement was that the book doesn't utterly trash the idea of doing anything to fight against the Wyrm but suggests that it is going for the idea that any action might be pointless but that provides the player character context for doing their actions anyway. Which is an interesting mood to explore for a roleplayer, IMHO.<br /> <br /> It's not for everyone but it's not even something that wasn't present in other installments.</div> </div> </div> </div>But one of the biggest issues W5 has is a lack of context. Reading the W5 corebook one learns a lot about what the game is against and what parts of Garou-culture are bad - but there's no counter-point to that. Moreso, there's no perspective for gameplay in the book.<br /> <br /> Take Rage. It's decried as a bad thing and one of the main-reasons why Garou are the wrong tool to fix the world. They've removed Gnosis and folded it into Rage. You sit down with this game and every PC <i>has to use Rage</i>. So while it's one thing to have that pessimistic take in the book, it will be rendered completely meaningless at the table because mechanically everything has already been decided. It doesn't matter what any player decides to do, their PC is going to rely on Rage and use Rage as a resource. So if you want to take that pessimistic take of &quot;Garou can't fix anything because of Rage&quot;, W5 sets up a scenario where PCs are forced to use Rage and then STs are supposed to punish them for using Rage and show them that that's the wrong tool to fix the world. But there's no struggle here or any agency given to the players. There's nothing interesting happening here, it's outside of the control of the player, it's terrible for roleplaying and it ultimately just becomes a feel-bad-mechanic. If any ST actually goes through with the very pessimistic take on Rage, then players are forced to get punished by the ST for simply playing the game. There's nothing interesting about making players go through that. <br /> <br /> Or take Renown. The book makes a big deal about how bad Garou-society is (as shown by the fall of the Garou-Nation) and how Garou-Elders are assholes as well that exploit tradition. And so young Garou are disillusioned and have lost faith in things like the Litany. Okay, that might be interesting... except the Renown-mechanics don't reflect that one bit. In fact, what is going on instead is that is another bit where context has been removed and instead it's now all put on the shoulder of the ST. It's not as bad as H5 which is even more reliant on ST-fiat for its mechanics but Renown has been turned into a mechanic completely reliant on ST-fiat. No longer do you get lists of deeds that raise or lower Renown, no longer is Renown tied to any social event... now it's all just about what the ST thinks of what a Garou-PC does. A PC does something and the ST can immediately dole out a &quot;You're in chagrin!&quot; and then it's also up to the ST to define how the PC can redeem themselves. Say you want to play one of those rebellious young Garou that wants to ignore Garou-traditions... well, the ST can just dole out Honor-chagrins all day. There's no play happening here. It doesn't matter what any player wants to do with their Garou-PC. In the end, it's entirely dependent on the STs definitions of the three types of Renown. You wouldn't set this up this way if the game were truly about having young Garou try to reform Garou-norms and -traditions. There's no path here for players to have an impact on how Renown works. It's all entirely dependent on the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T12:42:39-08:00","id":1527943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527923#post1527923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, Heavy Arms, that's a very dismissive attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>You set the tone man. You started your whole defense of the Cult of Fenris with a bunch of dismissive prebuttals, and kept being dismissive of responses no matter how well cited or knee jerk.<br /> <br /> You haven't stepped it back, you haven't read the room, you're just barreling through it all despite the fact that nobody likes what you're selling.<br /> <br /> I'm being tame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also highly biased based on the idea that, a couple of times, I was overly forgiving to some vampire books. </div> </div> </div>No, it's biased by <b>every thread we've mutually engaged with talking about a WoD5 product</b>. Starting with the V5 playtests.<br /> <br /> This is what you always do. Whether you dislike or like a product in the end, you will always spend dozens of posts over multiple threads if they exist defending it because you seem to think there's some hardcore vital imperative to fighting for a part of the book that spoke to you regardless of whether it's in a bed of roses or a pile of shit. The whole, &quot;we can't pay attention to what Karim said!&quot; is as obvious of an example of it as possible: you actively push to ignore context if it means the hill you're fighting on might look bad to die on until you eventually get enough push back to stop.<br /> <br /> You have trained us to keep hammering you like this because it's the only way you'll eventually listen to us. And like multiple times before, even when you concede in one thread, it's just means you'll pick up the debate again in another thread. So we're going to play whack-a-mole, because this wasn't a worthwhile hill in your review thread, it's not actually one in this one, and it will probably be one or two more before you let it go and that sticks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have my issues with Werewolf Five and my review wasn't even that positive. </div> </div> </div>And people reacted to it pretty much the same way they're reacting to you here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My general statement was that the book doesn't utterly trash the idea of doing anything to fight against the Wyrm but suggests that it is going for the idea that any action might be pointless but that provides the player character context for doing their actions anyway. </div> </div> </div>Where does the book provide any context for PCs doing actions that might be pointless, but are still worth doing? There's no positive messaging towards this. There's no discussion of W5 being a noir style game. There's no game-play loop where you're actively rewarded for it as a player so you keep wanting to do it.<br /> <br /> I asked in your thread, and you didn't actually respond there, but I'll ask again: what about being a werewolf in W5 is actually &quot;awesome?&quot; What about it is something people would actually want to play?<br /> <br /> Being a werewolf isn't adding to the fun of playing a game with a stronger focus on existential issues. Playing a noir detective isn't more fun with Rage, and Hauglosk, and Harano, tacked on. Playing a mood is only interesting if the game actually works to add to the experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not for everyone but it's not even something that wasn't present in other installments. </div> </div> </div>If you understand it was present in the other editions without the radical changes to everything else, part of you knows that means W5 changed a bunch of stuff to - maybe, the text doesn't actually say this is the case - support a mood the game already supported.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527931#post1527931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are times for saying &quot;but maybe it's pointless...&quot; and the core of W:tA is not one of them. Again, you don't need the book feeling like it was inspired or directly written by the hand of the Urge Wyrm of Lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, if part of the goal of WoD5 is to make a game targeted to younger/newer fans, younger Millenials and Zoomers regularly poll as hating this sort of doomerism in their entertainment. They don't want an RPG of, &quot;you know that existential dread you feel because it seems like the world is failing, you elders screwed it up but aren't fixing it, everyone expects you to do it despite having less than previous generations to work with, and you can't even figure out if you care enough to try? Well this game is that, but to 11!&quot;<br /> <br /> Games, even ones that tackle serious, contemporary, real world stuff? They're still supposed to be fun. &quot;The urge of doomerism that you constantly feel is going to be constantly validated by this game,&quot; is not fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T15:41:04-08:00","id":1527960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You set the tone man. You started your whole defense of the Cult of Fenris with a bunch of dismissive prebuttals, and kept being dismissive of responses no matter how well cited or knee jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not being dismissive. I'm disagreeing. I also don't see how citing changes an opinion if you are citing material to go against the intent and presentation of them as effective villains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's biased by <b>every thread we've mutually engaged with talking about a WoD5 product</b>. Starting with the V5 playtests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which. Do you agree with anything I've ever said about WoD5 or are we just apparently somehow the opposite of everything? You seem particularly frustrated by my attitude and I'm not sure why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heav Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And people reacted to it pretty much the same way they're reacting to you here.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall, response has been very positive. I was given applause in a lot of places for being drama free. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where does the book provide any context for PCs doing actions that might be pointless, but are still worth doing?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, too, that antagonists can often be intertwined<br /> or have subsidiaries that exist within the same category.<br /> For example, \u201cclimate instability\u201d or \u201crising authoritarianism\u201d<br /> or \u201cethnic nationalism\u201d could be considered<br /> a passive, systemic antagonist, whereas any number of<br /> Pentex Group (active, systemic) fronts (themselves active<br /> and systemic) could be contributing to it, as could any<br /> number of corrupt public officials (active, individual)\u200b pg. 212<br /> <br /> At the core of many of Werewolf\u2019s conflicts is the imbalance<br /> of the Triat and its effect on the mother-spirit Gaia.<br /> Gaia\u2019s time of dying serves as a universal inciting incident<br /> on a global and a historic scale, encouraging every Garou<br /> character to act now. <b>There\u2019s always something for the<br /> characters to do in Werewolf; there\u2019s always a need to<br /> fight back.</b><br /> <br /> A Silent Strider may seek to regain a lost artifact in a<br /> desperate effort to hold on to one last piece of their fallen<br /> lover\u2019s legacy, while a Hart Warden may have learned<br /> of the presence of a defiled Black Spiral Dancer caern<br /> and convinces her pack to take it back. A Bone Gnawer<br /> might venture into the Umbra to look for something\u2026<br /> anything\u2026<b> that he discovers there to try to stanch Gaia\u2019s<br /> bleeding. All three are different approaches to the same<br /> contextualizing incident of Gaia\u2019s death and the threat<br /> the degrading state of the world still represents</b>.page 214<br /> <br /> <b>Fighting the Wyrm or another Triatic \u201cbad actor\u201d<br /> and its proxies may not be the smartest or most effective<br /> thing for the Garou to do, but it\u2019s rarely the worst thing<br /> they can do. Help the players understand that there is<br /> always something to do as a Garou. </b>If anything, there<br /> may be too many antagonists to confront, so roll up your<br /> sleeves and commence.\u200b page. 214","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-04-2024, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T16:09:09-08:00","id":1527961,"title":"","content":"How is the Gnawer on page 214 supposed to go into the Umbra to search for something when they'll likely end up torn apart just from being there? The time scale of damage doesn't typically allow for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T16:18:58-08:00","id":1527962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527961#post1527961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the Gnawer on page 214 supposed to go into the Umbra to search for something when they'll likely end up torn apart just from being there? The time scale of damage doesn't typically allow for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of places they could definitely improve the rules set. Like giving a system for removing Hauglosk and Harano.<br /> <br /> Doesn't need to be more than a line or two.<br /> <br /> &quot;A successful Chronicle victory without degenerating into fanaticism or depression, the PC can elect to remove a permanent point of Hauglosk.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T16:47:57-08:00","id":1527964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527962#post1527962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's plenty of places they could definitely improve the rules set. Like giving a system for removing Hauglosk and Harano.<br /> <br /> Doesn't need to be more than a line or two.<br /> <br /> &quot;A successful Chronicle victory without degenerating into fanaticism or depression, the PC can elect to remove a permanent point of Hauglosk.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mentioned in another thread but I think the better way to address this is to just bring back Ambition and Desire aka short-term-goal and long-term-goal. It's an additional source of WP-recovery (which you need in W5 in light of the mechanics reliant on WP) and the long-term-goal just gets an added &quot;... or you can erase a dot of Harano or Hauglosk&quot;. Also has the added benefit of getting players to think about short-term and long-term goals which then enables Storytellers to tailor gameplay to those wishes.<br /> <br /> Especially because your proposed mechanic is irrelevant anyway. &quot;Degenerating into fanaticism or depression&quot; is just Hauglosk 5 or Harano 5 and at that point, PCs hit a game-over-screen anyway. And there are no mechanics or lore/worldbuilding to suss out the differences between Hauglosk 2 or 4, let alone a scenario like having Harano 4 and Hauglosk 4 at the same time.<br /> <br /> There's an attempt here to produce something &quot;Humanity&quot;-esque that relates to what you have in V5 but it fails. Humanity in V5 is a track that goes up and down, one street where things move in two directions, up and down. Because V5 wants to simulate a vampire's struggle with keeping their humanity. In contrast, Harano and Hauglosk are two tracks. And they are on/off switches. Harano/Hauglosk 0 to 4 are utterly meaningless. You either have Harano/Hauglosk 5 or you don't. That's all the game cares about. And the fact that outside a rare Fetish you can't lower your Harano/Hauglosk rating, it's clear that this is less about a struggle and more about a &quot;doomed to failure&quot;-scenario. A Garou-PC isn't supposed to succeed according to W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T20:00:03-08:00","id":1527970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527743#post1527743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it presumes I haven't.<br /> <br /> Mind you, my entire premise is based on the Get NOT being racist in any RL way and getting better by Revised but I understand if that was missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, this does lead me to belive that you're familiar with the Get mindset, just as you have demonstrated familiarity with the way they fall in a &quot;Tribe Falls&quot;<ul><li>The whole point is that they do stuff, they don't care what others have to say about it, they go and do it. Being proactive can damn you to hell if you're being dumb about it, but the game as a whole takes the stance that being proactive is a problematic state in and of itself, and that's something deeply worrying in a game that's supposed to be about fighting for the world and protecting what you care for</li> <li>In W5 this is defined by Hagulosk, which is somehow a level of insane zeal and willingness to do anything it takes, yet it's a form of magical insanity that makes you more fascist in your outlook, while there is potential to that idea, how does that match with the rest of the nation? It's clear that multiple tribes do quite abhorrent things and there is zero moral or philosophical questioning of those things (something you have admitted Werewolf was quite keen on tackling)</li> <li>Why is this zeal equated with Fascism? This is something only the writers know and it comes from a ludicrous headspace of equating the Get with the Nazis, as presented in setting there is zero correlation with the drive to act no matter the moral implications with being &quot;a bootlicker&quot;, worshipping fascistic idols and surrounding yourself with racist mooks as your followers (see the adventure at the end of W5 and the bonus adventure they printed that details how some people want to be just like the Get and what their practices are</li> <li>The only reason why the Get need to be defined by Fascism rather than their actual state is because the Authors wanted to make sure we understood that they are a shorthand for dealing with rightwing extremism and wanted to use the Get as convenient targets due to their patchwork history without actually exploring the theme they are supposed to represent</li> <li>If we get beyond the authors being silly, it's quite simple to see that Haugolusk should be a supernatural illness of sorts that makes you into an extremist (this is also quite a stretch, but how else do you term it?), this is something that all the tribes should be subject to, and the Cult as a whole makes little sense as a Fallen Tribe, rather than a congregation of Garou of all stripes from all walks of life - heck, we see that the Red Talons and Black Furies are practically ready to join up as is from their writeups</li> <li>If their practices are about doing what has to be done at any cost, why is this something that's unclear to other Garou who will just stand there and twiddle their thumbs while they kidnap their members and take their Caerns acting like they've just been having a bad day? (see the adventure and the sample Get which are defined mostly as corrupters and saboteours of Garou rather than of the causes of Gaia's death)</li> <li>Going a step beyond, what's the narrative purpose of the Black Spiral Dancers now? How do they recruit? Why would they even bother? As described they're essentially twiddling their thumbs while the Cult is pretty much doing their jobs as corruptors and manipulators of the Garou (see NPC writeups and the adventures again)</li> </ul>Now you may want an extra heaping of grimderp for some sort of WoD purity's sake, but this is not how Werewolf rolled, especially throughout Revised.<br /> Werewolf is a game about hope and becoming better. And this game has no idea how to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527884#post1527884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of W5 at its absolute TLDR-est is, &quot;Do the same thing you did but angst more.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... and you believe this is a <b>GOOD </b>thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 01-04-2024, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T20:29:24-08:00","id":1527972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527962#post1527962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's plenty of places they could definitely improve the rules set. Like giving a system for removing Hauglosk and Harano.<br /> <br /> Doesn't need to be more than a line or two.<br /> <br /> &quot;A successful Chronicle victory without degenerating into fanaticism or depression, the PC can elect to remove a permanent point of Hauglosk.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if that's considered desirable from the developer's point of view. As I said earlier in one of these threads, I think the design intent is pretty clear that a W5 chronicle should not last more than a half-dozen to a dozen sessions. It feels like neither the setting or the rules are designed for long-term play the way that Legacy editions were or even V5 is. Certainly having two different trackers that will permanently remove a character from the campaign with virtually no way to reduce them (despite clear feedback from playtesters that this was problematic) seems very indictive of that design philosophy.<br /> <br /> So you could hack it with house rules, but I doubt we'll see anything official in this regard. If they wanted some way to remove or reduce Hauglosk/Harano they wouldn't have made the points permanent to begin with, or would have included a system to reduce points, or not had the systems permanently turn your PC into an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-05-2024, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T21:58:19-08:00","id":1527976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527972#post1527972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on if that's considered desirable from the developer's point of view. As I said earlier in one of these threads<b>, I think the design intent is pretty clear that a W5 chronicle should not last more than a half-dozen to a dozen sessions. </b>It feels like neither the setting or the rules are designed for long-term play the way that Legacy editions were or even V5 is. Certainly having two different trackers that will permanently remove a character from the campaign with virtually no way to reduce them (despite clear feedback from playtesters that this was problematic) seems very indictive of that design philosophy.<br /> <br /> So you could hack it with house rules, but I doubt we'll see anything official in this regard. If they wanted some way to remove or reduce Hauglosk/Harano they wouldn't have made the points permanent to begin with, or would have included a system to reduce points, or not had the systems permanently turn your PC into an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I don't get that at all. This is where I prevent myself from sticking my foot in my mouth by clarifying I think the only reason that is the case is because the rules are ridiculously punishing like V:TM 5 humanity rules and frenzies seemed to be until we saw LA by Night. We then discovered that the storyteller expected you to roll 4-5 times maybe in an entire session versus the dozens of roles that some Storytellers had in their games and would make rousing the Beast unplayable.<br /> <br /> In this case, Hauglosk and Harano are presently designed to destroy you utterly but all of the Examples of Play indicate fairly long term Chronicles where you're defending a Caern or territory or going through BIG EMOTIONAL ARCS.<br /> <br /> Which is to say you're not wrong but I think it's because the Developers fucked up in explaining themselves not because of design intent.<br /> <br /> Here's some examples of what I mean and I could be wrong:<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Payoff</b><br /> <br /> As is appropriate to narrative planning, the characters<br /> may acquire a specialized Skill, Gift, or strange McGuffin<br /> that is not immediately useful,<b> but under specific circumstances<br /> you introduce later, the reward becomes essential.<br /> Such rewards encourage engagement, commitment, and<br /> experimentation with the world. </b>It\u2019s like finding a key<br /> and knowing the lock is going to turn up sooner or later. Page 219<br /> <br /> <b>Anticipating Rewards</b><br /> <br /> Going back all the way to the game loop model at the<br /> beginning of the chapter, the reward cycle moves from<br /> objective to challenge to reward.<br /> <br /> The objective-challenge-reward cycle moves in a loop<br /> but can be broken easily in the transition from objective<br /> to challenge, thus resetting a step. Failure to confront the<br /> antagonist in a viable way can result in failure or setback,<br /> and potentially put the pack in a position where it might<br /> even rethink its objective. And let\u2019s face it, the dice play<br /> some role in decision. Bad luck can also result in delays or<br /> defeat, and in a step backward to the objective.<br /> <br /> <b>With a bit of forethought, though, you can foreshadow<br /> the next antagonist through incremental midloop<br /> rewards. </b>For example, searching the body of the eviscerated<br /> businessman might produce a key to a lockbox at a<br /> nearby bank, which holds important documents linking<br /> the Pentex Group front the pack has been investigating<br /> to an illegal arms purchase. Here, the reward is not only<br /> ripping the guts out of the antagonist, but also gaining<br /> access to important information that can prove useful to<br /> confronting the next challenge.<br /> <br /> <b>Some players appreciate a few hard-won rewards<br /> that serve as trophies marking their victories. Other<br /> players enjoy a faster rate of wins, possibly with smaller<br /> but progressive gains. In each case, players should come<br /> away with a sense that they invested their time, made the<br /> appropriate effort, and earned their rewards.\u200b </b>Page 220","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T22:03:16-08:00","id":1527977,"title":"","content":"No, the design intent was completely fucked up. Making Werewolf operate with degeneration mechanics like Vampire is the Worst Decision; the people who created Werewolf learned this when they originally intended to make it about cursed people changing during the full moon types, and then rapidly changed it to not make it play like a slightly angrier version of Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T22:19:12-08:00","id":1527978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527970#post1527970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent, this does lead me to belive that you're familiar with the Get mindset, just as you have demonstrated familiarity with the way they fall in a &quot;Tribe Falls&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. :thumbs up:<br /> <br /> [quote]Why is this zeal equated with Fascism? This is something only the writers know and it comes from a ludicrous headspace of equating the Get with the Nazis, as presented in setting there is zero correlation with the drive to act no matter the moral implications with being &quot;a bootlicker&quot;, worshipping fascistic idols and surrounding yourself with racist mooks as your followers (see the adventure at the end of W5 and the bonus adventure they printed that details how some people want to be just like the Get and what their practices are]/quote]<br /> <br /> Well Hauglosk isn't defined as zeal or fanaticism per se but self-righteousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Hauglosk</b><br /> <br /> In a desperate fight against an overwhelming<br /> enemy, the ends justify the means. Everything<br /> is on the table. Victory at any cost. This is<br /> hauglosk, the conviction that your absolute<br /> moral certainty justifies everything you do.<br /> Hauglosk is a state of extreme righteousness.<br /> A Garou in a state of hauglosk believes that the<br /> cause is all, that their way is the only way. If<br /> more harm than good is caused, well, that\u2019s a<br /> cost that must be paid. Page 52<br /> <br /> It's effectively believing in Tautological Templarness (see TV tropes) which is, TLDR, &quot;I am righteous so everything I do is righteous. How do I know I am righteous? Because everything I do is righteous.&quot; Which is a real life Far Right mentality where the identification as a subject is more important than any actual behavior to be a subject. Speaking as someone who grew up in the Bible belt, &quot;I am a Christian, therefore I can adulter and swear and persecute people because I am saved. However, someone who isn't saved and is a good person is evil because they are not a Christian.&quot; Which is something that would appal Rabbi Joshua Ben Joseph.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Cult of Fenris (heretofore no longer known as the Get), they have adopted the mentality that they're the only people doing shit to save Gaia and everyone else isn't doing enough. The thing is that the book doesn't clearly communicate is <b>this is wrong</b>. The problem with W5 is one that is only solved by (and I hate myself for this) <b>Earthblood</b> and <b>Heart of the Forest</b> that are still canon as far as I know.<br /> <br /> What are the Garou doing?<br /> <br /> * Apparently exactly what they've always been doing in fighting to save the Earth.<br /> ** Cahill goes on a murder spree through Endron Oil but is also working with environmentalist humans to sabotage the company's efforts to destroy Gaia's sacred places.<br /> ** The protagonist of Heart of the Forest in my game organized protests and pacifist activim to save the Polish national forest.<br /> The Garou haven't STOPPED any of what they're doing or at least I don't think the intent in the book is but they've become more circumspect and trying to figure out new avenues. The Cult, however, is not only murdering everyone they can but murdering their fellow Garou because they think they're not doing their part--which is fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> And yes, I just said FUCKING EARTHBLOOD has artistic merit now ince it is the necessary example the book needed.<br /> <br /> I beat that game and am not getting those hours back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason why the Get need to be defined by Fascism rather than their actual state is because the Authors wanted to make sure we understood that they are a shorthand for dealing with rightwing extremism and wanted to use the Get as convenient targets due to their patchwork history without actually exploring the theme they are supposed to represent </div> </div> </div>I fully admit that someone wanted to go FAR harder on this than the final result. The Swords of Heimdall were destroyed by the Get of Fenris in Revised and the white supremacy issue was resolved in the Get. Go team. Bringing it back is an immensely stupid idea and I'm glad they didn't and that smarter minds prevailed. However, someone still decided to call the Cult of Fenris Nazis and fascists repeatedly which does rather imply some things even if in-text they only appear to be Garou supremacists.<br /> <br /> But I also take the CULT of Fenris as basically embracing the accusations about the Garou Nation taken up to the 11.<br /> <br /> * Forced breeding<br /> * Obsession with lineage<br /> * Obsession with honorable death<br /> * Willingness to wage unrestricted war against civilians<br /> * Being violent stupid meatheads<br /> <br /> The book is overly critical of the Garou but the idea wa to give the Cult of Fenris basically the place where all those ideas go to die. I hate quoting a certain TERF but the Death Eaters aren't preaching anything that the conservative powers that be in Harry Potter don't already believe.<br /> <br /> They just take it to the extreme and that's the relationship between extreme conservativism and fascism. The latter take the beliefs to the Far Right &quot;logical&quot; conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going a step beyond, what's the narrative purpose of the Black Spiral Dancers now? How do they recruit? Why would they even bother? As described they're essentially twiddling their thumbs while the Cult is pretty much doing their jobs as corruptors and manipulators of the Garou (see NPC writeups and the adventures again) </div> </div> </div>\u200bI mean, I basically said my opinion was:<br /> <br /> Cult of Fenris - Technocracy<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers - Nephandi<br /> <br /> This isn't adding nuance but simply that the baddies think they're righteous. The thing is that I really think this attitude of, &quot;These guys fucking suck and deserve to be destroyed&quot; was the attitude I want them to take with the Technocracy in Mage.<br /> <br /> But it showed up here for some reason. Also with one Tribe versus a Breakaway Alliance of members of other tribes. Which seems like it would have been better as I mentioned. But, at least, no reason not to think the Cult of Fenris has non-Get members who joined up later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T22:21:37-08:00","id":1527979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527977#post1527977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the design intent was completely fucked up. Making Werewolf operate with degeneration mechanics like Vampire is the Worst Decision; the people who created Werewolf learned this when they originally intended to make it about cursed people changing during the full moon types, and then rapidly changed it to not make it play like a slightly angrier version of Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is one of those cases where it's mostly something that was always there but is suddenly hugely prominent and with mechanics.<br /> <br /> Like if a Vampire edition suddenly made GOLCONDA a major part of the thing.<br /> <br /> Harano always existed in W5.<br /> <br /> So did the flaws of the Garou Nation as far back as the Storyteller's Handbook. I remember someone said in-universe in that book, &quot;The biggest lie the Garou Nation tell themselves is they're a nation at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"250\" height=\"325\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/W/MEDIAX_792452-T2/images/I/81YWrxWciQL._AC_UF1000,1000_QL80_.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/W/MEDIAX_792452-T2/images/I/81YWrxWciQL._AC_UF1000,1000_QL80_.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/W/MEDIAX_792452-T2/images/I/81YWrxWciQL._AC_UF1000,1000_QL80_.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T22:45:59-08:00","id":1527980,"title":"","content":"I am adding my 2 cents with the caveat that I have no skin in this argument. Still, if folks are seeking alternative Harano mechanics, I'm incredibly fond of the Harano mechanics in MET Werewolf: the Apocalypse. With the global destruction of many caerns, it's much easier for a Garou to experience Harano, which is no longer an affliction that strikes elders and some lupus, but is pervasive, comes in degrees of intensity, and affects all Garou on a spiritual level. The way Harano is addressed has also become much more widely understood by the Garou, and it's strengthening the bonds the Garou have by participating in moot rites and doing things to affirm their faith in Gaia that abate the effects of Harano. I love it because it allows the Garou agency to be more involved in their Septs and do things they should do anyway to address the affliction, i.e., focusing less inward and more on their community and pack. I'm not sold on Hauglosk (I think Seethe is a much cooler mechanic), but for all their flaws, I have to hand it to BNS for how they handled Harano, and I wish Renegade had done the same. Harano comes in stages with different specific effects (it can make one careless, suppress their rage, incapacitate, et al.)<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1429_1704437068453_557\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1429\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1429\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1429&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T22:54:32-08:00","id":1527981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527978#post1527978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, someone still decided to call the Cult of Fenris Nazis and fascists repeatedly which does rather imply some things even if in-text they only appear to be Garou supremacists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cult of Fenris is directly linked to Nazis <b>in-text</b>. Since you keep ignoring the direct reference that exists in the W5 corebook, how about Deepest of Wounds, one of the first W5 adventures released by Renegade? The Cult of Fenris is the big bad in that adventure and so you have Cult of Fenris NPCs in that adventure.<br /> <br /> So the main-Cult of Fenris guy is Black Lung but he has a hypeman called Draug/Eli Markkanen (once again a Nordic reference linked to the Cult of Fenris as well) and here's how he's described:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite having better social acumen than Black Lung, Draug was no less a Fenris fanatic. He looked down on the rest of the sept as ineffectual and<br /> unwilling to make hard decisions. Draug had no qualms leveraging \u201cdeplorable\u201d, hateful and prejudiced aspects of human society<b> like the white nationalist movement and neo-Nazism</b>. His ideas were unwelcome by everyone except Black Lung, which is why the two stuck together. </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> And once again the Cult of Fenris has been <i>directly </i>linked to Nazism in the text! So your claim that the Cult of Fenris are merely Garou supremacists in-text is objectively false. It's obvious at this point (except for you apparently) that in W5 there's a link between Nazism and the Cult of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T23:07:56-08:00","id":1527983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527981#post1527981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cult of Fenris is directly linked to Nazis <b>in-text</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I said in the post.<br /> <br /> Which you KNOW because you read it.<br /> <br /> They're <i>called </i>Nazis.<br /> <br /> DESPITE not having any white supremacist beliefs. Just having Garou supremacist ones.<br /> <br /> It's annoying and confusing.<br /> <br /> And your example flat out PROVES IT. It says he'd not be welcome in any place other than Black Lung and leveraging them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T23:18:16-08:00","id":1527985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527983#post1527983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which I said in the post.<br /> <br /> Which you KNOW because you read it.<br /> <br /> They're <i>called </i>Nazis.<br /> <br /> DESPITE not having any white supremacist beliefs. Just having Garou supremacist ones.<br /> <br /> It's annoying and confusing.<br /> <br /> And your example flat out PROVES IT. It says he'd not be welcome in any place other than Black Lung and leveraging them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so now your claim is &quot;They're called Nazis but that doesn't mean they're Nazis actually.&quot;... Come on! That's a ludicrous thing to say!<br /> <br /> You know why it says &quot;other than Black Lung&quot;...? Because he's the only other <i>Cult of Fenris</i> NPC in the adventure! The text is making it very obvious that Cult of Fenris beliefs are directly linked to Nazism.<br /> <br /> And you know what the Renegade-adventure proves? They are going to keep putting out Cult of Fenris NPCs with Nazi beliefs and writing that talks about Cult of Fenris NPCs having Nazis beliefs. Because that's clearly the intention of W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T23:51:18-08:00","id":1527988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527985#post1527985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, so now your claim is &quot;They're called Nazis but that doesn't mean they're Nazis actually.&quot;... Come on! That's a ludicrous thing to say.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fascism</b><br /> <br /> Werewolf is not a fascist friendly game. Because it\u2019s a<br /> horror game about contemporary issues, it can be a game<br /> where fascism as a theme or fascists as characters show<br /> up. After all, they\u2019re an unfortunate part of the real<br /> world we all inhabit.<br /> <br /> In the simplest terms, you can use Nazis of whatever<br /> stripe seems most appropriate for your setting as enemies.<br /> After all, who doesn\u2019t want to go full Wolfenstein<br /> every now and then? In Werewolf, you can confront the<br /> problems of the world and rip their face off. Nazis are<br /> certainly a problem!<br /> <br /> As with all other potentially difficult themes, participants<br /> can have wildly different reactions and wishes<br /> regarding fascism depending on their personality and<br /> background. For some, Nazis are cartoonish enemies to<br /> be ripped in half. For others, they\u2019re a clear and present<br /> danger, the people who are calling for them to be eradicated.<br /> <br /> This is another topic you may wish to discuss during<br /> session zero especially if it\u2019s expected that fascists or<br /> fascism plays a significant part in the chronicle. What<br /> are the players\u2019 specific comfort levels with the subject?<br /> Remember that people are highly individual. One player<br /> whose life has been impacted by fascism may not wish to<br /> see them in the game, while another with similar experiences<br /> enjoys blasting them to bits.<br /> <br /> Note that in Werewolf, themes of fascism may be<br /> present in the social realm of the players\u2019 characters. A<br /> friend goes over to the Cult of Fenris, seduced by their<br /> message of simpleminded morality. A player may decide<br /> to explore themes of ecofascism in their own character<br /> by skirting close to hauglosk. These situations create<br /> opportunities to grapple with fascism with more nuance<br /> than as simple enemies. How do you bring back a friend<br /> who has gone over to a hateful ideology? How do you<br /> avoid succumbing to bitterness and desperation, and the<br /> simple answers provided by a charismatic demagogue?\u200b<br /> page 321-322<br /> <br /> This is what I'm referring to and frankly its reductionist nonsense. The Cult of Fenris is not portrayed as having white supremacist beliefs but they're called Nazis, which basically just shows they're not interested in a proper portrayal of RL issues.<br /> <br /> If you're going to use cartoon fascists, treat them as cartoon fascists. The Empire, Friends of Humanity, and so on.<br /> <br /> But don't insult real world victims of the Nazis by comparing your cartoon fascists to the real thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:08:57-08:00","id":1527989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527979#post1527979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is one of those cases where it's mostly something that was always there but is suddenly hugely prominent and with mechanics.<br /> <br /> Like if a Vampire edition suddenly made GOLCONDA a major part of the thing.<br /> <br /> Harano always existed in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never been as prominent as Hunger in Vampire, nor is it comparable to Humanity loss, as the game never assumed that you would inevitably fall to Harano. When texts started giving it hard rules, there had to be some extreme break in the character's life, and even then, it was <i>still not an inevitability</i>. This is a diehard Vampire fan's idea of what's important in W:tA and what happens in a story. It's full of the bias of &quot;everything must be comparable to Vampire in every way&quot;. And for games that aren't like it at all, this is an absolutely terrible decision, like if they kept the Imbued but made it so that they had to psychically drain humans to gain Conviction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So did the flaws of the Garou Nation as far back as the Storyteller's Handbook. I remember someone said in-universe in that book, &quot;The biggest lie the Garou Nation tell themselves is they're a nation at all.&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>It also tries to push rivals to the Silver Fangs super hard, but the main narrative of the game didn't have much room for that, either. No matter what words you want to describe it, the Garou Nation was a cohesive society, and snippy soundbites don't really change that.<br /> <br /> (It also had way too much Joseph Campbell in it. Brr.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:20:52-08:00","id":1527992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527988#post1527988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fascism</b><br /> <br /> Werewolf is not a fascist friendly game. Because it\u2019s a<br /> horror game about contemporary issues, it can be a game<br /> where fascism as a theme or fascists as characters show<br /> up. After all, they\u2019re an unfortunate part of the real<br /> world we all inhabit.<br /> <br /> In the simplest terms, you can use Nazis of whatever<br /> stripe seems most appropriate for your setting as enemies.<br /> After all, who doesn\u2019t want to go full Wolfenstein<br /> every now and then? In Werewolf, you can confront the<br /> problems of the world and rip their face off. Nazis are<br /> certainly a problem!<br /> <br /> As with all other potentially difficult themes, participants<br /> can have wildly different reactions and wishes<br /> regarding fascism depending on their personality and<br /> background. For some, Nazis are cartoonish enemies to<br /> be ripped in half. For others, they\u2019re a clear and present<br /> danger, the people who are calling for them to be eradicated.<br /> <br /> This is another topic you may wish to discuss during<br /> session zero especially if it\u2019s expected that fascists or<br /> fascism plays a significant part in the chronicle. What<br /> are the players\u2019 specific comfort levels with the subject?<br /> Remember that people are highly individual. One player<br /> whose life has been impacted by fascism may not wish to<br /> see them in the game, while another with similar experiences<br /> enjoys blasting them to bits.<br /> <br /> Note that in Werewolf, themes of fascism may be<br /> present in the social realm of the players\u2019 characters. A<br /> friend goes over to the Cult of Fenris, seduced by their<br /> message of simpleminded morality. A player may decide<br /> to explore themes of ecofascism in their own character<br /> by skirting close to hauglosk. These situations create<br /> opportunities to grapple with fascism with more nuance<br /> than as simple enemies. How do you bring back a friend<br /> who has gone over to a hateful ideology? How do you<br /> avoid succumbing to bitterness and desperation, and the<br /> simple answers provided by a charismatic demagogue?<br /> page 321-322<br /> <br /> This is what I'm referring to and frankly its reductionist nonsense. The Cult of Fenris is not portrayed as having white supremacist beliefs but they're called Nazis, which basically just shows they're not interested in a proper portrayal of RL issues.<br /> <br /> If you're going to use cartoon fascists, treat them as cartoon fascists. The Empire, Friends of Humanity, and so on.<br /> <br /> But don't insult real world victims of the Nazis by comparing your cartoon fascists to the real thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are we just discounting the &quot;someone&quot; who wanted to turn the Get entirely into the Swords of Heimdall? Because I doubt that he was going to just leave that behind after all of the obstacles to making it happen suddenly disappeared. The last paragraph is also pretty clearly equating hauglosk to going over to the fascist pipeline, and that the Cult, being all about falling to Hauglosk, is the resulting hive of hate that's left after that.<br /> <br /> This is like a solitary fig leaf over the end goal that &quot;someone&quot; had, and I don't expect it to stay on for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:33:28-08:00","id":1527993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527992#post1527992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So are we just discounting the &quot;someone&quot; who wanted to turn the Get entirely into the Swords of Heimdall?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean we should discount him.<br /> <br /> It's a terrible fucking idea.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad everyone else at Paradox Interactive agrees.<br /> <br /> No mention of the Swords anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:33:30-08:00","id":1527994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527978#post1527978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Forced breeding<br /> * Obsession with lineage<br /> * Obsession with honorable death<br /> * Willingness to wage unrestricted war against civilians<br /> * Being violent stupid meatheads<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you get the forced breeding from, but that is aside my point.<br /> <br /> But you know what isn't on that list?<br /> * Cannibalism<br /> * Intentionally spreading diseases to kill humans<br /> * Supporting the US prison system with the sole intention of locking people up regardless of their guilt<br /> * Being a wetworker or a merc<br /> <br /> You know who have those details? The example PCs of some tribes. Zero Hauglosk suffering,too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:34:27-08:00","id":1527995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527994#post1527994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know where you get the forced breeding from, but that is aside my point.<br /> <br /> But you know what isn't on that list?<br /> * Cannibalism<br /> * Intentionally spreading diseases to kill humans<br /> * Supporting the US prison system with the sole intention of locking people up regardless of their guilt<br /> * Being a wetworker or a merc<br /> <br /> You know who have those details? The example PCs of some tribes. Zero Hauglosk suffering,too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was my point.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris being the 11 on the Garou traditional belief scale.<br /> <br /> They take all the evils of previous edition that the Garou kind of suffer from and get highlighted in W5 then go bannanas with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:43:32-08:00","id":1527997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527995#post1527995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was my point.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris being the 11 on the Garou traditional belief scale.<br /> <br /> They take all the evils of previous edition that the Garou kind of suffer from and get highlighted in W5 then go bannanas with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are example PCs for W5, doing things that BSDs and the Pure do. That and we have no evidence of the CoF eating people or spreading diseases/wetwork. They seem too focused on purity of purpose and the fight itself to do that.<br /> <br /> You can't turn what those example PCs do to 11, they are already at 12 from the outset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T01:48:06-08:00","id":1528000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527988#post1527988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I'm referring to and frankly its reductionist nonsense. The Cult of Fenris is not portrayed as having white supremacist beliefs but they're called Nazis, which basically just shows they're not interested in a proper portrayal of RL issues.<br /> <br /> If you're going to use cartoon fascists, treat them as cartoon fascists. The Empire, Friends of Humanity, and so on.<br /> <br /> But don't insult real world victims of the Nazis by comparing your cartoon fascists to the real thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed that this isn't how this topic should be treated. But you know who disagrees with you on that? Paradox! They are going to keep mentioning Nazism in relation to the Cult of Fenris and NPCs who belong to that faction. The RL-implications and positions of somebody being a Nazi aren't going to be outlined of course but the adventure Deepest of Wounds shows that they are going to keep mentioning Nazism and talk about how Cult of Fenris antagonists have Nazi beliefs.<br /> <br /> And you may not want to portray the Cult of Fenris as Nazis but the adventure Deepest of Wounds clearly does. You would have to change the Cult of Fenris NPCs in that adventure to <i>not </i>portray the Cult of Fenris as having Nazi-beliefs. So your idea of the Cult of Fenris not being Nazis is fanfiction since the official published material from Paradox/Renegade contradicts that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:34:09-08:00","id":1528009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528000#post1528000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed that this isn't how this topic should be treated. But you know who disagrees with you on that? Paradox! They are going to keep mentioning Nazism in relation to the Cult of Fenris and NPCs who belong to that faction. The RL-implications and positions of somebody being a Nazi aren't going to be outlined of course but the adventure Deepest of Wounds shows that they are going to keep mentioning Nazism and talk about how Cult of Fenris antagonists have Nazi beliefs.<br /> <br /> And you may not want to portray the Cult of Fenris as Nazis but the adventure Deepest of Wounds clearly does. You would have to change the Cult of Fenris NPCs in that adventure to <i>not </i>portray the Cult of Fenris as having Nazi-beliefs. So your idea of the Cult of Fenris not being Nazis is fanfiction since the official published material from Paradox/Renegade contradicts that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, I'm criticizing Paradox for it.<br /> <br /> I can happily defend the Fall of the Get of Fenris to being the Cult of Fenris in general (and feel the best thing to play with it is an ex-Get of Fenris) while also thinking they messed up the handling a great deal.<br /> <br /> And the two NPCs can be white supremacists also without the entire cult being but, yes, I will acknowledge they could indeed paint it as an official part of their ideology as a whole. Soft-locking the Swords of Heimdall idea in even if they rejected it in concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:36:14-08:00","id":1528010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527997#post1527997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are example PCs for W5, doing things that BSDs and the Pure do. That and we have no evidence of the CoF eating people or spreading diseases/wetwork. They seem too focused on purity of purpose and the fight itself to do that.<br /> <br /> You can't turn what those example PCs do to 11, they are already at 12 from the outset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we know the Cult of Fenris is waging war against the entirety of the Garou Nation and have some overthetop evils in the sample adventure including brainwashing magic.<br /> <br /> But the Sample PCs seem to be pretty standard Edgelord fair.<br /> <br /> The idea of the PCs being heroes of the Spawn and Riddick mold.<br /> <br /> That's nothing new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:53:20-08:00","id":1528012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528009#post1528009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, yeah, I'm criticizing Paradox for it.<br /> <br /> I can happily defend the Fall of the Get of Fenris to being the Cult of Fenris in general (and feel the best thing to play with it is an ex-Get of Fenris) while also thinking they messed up the handling a great deal.<br /> <br /> And the two NPCs can be white supremacists also without the entire cult being but, yes, I will acknowledge they could indeed paint it as an official part of their ideology as a whole. Soft-locking the Swords of Heimdall idea in even if they rejected it in concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what's going to happen is that as you mentioned the Cult of Fenris is supposed to be Garou-ideology turned up to 11 and what will keep happening is that writers take that idea of the Cult as radicals and one way in which they will express that radical nature is to keep talking about Cult of Fenris Garou having Nazi-beliefs. It will be just this quick way of explaining why this is a radical Garou who's an antagonist. So &quot;This Garou is a Nazi.&quot; will keep popping up whenever the topic of the Cult of Fenris comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T06:19:27-08:00","id":1528016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528012#post1528012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what's going to happen is that as you mentioned the Cult of Fenris is supposed to be Garou-ideology turned up to 11 and what will keep happening is that writers take that idea of the Cult as radicals and one way in which they will express that radical nature is to keep talking about Cult of Fenris Garou having Nazi-beliefs. It will be just this quick way of explaining why this is a radical Garou who's an antagonist. So &quot;This Garou is a Nazi.&quot; will keep popping up whenever the topic of the Cult of Fenris comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, if it happens, will be dumb.<br /> <br /> Give them perfectly Garou appropriate views like restarting the Impergium or killing every McDonalds, err, O'Tolley's employee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T06:37:38-08:00","id":1528019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528010#post1528010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, we know the Cult of Fenris is waging war against the entirety of the Garou Nation and have some overthetop evils in the sample adventure including brainwashing magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, there is no Nation any more. That and from the text, I got the impression the CoF were more interested in fighting the Wyrm than what remains of the Nation. That is why they left in the first place. Even in the Deepest Wounds, they want the other sept to join them, not to destroy it. That doesn't seem like a war on the remaining garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528010#post1528010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Sample PCs seem to be pretty standard Edgelord fair.<br /> <br /> The idea of the PCs being heroes of the Spawn and Riddick mold.<br /> <br /> That's nothing new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for WtA though. Not when the whole point of the CoF is that they take terrible actions in defense of Gaia and so aren't heroes. Not when one of the mechanics is turning into a fanatic.<br /> <br /> Eating humans, infecting wells, etc. are things that BSDs do and one method is taken straight from the Fire-Touched from Forsaken. The bad guy factions.<br /> <br /> To present these guys as player characters in this context is to completely undermine the point of both CoF and Hauglosk. If you can start with a maneater with a body count and zero Hauglosk points, then what makes the CoF worthy of Hauglosk 5?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, they took one of the most hated tribes in WtA and actively made it WORSE by decrees most edgelords wouldn't dare to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 01-05-2024, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T08:31:34-08:00","id":1528024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1527993#post1527993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean we should discount him.<br /> <br /> It's a terrible fucking idea.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad everyone else at Paradox Interactive agrees.<br /> <br /> No mention of the Swords anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that's going to be difficult. He basically runs the nitty gritty of the WoD part of PDX's operations. So, this botched handling of the fall of the Get? Engineered by him, and couldn't have any other shape but that because he was behind it. The books that keep going on in the line? He's in charge of approval by PDX, and can likely pull a Changing Ways on anything to insert more bad Werewolf Nazi Danganronpa shit. Unless there's another major international incident involving the WoD that happens on his watch, he'll still be there.<br /> <br /> The rest of PDX doesn't seem to be disagreeing with him, either. They're either going to tell him to be more circumspect, or at the higher corporate level, to not care. That latter point, a nicely succinct reasoning why there's utter and craven cowardice in VV5 to not condemn corporate operational structure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T08:32:43-08:00","id":1528025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528016#post1528016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which, if it happens, will be dumb.<br /> <br /> Give them perfectly Garou appropriate views like restarting the Impergium...</div> </div> </div> </div>No Garou thinks that's even possible. Because it isn't! Through all of Revised, they saw it, realize it, know it, and don't bring it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T09:43:54-08:00","id":1528032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1524874#post1524874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THEN, there is the &quot;you shouldn't try anything&quot; message. Which in a game about environmental destruction is... poorly thought out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because for a capitalist company, that is what they want people to think. Imagine a CEO and the acionists reading a book written by your company, saying, &quot;So, take down the rich, destroy the capitalist system, and substitute by a more community-centered system is the way to save Gaia. And the Garou can only do this if they organize, and organize the kinfolks and the humans from the communities to which they belong.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T10:14:22-08:00","id":1528037,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of this gem regarding the disparity between what was published in V5 vs W5 <div align=\"center\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:47:49-08:00","id":1528047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528037#post1528037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded of this gem regarding the disparity between what was published in V5 vs W5 <div align=\"center\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1528035&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div></div> </div> </div> </div>This was in V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T13:58:14-08:00","id":1528058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528032#post1528032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because for a capitalist company, that is what they want people to think. Imagine a CEO and the acionists reading a book written by your company, saying, &quot;So, take down the rich, destroy the capitalist system, and substitute by a more community-centered system is the way to save Gaia. And the Garou can only do this if they organize, and organize the kinfolks and the humans from the communities to which they belong.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, our examples include EARTHBLOOD and HEART OF THE FOREST under Paradox.<br /> <br /> Earthblood has you murder 1000 people to stop Exxon, err, Endron.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest is all about activism to save Poland's national forest.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're going to see much of a change from W:TA's environmental themes save for, &quot;We're doing it DESPITE fucking it up.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T14:09:40-08:00","id":1528059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528058#post1528058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, our examples include EARTHBLOOD and HEART OF THE FOREST under Paradox.<br /> <br /> Earthblood has you murder 1000 people to stop Exxon, err, Endron.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest is all about activism to save Poland's national forest.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're going to see much of a change from W:TA's environmental themes save for, &quot;We're doing it DESPITE fucking it up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither Heart of the Forest nor Earthblood are canon to the current W5 lore.<br /> <br /> How do I know this? Because both games were made while W5 was under either the in-house team (Heart of the Forest) or Hunters Entertainment (Earthblood.) The Renegade version of the game is very recent and only the boardgame Retaliation is canon to it, minus the name of Hart Wardens.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest had good Fenrir in it and it was allowed to have the Pc come from a Fenrir lineage. Something which I highly doubt would have been possible once the game switched devs.<br /> <br /> Plus, when you are giving the game devs the lore, you aren't going to keep updating them on the changes constantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T14:37:21-08:00","id":1528060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528059#post1528059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither Heart of the Forest nor Earthblood are canon to the current W5 lore.<br /> <br /> How do I know this? Because both games were made while W5 was under either the in-house team (Heart of the Forest) or Hunters Entertainment (Earthblood.) The Renegade version of the game is very recent and only the boardgame Retaliation is canon to it, minus the name of Hart Wardens.<br /> <br /> Heart of the Forest had good Fenrir in it and it was allowed to have the Pc come from a Fenrir lineage. Something which I highly doubt would have been possible once the game switched devs.<br /> <br /> Plus, when you are giving the game devs the lore, you aren't going to keep updating them on the changes constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think that assumption is made with the conclusion in mind because <b>Heart of the Forest</b> and <b>Earthblood</b> are still being sold.<br /> <br /> When Paradox wants something declared non-canon, they take it off the shelves as we see with the mobile games they produced and then removed.<br /> <br /> Also, Heart of the Forest is the first place we learned of the Get of Fenris' fall to fascism and evil. People shit talk them throughout the game. You are of Get lineage but expected to join one of the other tribes. I should point out that isn't against the design philosophy of W5 as there's literally a Loresheet in the back of the book about that.<br /> <br /> <b>Renunciate of Fenris </b>is bascially made in mind with the idea the player character is a Get of Fenris who has seen Wolf go rogue as well as the rest of the tribe go crazy.<br /> <br /> <b>** Esteemed</b><br /> Garou were present<br /> during your renunciation of<br /> Fenris and made you a bit of<br /> an example for others. Your<br /> Renown is considered one<br /> lower than its actual value<br /> during social interactions at<br /> moots. However, none may<br /> question your ferocity \u2014 if<br /> you ever have a situation<br /> that would cause you to Lose<br /> the Wolf because of a failed<br /> Rage check, you may make<br /> an additional Rage check; if it<br /> succeeds, your Rage remains<br /> at 1 instead of dropping to 0.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Unbroken: </b>Despite renouncing<br /> Wolf, the great spirit\u2019s<br /> patronage taught you fearlessness<br /> that persists within<br /> you. When a Gift or other<br /> supernatural effect would<br /> engender fear in you, you may<br /> gain two dice with which to resist,<br /> when such an advantage<br /> is possible. Should you do so,<br /> however, you lose one die to<br /> resist frenzy for the remainder<br /> of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Channeled Fury:</b> Fenris\u2019<br /> asperity remains strong in<br /> you. Once per scene you may<br /> opt to automatically succeed<br /> at any single Rage check to<br /> activate a Gift with a pool roll,<br /> but you also incur an extra<br /> Brutal result on that pool roll.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Last Howl:</b> You have witnessed<br /> firsthand the effects<br /> of hauglosk, having watched<br /> the glint of fanatical zeal fall<br /> kindle in your compatriots\u2019<br /> eyes \u2014 but not so in yours.<br /> Once per chronicle, if you<br /> mark your last hauglosk box,<br /> you may make a Rage check;<br /> if that Rage check fails, untick<br /> that last hauglosk box. Congratulations:<br /> You\u2019ve fought<br /> your way back from the brink<br /> <br /> Last Howl is notably so far the only proof that Hauglosk can be reduced in-universe but, apparently, can be at the ST's discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-05-2024, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T14:50:41-08:00","id":1528061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528060#post1528060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Last Howl is notably so far the only proof that Hauglosk can be reduced in-universe but, apparently, can be at the ST's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so, I'm going to hit you with a common complaint about how the Triat books cleared up a lot but still didn't get the message out: a fat load of good this does if it's not in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T15:30:14-08:00","id":1528063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528061#post1528061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so, I'm going to hit you with a common complaint about how the Triat books cleared up a lot but still didn't get the message out: a fat load of good this does if it's not in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the above IS in the corebook.<br /> <br /> It's on page 298.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T15:37:18-08:00","id":1528064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528063#post1528063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the above IS in the corebook.<br /> <br /> It's on page 298.</div> </div> </div> </div>So was the Triat in Legacy editions. The full clarifications about the story of the Triat? Not so much. The overwhelming message for W5 is still &quot;You can't really expect to reduce Hauglosk&quot;, and given that people would probably be hard pressed to pay 55 USD for a book that hardly gives them much to work with, paying 35 USD more is probably something that would rightly make them angry, given that the W5 core seems to have wasted so much of its page count on shrugging with non-answers. This is the worst part of 90s-style game design, trying to get people to chase future books with artificial &quot;mysteries&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T15:42:30-08:00","id":1528065,"title":"","content":"It's a glaring absence but I don't think the absence is evidence of absence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T16:58:16-08:00","id":1528068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528060#post1528060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last Howl is notably so far the only proof that Hauglosk can be reduced in-universe but, apparently, can be at the ST's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, anything can happen at the ST's discretion.<br /> <br /> The takeaway though is that reducing Hauglosk is intended to be extremely rare and difficult for players to accomplish. It requires a specific 5 dot Loresheet, and you can only do it once per chronicle (so effectively you maybe get 6 Hauglosk points instead of 5 before turning into an NPC but there's still the possibility that you fail your Rage roll so you're SOL anyway). Any other way to reduce Hauglosk (or Harano) would likely need to have similar requirements and difficulties. Ultimately it's seems that removing Harano/Hauglosk isn't something that's intended for every PC at the table to be able to do, and certainly not with anything approaching frequency, ease or certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T17:56:03-08:00","id":1528070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528060#post1528060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last Howl is notably so far the only proof that Hauglosk can be reduced in-universe but, apparently, can be at the ST's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a talisman in the book as well that does that (of course with the caveat that said talisman is super-rare; Gaia's Tear pg 188).<br /> <br /> But Harano/Hauglosk is poorly handled in W5. Mechanically, as far as PCs are concerned it's pretty much a doom-spiral. The trackers for Harano/Hauglosk are only increasing and if you dig into the corebook you can occasionally find edge-cases in the rules that allow a PC to reduce their Harano/Hauglosk. But narratively, it's weirdly very forgiving. Just take the descriptions from pg 51 to 53. Those sections suggest PCs can snap Garou-Elders out of Harano or Hauglosk. And yet, mechanically it's just this death-march to hitting a game-over screen with Garou-PCs. The descriptions from 51 to 53 suggest a dynamism that just isn't there in the mechanics of the game.<br /> <br /> There would be value in not making Harano 5 and Hauglosk 5 automatic fail-states for PCs because not only would you get gameplay out of PCs dealing with another PC hitting Harano or Hauglosk 5 but this would also introduce mechanics for the very thing that gets mentioned on pg 51 to 53. Of course, we instead get into contradictory claims from the W5 corebook here. Those pages suggest gameplay around snapping Garou out of Harano and Hauglosk but mechanically, any PC who hits Harano 5 or Hauglosk is doomed forever according to the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I believe Harano/Hauglosk needs to be reworked both as a mechanic and conceptually. I did it once during the one time I ran W5 for the sake of trying out what's in the book but if it were up to me I would never run W5 with Harano/Hauglosk in the way they are presented in the W5 corebook, both conceptually and in terms of mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T18:49:33-08:00","id":1528076,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my take on it is they should do it like Bloodlines or willpower.<br /> <br /> &quot;You do a big good or worthy accomplishment and lose one.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T19:47:04-08:00","id":1528081,"title":"","content":"I can't say that I share your boundless optimism in this edition, given the people at the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T19:57:01-08:00","id":1528082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528081#post1528081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say that I share your boundless optimism in this edition, given the people at the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fine&quot; is closer to how I feel about the edition than &quot;boundless optimism.&quot; It's a 3 star book, IMHO and that's out of 5.<br /> <br /> It's not bad but it's not particularly well organized either.<br /> <br /> The majority of, &quot;WHAT DO GAROU DO?&quot; is listed in the tribe section where it describes them as doing all the usual adventures versus in the Storytelling section.<br /> <br /> Black Furies in play might expect to liberate a victim<br /> from an oppressor, overcome the local media\u2019s manufactured<br /> consent to a hazardous power plant, dismantle that<br /> recalcitrant chemical plant, and demolish a caern that\u2019s<br /> too tainted by its previous occupiers to reclaim. Page 60<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers in play might expect to infiltrate a<br /> restricted area, pilfer a compromised journalist\u2019s laptop,<br /> eavesdrop on dirty cops, witness an illicit deal happening,<br /> and surmise how they\u2019re all related\u200b page 62<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia in play might expect to discover a<br /> cache of artifacts left by legendary Garou, discern the<br /> true nature of a trickster-spirit, heal the injury others<br /> suffer, or puzzle out the solution to an Umbral quandary.\u200b Page 64","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-05-2024, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T22:26:38-08:00","id":1528083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528082#post1528082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Fine&quot; is closer to how I feel about the edition than &quot;boundless optimism.&quot; It's a 3 star book, IMHO and that's out of 5.<br /> <br /> It's not bad but it's not particularly well organized either.<br /> <br /> The majority of, &quot;WHAT DO GAROU DO?&quot; is listed in the tribe section where it describes them as doing all the usual adventures versus in the Storytelling section.<br /> <br /> Black Furies in play might expect to liberate a victim<br /> from an oppressor, overcome the local media\u2019s manufactured<br /> consent to a hazardous power plant, dismantle that<br /> recalcitrant chemical plant, and demolish a caern that\u2019s<br /> too tainted by its previous occupiers to reclaim. Page 60<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers in play might expect to infiltrate a<br /> restricted area, pilfer a compromised journalist\u2019s laptop,<br /> eavesdrop on dirty cops, witness an illicit deal happening,<br /> and surmise how they\u2019re all related page 62<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia in play might expect to discover a<br /> cache of artifacts left by legendary Garou, discern the<br /> true nature of a trickster-spirit, heal the injury others<br /> suffer, or puzzle out the solution to an Umbral quandary.\u200b Page 64</div> </div> </div> </div>We are so far in the hole that three stars here is boundless optimism. Those summations by tribe, incidentally, are often redundant and/or outside the character of the tribe. Bone Gnawers should not be wolf nosferatu. It's testament to the shallow understanding of what Garou can do and attribution of everything terrible to them - as with vampires - that the writing team saw a down and out, frequently urban tribe and immediately said &quot;what if they did they same thing in the Garou Nation (which we unmade anyway) that the Nossies do in vampire culture?&quot; instead of keeping them as an urban and at times rural defense league, an actual place where the outcasts go instead of one where they seem to have to earn their keep to Garou that don't even seem to give a shit anymore.<br /> <br /> From start to finish, this project was brought down by V:tM, in every conceivable way. I wouldn't give it anything. I surely am not going to pay 55 USD for a book with no usable information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T00:53:17-08:00","id":1528086,"title":"","content":"The sheer number of them that would be equally at home with what H5's Driven get up to is also an issue. Most of them aren't even explicitly supernatural, and thanks to others changes to the setting, the few that focus on the supernatural side of the WoD are left to the same outsider and low-information position It only further hammers home the implication that the Garou are all better losing the wolf and then using their limited knowledge of the supernatural world to help human activists be more successful by knowing what they're missing when things just don't seem to go right despite their best plans and efforts. The Black Furies overlap a ton with the Martial Creed, the Bone Gnawers with the Underground Creed, and the Children of Gaia with the mystic side of the Inquisitive Creed.<br /> <br /> Something H5 is actually better at, is how having a mixed group is beneficial. H5 puts more focus on the &quot;what do they do?&quot; when talking about Cells (aka the group the PCs all belong to), while the combination of Creed and Drive informs what role and benefit a hunter brings to the equation.<br /> <br /> By putting such concepts in the Tribe write ups, they become divorced from the base group unit of the pack. Instead of talking more about how to establish what individual packs do, to then see how different Tribe and Auspice combinations can combine towards a unified goal or ideal, the entries focused on the Tribes makes things sound disconnected where members of the same pack will go off and do their own things rather than work together even if they're seeking the same end result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T01:14:44-08:00","id":1528087,"title":"","content":"Auspice was not accounted above, but then again the DEVS didn't much care for it.<br /> <br /> The suggested characters range from very mild (A Silver Fang former COLLEGE football star?) to ghost pepper (infecting villages) and few of them would, as Heavy Arms said, do better as human characters.<br /> <br /> Because Rage in W5 doesn't really allow you to do some of the jobs. Sawbones works as a backalley doctor, a job that is very stressful and includes a lot of moments where you'd easily end up at Rage 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T01:51:38-08:00","id":1528088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528086#post1528086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sheer number of them that would be equally at home with what H5's Driven get up to is also an issue. Most of them aren't even explicitly supernatural, and thanks to others changes to the setting, the few that focus on the supernatural side of the WoD are left to the same outsider and low-information position It only further hammers home the implication that the Garou are all better losing the wolf and then using their limited knowledge of the supernatural world to help human activists be more successful by knowing what they're missing when things just don't seem to go right despite their best plans and efforts. The Black Furies overlap a ton with the Martial Creed, the Bone Gnawers with the Underground Creed, and the Children of Gaia with the mystic side of the Inquisitive Creed.<br /> <br /> Something H5 is actually better at, is how having a mixed group is beneficial. H5 puts more focus on the &quot;what do they do?&quot; when talking about Cells (aka the group the PCs all belong to), while the combination of Creed and Drive informs what role and benefit a hunter brings to the equation.<br /> <br /> By putting such concepts in the Tribe write ups, they become divorced from the base group unit of the pack. Instead of talking more about how to establish what individual packs do, to then see how different Tribe and Auspice combinations can combine towards a unified goal or ideal, the entries focused on the Tribes makes things sound disconnected where members of the same pack will go off and do their own things rather than work together even if they're seeking the same end result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with all of the decisions made for how they've divided up the tribes and I think they could have had a lot more flavor and power blocks than they've added even if they did want to make them all very global.<br /> <br /> For example, the Hart Wardens are suddenly all Caern Guards and that has absolutely no relationship to the Fianna of old as far as I can tell. They could easily have made them the &quot;Galliard&quot; tribe the same way that the Ghost Council used to be the Theruge tribe (and still is). Guarding territory isn't an identity the way, say, &quot;Bard&quot; is in a way that is easily understood and universal.<br /> <br /> They could have also incorporated the Nuwisha so there was a Ragabash Tribe and given people some more options rather than just distracting them. Especially as Coyotes being separate from Werewolves was always silly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T01:53:10-08:00","id":1528089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528087#post1528087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspice was not accounted above, but then again the DEVS didn't much care for it.<br /> <br /> The suggested characters range from very mild (A Silver Fang former COLLEGE football star?) to ghost pepper (infecting villages) and few of them would, as Heavy Arms said, do better as human characters.<br /> <br /> Because Rage in W5 doesn't really allow you to do some of the jobs. Sawbones works as a backalley doctor, a job that is very stressful and includes a lot of moments where you'd easily end up at Rage 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>My inclination is that the &quot;Character Archetypes&quot; are getting more attention in this thread and general reactions than I ever gave them in the entire history of WOD. They're just there to throw things at the wall and &quot;cannibal Red Talon&quot; and &quot;Bio-weapon supervillain&quot; are just there to spark ideas of the variety that they can come in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T02:12:37-08:00","id":1528091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528089#post1528089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My inclination is that the &quot;Character Archetypes&quot; are getting more attention in this thread and general reactions than I ever gave them in the entire history of WOD. They're just there to throw things at the wall and &quot;cannibal Red Talon&quot; and &quot;Bio-weapon supervillain&quot; are just there to spark ideas of the variety that they can come in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are in opposition to the whole tone and especially the whole &quot;Garou are bad because they do awful things and being a fanatic nets you Hauglosk points&quot; thing. When presenting example characters, you shouldn't have ones that for sure get Hauglosked to hell and back once they enter play. If a Red Talon cannibal has zero Hauglosk, why does a CoF saboteur have 5?<br /> <br /> On top of everything, this was their chance to make the Talons less hated and easier to play. Instead, they decided to double down in their worst aspects and add some new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T03:01:30-08:00","id":1528093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528091#post1528091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they are in opposition to the whole tone and especially the whole &quot;Garou are bad because they do awful things and being a fanatic nets you Hauglosk points&quot; thing. When presenting example characters, you shouldn't have ones that for sure get Hauglosked to hell and back once they enter play. If a Red Talon cannibal has zero Hauglosk, why does a CoF saboteur have 5?<br /> <br /> On top of everything, this was their chance to make the Talons less hated and easier to play. Instead, they decided to double down in their worst aspects and add some new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly red talons revised does a great job on that by articulating their ideas and beliefs, explaing the variation on outlooks (hawks vs doves) and elaborating on what the red talons actually contribute to the garou nation. Along with some solid rp tips on running lupus <br /> <br /> On reflection it's a real shame w5 chose not to build on revised werewolf in general. It'd actually be pretty neat to see a garou reformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T04:42:53-08:00","id":1528096,"title":"","content":"I liked Revised but sometimes I felt it went a little too far in trying to tone down the Garou's flaws. The Garou are never at their most interesting save when they're deeply fucked up institutionally.<br /> <br /> Basically, barbarian berserkers and kings stuck in the 20th/21st centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T04:51:27-08:00","id":1528097,"title":"","content":"Conceptually we know what Auspice and Tribe are supposed to do/represent in the game. Well, partly, I guess... It's a bit confusing actually. In the previews, it said &quot;Tribe is what you do and Auspice is how you do it.&quot; whereas in the released book on pg 59 it's &quot;Auspice is what you do and Tribe is why you do it.&quot;. In both versions using only verbs to answer those categories was a bit weird. Never understood that obsession with only using verbs...<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Auspice-part can be written off because in the end Auspice has been rendered largely irrelevant by the game, both in terms of mechanics and roleplaying. Since much of the context and depth of Garou-society has been stripped away, there isn't a lot of substance to roleplaying your Auspice and mechanically Auspice only matters when it comes to picking Gifts.<br /> <br /> With the Tribes (whether in answer to &quot;What you do?&quot; or &quot;Why you do it?&quot;), I think the biggest issue is that too little reimagining happened here. First, there's the issue that even with two NPC-Tribes, that still leaves 11 Tribes to pick from. In a broad categorization like &quot;What you do?&quot; that's way too much and so the result is that there's quite a bit of overlap between the Tribes. Second, aside from the Black Furies and the Native American Tribes the Tribes haven't seen any kind of re-imagining. Instead, the only move made here was to strip context and lore/worldbuilding away from the Tribes. Sometimes it's to erase ties to specific human ethnicities or regions and other times it's just bits of lore/worldbuilding that would make the Tribes as concepts more specific. Not only was the process not very thorough but the work wasn't put in to actually reimagine the Tribes under the goal of &quot;What you do?&quot;/&quot;Why you do it?&quot;. Kinfolk and Pure Breed have been removed and the idea of becoming a Garou due to blood-relations has been de-emphasized and yet the W5 writers left the Silver Fangs as a Tribe of &quot;inherited aristocracy&quot; instead of reimagining what it means to be the leadership-Tribe in the new vision of W5. Silent Striders with the completely ambiguous to the point of irrelevancy curse have a similar problem. Since the SIlent Strider's ties to the Setites and Egypt has been removed, why not completely reimagine the Tribe as one of wandering, scouting and exploring...? The fact that despite erasing lore/worldbuilding the concepts of the Tribes are still somewhat beholden to their previous versions puts needless limits on how to make the Tribes answer the question of &quot;What you do?&quot;/&quot;Why you do it?&quot;. Naturally, this isn't how the Tribes were conceptualized in previous editions, so it will create problems when you try to take these concepts and flatten them in an effort to fit the new conception of the Tribes. And so you get Tribal concepts instead that feel stripped down and bland instead of providing inspiration to players for what they want to play. Additionally, they may have strived to remove lore/worldbuilding but people know from V5 and the Clans there that there should be a bit of lore/worldbuilding attached to those Tribes. And at that point, you just then get people who immediately will go back to the previous editions and when a Tribe like Bone Gnawers makes someone curious, they're not working with any new conception that W5 was going for but will instead go back to the Bone Gnawers lore of previous editions as the worldbuilding of the W5 version isn't strong enough to stand on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T06:32:58-08:00","id":1528100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528097#post1528097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually we know what Auspice and Tribe are supposed to do/represent in the game. Well, partly, I guess... It's a bit confusing actually. In the previews, it said &quot;Tribe is what you do and Auspice is how you do it.&quot; whereas in the released book on pg 59 it's &quot;Auspice is what you do and Tribe is why you do it.&quot;. In both versions using only verbs to answer those categories was a bit weird. Never understood that obsession with only using verbs...<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Auspice-part can be written off because in the end Auspice has been rendered largely irrelevant by the game, both in terms of mechanics and roleplaying. Since much of the context and depth of Garou-society has been stripped away, there isn't a lot of substance to roleplaying your Auspice and mechanically Auspice only matters when it comes to picking Gifts.<br /> <br /> With the Tribes (whether in answer to &quot;What you do?&quot; or &quot;Why you do it?&quot;), I think the biggest issue is that too little reimagining happened here. First, there's the issue that even with two NPC-Tribes, that still leaves 11 Tribes to pick from. In a broad categorization like &quot;What you do?&quot; that's way too much and so the result is that there's quite a bit of overlap between the Tribes. Second, aside from the Black Furies and the Native American Tribes the Tribes haven't seen any kind of re-imagining. Instead, the only move made here was to strip context and lore/worldbuilding away from the Tribes. Sometimes it's to erase ties to specific human ethnicities or regions and other times it's just bits of lore/worldbuilding that would make the Tribes as concepts more specific. Not only was the process not very thorough but the work wasn't put in to actually reimagine the Tribes under the goal of &quot;What you do?&quot;/&quot;Why you do it?&quot;. Kinfolk and Pure Breed have been removed and the idea of becoming a Garou due to blood-relations has been de-emphasized and yet the W5 writers left the Silver Fangs as a Tribe of &quot;inherited aristocracy&quot; instead of reimagining what it means to be the leadership-Tribe in the new vision of W5. Silent Striders with the completely ambiguous to the point of irrelevancy curse have a similar problem. Since the SIlent Strider's ties to the Setites and Egypt has been removed, why not completely reimagine the Tribe as one of wandering, scouting and exploring...? The fact that despite erasing lore/worldbuilding the concepts of the Tribes are still somewhat beholden to their previous versions puts needless limits on how to make the Tribes answer the question of &quot;What you do?&quot;/&quot;Why you do it?&quot;. Naturally, this isn't how the Tribes were conceptualized in previous editions, so it will create problems when you try to take these concepts and flatten them in an effort to fit the new conception of the Tribes. And so you get Tribal concepts instead that feel stripped down and bland instead of providing inspiration to players for what they want to play. Additionally, they may have strived to remove lore/worldbuilding but people know from V5 and the Clans there that there should be a bit of lore/worldbuilding attached to those Tribes. And at that point, you just then get people who immediately will go back to the previous editions and when a Tribe like Bone Gnawers makes someone curious, they're not working with any new conception that W5 was going for but will instead go back to the Bone Gnawers lore of previous editions as the worldbuilding of the W5 version isn't strong enough to stand on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I don't think much of the lore has been that changed in a few of the areas above:<br /> <br /> * The Bone Gnawers are described as basically the same way as they always were. Just sneakier.<br /> <br /> * Eh, Silver Fangs being inherited aristocracy is something that removing would effectively get rid of them as a concept competely because that's their thing. Mind you, as we saw with the Silver Fangs, they were about challenges and positions and manuevering as well so you could easily do that with adopted heirs and other alliances without getting deeply into the idea of aristocrats. Besides, there's plenty to do with the idea some families have histories of werewolfdom without tying it to genetics completely.<br /> <br /> * The Silent Striders ARE reimagined as nothing but explorers and wanderers doing travel for some reasosn.<br /> <br /> What irritates me is the Shadow Lords used to have the role of trying to take over the Garou Nation and being the &quot;bad&quot; tribe but they've been more or less ignored since 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> They should have been the guys to defect or lead a revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T06:47:39-08:00","id":1528101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528100#post1528100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> * The Bone Gnawers are described as basically the same way as they always were. Just sneakier.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To take one:<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers in &quot; Legacy&quot; are an incredibly diverse Tribe with fingers in many different aspects of Survival. They range from Appalachian hill farmers, to Ratkin on a slightly lower dose of meth, to nomadic guardians of the roadways, to a modern take on Robin Hood and building communities, to a wolfish take on NYC Guardian Angels, The Fisher King writ large, an entire segment trying to find a way off of Gaia before she dies and find there way to a new world and a hundred other aspects.<br /> <br /> W5 Bone Gnawers are literally The Ratfinks Camp with all the depth, flavour and history removed, and thats it...thats all BGs do in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:07:09-08:00","id":1528102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528100#post1528100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I don't think much of the lore has been that changed in a few of the areas above:<br /> <br /> * The Bone Gnawers are described as basically the same way as they always were. Just sneakier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a bit of lore has been stripped away here. The focus used to be on their low-social-status and survival against the odds. Now it's one of the couple of Tribes focused on finding hidden things, objects or knowledge. I think the Favor that the Black Furies have in W5 would've suited the Bone Gnawers better as well because going up against the people who looked down on them and underestimated them was also a key-part of the Tribe. And their low social status among Garou is now another bit that's left unexplained via &quot;Who knows why it's like this...&quot;, another instance of poor writing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Eh, Silver Fangs being inherited aristocracy is something that removing would effectively get rid of them as a concept competely because that's their thing. Mind you, as we saw with the Silver Fangs, they were about challenges and positions and manuevering as well so you could easily do that with adopted heirs and other alliances without getting deeply into the idea of aristocrats. Besides, there's plenty to do with the idea some families have histories of werewolfdom without tying it to genetics completely. </div> </div> </div>That's what I mean: Remove it completely. W5 doesn't want to emphasize bloodlines and direct family. An &quot;inherited aristocracy&quot; doesn't fit into that. What W5 wants out of a Tribe is an answer to &quot;What do do you do?&quot;. The leadership and authority focus of the Tribe is what matters, not the aristocracy-bit. As mentioned in the Storytelling-chapter under &quot;Theme: Familism&quot;, W5 wants to be a game of &quot;found family&quot;. Just discard the aristocracy bit completely and come up with a new concept. The principle is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. There's no need for any Tribe to have any connection whatsoever to how they used to be like in previous editions. Renaming them might also help in communicating that. And look, they were fine to do that with the Native American Tribes and erase that representation, so there's no need for Silver Fangs to have to be an aristocracy-based Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The Silent Striders ARE reimagined as nothing but explorers and wanderers doing travel for some reasosn. </div> </div> </div>That's incorrect. Something is still forcing Silent Striders to wander in W5. That's where the Ban comes from after all. It's just that nobody knows what it is exactly and whether it's a curse or something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What irritates me is the Shadow Lords used to have the role of trying to take over the Garou Nation and being the &quot;bad&quot; tribe but they've been more or less ignored since 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> They should have been the guys to defect or lead a revolution. </div> </div> </div>Well, I think in general every Tribe should've gotten a section with two or three short paragraphs that is called something like &quot;This Tribe in the Age of Apocalypse&quot;. Just to give an impression of how each Tribe handled the fall of the Garou-Nation, Gaia dying/being dead and maybe a story-hook or two for playing a member of that Tribe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:25:21-08:00","id":1528104,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think you are a bit confused about the roles of each aspect of a garou.<br /> <br /> Breed is your origin, no longer statted.<br /> <br /> Auspice is what you do, THIS is what is akin to a clan among the garou. Something that steers you from the day you become a supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> Tribe is like a Sect, the community you keep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:46:17-08:00","id":1528107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528104#post1528104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think you are a bit confused about the roles of each aspect of a garou.<br /> <br /> Breed is your origin, no longer statted.<br /> <br /> Auspice is what you do, THIS is what is akin to a clan among the garou. Something that steers you from the day you become a supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> Tribe is like a Sect, the community you keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I mean: If W5 really wants to redefine Tribes to be an answer to &quot;What do you do?&quot;/&quot;Why do you do it?&quot; then there should've been way more consideration given to the way Tribes need to be portrayed differently compared to previous editions. Additionally, it would have also helped to give Auspice more of a presence in the game in terms of mechanics and worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T11:40:05-08:00","id":1528113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528104#post1528104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think you are a bit confused about the roles of each aspect of a garou.<br /> <br /> Breed is your origin, no longer statted.<br /> <br /> Auspice is what you do, THIS is what is akin to a clan among the garou. Something that steers you from the day you become a supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> Tribe is like a Sect, the community you keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, that's not how it's described at all.<br /> <br /> Each of the tribes are described by WHAT they do.<br /> <br /> I just provided a bunch of examples of adventures and what they do. Also, all of the Garou hang out at the same septs with diverse populations.<br /> <br /> * Black Furies are about GREAT JUSTICE<br /> * Bone Gnawers about sneaking around and living in the lower echelons of society<br /> * Children of Gaia are about understanding bonds and meanings of people<br /> * Hart Wardens are protecting caerns and sacred places<br /> * Galestalkers are the trackers<br /> * Ghost Council are about doing magic shit<br /> * SIlent Striders explore the world and travel<br /> * Glass Walkers love technology and the Weaver<br /> * Shadow Lords are about being ambitious assholes<br /> * Silver Fangs actually do the leading","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-06-2024, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T17:13:23-08:00","id":1528134,"title":"","content":"Not to be contrarian, but I believe in W5 Auspice is what you do, and Tribe is how you do it. At least that is what PDX has been pounding into us since they first announced the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T02:20:10-08:00","id":1528145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528113#post1528113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, that's not how it's described at all.<br /> <br /> Each of the tribes are described by WHAT they do.<br /> <br /> I just provided a bunch of examples of adventures and what they do. Also, all of the Garou hang out at the same septs with diverse populations.<br /> <br /> * Black Furies are about GREAT JUSTICE<br /> * Bone Gnawers about sneaking around and living in the lower echelons of society<br /> * Children of Gaia are about understanding bonds and meanings of people<br /> * Hart Wardens are protecting caerns and sacred places<br /> * Galestalkers are the trackers<br /> * Ghost Council are about doing magic shit<br /> * SIlent Striders explore the world and travel<br /> * Glass Walkers love technology and the Weaver<br /> * Shadow Lords are about being ambitious assholes<br /> * Silver Fangs actually do the leading</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is a massive issue in this; While a tribe can tell you a lot, your auspice should decide most of your methods. The tribe is your culture and traditions and therefore how you do things.<br /> <br /> In W5, your auspice doesn't really mean anything mechanically outside gift-lists. All the pressure for purpose is put on your tribe, which then results in these very narrow takes on them.<br /> <br /> What a Red Talon ahroun does is very different from what a Red Talon philodox does, but it isn't truly discussed in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T02:46:54-08:00","id":1528147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528096#post1528096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Revised but sometimes I felt it went a little too far in trying to tone down the Garou's flaws. The Garou are never at their most interesting save when they're deeply fucked up institutionally.<br /> <br /> Basically, barbarian berserkers and kings stuck in the 20th/21st centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall one of the main themes of Revised was the way forward-how they stop being foul ups and what actuallu works with them. I also think the idea anachronistic societies don't have nuances misses the point of how these issues occur....and people in general.<br /> <br /> Its easy write of the toxic aspects as some sort of clumsy archeotype but it's better writting to explain the nuances<br /> <br /> For example while the dove factions of the talons (forest guardians and whelps compromise) may not advocate proactive genocide its made very clear they will kill you without hesitation once they're sure it's the correct move.<br /> <br /> Likewise the hawk factions can vary a lot, i know id rather deal with a predator King over a dying cub anyway of the week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-07-2024, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T02:50:51-08:00","id":1528148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528134#post1528134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be contrarian, but I believe in W5 Auspice is what you do, and Tribe is how you do it. At least that is what PDX has been pounding into us since they first announced the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone else notice that this is the wrong way to do it and tribe should be what you do and auspice how you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T03:55:15-08:00","id":1528150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528148#post1528148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone else notice that this is the wrong way to do it and tribe should be what you do and auspice how you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with you there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T13:25:24-08:00","id":1528338,"title":"","content":"Take a week off and everything seems to fall apart on me. Yikes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART THREE</span><br /> <br /> The Letter<br /> <br /> As the various &quot;discussions&quot; about the previews wound down, an open letter was posted online from one of the consultants brought in on the first iteration of trying to come up with W5. In it, the writer brought up his reactions trying to work on the project. Basically, he was forced to work under very specific preconceived conditions brought up by the head designer. While some of his were taken into consideration, problems arose with the head designer who seemed to know exactly what should W5 should look like, even if it meant totally breaking down all previous editions of the game. Although there were problems with those editions, some of the head designers ideas were causing friction within that first group. Ultimately, that group was removed from the process, and the final format of W5 went through two other groups before it was completed.<br /> <br /> The initial opinions on the letter were mostly positive, especially within those fan groups who were already distrustful of the way W5 seemed to be heading. Even some not as supportive were giving the letter's writer the benefit of the doubt. However, there was a fraction of fans who attacked the writer's motives, as well as his recounting. The majority of these fans were the same ones who went after the older fans who were compiling about the loss of the Get. Many of the attacks were on the writer himself, saying what he was doing was wrong and that he posted the letter just because of the publicity surrounding the release of W5.<br /> <br /> What strikes me as most important is that these fans denouncing this letter were the very ones saying that older fans were being fascist for supporting the Get as it was written. Now, one of the traits of fascism is the suppressing of minorities. Other ideologies have this trait as well. So, the W5 fandom was supporting a possible fascist action while decrying fascism in others. That is a very big &quot;Paradox.&quot; (Sorry about the pun.)<br /> <br /> In my experience, whenever someone has radically opposing views on similar issues/topics, it is usually because they are hiding their true beliefs or lying for a certain benefit. The view that needs drawn out explanations is the one more suspect, although more concise opinions with absolute statements can be as well. In this situation, it seems that W5 fans, most of whom hadn't even seen the complete book at the time unless they had pre-order the physical copy and had gotten the advance PDF, needed to support the book no matter what. Some may have even joined social media just so that they could express their opinions over what they thought was &quot;the best game ever.&quot; [I'll be coming back to this point later on.]<br /> <br /> Now, if the management over W5 had preconceived notions about what the game should be like, their views would be ones that took hold. However, when others are brought in, their views need to be heard and acknowledged. This is necessary even when these views run counter to what management wants to hear. The letter shows that the first group was trying to keep as much of previous editions as possible, in a way that still worked with the views of management. The heads weren't listening, wanting their vision to be the main one, so the first group of consultants were let go. Explanations about why and how the heads came up with their views have been developed, none of which have been truly confirmed. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T19:57:25-08:00","id":1528349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528338#post1528338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a week off and everything seems to fall apart on me. Yikes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART THREE</span><br /> <br /> The Letter<br /> <br /> As the various &quot;discussions&quot; about the previews wound down, an open letter was posted online from one of the consultants brought in on the first iteration of trying to come up with W5. In it, the writer brought up his reactions trying to work on the project. Basically, he was forced to work under very specific preconceived conditions brought up by the head designer. While some of his were taken into consideration, problems arose with the head designer who seemed to know exactly what should W5 should look like, even if it meant totally breaking down all previous editions of the game. Although there were problems with those editions, some of the head designers ideas were causing friction within that first group. Ultimately, that group was removed from the process, and the final format of W5 went through two other groups before it was completed.<br /> <br /> The initial opinions on the letter were mostly positive, especially within those fan groups who were already distrustful of the way W5 seemed to be heading. Even some not as supportive were giving the letter's writer the benefit of the doubt. However, there was a fraction of fans who attacked the writer's motives, as well as his recounting. The majority of these fans were the same ones who went after the older fans who were compiling about the loss of the Get. Many of the attacks were on the writer himself, saying what he was doing was wrong and that he posted the letter just because of the publicity surrounding the release of W5.<br /> <br /> What strikes me as most important is that these fans denouncing this letter were the very ones saying that older fans were being fascist for supporting the Get as it was written. Now, one of the traits of fascism is the suppressing of minorities. Other ideologies have this trait as well. So, the W5 fandom was supporting a possible fascist action while decrying fascism in others. That is a very big &quot;Paradox.&quot; (Sorry about the pun.)<br /> <br /> In my experience, whenever someone has radically opposing views on similar issues/topics, it is usually because they are hiding their true beliefs or lying for a certain benefit. The view that needs drawn out explanations is the one more suspect, although more concise opinions with absolute statements can be as well. In this situation, it seems that W5 fans, most of whom hadn't even seen the complete book at the time unless they had pre-order the physical copy and had gotten the advance PDF, needed to support the book no matter what. Some may have even joined social media just so that they could express their opinions over what they thought was &quot;the best game ever.&quot; [I'll be coming back to this point later on.]<br /> <br /> Now, if the management over W5 had preconceived notions about what the game should be like, their views would be ones that took hold. However, when others are brought in, their views need to be heard and acknowledged. This is necessary even when these views run counter to what management wants to hear. The letter shows that the first group was trying to keep as much of previous editions as possible, in a way that still worked with the views of management. The heads weren't listening, wanting their vision to be the main one, so the first group of consultants were let go. Explanations about why and how the heads came up with their views have been developed, none of which have been truly confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the cultural matter is what derailed the Get of Fenris. Which is specifically there was a controversy regarding Get of Fenris that had happened in 1st/2nd Edition to Revised but that the Get of Fenris had long since gotten past it in-universe. RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA made the Get of Fenris have a huge chunk of Slavic members, which kind of undermines any serious claim of them being the Nazi faction and the Swords of Heimdall were exterminated by the Get of Fernis.<br /> <br /> Which means, essentially, the issue had been settled 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> Then it got REVIVED by the modern designers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-10-2024, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T20:43:46-08:00","id":1528350,"title":"","content":"I saw a typo, corrected it, and now the post has been flagged as spam.<br /> <br /> FFS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T14:07:42-08:00","id":1528393,"title":"","content":"So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17984\" data-vbnamecard=\"17984\">Toby Weingarten</a> did you have fun with the book and the in depth review, and was the 23 page discussion an expected outcome?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T07:35:07-08:00","id":1528413,"title":"","content":"The letter basically made me switch from accepting the Fenrir as gone to being angry at the Brand Manager.<br /> <br /> Because it is one thing to take out a tribe because you don't want to engage in the discussion of fascism in the game. It is ENTIRELY another to take the tribe in question and make it an over the top foe that is always wrong. Especially when Red Talons are kept and BSDs can be redeemed.<br /> <br /> But there is also the sheer ignorance and refusal to listen to the letter writer. W5 was billed as the more progressive version of WtA, but I'd say many older books win by actually listening to their Native consultants. When you are working on a product such as WtA, you need to be humble enough to admit you do not know how another culture handles things and listen to those who know. Instead, concepts such as taboo words were not understood and later W5 ended up saying oral storytelling sucks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:11:20-08:00","id":1528426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528413#post1528413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The letter basically made me switch from accepting the Fenrir as gone to being angry at the Brand Manager.<br /> <br /> Because it is one thing to take out a tribe because you don't want to engage in the discussion of fascism in the game. It is ENTIRELY another to take the tribe in question and make it an over the top foe that is always wrong. Especially when Red Talons are kept and BSDs can be redeemed.<br /> <br /> But there is also the sheer ignorance and refusal to listen to the letter writer. W5 was billed as the more progressive version of WtA, but I'd say many older books win by actually listening to their Native consultants. When you are working on a product such as WtA, you need to be humble enough to admit you do not know how another culture handles things and listen to those who know. Instead, concepts such as taboo words were not understood and later W5 ended up saying oral storytelling sucks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few caveats that should be noted in the letter:<br /> <br /> * They did remove the taboo words.<br /> <br /> * A bigger issue is the work that they did incorporate from Sambrano but didn't give proper credit to.<br /> <br /> * The Get of Fenris becoming the Cult of Fenris is something that Sambrano was against but that wasn't what he was really concerned about. He even mentions it was something he was speaking at as a fan rather than a Native consultant.<br /> <br /> (Basically, not from a &quot;this is racist&quot; perspective but, &quot;this is a bad idea&quot;)<br /> <br /> * The primary issue Sambrano had was the fact that he felt the Native focus should be continued rather than de-emphasized as a whole when the line was going in a &quot;culturally agnostic&quot; role.<br /> <br /> Really, I think the big issue is the lack of accreditation, which is not cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:18:48-08:00","id":1528437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528426#post1528426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a few caveats that should be noted in the letter:<br /> <br /> * They did remove the taboo words.<br /> <br /> * A bigger issue is the work that they did incorporate from Sambrano but didn't give proper credit to.<br /> <br /> * The Get of Fenris becoming the Cult of Fenris is something that Sambrano was against but that wasn't what he was really concerned about. He even mentions it was something he was speaking at as a fan rather than a Native consultant.<br /> <br /> (Basically, not from a &quot;this is racist&quot; perspective but, &quot;this is a bad idea&quot;)<br /> <br /> * The primary issue Sambrano had was the fact that he felt the Native focus should be continued rather than de-emphasized as a whole when the line was going in a &quot;culturally agnostic&quot; role.<br /> <br /> Really, I think the big issue is the lack of accreditation, which is not cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did remove the taboo words, yes. But not before trying to erase Gale Stalkers and wanting to keep the skin in the old name for Stolen Moons. So it was a fight Sambrano had to fight hard and it is because of their extra work to show why the old names were bad that the company relented.<br /> <br /> The thing is, they were hired as a writer, NOT as a Native consultant. They liked the setting enough to do the extra work of one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:22:42-08:00","id":1528440,"title":"","content":"The lack of attribution was already bad but I'm also disturbed by how they used JF Sambrano's version of the Ghost Council as a blueprint for the version we ended up getting. Not only that but it comes off like a bad translation of what Sambrano intended the Ghost Council to be like. The core concept in Sambrano's version was that the Ghost Council are at their heart teachers who seek every kind of knowledge (even the dark, forbidden kind) and then decide what should be shared with other Garou and what not. And they're called Ghost Council because they will even consult dark sources like ghosts.<br /> <br /> The pitch for the Ghost Council in the released book is much weaker (pg 40): &quot;Garou of the Ghost Council favor unconventional approaches and challenge taboos to use rivals\u2019 weaknesses against them in service to Gaia.&quot; It also theoretically gets in similar hot water as the Red Talon depiction. &quot;Challenging taboos to use rivals' weaknesses against them&quot;... okay, so the Ghost Council Garou is breaking a taboo and thereby exploits an enemy's weakness. And so the enemy is, for example... a Pack of Black Spiral Dancers. So what does that mean? It isn't a very good concept - especially in light of the existence of the Cult of Fenris. The Tribe-section even has the phrase &quot;the ends justify the means&quot; to describe the Tribe's mindset. Another Tribe like the Red Talons who is easily just as extreme as the Cult of Fenris in terms of how they're described. And the Tribe is now called Ghost Council because for whatever reason the Tribe-members all call each other &quot;Ghosts&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:35:00-08:00","id":1528443,"title":"","content":"If I may once more show my Grognard status (you can claim to be Old School after 20 years, IMHO), UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON showed the problem with Ghost Council pretty much from the get go.<br /> <br /> They wanted it to be the Garou Tremere and the fact it was explicitly a Native tribe and not the &quot;Garou who do the spooky stuff&quot; always ran head first into things.<br /> <br /> So the Ghost Council ran the Farnum Occult HQ despite the fact its Patron Spirit was Jupiter versus the Glass Walkers (as a city based caerun) or the Shadow Lords (because Jupiter being a face of Grandfather Thunder made too much sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:52:26-08:00","id":1528447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528443#post1528443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may once more show my Grognard status (you can claim to be Old School after 20 years, IMHO), UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON showed the problem with Ghost Council pretty much from the get go.<br /> <br /> They wanted it to be the Garou Tremere and the fact it was explicitly a Native tribe and not the &quot;Garou who do the spooky stuff&quot; always ran head first into things.<br /> <br /> So the Ghost Council ran the Farnum Occult HQ despite the fact its Patron Spirit was Jupiter versus the Glass Walkers (as a city based caerun) or the Shadow Lords (because Jupiter being a face of Grandfather Thunder made too much sense)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I liked JF Sambrano's version of the new focus of them being a Tribe of teachers who try to sort through all available knowledge in order to figure out what's worth being shared with other Garou and what's not. Instead of them just being these super-fans of occult and mystical knowledge. Of course, over the years the Tribe gained some other wrinkles as well (building connections to minorities around the world) but I think reframing the whole knowledge-seeking by making &quot;teaching&quot; a core-part of the Tribe was a great idea and would've been a good basis for a new version of the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T13:35:52-08:00","id":1528452,"title":"","content":"One thing I really appreciated, however short it was, was the inclusion of rules for Slashers as a form of Formori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T16:31:51-08:00","id":1528457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528452#post1528452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I really appreciated, however short it was, was the inclusion of rules for Slashers as a form of Formori.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been a thing in Werewolf since 1993?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T16:43:56-08:00","id":1528458,"title":"","content":"Not only were Slashers in the game since 1993, they were brought back and given a new variant in W20. So it's not like Slashers were even an obscure Fomori that W5 &quot;brought back&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T17:24:57-08:00","id":1528462,"title":"","content":"Weird, I somehow missed that. I am a huge slasher fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T19:34:16-08:00","id":1528471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528462#post1528462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, I somehow missed that. I am a huge slasher fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're technically called Gorehounds. That might have thrown you off the trail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T11:16:09-08:00","id":1528552,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART FOUR</span><br /> <br /> Where Credit Is Due<br /> <br /> One last set of issues came up in the W5 previews. Some contributors from the first two iterations of the design noted that their work was being used. These creators wondered if they were going to be given full credit for their work. After W5 came out, it was also noted that some material from V5 had been lifted, sometimes altered slightly, and placed into the new work. This is important because, while each book was made under the auspices of the same company, different licensees worked on each one. While this means that technically such 'lifting' was done in-house, which is common and allowable, this instance is a little murkier as V5 was ultimately published by Modiphius via a temporarily reborn White Wolf and W5 was published by Renegade Studios (which also now does V5 since the new White Wolf no longer exists and the rights were shifted). A look at the credits pages of the two books will show an unexpected difference between the two games.<br /> <br /> The most obvious difference is that W5 alphabetized their listing while V5 did not. I don't want to hazard a guess at what V5's style is, but in might be based on the amount of work each person contributed. Of the five main writers of V5, only two wrote for W5, with none of the additional writers mentioned. It is worth noting that the two lead designers of V5 who didn't write for W5 did get secondary mentions, probably due to the fact that they may have come up with some of the basic systems that form the basis of all of the new WOD5 game lines. There may have been some friction with these two and the one who stayed, and that is why some systems were not used in W5 in some form, but others from V5 were. Also, V5 had three editors, one of whom was a lead designer for both games, while W5 only has one editor. The writers for the material taken from V5 might be listed here, but I can't prove it.<br /> <br /> Another aspect is that multiple groups were called in to check on the issues of diversity. From my readings, much of the direct human influences on the game had been removed, so the need for diversity might not be as paramount as when actual cultures were tied directly to the Garou. I guess problems with such matters were important to prevent based on similar events from other books. No one person is specifically named from said groups, so if they contributed any extra material, they weren't credited.<br /> <br /> Finally, no one from the first two iterations of the W5 design teams seems to have been credited.<br /> <br /> For artwork, V5 had three directors, only one of which continued onto W5. Aside for that art director, no other artist from V5 was carried over to W5. This doesn't include the photographers from V5, as W5 used illustrations only. This also brings up the fact that all of the photographers' models were given credit, as they could be identified. None of the individuals used as tracing models were mentioned in W5, possibly because their images had to be completely altered to prevent litigation. <br /> <br /> Multiple playtesters for each game were given credit, with more for V5 than W5. This includes a blanket thank-you to many testers whose names were not listed in V5. I am not sure if the lack of testers could have contributed to the issues many are facing with the game.<br /> <br /> There is one last glaring omission from the credits, the names of all of the designers for the four previous editions of <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse.</i> V5 lists all of the creators for their previous editions, including a dedication to one who had died before V5 came out. Yet, W5 doesn't mention anyone. Now, not acknowledging the work by someone who was not an official member of the final version is wrong. Their names should be mentioned where credit is due. However, ignoring the hard work of those who lead the way for W5 is hubris on a whole other level. Sure, W5 is a 'retcon' more than a continuation, but terms and core principles were still brought over. And the game is called '<i>Fifth Edition</i>' not 'brand new werewolf game.' I have mentioned how the lead designer seems to dislike, if not hate, at least portions of the previous editions, yet he was still given free rein to write W5. If he hates it so much, why was he even put on as lead? Does he really think of himself as that much better than those who laid the groundwork for him that he could ignore or rewrite history? This definitely could be the case, considering how different W5 is to both the previous editions of <i>W:tA </i>as well as to V5. Some would even say such actions are fascist in the ways they are trying to make everyone forget what has happened.<br /> <br /> One last post before the final verdict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T15:52:33-08:00","id":1528571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528552#post1528552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART FOUR</span><br /> <br /> Where Credit Is Due<br /> <br /> One last set of issues came up in the W5 previews. Some contributors from the first two iterations of the design noted that their work was being used. These creators wondered if they were going to be given full credit for their work. After