d on similar events from other books. No one person is specifically named from said groups, so if they contributed any extra material, they weren't credited.<br /> <br /> Finally, no one from the first two iterations of the W5 design teams seems to have been credited.<br /> <br /> For artwork, V5 had three directors, only one of which continued onto W5. Aside for that art director, no other artist from V5 was carried over to W5. This doesn't include the photographers from V5, as W5 used illustrations only. This also brings up the fact that all of the photographers' models were given credit, as they could be identified. None of the individuals used as tracing models were mentioned in W5, possibly because their images had to be completely altered to prevent litigation.<br /> <br /> Multiple playtesters for each game were given credit, with more for V5 than W5. This includes a blanket thank-you to many testers whose names were not listed in V5. I am not sure if the lack of testers could have contributed to the issues many are facing with the game.<br /> <br /> There is one last glaring omission from the credits, the names of all of the designers for the four previous editions of <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse.</i> V5 lists all of the creators for their previous editions, including a dedication to one who had died before V5 came out. Yet, W5 doesn't mention anyone. Now, not acknowledging the work by someone who was not an official member of the final version is wrong. Their names should be mentioned where credit is due. However, ignoring the hard work of those who lead the way for W5 is hubris on a whole other level. Sure, W5 is a 'retcon' more than a continuation, but terms and core principles were still brought over. And the game is called '<i>Fifth Edition</i>' not 'brand new werewolf game.' I have mentioned how the lead designer seems to dislike, if not hate, at least portions of the previous editions, yet he was still given free rein to write W5. If he hates it so much, why was he even put on as lead? Does he really think of himself as that much better than those who laid the groundwork for him that he could ignore or rewrite history? This definitely could be the case, considering how different W5 is to both the previous editions of <i>W:tA </i>as well as to V5. Some would even say such actions are fascist in the ways they are trying to make everyone forget what has happened.<br /> <br /> One last post before the final verdict.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the description you gave, I can only think that they found someone to head the project for reasons, and they put him to do a project he didn't want to do so he did what he wanted and did the minimum to justify the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:54:20-08:00","id":1528680,"title":"","content":"I have to admit this does feel a bit like it was written by the Pentex Subsidiary of Black Dog Games with how much it takes a crap on being a glorious warrior for Gaia. Yes, the Garou weren't very good at sysmetic change and yes, they absolutely were losing to Pentex. I would go so far to say that Pentex is the reason the Garou lost as they were a complete game changer in the fight against the Wyrm moving from Dungeons and Dragons to Sim City.<br /> <br /> However, the biggest problem with W5 is it's not really doing a very good job of selling the premise of the game to the players and I feel that is a mistake. There's nothing wrong with emphasizing the long-neglected personal horror element of the Garou to the public. I always have felt that there was a lot more that could be done there and that one of the all-time greatest W:TA supplements was the Ronin and Stolen Moon sections of OUTCASTS. Here, it just kind of goes on and on about the mistakes of the Garou and how it doesn't matter what they've done because Gaia is dead or dying.<br /> <br /> Fine but what SHOULD the Garou be doing? I feel it oversells its point to the level that a lot of players think the book says you shouldn't be fighting the Wyrm at all. Other sections of the book show you absolutely should and there's an adventure about a serial killing horticulturist formori your players stop. But I feel like a section about existentialism or noir might have beenfited the book. Basically a Geralt of Rivia, &quot;Fighting evil may be pointless but I will do so because, fuck it, not fighting just is even worse.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T18:30:48-08:00","id":1528695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528680#post1528680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit this does feel a bit like it was written by the Pentex Subsidiary of Black Dog Games with how much it takes a crap on being a glorious warrior for Gaia. Yes, the Garou weren't very good at sysmetic change and yes, they absolutely were losing to Pentex. I would go so far to say that Pentex is the reason the Garou lost as they were a complete game changer in the fight against the Wyrm moving from Dungeons and Dragons to Sim City.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not D&amp;D - Pendragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the biggest problem with W5 is it's not really doing a very good job of selling the premise of the game to the players and I feel that is a mistake. There's nothing wrong with emphasizing the long-neglected personal horror element of the Garou to the public. </div> </div> </div>It is when the game is hitting you on the back of the head with it like a shovel. Presumably to try to get you to play V:tM. Those Sabbat are notorious hard sellers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always have felt that there was a lot more that could be done there and that one of the all-time greatest W:TA supplements was the Ronin and Stolen Moon sections of OUTCASTS. Here, it just kind of goes on and on about the mistakes of the Garou and how it doesn't matter what they've done because Gaia is dead or dying. </div> </div> </div>(Points to the &quot;Gaia is Dead or Dying&quot; Jar)<br /> <br /> It works by taking a coin instead of leaving one. Coins are cursed and can only be abated by reading <i>Eternal Hearts</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T14:06:53-08:00","id":1528750,"title":"","content":"In terms of personal horror, you can see some attempts to get there with how punishing the game is (introducing Harano/Hauglosk as two quite unavoidable game-over-scenarios, for example) but as a horror-game it's quite bad. W5 just doesn't have enough of a coherent vision to meet the standards of a good horror-game. Harano and Hauglosk suck as mechanics in W5 (both implementations of when a Harano- or a Hauglosk-check should happen are just dumb game-design). The Crinos-Form in W5 can be a pain in the ass but if the dice-gods smile upon you it can also still make your PC the superpowered warrior Garou always were. The twilight-realm where your character can be quite powerful but also can suck ass (if the dice-gods don't like you) isn't a horror-game. Most of the &quot;horror&quot; W5 offers is just lackluster mechanics that don't do what they're supposed to do as they just thoughtlessly rely on setting up rolls that can be good or bad.<br /> <br /> Of course, W5's big excuse is ST-fiat... An ST might raise the difficulty for a Harano or Hauglosk check if they so choose, for example... The Danger-track in H5 relies on a similar excuse for its bad game-design. Of course, the Danger-Track in H5 is much worse because it's an absolutely meaningless thing, if anything a waste of space in the H5 corebook (calling the Danger-track a game-mechanic would be an insult to game-mechanics everywhere). Harano and Hauglosk don't reach that despicable level thankfully but both in terms of Chronicle Tenets and handling of Touchstones there's a lot of work that has more to do with the ST at the table than the actual &quot;mechanics&quot; proposed by the W5 corebook. This is still some lazy game-design where the corebook leaves most of the work to the ST at the table.<br /> <br /> Let alone the fact that Harano- and Hauglosk-tests are badly designed in the sense that a PCs best defense against them is accrue dots in both tracks at the same time. In terms of mechanics, a PC with Harano 4/Hauglosk 4 is less likely to fall than a PC with Harano 4/Hauglosk 0. That's dumb - but this is how the mechanics in W5 work.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with the developers' urge to make WtA with more punishing mechanics that this wouldn't be WtA anymore. With VtM the Humanity-track focuses on reminding the player that trying to be human while being a vampire is a struggle. And while they try to make it a struggle to be a werewolf in W5, these developers get just caught up in all these meta-debates of previous WtA-editions when it comes to the Umbra, combat prowess etc.<br /> <br /> It isn't H5 (a game that just sucks and is badly written/designed) but you see the echoes of that failure in W5. H5 is obsessed with telling you how bad hunter-orgs are and completely loses sight of being a game about local hunter-cells. W5 similarly completely loses sight of what the actual game is when it constantly complains about Garou and how bad they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T11:44:50-08:00","id":1528937,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART FIVE</span><br /> <br /> Bathing in the Aftermath<br /> <br /> Once W5 officially released, many of the rumors were finally confirmed. Those who were already predisposed not to like the game continued to point out the faults, while the supporters quickly tried to take the naysayers down. Reviews (from professionals, not like a regular fan such as I) were mixed. One extremely favorable review was revealed to have been written by someone who was doing freelance writing work on a supplement for W5, yet failed to mention the fact. However, the general trend was neutral to unfavorable.<br /> <br /> Online, the feuding continued. Fans of W5 begrudgingly conceded that W5 did have many errors, but only about the same amount as first edition. Fair point. Counterpoint: First edition was written by about five or six people, max, maybe with some other help, in about a year; meanwhile, W5 was written by over a dozen people, on and off, over five years, yet still managed to have about the same percentage of mistakes.<br /> <br /> The same W5 fans said that they had great success in playing games with new players. Emphasis on the 'new/less-experienced.&quot; Some of the bigger weaknesses of W5 (vague backstory, forced game play formats) are reduced when dealing with such groups. I've pointed that this seems to be W5's target demographic in previous phases. More experienced players could start to loose interest in maintained such limited possibilities. Few posts suggest that such players were familiar with other WOD games or even previous editions of W:tA.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned how I feel that some of the online posts are suspicious in other places. So many are highly enthusiastic about W5, while also suggesting that those who hate the new game are wrong. Not just on their opinions, but on why they have those opinions. I cannot fathom why these fans dislike fans of the older editions so much, even when presented with clearly fact-based explanations. There could be some false actors involved. Maybe so outside incentives. Either way, such possibilities come close to false advertising. The fact that many of the people involved with the game, both those still with the publishers or not, and particularly those who left fairly recently, have been rather cagey about the writing process raises some doubts.<br /> <br /> As of now, fans are starting to show their regrets about picking up W5. The hatred between groups are starting to slow down, but some W5 fans still are showcasing their views against those who aren't fans, more so than in the other direction.<br /> <br /> With these final points, I feel that I have presented enough evidence to provide a final grade. While grading a work based not specifically on its content, but on its representation within the larger gaming market, is outside of the norm, for this game, I feel that the many issues that have surrounded it since its formal announcement makes such a grade justifiable. <br /> <br /> Final grade: Incomplete. Too much is still unknown. However...<br /> <br /> I can speculate on what is known and suggest what could have happened and what still might be happening. Next time in Part Six.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T12:46:49-08:00","id":1528946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528937#post1528937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART FIVE</span>As of now, fans are starting to show their regrets about picking up W5. The hatred between groups are starting to slow down, but some W5 fans still are showcasing their views against those who aren't fans, more so than in the other direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel whenever there's new editions, there's always a divide between the new fans and the old.<br /> <br /> But the trick is figuring out how to reconcile the two.<br /> <br /> Not furthering the divide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:39:29-08:00","id":1528962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528946#post1528946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel whenever there's new editions, there's always a divide between the new fans and the old.<br /> <br /> But the trick is figuring out how to reconcile the two.<br /> <br /> Not furthering the divide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes that just isn't possible. Look at D&amp;D 4th edition. The divide within the fanbase couldn't be reconciled, and after many older fans went to a new company (Pathfinder) eventually Hasbro relented and released a 5th edition that basically rolled back almost all of the changes introduced in 4th edition. Of course, with Werewolf there's no other big &quot;werewolf&quot; game from a different company out there for customers to migrate to, so I suspect that many older Werewolf players will simply not purchase 5th edition - because that's what they wanted, a new edition, not a new game wearing the skin of the old one. And, while not as extreme as Hunter: the Reckoning, to a large degree that's what W5 feels like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:57:37-08:00","id":1528964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528962#post1528962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes that just isn't possible. Look at D&amp;D 4th edition. The divide within the fanbase couldn't be reconciled, and after many older fans went to a new company (Pathfinder) eventually Hasbro relented and released a 5th edition that basically rolled back almost all of the changes introduced in 4th edition. Of course, with Werewolf there's no other big &quot;werewolf&quot; game from a different company out there for customers to migrate to, so I suspect that many older Werewolf players will simply not purchase 5th edition - because that's what they wanted, a new edition, not a new game wearing the skin of the old one. And, while not as extreme as Hunter: the Reckoning, to a large degree that's what W5 feels like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not use D&amp;D4e as an example, as 1) I prefer it and 2e to other editions, if I have to play any form of D&amp;D, 2) 5e ended up having to use a fair bit of 4e, especially with 5e third party material that people like, such as Matt Colville's MCDM books. 4e, and 3) still very much D&amp;D and not a skin suit of its themes. In fact, it's quite the opposite on number 3; while W5 is a grisly shell of its IP stealing the moons of the W:tA of old, D&amp;D 4e just removed its own skin and pointed out how existing parts of the game worked with greater clarity, its guts open for all to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:06:32-08:00","id":1528967,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D also has an outsized influence on the perception of edition wars, because it has consistently done pretty big changes between editions resulting in a lot of fan division. Call of Cthulhu and Fate are both examples of games that haven't had any serious edition wars (CoC has more editions than any other game I can think of, but each edition is a very small change for it, and Fate actively avoids new editions whenever possible). It doesn't mean there's no edition wars outside of D&amp;D and the WoD, but the idea that their inevitable by virtue of how TTRPG editions &quot;are&quot; doesn't really bare out when you expand the sample set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:09:51-08:00","id":1528969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528967#post1528967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D&amp;D also has an outsized influence on the perception of edition wars, because it has consistently done pretty big changes between editions resulting in a lot of fan division. Call of Cthulhu and Fate are both examples of games that haven't had any serious edition wars (CoC has more editions than any other game I can think of, but each edition is a very small change for it, and Fate actively avoids new editions whenever possible). It doesn't mean there's no edition wars outside of D&amp;D and the WoD, but the idea that their inevitable by virtue of how TTRPG editions &quot;are&quot; doesn't really bare out when you expand the sample set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's basically the Amazon of Tabletop RPGs.<br /> <br /> Other systems can do fine, even great, but the difference in sales from D&amp;D and public perception to any other system is bottled water to the ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T19:19:31-08:00","id":1528975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528964#post1528964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather not use D&amp;D4e as an example, as 1) I prefer it and 2e to other editions, if I have to play any form of D&amp;D, 2) 5e ended up having to use a fair bit of 4e, especially with 5e third party material that people like, such as Matt Colville's MCDM books. 4e, and 3) still very much D&amp;D and not a skin suit of its themes. In fact, it's quite the opposite on number 3; while W5 is a grisly shell of its IP stealing the moons of the W:tA of old, D&amp;D 4e just removed its own skin and pointed out how existing parts of the game worked with greater clarity, its guts open for all to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>3rd edition D&amp;D still generally resembled 2nd edition D&amp;D and the setting was the same between both editions. There were some mechanical changes like streamlining Thac0, but overall you could see that 3rd edition was an updated version of 2nd edition. 4th edition was an entirely different game - some aspects were better, some were worse, but mechanically it bore little resemblance to the prior editions. Moreover, when you include the 100 year time skip for the Forgotten Realms, which caused the writers to toss much of the metaplot, setting lore and major NPCs into the garbage bin so they could do a &quot;reboot&quot; you ended up with a game called D&amp;D 4th edition, but other than the names of things, it didn't feel like a new edition of the same game, but rather a new game altogether. <br /> <br /> This is sort of where I'm seeing games like W5 or H5. V5 at least had some mechanical changes, but the setting is essentially the same one so V5 feels like a new edition of a prior game. But in neither H5's nor W5's cases is that true and both are functionally new games with new settings that simply reuse the names of the prior games. They feel less like new editions of an existing game and instead feel like brand new games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T04:47:40-08:00","id":1528991,"title":"","content":"I just looked at the section for Forms again and I noticed a bit I actually overlooked when I ran W5: From pg 134 &quot;Shifting form is a two-dice minor action and requires a Rage check, according to the form\u2019s cost. <b>(This cost must also be paid for each additional scene in which the Garou maintains the form.)</b>&quot; I definitely didn't do that. There were times when a player was in Glabro for more than one scene. But also... come on! This also brings up the same issue like with the scene-based damage from being in the Umbra. They really need to change the framing of time to real-world time or just not invoke these &quot;Pay a cost to do this and then pay again at the start of each following scene.&quot;-mechanics in the first place. Because for example when it says under Hispo that it can be used to travel long distances then it can only work if the ST turns the travelling into one scene. Any interruption (in other words &quot;new scene&quot;) would lead to more Rage-checks. I also feel like it's a real bummer to have to start a scene as ST by making everybody pay a cost or do a feel-bad roll like the Rage-check because this mechanic would make you lose Rage for just being in the scene which the player also has no control over. It's like the mechanics want to punish the player for just being in the vicinity of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T04:52:54-08:00","id":1528992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528991#post1528991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just looked at the section for Forms again and I noticed a bit I actually overlooked when I ran W5: From pg 134 &quot;Shifting form is a two-dice minor action and requires a Rage check, according to the form\u2019s cost. <b>(This cost must also be paid for each additional scene in which the Garou maintains the form.)</b>&quot; I definitely didn't do that. There were times when a player was in Glabro for more than one scene. But also... come on! This also brings up the same issue like with the scene-based damage from being in the Umbra. They really need to change the framing of time to real-world time or just not invoke these &quot;Pay a cost to do this and then pay again at the start of each following scene.&quot;-mechanics in the first place. Because for example when it says under Hispo that it can be used to travel long distances then it can only work if the ST turns the travelling into one scene. Any interruption (in other words &quot;new scene&quot;) would lead to more Rage-checks. I also feel like it's a real bummer to have to start a scene as ST by making everybody pay a cost or do a feel-bad roll like the Rage-check because this mechanic would make you lose Rage for just being in the scene which the player also has no control over. It's like the mechanics want to punish the player for just being in the vicinity of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also clearly forgot that some PCs AREN'T human-born. Because suddenly forcing a PC to turn into a wolf in public would create some very awkward scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T05:03:33-08:00","id":1528995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528992#post1528992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also clearly forgot that some PCs AREN'T human-born. Because suddenly forcing a PC to turn into a wolf in public would create some very awkward scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to avoid that, I as ST would have to remind a wolfborn PC with Rage 1 that they should shift into Homid or Lupus at the end of the scene to avoid being forced into &quot;Lost your wolf&quot;-status at the start of the next scene. And if you start the scene in &quot;Lost your wolf&quot;-status, you're really screwed because you have to wait until you can howl at the moon before you can use the supernatural Forms again. The end-effect of doing this is that this is the game trying to dissuade players from shifting into the supernatural Forms... but which are also the only Forms where you can use a lot of your Gifts! So it's really just punishment on top of punishment! God, this game just has so many feel-bad mechanics...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T05:12:31-08:00","id":1528999,"title":"","content":"And now that you've shown me Clement Lupus, we can now add low-content wolfdogs into the mix.<br /> <br /> I mean, coywolf would have been less stupid as yotes are more common in urban areas. But no, we can now have lupus forms that are so doggy they can't be mistaken for wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T10:04:13-08:00","id":1529012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1528975#post1528975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3rd edition D&amp;D still generally resembled 2nd edition D&amp;D and the setting was the same between both editions. There were some mechanical changes like streamlining Thac0, but overall you could see that 3rd edition was an updated version of 2nd edition. 4th edition was an entirely different game - some aspects were better, some were worse, but mechanically it bore little resemblance to the prior editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. 4e was still based on classes and levels and had a very 3e-like level progression where everyone used the same XP table. It's just that in 4e, fighters could do things other than just attack, attack, attack. There were still wizards with spellbooks, there were still multiple age categories of dragons, and you still adventured into dungeons. Arguably, 1e and 2e had a bigger break in how XP was handled alone (gp=xp to killing monsters and taking their stuff) and the change from combat matrices to THAC0. 2e also changed the bard dramatically, and 3e basically turned them completely into what 2e called Song Mages. Where are your tears for these?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, when you include the 100 year time skip for the Forgotten Realms, which caused the writers to toss much of the metaplot, setting lore and major NPCs into the garbage bin so they could do a &quot;reboot&quot; you ended up with a game called D&amp;D 4th edition, but other than the names of things, it didn't feel like a new edition of the same game, but rather a new game altogether. </div> </div> </div>That sounded like more of a problem with individual choices about the Realms... which I can't say that I'm too sympathetic to, given how they're basically the most bog-standard generic fantasy romp that the RPG industry has to offer. Athas got changed a bit, too, but that was more of a rewind to pre-Prism Pentad (which most fans of Athas were all for, so they could avoid the metaplot that started eliminating setting big bads); it does kind of sting that half giants are being emulated by goliaths, but 4e was cut down unceremoniously fast and so we never discovered if there could have been a way around Large characters (not that 3e did that any better, and 5e is cowardly and refuses to do anything out of the mold, resulting in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJFnK4qUFA4\" target=\"_blank\">Medium-sized centaurs that can ride horses</a>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is sort of where I'm seeing games like W5 or H5. V5 at least had some mechanical changes, but the setting is essentially the same one so V5 feels like a new edition of a prior game. But in neither H5's nor W5's cases is that true and both are functionally new games with new settings that simply reuse the names of the prior games. They feel less like new editions of an existing game and instead feel like brand new games. </div> </div> </div>This still wouldn't make sense unless you expanded what Garou and Imbued were capable of in general and just shifted a few more effects to rites, and made WoD5 versions of Promethean, Beast, and Deviant (4e had a lot more classes with way more variability; 5e tried to collapse everything down back to the &quot;basic classes&quot; and boy did those concepts sure collapse, alright).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T17:35:56-08:00","id":1529053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529012#post1529012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullshit. 4e was still based on classes and levels and had a very 3e-like level progression where everyone used the same XP table. It's just that in 4e, fighters could do things other than just attack, attack, attack. There were still wizards with spellbooks, there were still multiple age categories of dragons, and you still adventured into dungeons. Arguably, 1e and 2e had a bigger break in how XP was handled alone (gp=xp to killing monsters and taking their stuff) and the change from combat matrices to THAC0. 2e also changed the bard dramatically, and 3e basically turned them completely into what 2e called Song Mages. Where are your tears for these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, they completely got rid of Vancian spellcasting, a staple of Dungeons and Dragons. This was an important in-setting issue as well, called the Spell Plague, as all of the wizards and spell casters in the Forgotten Realms lost their ability to use magic and had to use this entirely new system, which in turn required a 100 year timeskip so that they could get the setting back up into a playable condition.<br /> <br /> Again, gameplay in D&amp;D 1st edition was pretty close to 2nd edition, and 3rd edition generally emulated it pretty well. Meanwhile 4th edition gameplay has a different playstyle in that revolves entirely around the idea of short rest powers and long rest powers (which never really existed in that form in 1st or 2nd edition, nor in 3rd edition until the introduction of the Tome of Nine Swords). This makes 4th edition feel like a very different game in terms of basic game mechanics, from earlier editions of D&amp;D. 5th edition essentially combined 3rd and 4th edition together in order to reconcile the old grognard fans with the newer 4th edition fans.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can argue that I'm wrong, and that 4th edition wasn't any different from the earlier editions, but there's a reason why many long-time D&amp;D players said that playing 4th edition D&amp;D didn't feel like playing D&amp;D and moved over to Pathfinder. The 4th edition D&amp;D era was the only era where D&amp;D was not the best selling RPG on the market, and was knocked off from that position by Pathfinder. That's also why 5th edition moved back towards bringing back classic D&amp;D staples (like Vancian magic) in order to get many of those older players to come back and has proven to be much more successful financially.<br /> <br /> So as to the greater argument, I'm not sure where you're going with this. You seem to be arguing that D&amp;D 4th edition wasn't much different from 3rd edition because it shared some concepts like levels and the idea of having dungeons and dragons in the setting? And that therefore W5 isn't functionally much different from W20 because it uses the same terminology and the mechanics are fairly close?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:31:50-08:00","id":1529072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529053#post1529053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, they completely got rid of Vancian spellcasting, a staple of Dungeons and Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you really going to throw this stone from the glass house of 5e?<br /> <br /> At any rate, Pseudo-Vancian casting's days were numbered the moment that computer adventure rpg designers looked at it and said, &quot;No.&quot; Its coffin accumulated more nails when 2e, in the Player's Option Spells and Magic book, provided mechanics for spell points. The sorcerer finished it off by slashing it in the throat in 3e, and no one cared.<br /> <br /> Also, the Diablo 2 box from '99. You'd better believe that I still have my copy of that trainwreck.<br /> <br /> But that brings us back to 5e also not really giving a shit about PVC. You can sling cantrips all day long, and they accumulate in damage equivalent to the attacks made by fighters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This was an important in-setting issue as well, called the Spell Plague, as all of the wizards and spell casters in the Forgotten Realms lost their ability to use magic and had to use this entirely new system, which in turn required a 100 year timeskip so that they could get the setting back up into a playable condition. </div> </div> </div>That just seems like the worst way to explain that in-setting. Not sure if it was an executive thing or not.<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> Again, gameplay in D&amp;D 1st edition was pretty close to 2nd edition[quote]<br /> <br /> Except for where in 2e you're no longer trying to haul up as much treasure as possible for the xp that you'd get. Or avoiding fights with monsters as much as possible (2e encouraged you to get into fights instead, as well as following a narrative). Also, the weapons don't have the same special effects by armor, and they made the monk a priest!... until it wasn't several years later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and 3rd edition generally emulated it pretty well. </div> </div> </div>A giant load of bullshit! Fighters were nerfed until they sat somewhere below the Moho, with their attacks clipped, their good saves limited to one category, and their choice of skills limited to &quot;me am dum jock fighter!&quot;. Clerics and druids became mutant atomic superbeings that could solo adventures and do anything. Nothing carried over from later 2e to help the warriors, not even from the High-Level Campaigns book, except for that damned circular attack. Which still left out that talent from Combat and Tactics that could endlessly increase jumping distance as many times as you could cared to keep dedicating proficiency slots to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile 4th edition gameplay has a different playstyle in that revolves entirely around the idea of short rest powers and long rest powers (which never really existed in that form in 1st or 2nd edition </div> </div> </div>Long rest powers were daily. Short rest powers were multiple times per day. Don't act like this is actually all that different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nor in 3rd edition until the introduction of the Tome of Nine Swords). This makes 4th edition feel like a very different game in terms of basic game mechanics, from earlier editions of D&amp;D. 5th edition essentially combined 3rd and 4th edition together in order to reconcile the old grognard fans with the newer 4th edition fans. </div> </div> </div>Aye, and a fine job ya did, too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, of course, you can argue that I'm wrong, and that 4th edition wasn't any different from the earlier editions, but there's a reason why many long-time D&amp;D players said that playing 4th edition D&amp;D didn't feel like playing D&amp;D and moved over to Pathfinder. </div> </div> </div>Because they forgot what editions changes were like or never lived with them? My cash-strapped group started playing with my DM's hand me downs from when his parents played 1e AD&amp;D. 2e had... quite the different atmosphere by the end, with Skills and Powers being a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 4th edition D&amp;D era was the only era where D&amp;D was not the best selling RPG on the market, and was knocked off from that position by Pathfinder. </div> </div> </div>The only month where 4e wasn't still outselling them was when it was discontinued.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's also why 5th edition moved back towards bringing back classic D&amp;D staples (like Vancian magic) in order to get many of those older players to come back and has proven to be much more successful financially. </div> </div> </div>I'd wager that the number of people who still want PVC are dropping off as the years go on, and no one is going to care about it because the old timers will shift to people who were raised on MP system CRPGs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So as to the greater argument, I'm not sure where you're going with this. You seem to be arguing that D&amp;D 4th edition wasn't much different from 3rd edition because it shared some concepts like levels and the idea of having dungeons and dragons in the setting? And that therefore W5 isn't functionally much different from W20 because it uses the same terminology and the mechanics are fairly close? </div> </div> </div>Like I said from the beginning, it was a bad analogy, most pointedly because 4e is good (it knows what it is and what it needs to do, and it accomplishes it, even if you didn't want to see how the sausage was made or admit that D&amp;D is really still just a wargame simulator on a small scale) and W5 is not (doesn't know what it wants to be, can't decide on anything, cribs from Vampire to fill up space, not even remotely like any of the games before it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:39:32-08:00","id":1529073,"title":"","content":"Addendum: 5e pretty much eliminated psionics as a distinct set of classes. Guess what doesn't feel like D&amp;D now!<br /> <br /> (It surely would be a clusterfuck to try playing Dark Sun with 5e, but I think that's the intention of the people on top... who do not want to admit that they are the sorcerer kings in this setup, and keep it locked up under the excuse that it's &quot;too full of controversial material&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, controversial because you're killing off unrepentant slavers, overthrowing tyrants, and trying to stymie and reverse the environmental damage they caused. Oh, and here we get to the true relevance to W:tA and W5!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T05:43:56-08:00","id":1529086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529073#post1529073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: 5e pretty much eliminated psionics as a distinct set of classes. Guess what doesn't feel like D&amp;D now!<br /> <br /> (It surely would be a clusterfuck to try playing Dark Sun with 5e, but I think that's the intention of the people on top... who do not want to admit that they are the sorcerer kings in this setup, and keep it locked up under the excuse that it's &quot;too full of controversial material&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, controversial because you're killing off unrepentant slavers, overthrowing tyrants, and trying to stymie and reverse the environmental damage they caused. Oh, and here we get to the true relevance to W:tA and W5!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I suddenly have discovered what my niche as a tabletop blogger is because I get a lot of praise and push back for my WOD5 articles being about trying to reconcile old lore with new lore.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/thirteen-tips-to-running-dark-sun.html\" target=\"_blank\">Guess what I wrote for Dark Sun</a>?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T11:46:17-08:00","id":1529098,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">PHASE FOUR PART SIX</span><br /> <br /> What Does All of This Mean<br /> <br /> Before I finish up, a recap. W5 would be an okay game once all of the errors are fixed, a game primarily targeting younger, less-experienced players looking for shorter campaigns. More experienced players might be turned off by the paired-down systems, vague back story, and limiting play styles focused away from lengthy stories. In particular, WOD veterans might find the disconnect from the styles of the other games, even the newer V5, off-putting. Specifically, fans of the older editions of W:tA will probably hate much of W5, as many favorite portions have either been eliminated or altered to the point of being totally different. As to the moral implications to the greater gamer community of the issues brought up in the creation of W5...<br /> <br /> When Paradox faced negative publicity on one of the first supplements to V5, they quickly got rid of the designers who they felt were most responsible and dropped Modiphius as publisher. The management left in charge was to start work on W5. However, someone had a particular dislike for Werewolf and had a distinct vision of how to change it. The first team created for this butted heads with the management on these changes, leading to the team being dissolved, while keeping management. A second team was brought in, but this one was dissolved as well. Finally, a third team was created serving under Renegade with a new designer brought in to help mitigate the excesses found in the previous teams. After some false starts, new material was coming out, including the surprise creation of H5. Then, W5 was announced in October 2022. The news was quickly met with decisive criticism, as both those for and against the changes voiced their views as interviews detailed the new game. By January 2023, the new designer left, just before the first of the previews came out involving traced artwork. As more previews came out, the social media campaigns for both sides tried to sway opinions, with those for W5 usually dismissing even the most logical arguments of those against. The harsh treatment of some of the first two teams came to light, again with some casting doubts on their veracity. Even after W5 came out, riddled with quite a few errors, much of the online opinion tried to make an argument that the game was still very good. As of now, late January 2024, there are still doubts about just how W5 will move forward and what the state of future games in the WOD5 line will be treated.<br /> <br /> I have three questions that need to be answered, and there might just be evidence somewhere that can justify this case.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Was there a deadline to making W5? </b>W5 feels rushed, especially due to the errors in it. One would have expected that the game was mostly finished when it was announced, yet we know that there were still parts that were being written/re-written. It feels like that there was something more than just booking printer time involved. Maybe it was just arbitrary. Maybe there was financial involvement in getting something out by a certain time. Perhaps there were legal reasons involving the IP and something had to be announced /published by a certain time or there would be legal repercussions. If Paradox had to do something within a certain time frame, then that could explain the unusual, faster turn-around for W5. If it was just booking a printer, then maybe there could have been a delay to create a better product. Something just feels off in this timeline.</li> <li><b>What was the social media involvement in the publicity campaign? </b>In other posts, I have mentioned how some of the social media outbursts feel suspicious. Just slightly too hostile in some regards to those not liking how W5 was going. Also, some of the previews almost feel that they were chosen specifically to instill debate and publicity, such as what happened with a recent V5 product. While those directly working for W5 kept most of their own ideas unknown, fans were being overwhelming supportive. I'm just wondering if they were all &quot;real,&quot; or was there some incentive to sparking such debate? The actual developers couldn't explain their own feelings over any problems with W5 without risking their employment, nor could they be too enthusiastic about W5 without sparking a false advertising claim. However, those not connected could expound on W5, if they were being truthful. If they were incentivized, then things begin to look murkier.</li> <li><b>Could W5 have been made to be not as perfect from the start? </b>Companies have many reasons for making bad products deliberately. This might be a reason for the handling of W5. Maybe it was meant to be an off product, at least originally. Maybe the outlook changed and Paradox needed W5 to be a hit at the last minute. Maybe W5 had to be a hit for the financial outlook to come out right, no matter what. It is hard to tell. As mentioned, someone in the management change hated W:tA on some level. Maybe they wanted W5 to be a failure, but others needed it to be a hit. It is hard to say. However, if W5 was always meant to be a bad product, then this is a huge disservice to all of the older fans of the game.</li> </ol><br /> When W5 was first announced, I was able to come up with a basic scenario incorporating the changes into the existing metaplot that afternoon, using just my memory of the books. Since then, I have been able to that to many of the other changes as well. I have even presented some of them in this review, some coming up on the fly after feedback from my posts. [Basically, the Garou have to fight a three-pronged battle against the Triatic Wyrm in Europe, America, and Africa. Secondary battles in the Amazon and with the Beast Courts in Asia, and maybe a bit of <i>Shattered Dreams</i> thrown in as well. The Garou win, but lose the war as Gaia is severely weakened. I'm thinking of starting a thread about my scenario and asking for opinions on it.] Now, if I could do that, then so could have the dozens of others who had worked on this for five years, with access to literally everything that had ever been written about Werewolf. For W5 to come out the way it did is a disservice to those fans from the past thirty years. Even if it was always going to be a complete reboot, there shouldn't have been this many mistakes. There shouldn't have been this much online battle between generations. There shouldn't have been this much distrust.<br /> <br /> If W5 was just a game I didn't like, I would have ignored it and went on with my life. However, I feel I have presented enough evidence to suggest that something more was going on in the creation and publicity for this game, implications that one might not want to support this game in the future. While I gave W5 an Incomplete earlier, if any of my above questions turn out to have bad answers, then I will have to give W5 an <b>F</b>. I would hate doing so, but I would have to on completely moral standards. So many people worked hard on W5, even if I don't really like it, and I don't want their work to go in vain. They might not have known what was in store for W5, but most probably just wanted to work on doing something they loved, or at least needed the money for. There are just too many unresolved issues for me to do otherwise. <br /> <br /> Finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T12:41:55-08:00","id":1529102,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;deadline&quot; note, I think it's generally perceived that ParaWolf was really trying to get W5 out in time for GenCon 2023, especially given its long production history and staff changeovers. There's content in the corebook that I don't necessarily disagree with, but I do disagree with the emphasis and page space afforded to it, especially at the expense of other elements. If there had been time for editing, rebalancing, etc., maybe some of the stuff in the corebook would be more digestible to me and others. Illustrating the Garou's flaws without painting them as Gaia's failchildren at every turn, giving the tribes more detailed writeups*, etc.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;social media&quot; element, I feel like we need to look at Achilli here. Even after leaving the team, he was still pushing for the book, and some of his comments about the old players didn't really go over well. But I do think there are parts that he had a vision for the book that he was trying to push for against the tide of what it was. Like his comments on how the Garou do have a rich, detailed, but contradictory oral history - the core book really doesn't do a lot to back that up, but I imagine that, if there was more time and someone in editorial cared, we could get more about the stories the Garou tell themselves than a lot of &quot;I don't know.&quot;<br /> <br /> But then we get the Fenrir stuff, where it becomes clear that Achilli was likely trying to cover someone else's ass. Let's look at the many reasons he offered for why the Fenrir had to go:<br /> <br /> -&quot;We decided to downplay all ethnic ties for the various tribes, so they didn't really fit.&quot; Almost as soon as he said this, everyone pointed out that there was still a tribe called the &quot;Fianna,&quot; which led to the &quot;Sorry, I'm sorry, I'm trying to undo it&quot; move of renaming them the Hart Wardens.<br /> -&quot;We couldn't really come up with four action verbs for them, like with the rest of the tribes.&quot; I'm not even going to dignify this with a rebuttal.<br /> -&quot;If we removed the ethnic ties, we'd effectively have a tribe full of Ahrouns, and that would be boring.&quot; They removed all the Indigenous elements from the Gale Stalkers, and they're still a warrior tribe with a distinctive ethos. They removed all the Celtic elements from the Fianna/Hart Wardens, and now, their duties seem to be &quot;what every Garou should be doing, but a little extra.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, if you trust Sambrano's accounts, all these excuses were meant to cover for the fact that editorial just wanted the Fenrir gone because they considered the concept toxic beyond repair. And even then, nobody felt the need to just come out and say, &quot;We don't trust you fuckers with Viking werewolves who hate weakness.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not going to go so far as to say &quot;This is Werewolf written by people who hated Werewolf,&quot; even if it seems like there are a lot of areas where editorial considered certain concepts to be utterly rotted and unsalvageable. But whatever aim existed for W5, it's clear the thumb was on the scale in some areas, and even noble gestures or attempts at nuance feel robbed by the effort to rush the book out before GenCon in a way that's anodyne enough not to piss the casual reader off.<br /> <br /> * Speaking of, I finally realized why some of the tribes didn't sit right after looking over their writeups. One of the major beats of the book is that the Garou need to fight <i>beyond</i> the war and focus on different fronts. Which would be easier, if some of these tribes weren't rewritten so that they're mostly focused on the war and the Garou.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies were once protectors of women and children, who they saw as the easiest targets of the Wyrm's deprivations. Now, they focus on vengeance, but the writeup emphasizes how much it's about <i>their</i> perception of injustice and restitution.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers once associated with and fought for the unhoused and economically disadvantaged, who <i>they</i> saw as the easiest target of the Wyrm's deprivations. Now, they're Garou Nosferatu, focused on getting secrets and intel for the war through associating with the disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia were the tribe most likely to find the root of suffering among mortals and cut it out at the source before the Wyrm could infect the wound. Now, they're mostly dedicated to the secrets of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Younger Brother were staunch advocates for Indigenous rights and vocal decolonialists. Now, the Gale Stalkers just hunt, all the time.<br /> <br /> This goes back to my idea that the book seems to be coming from the perspective that the Garou have never fought the war the right way before in their entire existence, and that is why they're losing. It effectively rolls back the tribes so that any advocacy they did outside of kicking the Wyrm in the teeth was either less important or nonexistent. Further, the writeups don't have the &quot;pivot&quot; moment that shows how they might turn these tactics towards new fronts - or if it does, it's not exactly showing them thinking differently, like with some of the more contentious Red Talon sample characters. The only tribes who really seem to be focused on advocacy outside of direct war against the Wyrm are the Black Furies (who are painted as doing it for their own self-righteousness), the Red Talons (who are still fighting to protect their own personal patch), and the Stargazers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","name":"JustinCognito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T12:43:39-08:00","id":1529103,"title":"","content":"Being used to Onyx Paths semi-open development where you can chat to the Devs and Writers the fact that none of those who worked on W5 have engaged with any of the fans pro or con just feels weird. The only one whose done the slightest bit of engagement is Justin who doesn't even work there anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T14:14:19-08:00","id":1529106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werew