stile in some regards to those not liking how W5 was going. Also, some of the previews almost feel that they were chosen specifically to instill debate and publicity, such as what happened with a recent V5 product. While those directly working for W5 kept most of their own ideas unknown, fans were being overwhelming supportive. I'm just wondering if they were all &quot;real,&quot; or was there some incentive to sparking such debate? The actual developers couldn't explain their own feelings over any problems with W5 without risking their employment, nor could they be too enthusiastic about W5 without sparking a false advertising claim. However, those not connected could expound on W5, if they were being truthful. If they were incentivized, then things begin to look murkier.</li> <li><b>Could W5 have been made to be not as perfect from the start? </b>Companies have many reasons for making bad products deliberately. This might be a reason for the handling of W5. Maybe it was meant to be an off product, at least originally. Maybe the outlook changed and Paradox needed W5 to be a hit at the last minute. Maybe W5 had to be a hit for the financial outlook to come out right, no matter what. It is hard to tell. As mentioned, someone in the management change hated W:tA on some level. Maybe they wanted W5 to be a failure, but others needed it to be a hit. It is hard to say. However, if W5 was always meant to be a bad product, then this is a huge disservice to all of the older fans of the game.</li> </ol><br /> When W5 was first announced, I was able to come up with a basic scenario incorporating the changes into the existing metaplot that afternoon, using just my memory of the books. Since then, I have been able to that to many of the other changes as well. I have even presented some of them in this review, some coming up on the fly after feedback from my posts. [Basically, the Garou have to fight a three-pronged battle against the Triatic Wyrm in Europe, America, and Africa. Secondary battles in the Amazon and with the Beast Courts in Asia, and maybe a bit of <i>Shattered Dreams</i> thrown in as well. The Garou win, but lose the war as Gaia is severely weakened. I'm thinking of starting a thread about my scenario and asking for opinions on it.] Now, if I could do that, then so could have the dozens of others who had worked on this for five years, with access to literally everything that had ever been written about Werewolf. For W5 to come out the way it did is a disservice to those fans from the past thirty years. Even if it was always going to be a complete reboot, there shouldn't have been this many mistakes. There shouldn't have been this much online battle between generations. There shouldn't have been this much distrust.<br /> <br /> If W5 was just a game I didn't like, I would have ignored it and went on with my life. However, I feel I have presented enough evidence to suggest that something more was going on in the creation and publicity for this game, implications that one might not want to support this game in the future. While I gave W5 an Incomplete earlier, if any of my above questions turn out to have bad answers, then I will have to give W5 an <b>F</b>. I would hate doing so, but I would have to on completely moral standards. So many people worked hard on W5, even if I don't really like it, and I don't want their work to go in vain. They might not have known what was in store for W5, but most probably just wanted to work on doing something they loved, or at least needed the money for. There are just too many unresolved issues for me to do otherwise.<br /> <br /> Finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making it clear that this is just a hypothesis.<br /> <br /> For 1. I believe it was just a friction of interests, assuming that the game actually took five years, I think it just got to the point where it was no longer possible to wait for the project to be ready. For 2. I have some experience in how internet groups work, not that much because I'm stuck for my sanity, but that may have just been the right argument within the right group + the controversies of previous editions and the rest happens spontaneously.<br /> For 3. I don't know if this is applicable in this case, but I know that with film franchises they need to deliver some related material within a deadline to avoid losing the rights, How knows if there were any similar circumstances here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T14:29:05-08:00","id":1529109,"title":"","content":"Given how unfinished and half-baked both H5 and W5 are, I really wouldn't be surprised if Paradox was treating any gameline not called V5 as copyright squatting at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T11:39:06-08:00","id":1529159,"title":"","content":"So, I want to start this little tirade with the things that made WtA so annoying/disgusting for some people. These are not my opinions, just what I've heard over the years.<br /> <br /> -It was racist<br /> -It was too positive for a WoD game<br /> -It didn't treat the garou monstrous enough<br /> -The umbra and spirits liking the garou made things too easy<br /> -Furry Captain Planet sucks<br /> -It isn't about werewolves<br /> -Red Talons were too edgelordy<br /> -Get of Fenris symbol is bad<br /> -It has bestiality in it<br /> -It is toxic masculinity and all its players are all too<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, looking at the By Nights Studios version of WtA and the ill-fitting additions to Changing Ways, you can see the direction of thought that had started in regards to what W5 would become. Things became more bleak, caerns were lost and the umbra became hard to traverse. The loss of Caerns and the Umbra's ease is a common theme in all the changes. It makes me think the setting was seen as too positive for a WoD game and where the PCs had elders they could trust.<br /> <br /> If look at the Forsaken, its own game now as it is, the same mentality is present. Hostile umbra, less infrastructure and a 'darker' setting.<br /> <br /> This mentality became the cornerstone of W5, with other changes being added as the world around it grew more aware of minority rights.<br /> <br /> As an aside, most of these accusations ignore all the actual in-game troubles of the umbra and garou society.<br /> <br /> Something that actually surprised me, given how common of a squick it is, the wolf-born have stayed. The garou born were a much,much,MUCH less mentioned breed and yet they were removed. It goes to show how most of the squick was people overthinking things.<br /> <br /> <br /> In all honesty, W5 suffers from many things but the biggest is how unpolished it is. It spends pages detailing how the garou failed but then offers no correct way to proceed. It is so focused on the CoF that it forgets the BSDs exist. It refers to old sept positions even though they are no longer in use. Nevermind the Clement Lupus and the form descriptions ACTUALLY making the old bestiality accusation more likely and example characters worse than the CoF.<br /> <br /> What do I think happened to make W5 like this? I personally think it was a mixture of clashing ideals and confusion about how to make the game 'fit WoD better' without making a completely new game. As I stated above, there have been a lot of accusations of WtA being too positive and not monstrous enough, simply because the game isn't as nihilistic as VtM is. I've seen many fan ways to 'fix' the setting and they all boil down to &quot;Gaia is dead/never existed and garou fought for nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I think a major part of W5 being in limbo was the cultural nature of the tribes. Unless you played the game, looking from outside in it might have looked like a game of Captain Ethnic and so it might have been hard to get people to develop it. Even if you did, then justified changes like J.F Sambrano suggested were earned through a lot of fighting and arguing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T12:50:20-08:00","id":1529169,"title":"","content":"The deadline<br /> <br /> It's hard to say how it's all correlated or why some things happened in the way that they did but I think there are three important factors to how this all turned into a very rushed project towards the end (despite the delays and switch in developer-teams). The first is Paradox's insistence on making it a Gen-Con-release. I don't think there's a lot of merit to having to do that in the age of the internet, digital releases and social media (like, for example, I bet getting Critical Role to play your game on stream is ten times better than having a booth at Gen Con with your new book in terms of publicity). But it is what it is... So this means there are only three release-dates in play: Gen-Con 2022, 2023 and 2024. Well, we got the first preview in October 2022 which is clearly too late for a 2022 release so that leaves 2023 and 2024. But one can understand that under that restriction you're gonna push hard for Gen-Con 2023. I mean, imagine... if they had delayed we still wouldn't have the book in our hands! Besides it wouldn't even matter to delay to 2024 because Justin Achilli decides to leave in January 2023. That's the second factor. And who knows why it turned out like that. But now that's another restriction. Also, it's unclear at what point it even became clear that this other &quot;deadline&quot; became a part of the development-process. But there's a third factor and that's the V5 Players Guide. That supplement is the rare exception where writers from the Paradox-in-house-team contributed to the book. Justin Achilli, Khaldoun Khelil and Karim Muammar (who also wrote parts of W5) contributed writing to the V5 Players Guide. Now the weird bit with the V5 PG is that it was originally scheduled to be released in Summer 2022 and was then delayed to early 2023. The official explanation from Renegade developers was that they needed time to &quot;make the book better&quot;... well, that sounds like PR-bullshit of course. But, interestingly, the development of this book fell into the very same timeframe as W5 went through the final stages of development (at least as far as writing was concerned).<br /> <br /> It could very well be that a lot of what we're looking here as shortcomings - the &quot;Who knows?&quot;-approach to the worldbuilding, the preference to erase stuff instead of keeping things as they were or replace something with a new, original idea or the uncredited reliance on previous work from the Hunters Entertainment - are the result of a development-team through a combination of various factors just cornered itself into having to rush this project. It would also explain the Glass Walker controversy with the art. Say it's only in late October that the writers even got to the part of writing the archetypes of the Tribes in the Tribe-chapter. And then they turned to the artist and told him to give them 44 (!) photorealistic drawings in less than half a year that correspond to the archetypes. The result: He cut corners in the whole process (sourcing, how much he traced vs original art)... and well, the rest is history as they say. (BTW, I think Renegade at least has stopped using him because he was part of every WOD5E-book the last couple of years but his art wasn't a part of the most recent Bloodstained Love)<br /> <br /> Social Media<br /> <br /> Just two comments on that:<ul><li>What's striking is that Justin Achilli was on Outstar's WOD-news-show quite a few times to add developer-commentary to the release of the H5 corebook. And he was on the show again for the October preview of W5. But after he left the presence of developers on the WOD-news-show has disappeared. There were no developer-interviews for Blood Sigil and Blood-Stained Love and also not an extra interview for the release of W5 (like with H5). Now with the Renegade-books it's less of an issue because they're doing their own online-events as well but when it comes to what's going on with the in-house-team at Paradox... Who knows what's going on over there these days... (At least, Outstar has a cohost on her show now because there was a time when Outstar fell ill and that meant... there simply were no WOD-news-shows which was a bit ridiculous)</li> <li>Justin Achilli had this habit of randomly giving these hot takes about the WOD. Was it helpful from a PR-perspective to go on Twitter and shout random, uncontextualized ideas into the void? Not really. And there were weird moments like with the verbs-thing with the Get of Fenris. For example, in one show with Outstar he called H5 a &quot;heist-game&quot;. Or he explained that Hunters in H5 don't need to have an equivalent to Humanity or something like Convictions and Chronicle Tenets because of something he called &quot;Sober Play&quot; because he reasoned that this would allow PCs to have &quot;free will&quot; and not be restricted by systems like a Humanity 4 in V5. Never understood what the deal was with these hot takes but that's how he operated. Also, he's pretty opinionated but if it were just a disagreement with his vision then it would be fine. But him talking about &quot;Sober Play&quot;, for example, was meaningless because in effect it just meant H5 looked at the mechanics of V5, haphazardly removed bits and pieces and that was it. And also the term &quot;Sober Play&quot; never appeared in the H5 corebook. If it really had been such a cornerstone of the development-philosophy why was it never mentioned in the book? But when you read the descriptions from JF Sambrano it seems like Karim Muammar is quite the opinionated person as well. Maybe that's what H5 and W5 are in the end: The lowest common denominator between two very opinionated people.</li> </ul><br /> Is the flawed state of W5 intentional?<br /> <br /> I think Paradox at large is far more invested in WOD as a brand for videogames than any RPG-books (although even on that front... so what happened to the two announced text-adventures for Hunter and Werewolf...?). When you go to the new WOD-website that is now found on the Paradox-website you will have a far easier time finding the site for Bloodlines 2 instead of the page where WOD in general is talked about (and links to the books on the Renegade-website). The books are a sideshow to Paradox.<br /> <br /> To Paradox, the only thing that matters right now isn't to plan for an M5 but rather to get Bloodlines 2 out the door in the hopes that it becomes a success. But I think similarly to W5, they are pushing for something to happen that simply won't. On the other hand, the only alternative to the problems mentioned above with the deadline would've been to delay the W5 corebook <i>yet again</i>. I would guess you would feel like you're going insane when you put people in charge of developing these RPG-books for the WOD and the projects keep getting derailed despite the changes you make to who's in charge and how the development is organized.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll see what the future will bring. My money is still on Paradox giving the development of the next corebook to Renegade and just dissolving most of the in-house team.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T13:58:31-08:00","id":1529174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529159#post1529159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something that actually surprised me, given how common of a squick it is, the wolf-born have stayed. The garou born were a much,much,MUCH less mentioned breed and yet they were removed. It goes to show how most of the squick was people overthinking things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, for all the jokes about the ethos of W:tA being &quot;Fuck this wolf or the earth will die,&quot; keeping the Lupus in can be all right if the idea of needing to propagate more Lupus is strictly kept to them, and we avoid weird things like that Homid-Lupus relationship or the Rite of Having A Litter from the much-reviled Tribebook: Children of Gaia Revised. It's a bit harder to keep in the Crinos-born whose name is linked to an Indigenous group associated with being &quot;half-breeds&quot; - and even if you change the name, you still have people who are effectively punished with some disability or another as a result of their parents having forbidden werewolf sex. It's a big hurdle to clear, and for all that I chide the W5 decisions that feel like &quot;That seems like a lot of work,&quot; I can't fault them for deciding this might be A Lot for new players to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","name":"JustinCognito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T15:42:32-08:00","id":1529176,"title":"","content":"Two issues: Continuance and consistency.<br /> <br /> With the first, I just mean &quot;You don't have to deal with that in the corebook.&quot; None of these WOD5E corebooks are meant to reproduce the tomes that are 20th Anniversary corebooks. And V5 even set a standard by launching with seven Clans in the corebook. You don't need all the options from previous editions to be immediately present (although I like the idea of making those other options available via free supplements like the V5 Companion whereas a specific supplement like Blood Sigils gets sold with the premise of expanding or offering more options for play). In that sense, it would have been fine to make H5 about local hunter-cells that have certain advantages and disadvantages/problems while hunter-orgs have different advantages and disadvantages/problems. And you just leave the door open for a supplement down the line that is all about playing a hunter working for a hunter-org. Instead, the H5 corebook is obsessed with making it clear that hunter-orgs are bad and that it's badwrongfun. The big issue with both the H5 and the W5 corebook are that they are very invested in closing doors for what potential supplements could explore.<br /> <br /> With the second, I'm talking about the changes W5 just addresses with erasure. The Crinos-Born and Kinfolk, for example. We're told that these troublesome elements needed to be excised because of the abuse, the breeding-talk and the social ostracization. But how about these three elements from V5: Thin-Bloods, Caitiff and the Blood-Bond. Is anything bad happening in V5 for those guys and whoever is affected by the last thing? In fact, let's quote the V5 Players Guide what it thinks of playing an All-Thin-Blood-Chronicle: &quot;Players new to Vampire can benefit from playing an all thin-blood chronicle. Thin-blood characters don\u2019t know any more about the world, or its history, or what vampires can do, than you do! This outsider perspective also allows players of older editions to painlessly reset their expectations of this new millennium of darkness.&quot; Imagine thinking that throwing a Thinblood-character into a Camarilla-run city is the ideal beginners-campaign. But by that standard W5 should definitely have kept the Crinos-Born and Kinfolk because they make for such tremendous &quot;beginners-campaigns&quot; according to the V5 PG. (Also, shoutout to the condescension of &quot;allows players of older editions to painlessly reset their expectations&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T18:43:59-08:00","id":1529188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529176#post1529176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two issues: Continuance and consistency.<br /> <br /> With the first, I just mean &quot;You don't have to deal with that in the corebook.&quot; None of these WOD5E corebooks are meant to reproduce the tomes that are 20th Anniversary corebooks. And V5 even set a standard by launching with seven Clans in the corebook. You don't need all the options from previous editions to be immediately present (although I like the idea of making those other options available via free supplements like the V5 Companion whereas a specific supplement like Blood Sigils gets sold with the premise of expanding or offering more options for play). In that sense, it would have been fine to make H5 about local hunter-cells that have certain advantages and disadvantages/problems while hunter-orgs have different advantages and disadvantages/problems. And you just leave the door open for a supplement down the line that is all about playing a hunter working for a hunter-org. Instead, the H5 corebook is obsessed with making it clear that hunter-orgs are bad and that it's badwrongfun. The big issue with both the H5 and the W5 corebook are that they are very invested in closing doors for what potential supplements could explore.<br /> <br /> With the second, I'm talking about the changes W5 just addresses with erasure. The Crinos-Born and Kinfolk, for example. We're told that these troublesome elements needed to be excised because of the abuse, the breeding-talk and the social ostracization. But how about these three elements from V5: Thin-Bloods, Caitiff and the Blood-Bond. Is anything bad happening in V5 for those guys and whoever is affected by the last thing? In fact, let's quote the V5 Players Guide what it thinks of playing an All-Thin-Blood-Chronicle: &quot;Players new to Vampire can benefit from playing an all thin-blood chronicle. Thin-blood characters don\u2019t know any more about the world, or its history, or what vampires can do, than you do! This outsider perspective also allows players of older editions to painlessly reset their expectations of this new millennium of darkness.&quot; Imagine thinking that throwing a Thinblood-character into a Camarilla-run city is the ideal beginners-campaign. But by that standard W5 should definitely have kept the Crinos-Born and Kinfolk because they make for such tremendous &quot;beginners-campaigns&quot; according to the V5 PG. (Also, shoutout to the condescension of &quot;allows players of older editions to painlessly reset their expectations&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand why the Crinosborn were considered to be ableist and the word for them was being misappropriated. It's not one that is a slur (though it has been in places) but it's a bit like naming your supernatural fairy-human hybrids, &quot;Welsh.&quot; The fact that they're all cursed by Gaia is also something that adds uncomfortable overtones that the disabled from birth are affronts to God dating back to when Jesus mentioned this was a stupid idea in the New Testament. Still, you'd think they could have fixed this easier.<br /> <br /> * Crinosborn are called, well, Crinosborn.<br /> * Crinosborn are a 1/10 chance of being born werewolves, same as any other kinfolk. Most are born humans.<br /> * They don't suffer any deformities or madness.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I thought this was the direction Revised was going with the Perfect M**** and all subsequent Crinosborn being lacking such. Sort of like killing the Swords of Heimdall was meant to put to rest that controversy.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of the Kinfolk feels far more inexplicable because that dramatically reduces story potential. The Kinian in Changeling: The Dreaming are extremely fun to play and you could do Kinfolk hunters, hedge mages, and support for your Garou friends. The forced breeding and abuse was something that is VERY trigger filled but you simply can say....that doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> It also reduces a lot of the nonviolent options that Garou are supposed to take against corporations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T19:18:09-08:00","id":1529190,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think the &quot;cursed by Gaia&quot; reason for Crinos-born disabilities is meant to be the canon answer, but rather just what some Garou assume it is. In fact, I don't think it's ever really given a canon answer and it's left open for interpretation, and it's just as likely to be a &quot;spiritual inbreeding&quot; or overconcentration of Garou-ness issue. I always figured the Crinos-born came first and the Litany law second, rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> Which comes with its own issues to sort out, I guess.But I don't know, it's never sat right with me to just remove the Crinos-born as disabled representation, or that their marginalization somehow makes the game problematic when it's a legitimate social issue the Garou have to overcome. I'm sure there are better ways to handle it, but if it were me, I would keep the core idea there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T19:54:12-08:00","id":1529193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529190#post1529190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think the &quot;cursed by Gaia&quot; reason for Crinos-born disabilities is meant to be the canon answer, but rather just what some Garou assume it is. In fact, I don't think it's ever really given a canon answer and it's left open for interpretation, and it's just as likely to be a &quot;spiritual inbreeding&quot; or overconcentration of Garou-ness issue. I always figured the Crinos-born came first and the Litany law second, rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> Which comes with its own issues to sort out, I guess.But I don't know, it's never sat right with me to just remove the Crinos-born as disabled representation, or that their marginalization somehow makes the game problematic when it's a legitimate social issue the Garou have to overcome. I'm sure there are better ways to handle it, but if it were me, I would keep the core idea there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, W:tA isn't really big on explaining things away by &quot;curses&quot;, and any insistence otherwise in-character is just that. It's more likely to be a form of chiminage, much like how Garou can't deal with silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:01:56-08:00","id":1529194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529190#post1529190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think the &quot;cursed by Gaia&quot; reason for Crinos-born disabilities is meant to be the canon answer, but rather just what some Garou assume it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can certainly claim that but if you have the law against Garou breeding up there along with, &quot;Don't do a cannibalism&quot; and &quot;save the world&quot; as well as all Garou-born suffering a horrible infirmity then have a &quot;Perfect Crinosborn&quot; show up as a sign of the End of the World.<br /> <br /> Well....<br /> <br /> It's hard to argue that message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:11:36-08:00","id":1529195,"title":"","content":"When one takes the full known factual nature of the WtA setting, the deformities have to be a curse. I've done really detailed breakdowns of this before, but the key points:<br /> <br /> 1) It is not inherent to shapeshifters. Some of the Fera simply can't reproduce with others of their kind, some have deformed kids, and some have kids that actually get bonuses. So any explanation of the &quot;spirit incest overloads the child&quot; doesn't work because it doesn't hold true across all of them.<br /> <br /> 2) The highest level of spirits created the Fera, and can impart or change aspects like what metal harms them, or various additional weaknesses.<br /> <br /> If it's not inherent to all shifters, and we know Gaia and the Celestines can impart significant changes, then the deformities must come from such high level influences. The only real alternative, is that it is innate to all shifters, but instead the ones that don't end up in deformities were altered to protect them instead (which doesn't really change the fundamental message in the metanarrative sense).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:12:11-08:00","id":1529196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529194#post1529194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can certainly claim that but if you have the law against Garou breeding up there along with, &quot;Don't do a cannibalism&quot; and &quot;save the world&quot; as well as all Garou-born suffering a horrible infirmity then have a &quot;Perfect Crinosborn&quot; show up as a sign of the End of the World.<br /> <br /> Well....<br /> <br /> It's hard to argue that message.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, though? The reason for the Perfect Crinos-Born being like that is never given or stated to be a &quot;curse lifting&quot;, only that their birth is significant. It's not even the only weird thing about their birth (they come from two other Crinos-born, which shouldn't be able to reproduce in the first place). It could easily be for any other reason, and that reason could even (and I think it actually does) vary between scenarios.<br /> <br /> And the Litany says a lot of things that are up for interpretation or arguably outdated. I'm not sure what the point here is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:17:44-08:00","id":1529197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529195#post1529195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one takes the full known factual nature of the WtA setting, the deformities have to be a curse. I've done really detailed breakdowns of this before, but the key points:<br /> <br /> 1) It is not inherent to shapeshifters. Some of the Fera simply can't reproduce with others of their kind, some have deformed kids, and some have kids that actually get bonuses. So any explanation of the &quot;spirit incest overloads the child&quot; doesn't work because it doesn't hold true across all of them.<br /> <br /> 2) The highest level of spirits created the Fera, and can impart or change aspects like what metal harms them, or various additional weaknesses.<br /> <br /> If it's not inherent to all shifters, and we know Gaia and the Celestines can impart significant changes, then the deformities must come from such high level influences. The only real alternative, is that it is innate to all shifters, but instead the ones that don't end up in deformities were altered to protect them instead (which doesn't really change the fundamental message in the metanarrative sense).</div> </div> </div> </div>These are good points, and I think this is where the concept needs to be clarified, because it's kind of arbitary that it would be so different across different Fera to me.A few of the differences make sense, but some of them just don't, and I think having a solid answer would help. If it is a curse, that needs to be changed, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:20:23-08:00","id":1529198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529196#post1529196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not, though? The reason for the Perfect Crinos-Born being like that is never given or stated to be a &quot;curse lifting&quot;, only that their birth is significant. It's not even the only weird thing about their birth (they come from two other Crinos-born, which shouldn't be able to reproduce in the first place). It could easily be for any other reason, and that reason could even (and I think it actually does) vary between scenarios.<br /> <br /> And the Litany says a lot of things that are up for interpretation or arguably outdated. I'm not sure what the point here is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> Which also eliminates any sense that the Crinosborn aren't still abominations to Gaia, especially when the Perfect Crinosborn sides with the BSD in many stories.<br /> <br /> But yes, is there any argument that the Crinosborn aren't abelist because, &quot;You could probably say they're not disliked by Gaia or cursed.&quot;<br /> <br /> ?<br /> <br /> Just asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-22-2024, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T20:30:58-08:00","id":1529199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529198#post1529198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, is there any argument that the Crinosborn aren't abelist because, &quot;You could probably say they're not disliked by Gaia or cursed.&quot;<br /> <br /> ?<br /> <br /> Just asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, to me, not everyone wants to avoid addressing marginalization within games. It's not something everyone should be forced to deal with if they don't want to, but WtA explicitly having disabled characters as a player option with mechanical support, even if it was kind of clumsy, is still meaningful to me and a lot of other people. It definitely needs a major update to clarify what exactly what causes it and to clean up any unfortunate implications, but I don't think the answer is &quot;not even trying.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T21:32:00-08:00","id":1529201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, to me, not everyone wants to avoid addressing marginalization within games. </div> </div> </div>I agree. These are good points, and I think this is where the concept needs to be clarified. I'm a fan of taking this in the direction of 'unreliable narrator' at my tabletops, where the notion of it being a &quot;curse/supernatural incest&quot; is something perpetuated by the Western Concordat to justify their treatment of the warborn. I do, however, think the warborn, and charachs especially, are synonymous with queerness. Their treatment wasn't just limited to heterosexual garou, but is extended to same-sex garou as well, regardless of whether they are bearing warborn children or not. If one were to make a minor shift away from everyday ableism, it can stand as a compelling representation of the Garou experience representing queerness, on a fundamental level. <a href=\"https://songoftrillium.tumblr.com/queerness\" target=\"_blank\">I wrote an essay</a> on this topic that kind of lays out more specifically what these parallels are and why I think simply deleting them in W5 wasn't an appropriate response. In short, it doesn't 'fix' the problem, but rather, it merely renders them invisible, which in many ways is even worse.<br /> <br /> An approach I'm taking to the warborn is to move away from giving them real-life disabilities and instead lend them aspects of horror that are indicative of an imbalance of Wyld influence, as though they are touched by The Flux. Things like a tree limb where a leg ought to be, a limb that cannot change it's wolf form, glowing fur patterns, significantly more eyes on one side of the head than the other causing blurred vision and headaches, and other features of supernatural asymmetry that inhibit their ability to operate openly in human society while still pushing narratives of social inequity and accommodation. Think less &quot;supernatural incest,&quot; and more &quot;pan's labyrinth&quot; or &quot;hellboy&quot; features at the heart of this mistreatment. This would hold space for explorations of queer culture as well as disability at the table without having able-bodied players caricaturing real-life disabilities. As for those wanting to have characters with real-life disabilities still, these features have always been available in merits and flaws, and no longer have to be compulsory, nor the reason for this codified ill treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T21:57:27-08:00","id":1529202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529199#post1529199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, to me, not everyone wants to avoid addressing marginalization within games. It's not something everyone should be forced to deal with if they don't want to, but WtA explicitly having disabled characters as a player option with mechanical support, even if it was kind of clumsy, is still meaningful to me and a lot of other people. It definitely needs a major update to clarify what exactly what causes it and to clean up any unfortunate implications, but I don't think the answer is &quot;not even trying.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm neuratypical in real life and my favorite Clan is the Malkavians and the Silver Fangs when they all suffered Derangements.<br /> <br /> I love playing half-elves and drow.<br /> <br /> I feel the Crinoborn just reduced the possibilities of roleplay in-universe. Garou on Garou relations really could have broadened the scope of the game world a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T22:01:40-08:00","id":1529204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529202#post1529202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm neuratypical in real life and my favorite Clan is the Malkavians and the Silver Fangs when they all suffered Derangements.<br /> <br /> I love playing half-elves and drow.<br /> <br /> I feel the Crinoborn just reduced the possibilities of roleplay in-universe. Garou on Garou relations really could have broadened the scope of the game world a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, same hat, among other things. But I think we're going to have to agree to disagree here, because I personally don't think that it would add all that much. It's just removing an element that could have been executed better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T22:55:02-08:00","id":1529206,"title":"","content":"I think we need to step back and look at the reason the garouborn/warborn/crinosborn existed in the first place;<br /> <br /> They were there to avoid the garou becoming too insular and breeding with only each other. Having the breed be a sterile result of the mating meant that the garou still had to go to humans and wolves for their offspring. And such have some connection to the world outside caerns.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, there was no such need to avoid insularity as the situation and the stakes were very different.<br /> <br /> But in W5, I do not know which solution is better. Even if who becomes garou is random now (allegedly), you still have tribes like the Fangs, Red Talons and BSDs that could basically remove themselves from the world now entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T00:08:14-08:00","id":1529210,"title":"","content":"On the ableism stuff:<br /> <br /> Two key points to remember, are that much like Younger and Older Brother, there are a lot of people that gravitated towards the deformities as prominent representation - even if problematic representation - because it was something rather than nothing. Unlike being able to work in disabilities as quirks or Flaws, having a prominent character creation choice that resulted in a disability helps push the unfairness of disabilities into the forefront of the topics that game touches on. It's not &quot;everyone gets a weakness, yours is just something a bit more real,&quot; like Malkavians. The Crinos-born were just screwed over. and it's not fair even in a game sense<br /> <br /> Second, a lot of disabled gamers hate the idea that being disable makes you &quot;stronger,&quot; aka things like Flaws giving you bonus points. This is something that actually come up in a panel Eddy did that they replayed on the Onyxpath Cast ages ago (keeping in mind that Eddy is hearing impaired). The whole idea of &quot;overcoming the adversity of your disability and being a stronger person for it,&quot; is a really toxic abilist narrative of its own. Disabilities are a drag on your life... that's kinda the whole deal. Learning ways to cope with them is just spending time and energy on that instead of thing you'd want to do. Medical treatments are more time, recovery, and money that means missing out on things you'll never get back in the hopes of being able to enjoy stuff later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T00:30:38-08:00","id":1529211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529210#post1529210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the ableism stuff:<br /> <br /> Two key points to remember, are that much like Younger and Older Brother, there are a lot of people that gravitated towards the deformities as prominent representation - even if problematic representation - because it was something rather than nothing. Unlike being able to work in disabilities as quirks or Flaws, having a prominent character creation choice that resulted in a disability helps push the unfairness of disabilities into the forefront of the topics that game touches on. It's not &quot;everyone gets a weakness, yours is just something a bit more real,&quot; like Malkavians. The Crinos-born were just screwed over. and it's not fair even in a game sense<br /> <br /> Second, a lot of disabled gamers hate the idea that being disable makes you &quot;stronger,&quot; aka things like Flaws giving you bonus points. This is something that actually come up in a panel Eddy did that they replayed on the Onyxpath Cast ages ago (keeping in mind that Eddy is hearing impaired). The whole idea of &quot;overcoming the adversity of your disability and being a stronger person for it,&quot; is a really toxic abilist narrative of its own. Disabilities are a drag on your life... that's kinda the whole deal. Learning ways to cope with them is just spending time and energy on that instead of thing you'd want to do. Medical treatments are more time, recovery, and money that means missing out on things you'll never get back in the hopes of being able to enjoy stuff later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. This is a really great articulation as to why the Crinos-born still have value despite the existence of disability flaws and the somewhat clumsy nature of its original implication. It's something that the game, at its core, is forced to confront as a major theme instead of set off to the side as something optional. And while I don't think the flaws giving bonus points was really meant as a &quot;disabilities make you stronger!&quot; narrative and rather just fitting them into a gameplay mechanic, it really is nice and (to me) empowering to have something that more accurately captures the reality of disability, both in its marginalization and its unfairness.<br /> <br /> It certainly has a lot of room for improvement, but at the same time, it's a refreshingly honest take in a lot of other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T02:18:49-08:00","id":1529214,"title":"","content":"I think there's two fairly straightforward paths to improvement. The first is very lore heavy in order to keep the literal born Garou part of the equation, and thus doesn't really fit with W6 (I've discussed this in past threads, the basic idea I have is that the Crinosborn were originally even harder to birth, but weren't deformed and were in fact honored and special for it - kinda like how the Nagah and Kitsune work already - but that the Garou themselves are responsible for a ritual that tainted the Crino-born). The second gets rid of the whole birth angle completely, and thus requires far less setting to implement: steal from BNS WtA with the Bitten.. By taking out being born that way you lose some of the disability representation (though lots of people develop disabilities later in life), but the idea that some times, randomly, humans that survive werewolf bites become werewolves has the benefits of the deformities stemming from a process that isn't how things were &quot;supposed&quot; to be. It also sots the Garou better into existing pop-culture werewolf media. This creates an upper class of born werewolves and a lower class of made werewolves, where the born werewolves are still ultimately responsible for the tactics and behaviors of their members that leads to increased risks of it happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T03:39:19-08:00","id":1529216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529210#post1529210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the ableism stuff:<br /> <br /> Two key points to remember, are that much like Younger and Older Brother, there are a lot of people that gravitated towards the deformities as prominent representation - even if problematic representation - because it was something rather than nothing. Unlike being able to work in disabilities as quirks or Flaws, having a prominent character creation choice that resulted in a disability helps push the unfairness of disabilities into the forefront of the topics that game touches on. It's not &quot;everyone gets a weakness, yours is just something a bit more real,&quot; like Malkavians. The Crinos-born were just screwed over. and it's not fair even in a game sense<br /> <br /> Second, a lot of disabled gamers hate the idea that being disable makes you &quot;stronger,&quot; aka things like Flaws giving you bonus points. This is something that actually come up in a panel Eddy did that they replayed on the Onyxpath Cast ages ago (keeping in mind that Eddy is hearing impaired). The whole idea of &quot;overcoming the adversity of your disability and being a stronger person for it,&quot; is a really toxic abilist narrative of its own. Disabilities are a drag on your life... that's kinda the whole deal. Learning ways to cope with them is just spending time and energy on that instead of thing you'd want to do. Medical treatments are more time, recovery, and money that means missing out on things you'll never get back in the hopes of being able to enjoy stuff later.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, but I don't think it would be viable, I mean, in theory you would have a condition that puts you at a disadvantage and without the bonus points it would be for nothing, it's a somewhat complicated situation to put the player in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T07:38:28-08:00","id":1529219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529216#post1529216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes sense, but I don't think it would be viable, I mean, in theory you would have a condition that puts you at a disadvantage and without the bonus points it would be for nothing, it's a somewhat complicated situation to put the player in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's how the crinos-born already work, though. They do have a few advantages as a breed, but those aren't related to their disabilities, which aside from maybe a few incidental things on a handful of deformities give them nothing in return.<br /> <br /> And you'd be surprised. My group in particular loves piling on flaws long past the point where they get freebies for them, just for the sheer flavor of it all. Some tables just really like facing adversity, and one thing I really appreciate about WoD in general is it's one of the few TTRPGS that gives you the tools for this without tying you down to being as mechanically-optimized as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T08:38:43-08:00","id":1529221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529219#post1529219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's how the crinos-born already work, though. They do have a few advantages as a breed, but those aren't related to their disabilities, which aside from maybe a few incidental things on a handful of deformities give them nothing in return.<br /> <br /> And you'd be surprised. My group in particular loves piling on flaws long past the point where they get freebies for them, just for the sheer flavor of it all. Some tables just really like facing adversity, and one thing I really appreciate about WoD in general is it's one of the few TTRPGS that gives you the tools for this without tying you down to being as mechanically-optimized as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of Crinos, I don't think it's the same thing, because if you make a Crinos character you can choose to make him albino, bald or another minor disadvantage or one that is relatively easy to compensate for, in fact I always wanted to try making a Crinos with claws fragile and that's why he prefer to fight with his fists, now things like being born without one of their senses or without a limb are on another level. So I believe it would be more social pressure that the ST may choose to &quot;ignore&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T08:59:14-08:00","id":1529222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529221#post1529221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of Crinos, I don't think it's the same thing, because if you make a Crinos character you can choose to make him albino, bald or another minor disadvantage or one that is relatively easy to compensate for, in fact I always wanted to try making a Crinos with claws fragile and that's why he prefer to fight with his fists, now things like being born without one of their senses or without a limb are on another level. So I believe it would be more social pressure that the ST may choose to &quot;ignore&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why flaws such as double jeopardy exist.<br /> <br /> Personally, I enjoy making up crinos born designs using the deformities. Whether it is an angel, a nocken, a crow,etc. you can really go wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T09:34:49-08:00","id":1529225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustinCognito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529174#post1529174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, for all the jokes about the ethos of W:tA being &quot;Fuck this wolf or the earth will die,&quot; keeping the Lupus in can be all right if the idea of needing to propagate more Lupus is strictly kept to them, and we avoid weird things like that Homid-Lupus relationship or the Rite of Having A Litter from the much-reviled Tribebook: Children of Gaia Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the way this squick appeared is always so curious. Because some tie it with the Red Talons killing people as WW being ultra edgy for having cannibalistic human hating dog raping werewolves (yes I have seen this take.) At times completely missing the point of the Talons as a reminder that WtA isn't about humanity the way VtM is.<br /> <br /> Then of course there is the equally kneejerk &quot;eww furries&quot; about it. At times even reminding players that they are playing wereWOLVES can get that reaction from some. Which then makes one wonder why they are playing WtA in the first place XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T09:45:05-08:00","id":1529227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529206#post1529206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we need to step back and look at the reason the garouborn/warborn/crinosborn existed in the first place;<br /> <br /> <b>They were there to avoid the garou becoming too insular and breeding with only each other. </b>Having the breed be a sterile result of the mating meant that the garou still had to go to humans and wolves for their offspring. And such have some connection to the world outside caerns.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, there was no such need to avoid insularity as the situation and the stakes were very different.<br /> <br /> But in W5, I do not know which solution is better. Even if who becomes garou is random now (allegedly), you still have tribes like the Fangs, Red Talons and BSDs that could basically remove themselves from the world now entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing....why would they?<br /> <br /> The assumption they would requires assumptions about the Garou by themselves that they would, all things considered, NOT be a part of the world around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T10:02:53-08:00","id":1529229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529227#post1529227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing....why would they?<br /> <br /> The assumption they would requires assumptions about the Garou by themselves that they would, all things considered, NOT be a part of the world around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it avoids issues like the Veil and means there is no need to risk bringing outsiders in. Everyone is already on the same page about the culture. You can see this well in Silver Fangs revised where they have SCHOOLS meant for the cubs.<br /> <br /> Like, I unironically think that in W5, there are BSD cities underground just existing separate from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T10:39:41-08:00","id":1529231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529227#post1529227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing....why would they?<br /> <br /> The assumption they would requires assumptions about the Garou by themselves that they would, all things considered, NOT be a part of the world around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ultimately a matter of the five decision pile-up involved in making the Garou more of an isolated people desperately fighting the last act of a losing war, but there's also the factor of the Curse. In Legacy editions, you got hit with a magic &quot;keep away&quot; button where anyone with permanent Willpower lower than your permanent Rage (and keep in mind the Garou themselves start at 3, maybe 4) would want to do anything to avoid talking to you for longer than a minute. I remember the Ahroun section of the Book of Auspices, written from the perspective of a Fenrir around WWII, who looks at the prospects of Ahrouns finding mates among the greater tide of humanity* and saying, &quot;...technically, the Litany says nothing about gay sex between Garou.&quot; This is why Animal Magnetism, gross and uncomfortable as it was, was described as explicitly getting around the Curse.<br /> <br /> * Yes, Kinfolk, but there was also a point that high Rage makes you a liability to your partner even if the Delirium/Curse isn't a factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28234-justincognito","name":"JustinCognito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T10:50:49-08:00","id":1529232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustinCognito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529231#post1529231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's ultimately a matter of the five decision pile-up involved in making the Garou more of an isolated people desperately fighting the last act of a losing war, but there's also the factor of the Curse. In Legacy editions, you got hit with a magic &quot;keep away&quot; button where anyone with permanent Willpower lower than your permanent Rage (and keep in mind the Garou themselves start at 3, maybe 4) would want to do anything to avoid talking to you for longer than a minute. I remember the Ahroun section of the Book of Auspices, written from the perspective of a Fenrir around WWII, who looks at the prospects of Ahrouns finding mates among the greater tide of humanity* and saying, &quot;...technically, the Litany says nothing about gay sex between Garou.&quot; This is why Animal Magnetism, gross and uncomfortable as it was, was described as explicitly getting around the Curse.<br /> <br /> * Yes, Kinfolk, but there was also a point that high Rage makes you a liability to your partner even if the Delirium/Curse isn't a factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and the Curse was something you could not really go around. Most humans have 3 WP, so anything above 3 Rage would make them think you as a very dangerous person. More Rage over the worse you were seen. You could have 10 WP and still that human would fear you.<br /> <br /> So garou being able to just breed with each other would save them from triggering the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T13:31:49-08:00","id":1529242,"title":"","content":"NB: The Curse also applies to wolves (all animals really) and spirits (though spirits tend to have higher WP, which made the Umbra more welcoming for the Garou.. but not a hard thing to tweak either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T13:41:59-08:00","id":1529244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529229#post1529229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it avoids issues like the Veil and means there is no need to risk bringing outsiders in. Everyone is already on the same page about the culture. You can see this well in Silver Fangs revised where they have SCHOOLS meant for the cubs.<br /> <br /> Like, I unironically think that in W5, there are BSD cities underground just existing separate from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Garou being isolated would just make their job THAT much harder and they would be even less able to do anything against the Wyrm. The Silver Fangs need money, the Glass Walker, and so on.<br /> <br /> Having the BSD have to kidnap new members also doesn't really change their character as a Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:09:44-08:00","id":1529253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529244#post1529244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having the BSD have to kidnap new members also doesn't really change their character as a Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more the BSDs can establish 'healthy' populations away from humanity, previously they produced/recruited massive numbers of Crinosborn but those numbers couldn't sustain the Hive because they still needed to kidnap humans and Wolves to maintain their numbers as they tend to go through Kinfolk fairly quickly with their social issues. Being able to breed using only Garou gives them a massive step up, sure they'll produce mostly humans and Wolves but that just increases their chances of getting Garou as the population waxes.....its horrific and terrible but it's a huge plus for the BSDs not to be reliant on stealing other Tribes kinfolk or tempting their Crinosborn away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:12:56-08:00","id":1529254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529253#post1529253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more the BSDs can establish 'healthy' populations away from humanity, previously they produced/recruited massive numbers of Crinosborn but those numbers couldn't sustain the Hive because they still needed to kidnap humans and Wolves to maintain their numbers as they tend to go through Kinfolk fairly quickly with their social issues. Being able to breed using only Garou gives them a massive step up, sure they'll produce mostly humans and Wolves but that just increases their chances of getting Garou as the population waxes.....its horrific and terrible but it's a huge plus for the BSDs not to be reliant on stealing other Tribes kinfolk or tempting their Crinosborn away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, I don't think that you can really pull that off with the way the BSD are portrayed.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's probably better to make it so the Garou are NOT isolated. Even the BSD.<br /> <br /> The abandoned gas station, the creepy community where they worship the thing in the cornfield, and so on are classics for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:20:08-08:00","id":1529255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529244#post1529244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Garou being isolated would just make their job THAT much harder and they would be even less able to do anything against the Wyrm. The Silver Fangs need money, the Glass Walker, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's thinking as a Company but thinking as an individual Garou with emotions and feelings and empathy there's no reason not to choose another Garou as your partner. They understand you, they are not constantly afraid of what could happen if you lose control, they know your struggles intimately, you are not constantly worried about hurting them, they are not afraid of you or the world you live in.<br /> <br /> Packs are composed, generally, of younger people constantly thrown into dangerous, high pressure situations with high trauma bonds forming ,without the Litany providing social pressure not to I can see large numbers of Packs turning to each other for comfort and understanding.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:21:52-08:00","id":1529256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529254#post1529254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, I don't think that you can really pull that off with the way the BSD are portrayed.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's probably better to make it so the Garou are NOT isolated. Even the BSD.<br /> <br /> The abandoned gas station, the creepy community where they worship the thing in the cornfield, and so on are classics for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But with W5s set up isolation is now a perfectly viable strategy in a way it never was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:29:26-08:00","id":1529258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529256#post1529256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. But with W5s set up isolation is now a perfectly viable strategy in a way it never was before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Because the set up seems that isolation is utter failure.<br /> <br /> They need to get fully in with the human world if they want to try to make any difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:32:13-08:00","id":1529259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529255#post1529255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's thinking as a Company but thinking as an individual Garou with emotions and feelings and empathy there's no reason not to choose another Garou as your partner. They understand you, they are not constantly afraid of what could happen if you lose control, they know your struggles intimately, you are not constantly worried about hurting them, they are not afraid of you or the world you live in.<br /> <br /> Packs are composed, generally, of younger people constantly thrown into dangerous, high pressure situations with high trauma bonds forming ,without the Litany providing social pressure not to I can see large numbers of Packs turning to each other for comfort and understanding.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly is probably the basis for many Garou ROMANCES but I doubt it's the basis for many Garou FAMILIES. Because the simple fact of marrying another Garou is that it is a completely untenable situation for having children, raising them, and providing for them. A Garou may only find true love with another Garou as a joining of equals but a fellow Garou cannot settle down with them unles they mostly retire from fighting the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Like Spider-Man, crime-fighting doesn't pay much and you're going need someone earning the bread too to pay not just for your families but the families of other Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:43:17-08:00","id":1529260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529258#post1529258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it? Because the set up seems that isolation is utter failure.<br /> <br /> They need to get fully in with the human world if they want to try to make any difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they just trying to survive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T16:22:31-08:00","id":1529262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529259#post1529259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It certainly is probably the basis for many Garou ROMANCES but I doubt it's the basis for many Garou FAMILIES. Because the simple fact of marrying another Garou is that it is a completely untenable situation for having children, raising them, and providing for them. A Garou may only find true love with another Garou as a joining of equals but a fellow Garou cannot settle down with them unles they mostly retire from fighting the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Like Spider-Man, crime-fighting doesn't pay much and you're going need someone earning the bread too to pay not just for your families but the families of other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well theres no Kinfolk support system anymore so having a kid means you absolutely are going to have to Lose The Wolf while you raise them and then go back to Garouing once your done.<br /> <br /> Garou no longer have people in the know that they can rely on, ordinary humans and wolves are unable to assist unless you choose to give your child away entirely which means they are even more isolated than ever before.<br /> <br /> You CAN'T have a relationship with an ordinary person without putting their life and mental health in constant danger, you have no choice but to go to other Garou. Kinfolk had knowledge and understanding of the stakes and sure it meant more pressure on them than was fair but it allowed Garou to have families without the constant threat of tragedy.<br /> <br /> In W5 if your not going with Garou then you are choosing to constantly traumatise an ordinary person simply by virtue of being near you.......this is unconscionable and untenable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T16:24:38-08:00","id":1529263,"title":"","content":"Well theres no Kinfolk support system anymore so having a kid means you absolutely are going to have to Lose The Wolf while you raise them and then go back to Garouing once your done.<br /> <br /> Garou no longer have people in the know that they can rely on, ordinary humans and wolves are unable to assist unless you choose to give your child away entirely which means they are even more isolated than ever before.<br /> <br /> You CAN'T have a relationship with an ordinary person without putting their life and mental health in constant danger, you have no choice but to go to other Garou. Kinfolk had knowledge and understanding of the stakes and sure it meant more pressure on them than was fair but it allowed Garou to have families without the constant threat of tragedy.<br /> <br /> In W5 if your not going with Garou then you are choosing to constantly traumatise an ordinary person simply by virtue of being near you.......this is unconscionable and untenable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T19:25:01-08:00","id":1529267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529260#post1529260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't they just trying to survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the entire Renown system means that no one is getting any Gifts unless they kill Wyrmspawn and do great deeds. It's even more dependent on it than before.<br /> <br /> The spirits aren't coughing up anything anymore unless the Garou show they deserve it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529263#post1529263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well theres no Kinfolk support system anymore so having a kid means you absolutely are going to have to Lose The Wolf while you raise them and then go back to Garouing once your done.<br /> <br /> Garou no longer have people in the know that they can rely on, ordinary humans and wolves are unable to assist unless you choose to give your child away entirely which means they are even more isolated than ever before.<br /> <br /> You CAN'T have a relationship with an ordinary person without putting their life and mental health in constant danger, you have no choice but to go to other Garou. Kinfolk had knowledge and understanding of the stakes and sure it meant more pressure on them than was fair but it allowed Garou to have families without the constant threat of tragedy.<br /> <br /> In W5 if your not going with Garou then you are choosing to constantly traumatise an ordinary person simply by virtue of being near you.......this is unconscionable and untenable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I'm hoping we'll receive more information about in new supplements. Human allies that may or may not be biologically related to Kinfolk and rites to allow them to see Garou and not suffer the Delirium. EARTHBLOOD had the caern working with a bunch of radical environmental activists and I'd like to see more of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-23-2024, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T19:54:45-08:00","id":1529268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529267#post1529267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the entire Renown system means that no one is getting any Gifts unless they kill Wyrmspawn and do great deeds. It's even more dependent on it than before.<br /> <br /> The spirits aren't coughing up anything anymore unless the Garou show they deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just chalk it up to the constant disconnect between different passages as to whether nothing has changed or everything has.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that's what I'm hoping we'll receive more information about in new supplements. Human allies that may or may not be biologically related to Kinfolk and rites to allow them to see Garou and not suffer the Delirium. EARTHBLOOD had the caern working with a bunch of radical environmental activists and I'd like to see more of that. </div> </div> </div>Garou usually hang back a bit even when they do have human allies. Else, you know, Delirium and/or risking the Veil. Summoning up a mist or other form of concealment can usually help, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T19:58:20-08:00","id":1529269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529268#post1529268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-righ