 Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T08:29:12-08:00","id":1529310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529309#post1529309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it comes up on occasion but only for story reasons.<br /> <br /> I prefer my players to make scenarios for it like describing how the 17 year old Garou girl once terrified her volleyball time and had to drop out or how a relationship was ruined.<br /> <br /> Forcing it on the players in the middle of a game just kills momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, you do you in your games.<br /> <br /> I mainly asked, because the Curse is the reason most garou in Legacy relied so heavily on kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T08:38:07-08:00","id":1529311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529310#post1529310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, you do you in your games.<br /> <br /> I mainly asked, because the Curse is the reason most garou in Legacy relied so heavily on kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did actually have some homebrewed gifts for the Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers that allowed you to live and work jobs and got rid of the &quot;Curse&quot; for an hour or Scene a Day.<br /> <br /> The players never used them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T10:25:53-08:00","id":1529315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529272#post1529272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with angst.<br /> <br /> Drizzt Do'Urden angsts. Angsting is cool. Spider-Man angsts. So does Daredevil and Batman. They also brood.<br /> <br /> You just need to do it while kicking ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it that difficult to accept that W:tA is a fundamentally different game that doesn't overlap with V:tM very much? When vampires and werewolves are slinking through nightclubs looking for &quot;prey&quot;, the vampires are looking for humans to victimize; the werewolves are looking for a hidden mockery or an evil spirit sticking to someone as part of a guerilla raid. There's little need for angst because the Garou aren't setting out to purposefully ruin someone else's night draining them of blood to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5x5Zv2i83cg\" target=\"_blank\">stick around forever</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T11:13:00-08:00","id":1529323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529315#post1529315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it that difficult to accept that W:tA is a fundamentally different game that doesn't overlap with V:tM very much? W</div> </div> </div> </div>Note I didn't mention V:TM in the slightest.<br /> <br /> You'll have to explain why you don't think werewolves should angst without mentioning vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T14:47:17-08:00","id":1529348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529323#post1529323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note I didn't mention V:TM in the slightest.<br /> <br /> You'll have to explain why you don't think werewolves should angst without mentioning vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't, because of V:tM is what the present RPG-side leadership wants every game to be. Also because V:tM is inextricably associated with angst, the leadership got an old V:tM dev to develop W5... the list goes on and on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T15:05:40-08:00","id":1529351,"title":"","content":"I'll do it even i I agree it's an unfair framing:<br /> <br /> WtA shouldn't focus on angst because there are other emotional dilemmas for games to focus on. Werewolves aren't broody types like Spider-man (though main continuity Spider-man is long since past that, and it was mostly a thing during his teen and college years), Daredevil, or Batman. Their powers are not accident's of fate or circumstance. They were chosen by powers of deity level as champions of said beings' cause. If we're talking comparisons to heroes, they're Superman* living in a world of cardboard, heirs to a legacy of a ancestor that knew they would be far stronger than humanity, and charged them to lead righteously. Superman of course has doubts, and flaws, and so on, but you don't associate him with angst and brooding. Much like another on point example, Captain America, their primary dramatic emotional conflicts are when these strong seemingly virtuous ideals they grew up with, and embraced, turn out not to work in an imperfect way. Harano was added to the games as a &quot;fail state.&quot; Garou that give up on the ideals they were chosen to lead the fight for - to wallow in angst, and brood in depression - have failed to endure the emotional trails of having power.<br /> <br /> When will you Rage? Is not a theme of broody angst. It is a question of how you will use you power when the time comes, and even how you figure out when the right time even is. There isn't a question of if such power is necessary, or if the Garou are right to have it. They were chosen for this task. Their drama is in living up to that burden.<br /> <br /> * - and hey, the things Superman has done to Lois Lane to protect his double identity are pretty resonant with how the Garou can treat their kin sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T15:14:30-08:00","id":1529352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529315#post1529315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it that difficult to accept that W:tA is a fundamentally different game that doesn't overlap with V:tM very much? When vampires and werewolves are slinking through nightclubs looking for &quot;prey&quot;, the vampires are looking for humans to victimize; the werewolves are looking for a hidden mockery or an evil spirit sticking to someone as part of a guerilla raid. There's little need for angst because the Garou aren't setting out to purposefully ruin someone else's night draining them of blood to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5x5Zv2i83cg\" target=\"_blank\">stick around forever</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it occurs to me that for all the insistence that the World of Darkness is about being grimdark - about players playing monsters - that's really not all that true for <i>most</i> of the game lines.<br /> <br /> There's dark subject matter at play, obviously. That's why it's the World of Darkness. And every game line gives players ample opportunity to play bad people.<br /> <br /> But most of the games are, by default, sympathetic to the factions positioned as &quot;Protagonists&quot;. Gaian Garou fight against the Wyrm. Hunters (big and small 'H') fight monsters. Wraiths want to get their affairs in order to pass on. Changelings just want to survive in a reality innately hostile to their existence. Mummies are immortals that need hurt no one to live forever, and also oppose Apothis. None of these splats NEED to be evil.<br /> <br /> With the exception of Demon: The Torment and Kindred of the East (who are just another kind of vampire), Vampire: The Masquerade is kind of the <i>outlier</i> in WoD. Where you're the villain protagonist unless you go out of your way to minimize harm. (I suppose there's also WoD: Mafia. I guess.)<br /> <br /> From a certain perspective, we as WoD fans only really assume it as a whole needs to be Grimdark because Vampire: The Masquerade was the first. Almost every game after deviated from this. (Hell, even early VtM was more accommodating to players running Friendly Neighborhood Vampires. It arguably only got really Grimdark later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T16:11:26-08:00","id":1529362,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> I should clarify before I continue that I was not asking about brooding sarcastically or backhandedly but genuinely wanted to hear the opinion. I should also clarify I think vampires definitely brood and werewolves definitely SHOULD brood (and always have) but they brood about VERY different things.<br /> <br /> Vampires brood about the fact they're Damned. They are going to murder an innocent person and if they've been a vampire more than ten years, have almost certainly already done so. They're trapped with a Beast that will ultimately destroy them and redemption is so hard as to be almost impossible.<br /> <br /> They are GUILT: THE WEEPING.<br /> <br /> Werewolves brood because they're Space Marines in Warhammer 40K meets Miami Vice.<br /> <br /> No, seriously.<br /> <br /> The Garou brood because all of them are trapped in a forever war that will eventually kill them. They've all lost friends and loved ones and pack mates to the seeming fruitless conflict with the Wyrm. Which is where the Miami Vice thing comes in. For such a jazzy neon-colored show, the show's producers already had the controversial view the War on Drugs was a mistake as well as a failure. The heroes fought bad guys and did good but the ability to WIN the War on Drugs was beyond anyone and every episode usually had a bunch of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Like Space Marines they can do immense damage to their enemy but they will never beat it because the enemy is modern civilization and we know as players the Garou will never beat that.<br /> <br /> There's very few &quot;happy&quot; Garou and what sort of psychopath would be?<br /> <br /> You are ever going back into the breach to face the spiritual reflection of the worst of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T18:30:21-08:00","id":1529371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529362#post1529362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> I should clarify before I continue that I was not asking about brooding sarcastically or backhandedly but genuinely wanted to hear the opinion. I should also clarify I think vampires definitely brood and werewolves definitely SHOULD brood (and always have) but they brood about VERY different things.<br /> <br /> Vampires brood about the fact they're Damned. They are going to murder an innocent person and if they've been a vampire more than ten years, have almost certainly already done so. They're trapped with a Beast that will ultimately destroy them and redemption is so hard as to be almost impossible.<br /> <br /> They are GUILT: THE WEEPING.<br /> <br /> Werewolves brood because they're Space Marines in Warhammer 40K meets Miami Vice.<br /> <br /> No, seriously.<br /> <br /> The Garou brood because all of them are trapped in a forever war that will eventually kill them. They've all lost friends and loved ones and pack mates to the seeming fruitless conflict with the Wyrm. Which is where the Miami Vice thing comes in. For such a jazzy neon-colored show, the show's producers already had the controversial view the War on Drugs was a mistake as well as a failure. The heroes fought bad guys and did good but the ability to WIN the War on Drugs was beyond anyone and every episode usually had a bunch of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Like Space Marines they can do immense damage to their enemy but they will never beat it because the enemy is modern civilization and we know as players the Garou will never beat that.<br /> <br /> There's very few &quot;happy&quot; Garou and what sort of psychopath would be?<br /> <br /> You are ever going back into the breach to face the spiritual reflection of the worst of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but this is also kind of missing the bigger picture. It's not that werewolves don't have anything to angst or brood over, or that it has no place in the game at all (hi, harano!). It's more that Werewolf, unlike Vampire especially, is a game about forward momentum and action. As stated before, it's &quot;When Will You Rage&quot;, not &quot;When Will You Be Mired In Guilt And Hopelessness.&quot; Regardless of how hopeless or not the war is, if you spend too much time brooding in Werewolf, it loses a lot of its unique identity as a game that is about direct action. Garou have to keep moving forward, no matter how hard things get. Otherwise it's no longer Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:11:21-08:00","id":1529379,"title":"","content":"Eh, Vampires don't have any reason for angst they know exactly what they are doing and are choosing to do it without any regard for the consequences.....they are choosing to feed other people into the woodchipper so that they can continue feeding people into the woodchipper....and thats it.<br /> <br /> Garou......are either going to destroy the woodchipper or throw themselves into it trying to jam it up for a few days.....any time spent brooding is allowing the woodchipper to continue functioning.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:13:17-08:00","id":1529380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529362#post1529362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should clarify before I continue that I was not asking about brooding sarcastically or backhandedly but genuinely wanted to hear the opinion. I should also clarify I think vampires definitely brood and werewolves definitely SHOULD brood (and always have) but they brood about VERY different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the crux of the matter: It's <i>very different</i>. Your list before had Drizzt Do'Urden, Spider-Man, Daredevil and Batman. These are characters with fears and anxieties but they're very different in terms of what those fears and anxieties are. Angst means different things in VtM and WtA. <i>More </i>angst isn't really something WtA needed. There are issues with the previous editions but I don't think a new edition of WtA should pursue something like &quot;Garou need to experience <i>more </i>angst.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:35:20-08:00","id":1529390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529362#post1529362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;23&quot;]Werewolves brood because they're Space Marines in Warhammer 40K meets Miami Vice.<br /> <br /> No, seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh.<br /> <br /> If you're ever wondering why a lot of us don't feel you as a serious poster on WtA... this sort of take doesn't help.<br /> <br /> Neither does that fact that neither property you just referenced deal with broody protagonists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou brood because all of them are trapped in a forever war that will eventually kill them. </div> </div> </div>No they don't, because - at least in legacy editions - they are part of a thousands of years old culture of noble sacrifice. They fight, even against hopeless odds, on the fervent and zealous belief that their deaths are worth it to fix what's broken. Even if the Apocalypse claims them all, they can win by taking the enemy down with them. The risk of death isn't a reason for them to brood or angst: they are living things that will eventually die. Unlike most of us, they know they have a path to dying for a cause greater than them in a fashion that will actually matter to the future.<br /> <br /> The Garou have hope and faith. That's what makes them so scary to us as the audience. They see this and do not despair, but push to fight harder. We know they're Wrong Genre Savvy. They're not Superman, who will eventually beat Darkseid if they dig down just a bit deeper and fight a bit harder, but they think they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are ever going back into the breach to face the spiritual reflection of the worst of humanity. </div> </div> </div>Yes. Because they will rage against the dying of the light, to the very last, even if their corpses are the pyre to keep the light lit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:37:41-08:00","id":1529391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529362#post1529362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> I should clarify before I continue that I was not asking about brooding sarcastically or backhandedly but genuinely wanted to hear the opinion. I should also clarify I think vampires definitely brood and werewolves definitely SHOULD brood (and always have) but they brood about VERY different things.<br /> <br /> Vampires brood about the fact they're Damned. They are going to murder an innocent person and if they've been a vampire more than ten years, have almost certainly already done so. They're trapped with a Beast that will ultimately destroy them and redemption is so hard as to be almost impossible.<br /> <br /> They are GUILT: THE WEEPING.<br /> <br /> Werewolves brood because they're Space Marines in Warhammer 40K</div> </div> </div> </div>[Abriodged Bardock] No! None of that! Shame on you! [/Abridged Bardock]<br /> <br /> I'll explain why in a beat or two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> meets Miami Vice.<br /> <br /> No, seriously.<br /> <br /> The Garou brood because all of them are trapped in a forever war that will eventually kill them. They've all lost friends and loved ones and pack mates to the seeming fruitless conflict with the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>It can be seen as fruitless, but fighting to stop the monster eating the heart of the world is never a waste. Also, they're not Spess Muhreens because Astartes set out to kill any potential ally they might have against Chaos from day 1 (that was Daddy God Emperor's decree), whereas with the Garou that was an... unintended consequence of their culture become extremely self-important about being at the front lines. The Garou aren't anywhere near as bad as the Catholic Space Nazis (in spite of what Karim might think of them in general and the Fenrir in particular).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are ever going back into the breach to face the spiritual reflection of the worst of humanity. </div> </div> </div>Sure you are. The game has you do it frequently. You'll probably run into something that can kill you, but that's better than worrying over whether or not you can do something. Even if you suck at a task that's sorely needed in the bleak days of the Apocalypse, like the UrbanMech, you're a Trashcan, not a Trashcan't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T19:53:56-08:00","id":1529392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529390#post1529390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they don't, because - at least in legacy editions - they are part of a thousands of years old culture of noble sacrifice. They fight, even against hopeless odds, on the fervent and zealous belief that their deaths are worth it to fix what's broken. Even if the Apocalypse claims them all, they can win by taking the enemy down with them. The risk of death isn't a reason for them to brood or angst: they are living things that will eventually die. Unlike most of us, they know they have a path to dying for a cause greater than them in a fashion that will actually matter to the future.<br /> <br /> The Garou have hope and faith. That's what makes them so scary to us as the audience. They see this and do not despair, but push to fight harder. We know they're Wrong Genre Savvy. They're not Superman, who will eventually beat Darkseid if they dig down just a bit deeper and fight a bit harder, but they think they are.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on this too, this is where the Garou not being (entirely) human also comes into play. They both perceive and live in a world that is just as much spirit as it is physical. As they're much more attuned to the natural flow of life and have a sort-of belief in a &quot;life&quot; after death, whether through stories told about their glorious deeds, reincarnation, or simply returning to Mother Gaia, they don't have all that much reason to fear death like a normal person would, let alone knowing that they're dying for a good cause.. This isn't to say that they don't care about losses at all, but more that you can't really compare their mentality to that of a mundane person, because they're just not. This goes doubly for Lupus and Crinos-Born, who were never human at all to begin with.<br /> <br /> But of course W5 wouldn't care about this, because it's moving too far away from being &quot;&quot;&quot;street level&quot;&quot;&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T20:17:05-08:00","id":1529393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529392#post1529392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To expand on this too, this is where the Garou not being (entirely) human also comes into play. They both perceive and live in a world that is just as much spirit as it is physical. As they're much more attuned to the natural flow of life and have a sort-of belief in a &quot;life&quot; after death, whether through stories told about their glorious deeds, reincarnation, or simply returning to Mother Gaia, they don't have all that much reason to fear death like a normal person would, let alone knowing that they're dying for a good cause.. This isn't to say that they don't care about losses at all, but more that you can't really compare their mentality to that of a mundane person, because they're just not. This goes doubly for Lupus and Crinos-Born, who were never human at all to begin with.<br /> <br /> But of course W5 wouldn't care about this, because it's moving too far away from being &quot;&quot;&quot;street level&quot;&quot;&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean one of the important things about older editions of Werewolf is that you could literally go visit your ancestors in the Umbra, and were secure in the knowledge that when you died, you'd be joining them there. They know for a fact that there absolutely is &quot;life-after-death&quot; so they're not going to be quite as worried about dying. Rather, the real worry was more about dying before they could accomplish their tasks, or help protect the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T21:13:07-08:00","id":1529398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529379#post1529379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Vampires don't have any reason for angst they know exactly what they are doing and are choosing to do it without any regard for the consequences.....they are choosing to feed other people into the woodchipper so that they can continue feeding people into the woodchipper....and thats it.<br /> <br /> Garou......are either going to destroy the woodchipper or throw themselves into it trying to jam it up for a few days.....any time spent brooding is allowing the woodchipper to continue functioning.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean a vampire who doesn't angst becomes a wight and dies quickly. Like 1 in a 100 vampires have the mindset for a Road or Path.<br /> <br /> You can't be a complete monster and survive as a vampire and you can't be good either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T21:14:22-08:00","id":1529399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529390#post1529390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh.<br /> <br /> If you're ever wondering why a lot of us don't feel you as a serious poster on WtA... this sort of take doesn't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I write comedic urban fantasy novels for a literal living so this is who I am.<br /> <br /> And if you don't think either property has brooding, I don't think you're very familiar with either.<br /> <br /> Warhammer 40K is all about the slow end of humanity and fighting tooth and nail as you slowly lose ground forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T22:05:38-08:00","id":1529401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529398#post1529398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean a vampire who doesn't angst becomes a wight and dies quickly. Like 1 in a 100 vampires have the mindset for a Road or Path.<br /> <br /> You can't be a complete monster and survive as a vampire and you can't be good either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if your angsting over stuff your going to do anyway knowing that the terrible things you are doing are ultimately self-serving and utterly unnecessary.....your basically just a liar.<br /> <br /> At least the Wight is honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T23:18:23-08:00","id":1529404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529393#post1529393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I mean one of the important things about older editions of Werewolf is that you could literally go visit your ancestors in the Umbra, and were secure in the knowledge that when you died, you'd be joining them there. They know for a fact that there absolutely is &quot;life-after-death&quot; so they're not going to be quite as worried about dying. Rather, the real worry was more about dying before they could accomplish their tasks, or help protect the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Ancestors Background meant that you could rejoin your family as long as they were around. While it's strongest with the Mokole, there is a strong Book of Life vibe that goes with W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T23:52:18-08:00","id":1529406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529399#post1529399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I write comedic urban fantasy novels for a literal living so this is who I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a biologist. What's your point? Neither of us writes WtA books for a living, so whatever our other life experiences are, they don't dictate (a) what the game as been about for 30 years or what it's about now, or (b) our ability to check irrelevancies at the door.<br /> <br /> If you want to bring being a professional in comedic writing into this? I don't think you're going to like the end result, because it's far more damning of your takes. You've basically done one of the worst things in comedy: &quot;of course I'm funny, so my joke was fine, therefore the audience that doesn't like it must be wrong!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you don't think either property has brooding, I don't think you're very familiar with either. </div> </div> </div>I've played, and watched played, far more WH40K wargames than I care to count. As I've pointed out multiple times, I was a war-gamer before I got into RPGs. Brooding doesn't happen much in WH40K because most people are playing as armies, not individual characters, and while some of the WH40K TTRPGs try to brood a bit in writing, in play it's just as combat happy power-fantasy as the war-game is. It's a franchise about picking a faction and killing its enemies in gratuitous and extreme ways; having long since lost any sight of its original satirical elements in favor of farcical murder extremes. Maybe the fiction is full of broody characters... but that never translates into what people seem to play.<br /> <br /> And Miami Vice is, as you noted, surprisingly good at subversive (for the time) and thoughtful stories, but it never becomes a show about brooding, because it needs to maintain the facade of glitz and glamor that would be ruined if most episodes were more like watching Forever Knight instead. &quot;That really makes you stop and think for a minute,&quot; isn't brooding. &quot;Special episodes&quot; aren't brooding.<br /> <br /> I also notice how you completely ignored me addressing my direct response to your post in favor of getting into this. I take it to mean that you know the whole &quot;brooding&quot; argument was bullshit, you're just throwing out references you are hoping people can't challenge you on, and are just going to be huffy since I fucking can call out your crap on all of this just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T06:13:42-08:00","id":1529418,"title":"","content":"I'm not a 40k player but my partner is and I've read some of the books so I've noticed that the setting has a lot of range of interpretation. Sometimes is gritty military drama, sometimes it's satirical or anything else.<br /> The two main series ive read are horus heresy which is an epic tragedy with strong references to paradise lost and Clapham Caine which has strong comedic overtones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T06:35:43-08:00","id":1529419,"title":"","content":"The thing about Space Marines is that these are trans-human characters. Of course, a lot depends on which writer we're talking about but the thing with Space Marines is that they aren't fully human. One of the undercurrents in the Horus Heresy series is Space Marines wondering what they would even do in a universe that is at peace and whether there's any place in such a universe for them. And the slogan &quot;They know no fear&quot; refers to them literally being incapable of feeling fear. And then there are of course the differences between various chapters/legions of Space Marines. Some care about protecting humans, some care far more about eliminating the enemy. If anything I think the Chaos Space Marines have more of a penchant for brooding (there's usually some perspective as they reminisce about how far they and their brothers have fallen). But the main-reason for all these issues is of course the Emperor who's an absolute asshole <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> The main-thing where the brooding of Space Marines connects with Garou is if you really focus on the idea of Garou being warriors who are absolutely dedicated to their mission and to fight the Wyrm wherever they can find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T06:48:59-08:00","id":1529421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529406#post1529406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a biologist. What's your point? Neither of us writes WtA books for a living, so whatever our other life experiences are, they don't dictate (a) what the game as been about for 30 years or what it's about now, or (b) our ability to check irrelevancies at the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying I roll my eyes DEEPLY at people who take things too seriously and can't poke fun at the humor. It's a boardgame and meant to be fun. If you can't laugh at the absurdities of the setting then I don't know why you'd play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529406#post1529406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also notice how you completely ignored me addressing my direct response to your post in favor of getting into this. I take it to mean that you know the whole &quot;brooding&quot; argument was bullshit, you're just throwing out references you are hoping people can't challenge you on, and are just going to be huffy since I fucking can call out your crap on all of this just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just silly.<br /> <br /> But I don't believe for a second every Garou is happily jumping into the jaws of the Wyrm and unafraid of death. Mostly because I hope their pack leaders slit their throats and cull them from the ranks of the Garou. Wastes of fur and pack. The Garou story is a TRAGEDY and removing that element is, for me, something that kills anything fun about the game. It's reducing it to the most uninteresting possible roleplay and any real versimilitude from the game.<br /> <br /> Yes, they must sacrifice their lives and they will do so but it is so the world can live another day. It is not because they're HAPPY to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-25-2024, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T06:57:14-08:00","id":1529422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529418#post1529418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a 40k player but my partner is and I've read some of the books so I've noticed that the setting has a lot of range of interpretation. Sometimes is gritty military drama, sometimes it's satirical or anything else.<br /> The two main series ive read are horus heresy which is an epic tragedy with strong references to paradise lost and Clapham Caine which has strong comedic overtones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I'm more a novel man.<br /> <br /> The Gaunt's Ghosts books are all about them doing immeasurable damage to the Chaos forces but as the novels move on, it becomes increasingly clear that none of the original Ghosts will survive or get their trophy planet.<br /> <br /> It is just a meat grinder.<br /> <br /> The tragedy and brooding about this realization is &quot;chef's kiss&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course tragedy and comedy are two sides of the same coin. The absolute worst and most boring way you could play Werewolf the Apocalypse for me would be. &quot;You fight the Wyrm and die heroically, saving the day. Wee!'<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T08:39:19-08:00","id":1529432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529421#post1529421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm saying I roll my eyes DEEPLY at people who take things too seriously and can't poke fun at the humor. It's a boardgame and meant to be fun. If you can't laugh at the absurdities of the setting then I don't know why you'd play.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to see chill boardgame players, there's BattleTech. We have UrbanMech memes and often play using bottlecaps as proxies!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's just silly.<br /> <br /> But I don't believe for a second every Garou is happily jumping into the jaws of the Wyrm and unafraid of death. Mostly because I hope their pack leaders slit their throats and cull them from the ranks of the Garou. Wastes of fur and pack. The Garou story is a TRAGEDY and removing that element is, for me, something that kills anything fun about the game. It's reducing it to the most uninteresting possible roleplay and any real versimilitude from the game.<br /> <br /> Yes, they must sacrifice their lives and they will do so but it is so the world can live another day. It is not because they're HAPPY to do so. </div> </div> </div>My head goes into the Abridged Android 16 speech to Gohan, and then I get really angry that the love that a Garou might have for the world around them (at least in the form of Touchstones) can't save them from Harano or Hauglosk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T08:51:47-08:00","id":1529434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529432#post1529432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head goes into the Abridged Android 16 speech to Gohan, and then I get really angry that the love that a Garou might have for the world around them (at least in the form of Touchstones) can't save them from Harano or Hauglosk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess for me it's my love of film noir ala Sin City.<br /> <br /> The system is corrupt, the world is corrupt, and you can't possibly save the world but you can save the little girl from the crazy Yellow Bastard.<br /> <br /> Even if you die trying.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and the World of Darkness has that feel to me. You don't stop fighting even if it's hopeless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T21:15:28-08:00","id":1529488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529434#post1529434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess for me it's my love of film noir ala Sin City.<br /> <br /> The system is corrupt, the world is corrupt, and you can't possibly save the world but you can save the little girl from the crazy Yellow Bastard.<br /> <br /> Even if you die trying.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and the World of Darkness has that feel to me. You don't stop fighting even if it's hopeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why does it feel like that is so absent W5? <br /> The Nation (as a whole) has stopped fighting. That is how it fell.<br /> And the only ones fighting back in an <i><b>organized<sup>1</sup> </b></i>fashion...are a villain faction. Seen as worse than the literal Tribe of people trying to end the world (and thereby kill everyone and everything).<br /> Sure the PCs will be more proactive, but then their meters will start to rise. The PCs are also new to the reality in a meta sense; they are just starting out in the world and the mechanical restrictions of the jaded/depression meter vs their fascism meter is only just starting to affect them. After all, even if they have been around for decades in-universe, they only start interacting with the crunch of the game once they hit play. Meaning that the play cycle is what we should expect from new wolves, not established npcs.<br /> <br /> W:tA can be angsty. &quot;Rage against the dying light&quot; is a great tagline FOR that angst. <br /> <i><b>W5 doesn't do much with it</b></i>, even touching on the idea that the world would be better off if all the Garou gave up the wolf and let their species go extinct. Ideally by helping in some other way. They have no purpose within the setting as written unless you take into account the legacy editions that you have been asked to forget and ignore. After all, you go rescue some campers from Banes and then you get angry (Rage), pushing you towards Hauglosk. Slowish, (depending on what need there is to roll dice), rather than immediately but yeah. <br /> <br /> Look, some of the changes were needed, others weren't awful. But as whole...<br /> W5 doesn't feel like a cohesive game on it's own. Werewolf the Apocalypse shouldn't feel like unbalanced supplement book with weird setting implications.<br /> <br /> 1) And that part is made worse as the game implies organizing humanity to pull back from ecological disaster as one of the things that would help, if only werewolves had any tools for the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T23:08:21-08:00","id":1529492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529421#post1529421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying I roll my eyes DEEPLY at people who take things too seriously and can't poke fun at the humor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're justifying being a condescending ass by making up other people's mental processes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a boardgame and meant to be fun. If you can't laugh at the absurdities of the setting then I don't know why you'd play. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's very fun. It's fun because you don't waste time brooding when that's not what the game is about. Claiming WH40K should be broody, is claiming it should be unfun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's just silly. </div> </div> </div>No, you just hate being wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't believe for a second every Garou is happily..... </div> </div> </div>Who said that? Who used the word happy?<br /> <br /> Nobody. You're lying. You're a liar. You're not a funny, you're just lying to yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529422#post1529422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I'm more a novel man.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet again, we come to a familiar problem:<br /> <br /> CT read a novel, and thus is the master of what a game is about.<br /> <br /> Don't lecture me about what I know about a game because you read a supplemental novel that you liked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The absolute worst and most boring way you could play Werewolf the Apocalypse for me would be. &quot;You fight the Wyrm and die heroically, saving the day. Wee!' </div> </div> </div>No, you've made it clear the worst way to play WtA is to play it with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T05:32:54-08:00","id":1529499,"title":"","content":"Cool off, everyone. I appreciate some people are very upset by this new edition of the game, by views people are expressing, and the ways in which they're expressing them. If this forum topic is causing you aggravation, please leave it. If people act either passive aggressively or outright aggressively, bans will follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T05:52:48-08:00","id":1529500,"title":"","content":"You got it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T22:13:56-08:00","id":1529535,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we can try to aim in a positive direction.<br /> What are some of the changes in W5 that improve the game?<br /> I think some of the name changes are for the better, though some choices don't quite click with me yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T22:37:19-08:00","id":1529536,"title":"","content":"I was originally optimistic about the notion that Garou don't automatically produce Crinos-born among their own. I still try to maintain a positive outlook on that part, even if the game needs rethinking to accommodate and re-name the Crinos-born instead of getting rid of them (following the trend of the Shinju and Ahi, probably).<br /> <br /> The rules for Rage used to not allow some Garou and Fera to frenzy at all outside of some rare occasions that were up to the ST or voluntary using the Gift: Primal Rage. It is good that anyone could potentially frenzy, even if, again, the mechanics could really use some hammering, folding, and other measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T23:41:45-08:00","id":1529538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529535#post1529535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we can try to aim in a positive direction.<br /> What are some of the changes in W5 that improve the game?<br /> I think some of the name changes are for the better, though some choices don't quite click with me yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst the name changes are a positive they are something that a lot of WtA fans changed themselves decades ago....so after years of actively preventing W20 developers and writers from making the changes Paradox should get zero credit for being part of the problem and being very late to the Party.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T23:46:45-08:00","id":1529539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529538#post1529538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whilst the name changes are a positive they are something that a lot of WtA fans changed themselves decades ago....so after years of actively preventing W20 developers and writers from making the changes Paradox should get zero credit for being part of the problem and being very late to the Party.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but again, I am trying to be positive. There are not a lot of changes or advancements in W5 that I feel positively about. So I listed the first one I could think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T00:36:28-08:00","id":1529540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529535#post1529535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we can try to aim in a positive direction.<br /> What are some of the changes in W5 that improve the game?<br /> I think some of the name changes are for the better, though some choices don't quite click with me yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529062-w5-remix-of-rules-and-settings\">This</a> is already a great remix, but here are some of my thoughts regardless;<br /> <br /> -Drop the dog references. Wolves are not dogs. Unless the character is a little person, there is no way anyone would be okay with a 60kg animal running loose. Let alone a hispo.<br /> -Either drop the post-apocalypse thing or make it so it is ACTUALLY affecting everyone. They don't have to know it is supernatural, just that some massive global catastrophe happened.<br /> -Either address each tenet of the Litany or address how with it gone younger garou are doing whatever.<br /> -Drop the CoF. Either don't have a fallen tribe or make it Red Talons/Silver Fangs.<br /> -Make using Rage dice voluntary outside Frenzies. Also make it so you can use Rage dice one at a time if you want to.<br /> -Garou can have jobs thanks to the above changes. W5 is a new setting so let's be forgiving.<br /> -Focus on action over misery, remove the pages upon pages of 'garou suck.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T08:35:33-08:00","id":1529553,"title":"","content":"I think one way you could make it work is to take all the premises of the game (Age of Apocalypse, Garou suck, Gaia's dead/dying etc.) and instead of trying to solve the part of &quot;So now what?&quot; optimistically, you zig instead of zag and go full nihilistic.<br /> <br /> So the premise of the game is more something like this:<br /> <i>You play Garou, avatars of a failed idea. They've tried their best and they failed. They weren't the heroes Gaia needed to survive. But the PCs are still there - basking in the tales of old at a Moot, trying to earn Renown to add new tales and you're still fighting. Things are so bad out there. You gotta do something, right? But Garou trying to save the world is akin to the French cavalry charging a German machine-gun position in WWI. The dead ones are the lucky ones. At least they died with honor. The rest are just insane. There are the ones who fight because they don't know what else to do (Hauglosk), the ones who just wait because they have looked at the world with open eyes and know death when they see it (Harano) and the third group, the most insane of all, who close their eyes and ears to what's in front of them and hope for a better tomorrow (which will never come). </i><br /> <br /> Of course, something depressing like that needs buy-in from the players. And it certainly isn't how I would wanna play WtA. But I think that way the mechanics will at least be helpful in pushing the intended themes instead of standing in the way of it. And, for example, triggering Harano/Hauglosk-tests and making full use of the WP-recovery and &quot;instantly go to Rage 5&quot;-power should be embraced rather than feared because that's the horror you're aiming for. Like with insanity in a Call of Cthulhu game. Still think it feels a bit odd to do that with werewolves but oh well... At least that way you can work with the game's mechanics rather than struggling against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T10:51:56-08:00","id":1529556,"title":"","content":"Werewolf:- For When Your Too Depressed For Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T11:09:01-08:00","id":1529559,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what I was thinking of was Peter Watts' novel Blindsight and how vampires are used there. That kind of nihilism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T16:32:01-08:00","id":1529571,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit late here, but I want to talk about the point about Warhammer 40K and angst.<br /> <br /> While some characters in 40K angst - questioning the morality of their actions, be tortured by what they've seen or done, etc - these are the exceptions. The novels have a lot of them, out of necessity. But, again, the protagonists of the novels are exceptional.<br /> <br /> Most characters in 40K, regardless of army, <i>never</i> question the morality of their actions. Because, as Games Workshop need to remind certain segments of the fanbase depressingly often, &quot;There Are No Good Guys in 40K&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some armies don't angst because it's simply not in their nature. Chaos Daemons are &quot;elementals&quot; of Chaos, devoted to their particular brand of passion and principle, regardless of utility. Neither a Keeper of Secrets, nor any of their Daemonettes, will stop to feel bad about what they're doing nor question why. They are Daemons of Slaanesh, doing things to excess is just what they do. Same with Orks, who think fighting is fun, and Tyranids, who are bioweapons slaved to an alien intelligence beyond human comprehension and know only hunger.<br /> <br /> Mortal followers of Chaos might angst, rarely and on an individual basis. Mostly those who date back from the Horus Heresy and remember they used to be better. (Or the Thousand Sons, who never asked for any of this, at least among those who aren't dust). But most of them are either fanatics for the Ruinous Powers (Word Bearers), overwhelmed by the Ruinous Powers (World Eaters, Death Guard, Emperor's Children), have a massive axe to grind against the Imperium (Black Legion, Red Corsairs), or are power-hungry monsters who do evil because it feels good (Iron Warriors, Night Lords, Creations of Bile, etc). The fact they continue serving Chaos or do Chaos things means they're already highly motivated to be bastards. If they feel angst, it's incidental, and won't stop them. Nor do they worry if what they do is wrong, because they either don't care or think they're in the right.<br /> <br /> Most Xenos factions that aren't violent by nature either think what they do is right (Tau, Genestealer Cults), or fight for survival (Craftworld Eldar, Tau again), or have axes to grind (Leagues of Votann, Necrons). Even the Drukhari, the Dark Eldar, need to do piratical things to maintain their empire, and torture people to keep Slaanesh from eating their souls. Even they don't angst about the evil they do, though. They don't NEED to do any of that, as other Eldar factions show. They do it because it's what they've been doing for thousands or millions of years, and because it's <i>fun</i>.<br /> <br /> Point is, none of the Xenos factions agonize too heavily over the wars they wage. Craftworld Eldar are the most likely to angst, because Elves. Mostly about how they lost everything, and now get to watch the filthy Monkeigh (and the Tau) follow their example as empires on a slippery slope to ruin.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Imperium, it is a fanatical, fascist theocracy. Those that angst about it are few and far between, made all the more notable for the <i>rarity</i> of their clarity. The Imperium does not question the morality of their actions. They believe they are justified in all they do, period. That all mutants, aliens, and heretics must die. That the Imperium must conquer everything. That the Emperor is a god, and all must worship him or die. Anyone who disagrees must be purged, because Disagreement is Treason.<br /> <br /> Ibraum Gaunt and Ciaphus Caine are protagonist Commissars, because they're reasonable enough to be the viewpoint characters of books where they're meant to be viewed sympathetically. Every other Commissar will put a bolt in the back of a guardsman's head for being insufficiently brave in the face of suicidal danger or who isn't committing enough war crimes. Commissars, <i>as an explicit bit of lore</i>, are chosen from prospective recruits for their willingness to murder their own best friends if ordered (because they were ordered to do exactly that).<br /> <br /> Space Marines, barring rare exceptions individually and as chapters (Lamenters, Salamanders), are indoctrinated child soldiers who are made psychologically incapable of questioning their mission. Wherever possible, angst is <i>engineered out</i> of their brains. (Some angst about specific things, like the Blood Angels, with their blood thirst and eventual slide into indiscriminate, permanent homicidal rage). By and large, Space Marines are designed as weapons to protect/further the interests of the Imperium as an institution.<br /> <br /> <br /> At least with Garou, who are similarly meant to be Gaia's living weapons, they're fighting against the ruin and death of life itself. Rather than to prop up a fascist state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T07:41:49-08:00","id":1529591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524711-review-of-w5?p=1529571#post1529571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit late here, but I want to ta